window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":401,"title":"Chapter 401 - 254: Dragon Spear","paragraphs":["A bit of color returned to Xiao Wan’er’s face as it bloomed into a smile. \"If all goes smoothly, the academy should be built before the Spring Festival.\"","Chen Yi smiled and agreed, \"That’s quite fast.\" He then turned to Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang to ask how the disciples from the Celestial Sect were adjusting.","Shen Huatang didn’t have much to say.","These past few days, she had been busy helping Xiao Wan’er with matters concerning the Medical Dao Academy.","In contrast, Xie Tingyun, the senior disciple of the Celestial Sect, was quite attentive to the matter.","She visited the residence where the Celestial Sect disciples were staying almost every day to check on them.","The situation was largely the same as what Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao had described.","Even if some disciples weren’t used to the local customs of Shu State, they were all willing to endure it for the sake of the silver.","Chen Yi had a clear picture of the situation. He planned to have Hundred Herbs Hall take its first step once Yan Sea sent word back about the conditions in Guangyuan.","Only by establishing branches of Hundred Herbs Hall all over Shu State could he resolve the Xiao Family’s shortage of silver coins sooner.","They made small talk for a few moments.","Xiao Wan’er brought up the incident in the West Market, frowning. \"To think Jianghu People are committing murder in broad daylight right here in Shu State City. The situation this year is truly dire.\"","Chen Yi smiled impassively. \"I heard that Spearman has a grudge against the people from Poshisu Country?\"","\"I don’t think so.\"","\"Grandfather just sent someone to tell us that the residence will be on high alert for the next few days. He also told us not to go out unless it’s important.\"","After a pause, Xiao Wan’er looked at him and said, \"You should be careful too, brother-in-law.\"","Chen Yi put down his bowl and chopsticks, nodding with a smile. \"Guiyun Academy and Hundred Herbs Hall. I won’t go anywhere else.\"","He silently added a few more places in his mind.","’Like Spring Rain Building, Chuansi Street, the East Market, and so on.’","There was no helping it.","He wouldn’t be able to rest easy for a while.","Perhaps sensing his thoughts, Xiao Wan’er looked at him with her beautiful eyes and insisted, \"You should still take more people with you when you go out. The residence has Armored Warriors.\"","\"Don’t worry, I’ll be more careful from now on...\"","Chen Yi agreed to everything, his gaze sweeping toward the Qingjing Residence.","He knew that the Old Marquis must have sensed something to increase the security in the residence.","However, it was more likely that Liu Hong’s side had made some unusual moves.","’Considering the time...’","’Liu Hong should be getting anxious by now, right?’","...","Chen Yi’s guess was correct.","After leaving the Governor’s Office, Liu Hong had just entered his inner residence when he coldly ordered someone to summon Liu Taoyao and Zhao Shichang.","In the study, he berated them for well over an hour before finally sitting down in the Grandmaster’s Chair, sipping his tea as he asked:","\"Shichang, you’ve always been meticulous. What are your thoughts on this matter?\"","Zhao Shichang glanced at the profusely sweating Liu Taoyao, thought for a moment, then stepped forward, bowed, and said:","\"My Lord, the men who appeared in Heiyu Lane today were the same mysterious Spearman and the ’Sword Madman,’ Liu Lang, who previously ruined our plans at the Bright Moon Building.\"","\"Therefore, the most important thing right now is to find out why they killed Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao.\"","Hearing this, a trace of worry appeared on Liu Hong’s stern face.","\"That is precisely what worries me.\"","\"Those two killed Wen’er in Iron Wall Town, which indirectly caused the three hundred thousand taels of silver Wen’er was giving to Xiao Dongchen to fall into the Xiao Family’s hands, resolving their pressing financial crisis.\"","He paused, then looked at Zhao Shichang and Liu Taoyao. \"I am truly worried that he is one of Marquis Xiao’s men.\"","Liu Taoyao opened his mouth, wanting to say something, but when he remembered that he was the one who had failed to guard against \"Liu Wu\" yesterday, he was too embarrassed to speak.","Zhao Shichang, however, didn’t hesitate. He replied directly, \"My Lord, I speculate that those two are likely not with the Xiao Family.\"","\"Oh? And why do you say that?\"","\"If they were working for the Xiao Family and had overheard our conversation last night, they likely wouldn’t have directly killed Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao.\"","\"Given the Old Marquis’s cautious nature, he would surely know that keeping Lv Jiunan alive would be more advantageous if he wanted to deal with you.\"","Liu Hong nodded slightly, his expression softening a little. \"Correct.\"","\"Before Xiao Fengchun died, if Marquis Xiao had discovered my collusion with the people of Poshisu Country, he would have certainly led men to arrest me himself.\"","\"Under the current circumstances, he would indeed be more cautious. He would likely choose to capture Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao to force my hand.\"","At this, he turned his head to look out the window.","Beneath the high-hanging bright moon, he could only see a few points of light and a stretch of shadowy buildings.","\"If Liu Wu and Liu Lang are not Marquis Xiao’s men, then why would they attack Lv Jiunan?\"","Zhao Shichang said with some hesitation, \"My Lord, that is also what I do not understand.\"","\"Logically speaking, those two should have no grudge against you. Even if they dislike people from Poshisu Country, it shouldn’t have led them to kill someone right here in the Prefecture City.\"","\"Moreover, Lv Jiunan had already stated that he was King Landu’s brother, yet he was still killed by that Liu Wu...\"","He glanced at Liu Hong and, seeing no reaction, continued:","\"I believe his actions are like malicious sabotage, or even...\"","\"Even what?\"","\"Even that he might be trying to deliberately infuriate King Landu.\"","Hearing this, Liu Hong’s brow furrowed slightly as he lowered his head in thought.","Liu Taoyao, who was beside them, asked, \"Isn’t he afraid of King Landu coming to Shu State to kill him?\"","Zhao Shichang shook his head gently. \"King Landu is indeed powerful, but he can’t possibly come to Shu State alone.\"","\"After all, Shu State is not far from the heart of the Central Plains. It would only take half a day for several Grandmasters to arrive.\"","\"The moment he shows his face here, he will certainly be intercepted and killed.\"","He paused briefly, pondering. \"If he wants to avenge this, his only option is to bring the horse bandits of the Peacock King Banner with him, but...\"","\"But if that were to happen, it would be tantamount to a full-scale invasion by Poshisu Country, which would give the Dingyuan Army reason to mobilize and deploy.\"","Realization dawned on Liu Taoyao’s face. \"So he’s certain King Landu can’t come?\"","\"It’s possible, but King Landu won’t let this go so easily either.\"","After listening to their conversation, Liu Hong vaguely grasped a few suspicious points.","’King Landu, King Landu... and also...’","A flash of insight struck him, and he suddenly asked, \"Shichang, have you considered Asutai’s disappearance in all this?\"","Zhao Shichang froze for a second and subconsciously shook his head before it dawned on him.","\"My Lord, are you saying...\"","\"That Asutai’s disappearance is also related to those two?\"","Liu Hong nodded with a solemn expression. \"The two incidents are too coincidental. I can’t help but be suspicious.\"","\"But, but why would he do that?\"","\"Abducting Asutai, besides foiling your plans, My Lord, would only enrage the Left King.\"","\"Exactly.\"","\"Think about it. What will Left King Mu Hage do once he’s enraged?\"","Zhao Shichang followed his line of thought. \"He probably wouldn’t attack Mengshui Pass for an unfavored youngest son.\"","\"The current internal strife within the Barbarian Race wouldn’t allow him to do so either.\"","\"So, as a second-best option, his most likely course of action would be to vent his anger on that audacious band of horse bandits from Poshisu Country.\"","Liu Hong nodded upon hearing this, his face growing somber. \"There’s more to this than meets the eye.\"","\"If Asutai doesn’t return to the Barbarian Race soon, the Left King will likely send men to clear out the horse bandits along the Ancient Tea-Horse Road, which will in turn provoke the people from the Pirate Alliance.\"","\"Add Lv Jiunan’s death to the mix, and King Landu will be forced to come to Shu State even if he doesn’t want to.\"","Liu Taoyao finally understood. \"Father, does that mean we should find Asutai as soon as possible?\"","Zhao Shichang immediately bowed and agreed, \"My Lord, I will order a city-wide search at once. We must find him.\"","Liu Hong grunted in acknowledgment and added, \"Also, the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office and the Imprisonment Department. First thing tomorrow morning, I will order them to apprehend the culprits as quickly as possible.\"","\"Only by capturing Liu Wu and Liu Lang can this situation be de-escalated.\"","After discussing their plan, Zhao Shichang left first.","Liu Hong looked at Liu Taoyao, who was still kneeling on the floor, his face flickering between light and shadow in the dim candlelight.","Silence fell for a long moment.","Liu Hong then leaned back in his chair, rubbing his temples. \"Now, do you understand your mistake?\"","Liu Taoyao lowered his head and said remorsefully, \"I was wrong. I beg for your forgiveness, Father.\"","\"I won’t blame you, of course. I only hope this incident will teach you a lasting lesson.\"","\"Yao’er, I watched you grow up.\"","\"Over the years, you have matured a great deal in the Government Office and the residence, but you have one flaw—you are far too arrogant and self-willed.\"","Liu Hong looked at him, his face devoid of expression. \"Just like last night.\"","\"Liu Wu’s appearance was suspicious, yet you actually thought of recruiting him. Isn’t that laughable?\"","Liu Taoyao’s face was filled with regret as he bowed low, his forehead nearly touching the ground. \"Father, I know I was wrong.\"","\"Ah, Yao’er, there is no turning back for either of us now.\"","\"From now on, every step must be taken with caution and discretion. A situation like last night must never happen again.\"","\"I will remember.\"","Hearing this, Liu Hong’s expression softened somewhat. He waved his hand. \"Enough. Go back and assist Shichang.\"","\"Yes.\"","Just as Liu Taoyao was getting up, Liu Hong suddenly gave another order. \"Also, have Liu Tianming make a trip to Mei Village tonight. He’ll know what to do.\"","\"Father, you... you’re going to use them?\"","\"An army is trained for a thousand days to be used in a single moment. It’s about time they got some exercise.\""]},{"number":402,"title":"Chapter 402 - 255: Since Yi Was Born, Why Must Fan Exist?","paragraphs":["Spring Rain Building.","As daylight faded, red lanterns were lit one by one, casting a brilliant glow upon the four-story pavilion.","Inside the main hall, a crowd was surging.","Amidst the fluttering draperies and silk curtains, the air was filled with song and dance.","Although the Spring Rain Building wasn’t a Qin Building that dealt exclusively in the flesh trade, it was still a place where beauty was used to entertain guests.","People from all walks of life gathered here, gossiping about everything under the sun, so naturally, they wouldn’t miss out on the latest major events.","While most of it was just boasting, there were a few well-informed individuals among them.","\"Heiyu Lane was a real tragedy today. Dozens of people died. The bodies have piled up and filled the forensic room at the Imprisonment Department.\"","\"I don’t know what kind of deranged maniac did it. They didn’t even spare the beggars and Wandering Martial Artists who were just watching.\"","\"I heard they were killed by hidden weapons. It might have been a Black Magic Master from Poshisu Country. The Cultivation Techniques they practice are all those kinds of evil arts.\"","\"So far, there’s no concrete news from the Government Office. No one knows why those two started fighting in the city.\"","\"Luckily, Heiyu Lane is sparsely populated. Otherwise, who knows how many more would have died violent deaths.\"","\"I heard that ’Dragon Spear’ appeared in Iron Wall Town before. He’s the one who killed the second young master of the Jing State Liu Family.\"","\"Is that so?\"","\"Then the Jing State Liu Family will never let him get away with it.\"","\"Exactly. With the Liu Family’s power, they definitely won’t let the matter rest.\"","\"But what’s strange is that the Imprisonment Department hasn’t issued a warrant for the arrest of Liu Wu or ’Sword Madman’ Liu Lang...\"","However, most of the patrons couldn’t care less about this.","Their eyes were fixed on the young women on the stage, and their lips spoke only of romantic trifles.","\"Everyone, we came here to have fun! Why talk about such sordid affairs?\"","\"Come now, Madam Bao, bring this young master a pot of Divine Bull Tea. This young master is feeling quite exhausted today...\"","The boisterous clamor from downstairs did not affect the person in the quiet room on the fourth floor in the slightest.","The General had changed into a set of blue brocade robes and a formal cap. Dressed up, he looked rather handsome.","But at this moment, his expression was contemplative. His fingers tapped a rhythmic beat on the redwood table, as if he were waiting for something.","Amidst the steady tapping, Lou Yuxue sat on a nearby chair, her head lowered, a strange light flashing in her eyes from time to time.","That Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao had died at Liu Wu’s hands was completely beyond her expectations.","Even though she had brought Liu Wu to meet Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao last night and had noticed his attitude toward them, she still couldn’t understand why he would kill them.","’It was clearly his first time meeting Lv Jiunan.’","Lou Yuxue sighed to herself. ’If I had known that bastard Liu Wu was so untrustworthy, I never would have agreed to cooperate with him.’","’Not only did I not earn any silver, but I almost got dragged down with him.’","And to make matters worse, she had no way of reporting this truthfully to the Lord General.","Just now, when the General had asked about the details of her meeting with Lv Jiunan last night, she hadn’t dared to mention that Liu Wu had been there.","There was nothing she could do. Lv Jiunan’s death had affected the White Tiger Guard’s plans.","Especially the Lord General’s plans.","After all, he was waiting for Lv Jiunan to deliver a message to King Landu about arranging a meeting.","Now, with this situation, even if King Landu did come, it would only be to seek revenge on Liu Wu.","’If the General learns the truth, I’m afraid I’ll be punished too.’","’You bastard! Couldn’t you have asked me before you went and killed them?’","’And you still expect me to help you buy grain? In your dreams!’","Lou Yuxue made up her mind. The next time she saw Liu Wu, she would definitely confront that bastard and ask why he had put her in this position.","Just as she was thinking this, the General’s tapping on the table stopped. \"Lady Tiger, have someone inform Simurgh Phoenix to come here for a meeting.\"","\"Yes.\"","Lou Yuxue did not dare to delay. She rose, gave a few instructions to the Iron Banner Officer waiting outside the door, and then returned.","The General glanced at her. \"What do you know about Liu Zhaoxue?\"","Lou Yuxue was taken aback. \"The Liu Family’s third miss?\"","\"I have only met her twice in Shu State. I only know that she came to Shu State to expand Xinglin Hall’s business.\"","\"However, on the night of the Mid-Autumn Festival, after attending the poetry gathering at Guiyun Academy, she rushed back to Jing State overnight to mourn a death in her family and has not appeared in Shu State since.\"","The General gave a noncommittal nod. \"She’s back.\"","\"Coming back at a time like this... is it still for Xinglin Hall?\"","\"Not just for that. Perhaps we have both underestimated that woman.\"","Seeing Lou Yuxue’s confused expression, the General began to recount his discoveries from during the day.","After explaining everything in detail, he said, \"I suspect that Liu Wu is indeed one of Liu Zhaoxue’s people. What he told you before was all true.\"","After hearing this, a look of astonishment and confusion appeared on Lou Yuxue’s face.","’Could it be that my suspicions have been wrong all along?’","’Has Liu Wu been lying to me this whole time?’","’He’s not from one of the great Noble Families of Shu State close to the Xiao Family at all?’","From the first time he appeared at the Spring Rain Building until last night, he had already changed his identity several times.","A mix of truth and lies, all shrouded in secrecy.","It had reached the point where even she, an experienced White Tiger Guard Silver Banner Officer, could no longer tell what was real.","\"Then... then when the Pavilion Master suspected he was the Fledgling, doesn’t that mean... doesn’t that mean...\"","The General nodded and sighed. \"The Pavilion Master must have misjudged. This Liu Wu has nothing to do with the Fledgling.\"","\"On the night the summer grain in the Three Towns was burned, the Fledgling was indeed with the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","Hearing this, Lou Yuxue murmured, \"My investigation yielded the same result.\"","Even though she had discovered Liu Wu’s identity, she felt no sense of joy, only defeat.","If the Lord General hadn’t come to Shu State and tracked Liu Wu to the residence where Liu Zhaoxue was staying, she had no idea how long it would have taken her to uncover the truth.","After a moment of silence, Lou Yuxue collected her thoughts and asked, \"My Lord, what are your plans now?\""]},{"number":403,"title":"Chapter 403 - 255: Since Yi Was Born, Why Fan Too?","paragraphs":["\"Lv Jiunan is dead, and the horse bandits under the Peacock Banner in Shu State City have gone into hiding. Do you still intend to contact King Landu?\"","The General shook his head. \"Let’s wait and see for a few more days.\"","\"Lv Jiunan was King Landu’s blood brother. Whether he comes seeking revenge or not, he will surely send someone to investigate what happened.\"","\"I’ll find a way to contact him then.\"","\"So for now, I must trouble you to stand guard here.\"","\"If anyone from the Peacock King Banner appears, send word to me immediately.\"","Lou Yuxue answered, \"Yes,\" then asked hesitantly, \"My lord, this subordinate... this subordinate does not know the purpose of your meeting with King Landu?\"","The General paused for a moment, then looked at her and replied, \"Fine. At this point, I won’t hide it from you.\"","\"The reason I want to see King Landu is to complete a transaction with him.\"","A transaction?","Lou Yuxue was inwardly alarmed, thinking he wanted to hire those horse bandits to plunder certain people along the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.","But the General saw through her thoughts, waved his hand with a smile, and said, \"It’s not the kind of transaction you’re thinking of.\"","\"Rather, it’s about the evidence King Landu possesses—correspondence with certain ministers in Shu State.\"","Forgetting herself, Lou Yuxue’s expression shifted. \"My lord, are you saying someone in Shu State is secretly colluding with the Peacock King Banner?\"","\"This... this... Aren’t they afraid the Holy Emperor will become enraged and exterminate their nine generations of kin?\"","The General chuckled, turning his head to look north. He spoke with deep meaning:","\"Shu State is on the frontier of the Wei Dynasty, after all. The heavens are high, and the emperor is far away. When certain people’s ambitions swell, it’s inevitable that their minds will wander.\"","\"Especially after word of what the Ji State Trading Company has been doing up north began to spread, there has been no shortage of imitators here in Shu State.\"","\"Selling ironware, armor, maintaining private armies... Do you think the White Tiger Guard could possibly be unaware of these things, one by one?\"","Lou Yuxue’s brow furrowed slightly. \"Do you have targets in mind, my lord? This subordinate can also use the Bright Moon Building to gather evidence of their crimes.\"","The General shook his head. \"There’s no need for you to get involved.\"","\"After this period is over, the Pavilion Master’s appointment will come through. You will then be a Golden Banner Officer, and I’ll have more important matters to assign to you.\"","After a pause, he said with a smile, \"Besides, the Lord Pavilion Master and I intend to use that evidence to pave the way for someone.\"","\"Under normal circumstances, why would the White Tiger Guard need to make a deal with King Landu? We can arrest people on suspicion alone.\"","Lou Yuxue nodded in agreement and didn’t press the matter further.","She was just curious who the Lord Pavilion Master and the Lord General were paving this path for, that they would take such a cautious, roundabout approach with King Landu.","’Are they trying to wipe away all traces of the White Tiger Guard’s involvement?’","’Or is it that they absolutely need hard evidence?’","Lou Yuxue had no way of knowing. She only knew that the situation in Shu State was likely about to be thrown into chaos.","Especially since that trouble-making bastard was still here...","Just then, a knock sounded from outside the quiet room. An Iron Banner Officer wearing a black iron mask pushed the door open, entered, and said with a salute:","\"Reporting to you, my lord. We have news from the other side.\"","The General asked, \"What have they been up to?\"","\"After Governor Liu finished his duties, he spent four hours in the study with Liu Taoyao and Zhao Shichang.\"","\"The specifics of their conversation are unknown.\"","\"But after Liu Taoyao and Zhao Shichang left, they didn’t return to their residences to rest. Instead, they left the Liu Family estate, and their whereabouts are unknown.\"","\"And Liu Hong?\"","\"He has gone to bed.\"","The General grunted in acknowledgment and waved for him to leave.","After a moment of thought, he said pensively, \"It seems Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao must have been in contact with Liu Hong.\"","Lou Yuxue’s eyes widened slightly. \"My lord, are you saying... Liu Hong is involved with the Peacock King Banner?\"","Recalling what the General had just said, she couldn’t help but be suspicious.","It was just that, as far as she knew, Liu Hong had been in Shu State for many years and was considered diligent and conscientious, never having shown any signs of impropriety.","How could he suddenly get mixed up with horse bandits from the Poshisu Country?","The General shook his head and said, \"It’s not certain yet.\"","\"However, judging by how decisively Liu Wu killed Lv Jiunan, that old fox Liu Hong must be up to no good.\"","\"If I’m not mistaken, Liu Zhaoxue is using this to put Liu Hong in his place.\"","Hearing this, a phrase suddenly popped into Lou Yuxue’s mind.","Reversed Celestial Spirit.","Consider this: one was the Governor of Shu State, the other was the third daughter of the main branch of the Jing State Liu Family.","With such a huge gap in their status, even if Liu Zhaoxue had discovered some leverage over Liu Hong, how would she dare have Liu Wu do such a thing?","Wasn’t she afraid Liu Hong would have her killed?","The General shared her suspicion. He said pensively, \"Perhaps there are details we don’t know about.\"","\"When Simurgh Phoenix arrives later, the two of you will investigate this matter together.\"","\"Yes...\"","...","「Inside Tingyu Pavilion.」","Rainwater dripped from the roof tiles, the PITTER-PATTER sound echoing endlessly.","Amplified by Empty Bamboo, the sound traveled far.","But none of this affected Chen Yunfan in the slightest.","He held a sword in one hand, practicing in the Martial Arts Arena in the central courtyard.","His movements were fluid and free, his Swordsmanship at times agile, at times tyrannical, at times cunning, filling the courtyard with flashes of his blade.","Chun Ying held a lantern, watching quietly from the side, a little puzzled.","For some reason, she felt that Chen Yunfan was somewhat agitated today.","Ever since he returned from the Governor’s Office, he hadn’t even eaten dinner, instead spending all his time practicing his sword in the Martial Arts Arena.","From time to time, he would grit his teeth and mutter a few words.","The words were mumbled and unclear, so Chun Ying couldn’t make out what he was saying, but she knew someone must have angered him.","Even Ning Yu, who was standing nearby, had noticed.","But he was always a man of few words and would never pry.","The simple and honest Niu Mountain said even less, merely whispering praise for Chen Yunfan’s Swordsmanship.","\"Brother Ning, the Young Master’s Sword Dao has improved again, hasn’t it?\"","\"It has... No, I’m warning you, don’t call me Brother Ning!\"","\"Ning... So, has the Young Master improved or not?\"","\"He has!\"","Chun Ying ignored the two clowns. Seeing that Chen Yunfan had finished a set of sword forms, she thought for a moment before stepping forward to offer him a towel."]},{"number":404,"title":"Chapter 404 - 255: Since There Is Yi, Why Must There Be Fan?","paragraphs":["\"Young Master, you’ve been training for six hours. You should rest for a bit.\"","Chen Yunfan hesitated for a moment, then sheathed his sword. He took the towel and wiped the sweat from his forehead, a hint of displeasure still on his face.","He looked up at the moon and stars in the night sky and asked, \"Has there been any word from over there?\"","Chun Ying shook her head. \"Not yet.\"","\"It’s a long and arduous journey. Even for the White-robed Minister, it will take time to contact the master.\"","Chen Yunfan was well aware of this, but he couldn’t help but feel anxious when he thought of Chen Yi’s terrifying Martial Arts Cultivation.","This was especially true after he learned what happened in Heiyu Lane today. It was clear to him that the gap between him and Chen Yi hadn’t shrunk; it had grown even wider.","—To kill Lv Jiunan with a single strike.","He didn’t need to think twice to know that was a feat he couldn’t accomplish.","Forget a single strike—he wasn’t sure he could defeat Lv Jiunan even in a hundred or a thousand moves.","’Black Magic may not compare to the Witchcraft and Gu Poison Dao, but it’s still not something to be trifled with.’","’Especially with those deadly poisons. If it were me, I would never have been so reckless as to get close to Lv Jiunan.’","’Only Brother Yi, a Medical Saint Hand like him, wouldn’t be afraid of being hit with a deadly poison.’","As Chen Yunfan thought about all this, his expression grew even more sour.","After wiping the sweat from his face, he let out a sudden sigh. \"If there is an Yi, why must there be a Fan?\"","Chun Ying heard this clearly. She gave Chen Yunfan a quizzical look and asked:","\"Young Master, why would you say that?\"","She was well aware that Chen Yunfan held Chen Yi in high regard, and she knew their relationship was far from ordinary.","But she truly couldn’t fathom why Chen Yunfan would say such a thing.","In her eyes, even if Chen Yi was an instructor at Guiyun Academy and had achieved Perfection in the Calligraphy Dao, he was no match for Chen Yunfan, who had become the top scholar in the imperial examinations and now served in the Governor’s Office.","Chen Yunfan glanced at her. He didn’t tell her the truth, just offered a vague reply.","\"Well... my Calligraphy Dao can’t compare to his, and I’m not as lucky.\"","\"Luck?\"","\"Don’t ask so many questions. Just help me keep an eye on things...\"","After a bit more small talk, Chen Yunfan was about to go wash up and change his clothes when he saw a carriage pull up in the distance and stop outside the Martial Arts Arena.","Cui Qingwu alighted gracefully and said with a smile, \"Brother Yunfan, just finished cultivating?\"","Chen Yunfan nodded and gestured toward her. \"Are you... heading out?\"","\"Yes, Yunqing Building is hosting two banquets tomorrow. I’m going to take inventory of the drinks.\"","Cui Qingwu offered an excuse, but she didn’t fool Chen Yunfan.","He had long since known that Cui Qingwu was part of the White Tiger Guard, but he didn’t let on.","\"Be back soon. I’m going to get some rest.\"","Seeing him about to leave, Cui Qingwu raised a hand and said, \"Brother Yunfan, I plan to visit Sister Wan’er the day after tomorrow. Do you want to come along?\"","\"To the Xiao Family?\"","An image of Chen Yi’s face flashed through Chen Yunfan’s mind, and he waved his hand in irritation.","\"No, definitely not...\"","He decided that until he achieved a breakthrough in his Sword Dao, he would appear before Chen Yi as little as possible to avoid the unbearable pressure.","Once he was a good distance away, Cui Qingwu gave Chun Ying a thoughtful look and asked:","\"Is he in a bad mood today?\"","Chun Ying shook her head. \"I’m not sure either.\"","She didn’t answer truthfully, inwardly guessing that Chen Yunfan’s mood had something to do with Chen Yi.","She just didn’t know what Chen Yi could have done to bother Chen Yunfan so much.","Cui Qingwu gave her a long, searching look, then nodded without another word, turned, and climbed into her carriage before leaving.","Chun Ying lowered her head in thought for a moment before summoning Ning Yu and whispering an order:","\"Go find out what happened at the Governor’s Office today.\"","\"Yes...\"","...","「Spring Lotus Garden, the Purple Bamboo Forest.」","Chen Yi slowly practiced his Mountain Shattering Fist, keeping his movements as quiet as possible so as not to disturb Xie Tingyun and the others.","The day’s events had left him feeling unsettled, which inevitably affected his Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill.","That was why he had come to the Purple Bamboo Forest to practice and clear his head.","’Liu Hong will make one of two moves next: either find Asutai, or distance himself from Lv Jiunan’s death.’","’He won’t make any big moves on the first count, unless he wants to alarm all the major powers in Shu State.’","’As for the second, it’s still unclear. That will depend on how King Landu reacts.’","’Then there’s the matter of the White Tiger Guard.’","’I imagine Lv Jiunan’s death is causing that Golden Banner Officer a huge headache.’","’And finally, there’s the Xiao Family...’","As these thoughts ran through his mind, Chen Yi’s movements never paused.","The faint wind from his punches rustled the bamboo leaves, causing a few to drift to the ground.","’Ultimately, I will have to use the Xiao Family to eliminate Liu Hong. Best to finish it all in one decisive blow.’","’The same goes for all those other demons and devils.’"]},{"number":405,"title":"Chapter 405 - 256: He Is My Son","paragraphs":["Countless eyes were currently on the Xiao Family.","This included the Dingyuan Army of the Three Towns and the Noble Families close to the Xiao Family.","Any move they made would be instantly detected.","Elder Master Xiao and Xiao Jinghong were under particularly intense scrutiny.","Furthermore, the Xiao Family’s ranks were thin; the old were old, the young were young, and talent was scarce.","Fortunately, Xiao Jinghong was struggling to hold things together. Otherwise, their situation would be even worse.","Chen Yi knew this, which was why he had chosen to abduct Asutai and Lv Jiunan and hide them away.","Only by doing so could he throw Liu Hong into disarray, thereby pushing the situation in Shu State toward chaos.","And such a situation, conversely, would benefit the Xiao Family.","They had long been at the center of the storm, growing accustomed to such circumstances over the years and preparing for the day they would be besieged on all sides.","When everyone sensed that something was amiss and found a knife hanging over their own heads, leaving them scrambling to save themselves, who would still spare a thought for the Xiao Family?","’Liu Hong must believe Lv Jiunan is dead, and that no one else could possibly discover his connection to King Landu.’","’Furthermore, Lv Jiunan’s death has, to some extent, covered up the fact that the East Market Grain Storehouse was burned down.’","’Therefore, Liu Hong’s next move will definitely be to focus on finding Asutai.’","As Chen Yi contemplated his next moves, he finished practicing his fist and step techniques, such as the Mountain Shattering Fist and the Hundred Flowers Palm.","He slowly concluded his practice, exhaled a long breath, and tilted his head up to the night sky.","Moonlight and starlight filtered through the branches and leaves of the Purple Bamboo, scattering specks of brilliance that coated everything in a silvery sheen.","A cool breeze rustled by, causing bamboo leaves to drift down in a scene of serene, natural beauty.","Chen Yi looked away, tidied up the Purple Bamboo Forest, and returned to his room.","’It’s still not enough.’","’Even Elder Master Xiao can barely hang on for two or three years, let alone an ambitious man like Liu Hong.’","’I need to add more fuel to the fire.’","The closer people came to death, the more desperate they became.","Such was human nature, unchangeable by any external force.","Liu Hong was no exception.","Just as he was thinking, midnight arrived, and a golden light flashed before him:","[Daily Intel - Yellow-level Middle Grade: At noon, a disturbance will break out at the East Market Grain Store. Reward: A minuscule amount of Opportunity.]","Chen Yi glanced at it, a slight smile appearing on his face.","It didn’t take much to figure out.","With grain prices in Shu State having skyrocketed severalfold, it was indeed time for some chaos.","’Everything is ready; all that’s missing is the east wind.’","’Heh, but it won’t be long now.’","’That wind... is about to arrive.’","Smiling, Chen Yi finished cleaning up any traces of his presence in the Purple Bamboo Forest, returned to his room, and sat cross-legged on the bed to begin cultivating the Four Symbols Skill.","After more than an hour of contemplation, he had thoroughly perfected his plans, allowing him to finally immerse himself in Cultivation.","Ever since he broke through to the Fifth Grade, his Cultivation had continued to advance rapidly.","However, compared to his previous pace of advancing a minor stage every five days and breaking through a major Realm every half a month, his current rate of progress had slowed somewhat.","Six days had passed since he broke through to the Fifth Grade Realm, yet he still hadn’t reached the Middle Stage.","Fortunately, Chen Yi wasn’t impatient for quick success.","His Spear Dao had now reached Perfection, and he had also mastered the Dragon-Falling Spear Technique, which was more than enough to deal with Martial Artists in the Middle Three Grades Realm.","Even against someone with an Upper Three Grades Cultivation, he still had a fighting chance.","Of course, that was assuming their Technique Realm had not surpassed Minor Success, or had only just entered Great Success.","As Chen Yi’s mind sank into his Cultivation, strands of Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism surged toward him from all directions.","It poured into his meridians, flowing into his Dantian and Chest, all the way to the Forehead Acupoint Sea of Qi.","There, the four Divine Beast Spiritual Essences continuously refined it, gradually strengthening his True Essence.","Fluorescent light of red, gold, blue, and green swirled around his body, gradually enveloping him like a misty cloud.","...","While Chen Yi was cultivating peacefully, many others were destined for a sleepless night.","Elder Master Xiao was one of them.","However, aside from sensing the unrest in Shu State City and ordering the household to be on high alert internally while maintaining a relaxed outward appearance, he made no major moves.","The only reason he had not yet rested was because news had arrived from Guangyue Prefecture.","There were no surprises.","Duke Qian, Zhang Xuan, had readily agreed to lend them grain, promising to have it delivered to Shu State Prefecture City within half a month.","He was also sending an additional two hundred thousand in silver.","Elder Master Xiao looked at the letter in his hand, his old heart filled with relief.","\"At a critical moment, I must rely on an old friend’s help. I... SIGH.\"","Xiao Jing, who was by his side, consoled him, \"Marquis, you need not be so troubled. Desperate times call for desperate measures. Besides, you are doing this for the good of Shu State.\"","\"That may be so, but ever since I inherited the Marquis Position, I have never once asked another for help. I can’t help but find it unsettling.\"","Xiao Yuan had spent his life in the military, and he had almost always been the one helping others.","To suddenly be the one asking for help felt deeply awkward for a man of his proud nature.","Xiao Jing knew this well. He sighed inwardly and said quietly, \"I am incompetent and unable to share the Marquis’s burdens.\"","Elder Master Xiao put down the letter. \"This has nothing to do with you.\"","\"As the Commander of the Xiao Family’s Hidden Guard, your duty is to focus on gathering intelligence on everyone’s reactions and to guard the family. That is all.\"","\"If I sent you out to find silver, I can’t imagine you’d find any other way than to rob people.\"","Xiao Jing pressed his lips together. \"If the Marquis were to permit it, I...\"","Before he could finish, Elder Master Xiao shot him a glare. \"You dare?!\"","Xiao Jing hastily dropped to his knees. \"Forgive me, Marquis! I would not dare.\"","Elder Master Xiao snorted. \"The Xiao Family’s situation is indeed difficult, but we have not yet fallen so low as to resort to such dishonorable deeds!\"","\"If I were to truly do such a thing, wouldn’t the Xiao Family’s centuries of reputation be ruined in an instant?\"","\"When my time comes, how could I possibly face my ancestors?\"","Shame crossed Xiao Jing’s face. \"I misspoke. I beg the Marquis’s forgiveness.\"","Elder Master Xiao stared at him for a long moment before finally sighing. \"Enough, enough.\"","\"Our Xiao Family’s two-hundred-year foundation has always been supported by the fief our ancestors conquered. It is indeed a bit shameful.\"","\"Fortunately, Wan’er is a capable manager. The few Medicine Halls we own bring in a considerable profit each month, so the family does not want for food, clothing, or daily expenses.\""]},{"number":406,"title":"Chapter 406 - 256: He Is My Son","paragraphs":["\"Otherwise, I’m afraid I’d have to kneel before our ancestral tablets and confess my failures.\"","The Elder Master said this self-deprecatingly.","But Xiao Jing knew it wasn’t that the Xiao Family was poor at managing its assets; they simply chose not to.","If the Xiao Family Patriarchs over the generations had wanted to do so, they wouldn’t have just a single plot of land in Tonglin.","They would have long ago been like some of the other Noble Families, appearing to have exhausted their wealth when, in reality, they had used it all to acquire farmland.","It was said that the family of a certain minister in the court did exactly this.","They appeared to live frugally, but the family’s land holdings amounted to thousands upon thousands of acres.","After a century of inheritance, the silver coins in their cellars were piled mountain-high.","After a moment of silence,","The Elder Master leaned back in his chair and waved a hand, gesturing for him to rise.","\"Have you investigated what happened today?\"","Xiao Jing rose and replied, \"It’s been thoroughly investigated.\"","\"The two who died... one was Lv Jiunan, the other was named Ge Muxiao. They were both horse bandits under the Peacock King of Poshisu Country.\"","\"Moreover, Lv Jiunan was the third brother of King Landu—his full-blooded brother.\"","Elder Master Xiao frowned slightly. \"Then why did Liu Wu kill him?\"","Xiao Jing’s expression faltered. \"Forgive me, Marquis, but I do not know.\"","\"However, I have already arranged for men to investigate their movements in Shu State. If we can find where they were staying, we should be able to deduce a few things.\"","\"And Liu Wu?\"","\"He... he’s disappeared again.\"","\"Thousand Households Han Ruixuan of the Imprisonment Department hired expert trackers, but they couldn’t find any trace of him. All we know is that he’s still somewhere in the city.\"","The Elder Master nodded slightly, saying thoughtfully, \"Liu Wu... He has helped our Xiao Family several times now.\"","\"Do you think that’s why he killed Lv Jiunan this time as well?\"","\"Well...\"","Xiao Jing replied with some hesitation, \"I cannot be certain.\"","\"Lv Jiunan is different from those Evil Demonic Dao practitioners from the Bright Moon Building. He’s King Landu’s full-blooded brother. If someone in Shu State colluded with him, wouldn’t that mean...\"","He dared not say more.","But Elder Master Xiao already understood.","Poshisu Country was, after all, a foreign enemy.","If someone dared to conspire with a foreign enemy to harm the Xiao Family, it would be an act of outrageous treachery—it would be treason.","Killing intent instantly filled the Elder Master’s cloudy eyes. He ordered in a low voice, \"You must thoroughly investigate their past movements in Shu State.\"","\"Find out where they stayed, who they met, and what they did.\"","\"Report to me the instant you discover anything!\"","\"Yes!\"","\"Also, keep an eye out for Liu Wu. If you find him...\"","After a pause, the Elder Master shook his head. \"Never mind. Don’t alert him. If he provides any help, come report to me then.\"","Xiao Jing nodded to show he understood, then turned and left.","After he left,","The Elder Master took a letter from his robes.","The white envelope bore no signature, but he knew exactly who the sender was.","He sat quietly for a moment before opening the envelope, taking out the letter, and beginning to read:","Duke Dingyuan, my son Qingzhou is simple by nature. I’ve troubled you to look after him.","Xuanji will soon be setting off to return to Great Wei. If there is an opportunity, I will be sure to thank you in person.","Though it was only a few dozen words long, the Elder Master read it three times.","Only after reading it word by word, sentence by sentence, did he put the letter down, a trace of desolation on his face.","’Chen Xuanji has been in the Western Buddha Country for several years. Is he finally coming back?’","’He’s coming to question me...’","...","「Capital Prefecture.」","The bright moon hung high in a clear, vast sky, and the endless sea of stars was clearly visible.","At the foot of the Imperial City stood a heavily guarded five-story pavilion that looked completely unremarkable from the outside.","Inside, however, it was currently brightly lit.","The first floor was set up as a clothier’s shop. The outer room displayed hundreds of bolts of fabric in various colors, while the back had fitting rooms and a storeroom.","Deep within the storeroom was an inconspicuous door, hidden behind piles of fabric.","But behind the door, several guards in white robes and white masks stood watch.","Their gazes were cold as they stood motionless, hands gripping the long swords at their waists.","Even the occasional footsteps and quiet conversation from upstairs could not make their gazes waver in the slightest.","Meanwhile, in a quiet room deep on the fourth floor,","A man in a white robe embroidered with a python pattern stood at the window, calmly gazing at the night sky. He, too, was holding a letter.","By the dim candlelight behind him, one could vaguely make out several lines of large characters written in Wei Qing’s Style.","To my dear Father, from your son, Yunfan.","I have not seen you in several years and miss you greatly. I was overjoyed to hear that you will soon be returning from the Western Regions.","You have likely already heard that I became the top scholar in this year’s examinations. It’s nothing much to speak of, really—just the result of my diligent studies these past few years. Fortunately, I did not disappoint your expectations.","By the Holy Emperor’s grace, I was appointed to a position in the Shu State Governor’s Office. This, too, is hardly worth mentioning. A mere Advisor is a far cry from the positions you and Second Uncle hold.","...I have met with Fifth Brother, Chen Yi, several times.","He is living very well, dressed in finery and eating delicacies. He is now highly regarded by the Xiao Family and has even become an Instructor at Guiyun Academy by virtue of his Perfection Realm Calligraphy Dao.","When you return from the Western Regions, I hope you will not blame Mother for letting Fifth Brother marry into the Xiao Family. Of course, I would also like to know if you were aware of this matter.","Also, I wish to know this: Fifth Brother has started practicing Martial Arts, and his Cultivation is only three major Realms lower than my own. Were you the one who taught him?","Faintly visible before the word \"three\" was the word \"two,\" which had been messily blotted out.","The white-robed figure—Chen Xuanji—retracted his gaze. Looking at the letter in his hand, he softly recited:","\"Joy and sorrow, partings and reunions, all are part of life. The moon waxes and wanes, shines and dims. Such things have never been perfect. Let us hope for a long life, to share this same moonlight though a thousand miles may part us.\"","His tone was inscrutable, tinged with a hint of lament.","Before the last words faded, he crushed the letter in his hand and scattered the pieces out of the window.","’Given Yunfan’s restless nature, Qingzhou’s Martial Arts must have far exceeded his imagination for him to go to the trouble of sending this letter.’","As the saying goes, no one knows a son like his father.","Chen Xuanji knew Chen Yunfan’s character well, so it wasn’t difficult for him to deduce Chen Yi’s current Martial Arts Cultivation.","’The Lower Three Grades?’","’No, that’s not right. Qingzhou’s Cultivation should be in the Middle Three Grades.’","’Hah. A bunch of useless fools.’","Chen Xuanji wasn’t cursing just anyone; he was referring to the White Tiger Guard members in Shu State responsible for investigating Chen Yi’s Martial Arts Cultivation.","Thinking of the previous letters he had received, his eyes showed a flicker of displeasure.","But on second thought, he felt it was only to be expected.","Given Chen Yi’s temperament, if he truly wanted to hide himself, it would be impossible for anyone to detect his Martial Arts Cultivation or his Technique Realm.","It was just that his Martial Arts...","Chen Xuanji gently removed the white tiger pattern mask from his face, revealing a slightly pale complexion.","His features could be described as exceptionally handsome and refined.","Even though he was over forty, his face was still striking.","Below his sharp, sword-like brows was a pair of upward-slanting phoenix eyes. He had a high-bridged nose, full lips, and a calm, dignified expression.","’Counting the days, it’s been less than a year since Qingzhou arrived in Shu State.’","’For his Martial Arts Cultivation to reach the Middle Three Grades Realm in such a short time, there must be a secret I’m not aware of.’","If it were only that, it might be acceptable.","But Chen Xuanji knew there was more to Chen Yi’s Martial Arts than that.","He had guessed correctly—the Liu Wu who had appeared outside Iron Wall Town was, indeed, his son, Chen Yi!","’Liu Wu. Sixth Grade Cultivation, Spear Dao Perfection.’","’If Qingzhou is ’Liu Wu’... and you add his Perfection Realm Calligraphy Dao...’","For the first time in his life, Chen Xuanji felt a pang of regret.","A son so accomplished in both scholarship and martial arts, whom he had arranged to marry into the Xiao Family as a \"discarded pawn\"—how could he not feel regret?","’Thankfully, my uncles and the other elders don’t know about this yet. Otherwise, I’m afraid they would curse me relentlessly.’","As Chen Xuanji thought about this, his fingers gently stroked the white tiger pattern mask, and a look of helplessness crossed his face.","Chen Yi’s transformation had truly been beyond his expectations.","No, it would be more accurate to say it had *far* exceeded his expectations.","But the facts were the facts, and he had no choice but to accept them.","’A fledgling, heh...’","’He’s certainly turned into a great roc that blots out the sun.’","’But it seems he no longer belongs to the Chen Family.’","Chen Xuanji was no fool; he naturally understood the purpose behind Chen Yi’s actions.","Preventing the Bright Moon Building from burning the Three Towns’ summer grain in Iron Wall Town, and killing Liu Wen—all of it was undoubtedly for the Xiao Family.","And before that, the ’Liu Wu and Liu Lang’ who acted outside Shu State City were suspected of killing members of the Five Poison Sect.","’Thinking about it now, Qingzhou has done all of this for the Xiao Family.’","’Duke Dingyuan, it looks like I’m going to lose on this deal.’","Chen Xuanji gave a helpless smile, then placed the white tiger pattern mask back on his face.","The helplessness in his eyes gradually faded, replaced by calm.","In the blink of an eye, he had resumed the dignified air of the Great Wei Dynasty’s White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master.","’Although there have been some surprises, he is my son, after all.’","’We are connected by blood, after all...’","With this thought, Chen Xuanji flashed back to a spacious room deep on the second floor.","Several members of the White Tiger Guard in red robes were already kneeling on the floor.","\"Send a message to the General. Have him meet with King Landu as soon as possible. If necessary, he may proceed to the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.\"","\"Yes!\""]},{"number":407,"title":"Chapter 407 - 257: I... I’m Getting My Revenge","paragraphs":["「Five days passed in the blink of an eye.」","The weather in Shu State turned from sunny to overcast.","Gray clouds rolled like ocean waves, stretching for thousands of miles. A great sun, ringed by a pale halo, was faintly visible.","The lack of wind left the city feeling a bit muggy and stifling.","Much like the common folk coming and going in the East and West Markets, every face was tinged with a measure of sorrow.","\"The price of grain has gone up again.\"","\"Five days ago, a *dan* of fine grain cost one-and-a-half taels of silver. Three days ago, it rose to two taels of silver. And today, that Lin’s Grain Store opened with its listed price having soared to two and seven-tenths taels of silver.\"","\"The way I see it, tomorrow it’ll probably hit three taels of silver for a *dan* of grain.\"","\"Damn it, these crooked merchants!\"","\"When the price of grain drops, they’re all slower than the last. But when it goes up, they’re all trying to outpace each other!\"","\"If this keeps up, my family’s really going to run out of food.\"","\"Sigh, my boy’s been complaining he’s hungry for the past two days. Me, I haul sandbags all day, and it’s only enough to buy a single bowl of noodles...\"","This situation naturally led the common folk to complain.","Especially the poor families.","They toiled away every day, yet the money they earned wasn’t even enough for one person to eat their fill, let alone feed an entire family.","\"Damn it all, didn’t they say our Shu State had a good harvest this year? Why is there a grain shortage?\"","\"It was good, but it couldn’t stand up to natural and man-made disasters.\"","\"A while back, heavy rains caused the Chishui River to burst its downstream dams, flooding the fields in three counties to the east.\"","\"If the Governor’s Office hadn’t requested it, ordering those few County Yamens to release their grain stores, I’m afraid a famine would have broken out over there long ago.\"","\"And on top of that, here in our Prefecture City...\"","\"I heard a while back that the East Market Grain Store’s warehouse burned down, so the store had no choice but to raise its prices.\"","\"Who said that?\"","\"How come I heard it’s because the grain in Iron Wall Town was burned, and Marquis Xiao bought a huge amount of grain to replace it, which caused several grain stores to raise their prices?\"","\"Marquis Xiao? Impossible!\"","\"Just yesterday morning, someone from the Xiao Family posted a notice at the Government Office, explaining that the military grain for the Three Towns came from another source. How could it be the Xiao Family?\"","\"They say that, and you just believe it? I’m telling you, they’re the ones who bought it.\"","\"Hmph, you even dare to slander the Xiao Family? I think you’re tired of living!\"","\"You... Hey! Don’t hit me, don’t hit me! I was wrong...\"","It seemed like a farce, but in truth, similar incidents were happening all over the Prefecture City.","Of course, most people didn’t believe the Xiao Family was the culprit behind the rising grain prices. But when enough people say something, it’s inevitable that some will blindly follow.","This was especially true for the hungry, who began to point their fingers at the Xiao Family and the grain stores of the East and West Markets.","The Xiao Family was naturally aware of the situation internally, but with so many rumors flying around, even posting a notice wasn’t enough to shut everyone up.","\"Young Master, do you think those people are doing it on purpose?\"","Xiaodie clenched her little fists and waved them a few times, saying indignantly:","\"The Third Master already posted a notice at the Government Office door, but they just refuse to believe it! They insist that Iron Wall Town buying a large amount of grain is the real cause of the price hike.\"","Chen Yi stood before his desk, brush in hand, sketching on a piece of paper. He smiled and said:","\"You, you should listen less to what people outside the estate are saying. Just hear it and let it be, don’t go arguing with them.\"","\"With grain prices in the Prefecture City having multiplied, many people can’t eat their fill. They have a fire in their chests with nowhere to vent it, so naturally, they’ll be exploited by those with ulterior motives.\"","Hearing this, Xiaodie’s anger subsided a little. She asked, \"Young Master, are you saying someone is fanning the flames from behind the scenes?\"","\"Perhaps.\"","\"In any case, if the sky falls, the tall ones will hold it up. It’s best to let the masters of the house handle this matter.\"","As Chen Yi spoke, he finished a line drawing, set down his wolf hair brush, and picked up the sheet to blow the ink dry on the Yunsong Paper.","These past few days, he had spent most of his time practicing his Painting Skill. He had already practiced three techniques—ink-wash painting, line drawing, and color painting—to the Skilled Level.","He was already capable of using ink-wash painting to depict the magnificence of mountains and rivers, and of using line drawing to capture a person’s appearance and form.","The same was true for color painting.","He just hadn’t yet revealed his Minor Success in the Painting Dao and was still unsure what effect channeling the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism into a painting would have.","Fortunately, Xiao Wan’er wasn’t pressuring him, so he was in no rush to complete the portrait of the several members of the Xiao Family’s main branch.","Chen Yi glanced at his work, nodded in satisfaction, and called to Xiaodie, asking, \"Here, take a look. What do you think?\"","Xiaodie stopped the words on the tip of her tongue. She craned her neck to look at the painting in his hand, her big eyes blinking a few times in bewilderment.","After getting a clear look at the portrait on it, her mouth fell slightly open. She pointed at herself and stammered:","\"Y-Young Master, is... is this a painting of me?\"","Chen Yi smiled, nodded, and handed the painting to her. \"A gift for you.\"","Xiaodie took it, her heart filled with joy. \"Thank you, Young Master.\"","She looked at it again and again, a faint blush appearing on her cheeks.","\"But you’ve painted me so beautifully! I’m not this pretty, am I?\"","\"And also, why is the me in the painting wearing an orange cotton skirt? I already changed into a thicker little jacket today, you know?\"","Chen Yi was tidying up the clutter on his desk. He chuckled and chided, \"Why so many questions? Just take it.\"","He wouldn’t tell Xiaodie that his deepest impression of her was still from his period of confinement.","’Back then, Xiaodie’s cute outfit was certainly cute, but she also watched him like a hawk.’","’She’d stare at him all day long as he copied the Xiao Family rules.’","’He’d probably never forget it for the rest of his life.’","Xiaodie, of course, had no idea about any of this. She just thought he had intentionally painted a more beautiful version of her, and her little face remained flushed.","\"Young Master, you paint so well.\"","\"Is it that I paint well, or that you’re just good-looking?\"","\"Of course... of course your painting is good...\"","After a bit of banter, Chen Yi finished tidying the study, rose, and walked outside the wooden building. He looked up at the sky and said:","\"I’m heading out for a bit. You stay here and watch the garden.\""]},{"number":408,"title":"Chapter 408 - 257: I, I’ll Take Revenge","paragraphs":["Hearing the noise, Xiaodie hurried out and handed him an umbrella that was hanging under the eaves:","\"Young Master, it might rain today. You should take an umbrella.\"","She didn’t ask Chen Yi where he was going; her mind was still on that painting.","Chen Yi took the umbrella, gave a few instructions, and calmly strolled out of the Spring Lotus Garden.","For the past few days, he had spent most of his time in the Xiao Mansion.","During this period, he had only left once—to move Asutai and one of Liu Hong’s men, Zeng Zhifeng, to the house on Chuansi Street.","The rest of the time, he painted by day, practiced his Martial Arts by night, and went to Guiyun Academy to teach the Calligraphy Dao.","He cut the figure of a man unconcerned with worldly affairs.","But in reality, Chen Yi had been using various channels to keep abreast of the situation in the city.","These included the rising grain prices, the movements of several major grain merchants, the Xiao Family’s internal response, and Liu Hong’s activities.","The first three had proceeded almost exactly as he had predicted.","But Liu Hong’s side of things was a little different.","Chen Yi hadn’t expected him to be so brazen.","To find Asutai, the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office, the Imprisonment Department, and the City Guard Army had spent the last five days turning the Prefecture City upside down.","They searched house by house.","If Chen Yi hadn’t reacted in time by having Zhang Dabao dig a cellar in the Chuansi Street house to move both Asutai and Zeng Zhifeng, those officials would have discovered Asutai’s tracks long ago with only Pei Guanli to hide him.","And that wasn’t all.","What concerned Chen Yi most was that at some point, a number of unfamiliar faces had appeared in Shu State City.","According to Liu Lang, these people hid by day and moved by night, and their skills were anything but simple.","Although most were Martial Artists of the Lower Three Grades, they were so well-equipped that they didn’t resemble common Jianghu People at all.","Instead, they seemed more like soldiers with military training.","Furthermore, their Cultivation Techniques were unusual, and they possessed a Combined Attack Skill, which meant few Jianghu People could stand against them.","At first, Chen Yi suspected that members of the Five Poison Sect had arrived.","But after going to observe them himself, he confirmed that these elusive figures were all Liu Hong’s men.","The Xiao Family, who held the Marquis Position and commanded the troops of Shu State, had only three hundred Personal Guards and maintained no private army.","In this, they were outdone by Governor Liu Hong.","’Maintaining a private army... heh. Liu Hong certainly has some nerve.’","A smile touched Chen Yi’s face as he mulled these things over.","If it were otherwise, his scheme would be far less interesting.","Not long after, Chen Yi reached the front courtyard and saw Xiao Wan’er and Cui Qingwu walking toward him in the distance.","Trailing behind them were Shen Huatang and Cui Qingwu’s maid, Huan’er.","The group was chatting and laughing.","Chen Yi stopped and waited for them to draw closer before giving a slight bow in greeting. \"Miss Cui, Eldest Sister.\"","Xiao Wan’er had spotted him already, her smile brightening. Noticing the umbrella in his hand, she asked:","\"Brother-in-law, are you heading out?\"","Chen Yi smiled in reply. \"Based on the timing, the people Hundred Herbs Hall sent to investigate Guangyuan should have sent word back. I’m going to go ask about it.\"","Xiao Wan’er thought for a moment before it dawned on her. \"Shopkeeper Yan Hai?\"","\"That’s him.\"","\"Then hurry back.\"","Chen Yi shook his head. Just as he was about to leave, Cui Qingwu spoke up.","\"I hear things are a bit chaotic in the city right now. It would be best for you to be careful, Mr. Qingzhou, leaving the mansion alone.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er took the words to heart, her tone turning worried as she added her own caution:","\"Little Sister Qingwu is right. There’s been a lot of trouble in the city over the rising grain prices.\"","\"Brother-in-law, you should have the Personal Guards take you by carriage.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded, not refusing the offer.","As he agreed, he discreetly glanced at Cui Qingwu.","She was smiling brightly, and her reminder seemed to have been offered casually, but Chen Yi couldn’t help but feel that something was odd.","’Why does my brother Chen Yunfan’s fiancée seem to hold a bit of a grudge against me?’","’It wasn’t much, but he could tell.’","How could he know that for days, Chen Yunfan had been constantly mentioning his name in Cui Qingwu’s ear?","It had annoyed Cui Qingwu to no end, though she couldn’t quite put her finger on why it bothered her.","That was why she had said what she did.","As for her motive... she didn’t really have any malicious intent.","She just wanted to use the Marquis’s Mansion’s White Tiger Guard to see if Chen Yi was meeting with Chen Yunfan in secret.","Chen Yi, of course, knew none of this. Certain that he hadn’t given himself away, he put it out of his mind.","After bidding farewell to the women, he went to the front courtyard, called out for Liu Si’er, and took a carriage to Hundred Herbs Hall.","After finding an excuse to send Liu Si’er away, Chen Yi had Zhang Dabao take him directly to the house on Chuansi Street.","With the latest round of searches complete, the situation in Shu State City had calmed down.","It was time for him to meet with Asutai, the son of the Barbarian Left King, and that guard of Liu Hong’s.","「About an hour later.」","Chen Yi finished his disguise. He changed into a black cloak and donned a black iron mask.","Pei Guanli watched with envy, asking Zhang Dabao to disguise her as well.","Chen Yi was unable to dissuade her, so he relented and agreed.","\"A disguise is a good idea. From now on, you can use this face in public. It will help prevent your identity from being discovered.\"","Pei Guanli sat upright in her chair, letting Zhang Dabao apply a mask as thin as a cicada’s wing to her face. \"Don’t you worry, Brother-in-law,\" she said.","\"These last few days, I haven’t set a single foot outside, afraid that something would go wrong and affect your plans. I’m about to go stir-crazy from being cooped up.\"","Seeing her bottom lip jutting out in a pout so pronounced you could hang an oil bottle from it, Chen Yi laughed and offered a few words of comfort.","He promised her some kind of reward once this busy period was over.","\"What kind of reward?\"","\"You’ll find out.\"","Chen Yi didn’t make promises lightly, fearing the trouble it would cause if he couldn’t fulfill them.","But with Tiger Girl, he wasn’t worried.","After all, knowing her, she would be delighted even if he just gave her a painting.","After a bit more idle chat, Chen Yi instructed Pei Guanli to stand guard outside the door while he entered the hidden room located beneath the bed in the side chamber.","Dim, yellow candlelight illuminated the small, quiet room, in which lay a long, ten-foot bed plank.","Three figures lay upon it.","They were Lv Jiunan, Asutai, and Zeng Zhifeng.","At that moment, they were all under the influence of Immortal Drunk, sleeping soundly.","Chen Yi’s gaze swept over them before he inserted a silver needle into several of Asutai’s vital acupoints.","With a few simple twists, Asutai groggily opened his eyes and weakly sat up.","The moment he saw Chen Yi’s figure, a wary look appeared on his swarthy face.","\"Who... who... are... you?!\"","Asutai’s command of the Wei Language was clearly poor. His intonation was stiff and strange, his words slurred and indistinct.","Chen Yi understood him, however. He sat cross-legged opposite the young man, his eyes, visible over the mask, holding a hint of scrutiny.","Asutai was of a similar build to Chen Yi.","His rugged-looking face held a youthfulness similar to that of any ordinary young man from the Great Wei Dynasty.","It was only the \"barbarian slave\" brand on his face and a world-weariness born from hardship that made him seem older than his years.","After studying him for a moment, Chen Yi gestured for Asutai to relax. \"Who I am isn’t important. You only need to know that I’m here to help you.\"","\"Help... help me?\"","Asutai glared at him fiercely. \"Wei People... cannot be trusted!\"","Chen Yi gave a short, surprised laugh, knowing the young man still hated the man beside him, Zeng Zhifeng, for killing his people.","He thought for a moment, then pointed at Zeng Zhifeng. \"I’m not like him.\"","\"Both Wei People. What is... different?\"","\"He is in league with the Poshisu Country horse bandits. I am not.\"","Asutai’s expression froze. He whipped his head toward Zeng Zhifeng and growled through clenched teeth:","\"Horse bandits... kill!\"","With that, he slammed his fist into Zeng Zhifeng’s stomach.","Chen Yi froze for a second but made no move to stop him.","Zeng Zhifeng had, after all, once possessed the cultivation of the Middle Three Grades. Even without his cultivation, his body could withstand a few punches.","Of course, it wouldn’t be a problem if he couldn’t.","As long as Chen Yi was here, there were ways to keep him alive.","Asutai, however, wasn’t thinking about any of that. He rained several more punches down, the thuds echoing off Zeng Zhifeng’s body.","Even though Zeng Zhifeng was under the influence of Immortal Drunk, the blows made his eyelids flutter.","Seeing Asutai’s murderous expression, Chen Yi shook his head and, with a flick of his finger, sent out a blast of force that knocked him back.","\"That’s enough. He’s useful for now, so you can’t kill him.\"","Asutai panted heavily, still glaring at Zeng Zhifeng, his wide, bell-like eyes completely bloodshot.","\"Then can you... let me... kill him?\"","\"If you agree to my conditions, I’ll give you a chance to get your revenge. How about it?\"","\"I... I want revenge!\""]},{"number":409,"title":"Chapter 409 - 258: Fu... Isn’t Dead?","paragraphs":["Asutai wasn’t thinking about the bigger picture. He wasn’t worried about the overwhelming odds.","He hadn’t even figured out if Zeng Zhifeng had anyone backing him up.","All he had was the ferocity of his Barbarian Race and the hatred born from watching his people brutally killed before his very eyes.","His only target was Zeng Zhifeng.","\"Revenge. I... revenge!\"","\"He... must die!\"","With a low growl, Asutai slammed another punch into Zeng Zhifeng’s body.","His gaze, fixed on Chen Yi, was like that of a wild beast.","It was fierce and bloodthirsty, yet held a faint plea. His entire being was focused on killing Zeng Zhifeng.","Chen Yi raised a hand, signaling for him to be quiet. He smiled and said, \"I can help you, but you must understand, this is a deal.\"","Asutai nodded forcefully. \"I... know. Deal.\"","\"Like... we... burn the grain. That was... a deal.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. Pointing to Lv Jiunan on the other side, he asked, \"Was he the one who made the deal with you?\"","Asutai followed his finger and looked over. A blank look appeared on his face, a curious mix of the juvenile and the mature, and he shook his head. \"Not... him.\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment, then described Ge Muxiao’s features.","Asutai shook his head again. \"Was... *fuduo*... a friend.\"","\"’*Fuduo*’? A friend?\"","\"Yes. He was outside cage. Told me... burn grain, can escape.\"","\"Then do you remember what he looked like? His height? His age?\"","\"This... tall. Looked... thin. White clothes. Very... gentle...\"","Asutai gestured as he haltingly described the man’s appearance.","It wasn’t a clear picture, but a rough outline still formed in Chen Yi’s mind.","A man in white robes, about his own height, thin, and somewhat older than him—likely a middle-aged man.","’A gentle middle-aged man? This feels familiar...’","Chen Yi suddenly thought of Guiyun Academy, and his eyes flashed with realization.","’A scholar?’","’No wonder it felt so familiar.’","Chen Yi’s first suspect was the Mr. Lingchuan who had previously appeared at Lin Huai’an’s residence with Liu Taofang.","—Zhu Lingchuan.","’If it’s Mr. Lingchuan, then that would explain how Liu Hong knew so much about Liu Taofang’s dealings.’","’And Mr. Lingchuan likely had a hand in Lin Huai’an’s death as well.’","Although Chen Yi couldn’t be one hundred percent certain, when he connected all the recent events, Mr. Lingchuan emerged as the prime suspect.","’Interesting.’","’If Mr. Lingchuan is in league with Liu Hong, does that mean his backer, Deputy Commander Zhu Hao, is also mixed up with Liu Hong?’","’If that’s the case, it’s no wonder Liu Hong looked down on the paltry old grain Liu Taofang was messing around with.’","’How could a man who uses the power of the Ji State Trading Company to secretly smuggle ironware possibly care about such chicken feed?’","Chen Yi muttered to himself for a moment, but he had to marvel at Liu Hong’s caution and meticulousness.","He clearly had connections with the Poshisu Country’s Peacock King Banner and King Landu, yet he still chose to trade with King Landu through Zhu Lingchuan and the people from the Ji State Trading Company, all while hiding behind the scenes.","If he hadn’t found out about his son’s collaboration with Lin Huai’an, he probably wouldn’t have killed Lin Huai’an and cut off the Ji State Trading Company’s business.","At this thought, Chen Yi shook his head. Perhaps Liu Hong had other, deeper reasons for his actions.","He pushed those thoughts aside and looked at Asutai. \"Let’s put other matters aside for now and talk about this deal.\"","\"I can let you kill Zeng Zhifeng, and I can even let you kill the man behind him with your own hands.\"","\"But in return, you need to do something for me. And, I’ll say this up front: it’s very dangerous. I can’t guarantee you’ll survive.\"","Asutai nodded firmly. \"Okay!\"","He then immediately moved to smash his fist into Zeng Zhifeng’s head. \"I will... kill him!\"","THUMP.","Before the heavy fist could land, Chen Yi sent him flying with a flick of his hand.","\"Don’t be so impatient. I still have some questions for him.\"","\"And of course, I have a few questions for you, too.\"","Struck by the blow, Asutai flipped back to his feet. \"Ask.\"","He might have a blunt and straightforward nature, but he knew he was no match for Chen Yi. His eyes remained fixed on Zeng Zhifeng.","Seeing this, Chen Yi couldn’t help but chuckle.","This barbarian was just as the rumors described—fierce, savage, and uncivilized.","Fortunately, he didn’t need Asutai for anything complex, or it would have been quite the headache.","With that thought, Chen Yi began his questions unhurriedly. \"I hear you’re the son of the Barbarian Left King, Mu Hage?\"","Asutai nodded, his gaze never leaving Zeng Zhifeng, as if they were talking about someone else entirely.","\"Then how did you end up being captured by Poshisu Country horse bandits and made into a barbarian slave?\"","\"I... was herding. Someone knocked me out.\"","Chen Yi made a sound of surprise. \"Oh?\" he asked, a little taken aback. \"The son of a Left King has to herd livestock?\"","\"King-father... has six... sons. My mother... is dead. No power. So... I herd...\"","As they went back and forth, time passed quickly.","Chen Yi gained a better understanding of Asutai, Left King Mu Hage, and the general situation of the Barbarian Race.","Unlike the Wei Dynasty, the Barbarian Race was a confederation of many tribes.","The Celestial Wolf Tribe, led by the Great Monarch of the Barbarian Race, Ligelu, was the most powerful.","After them came the Black Bear Tribe and the Cyan Wood Tribe, commanded by Left King Mu Hage and Right King Errisen, respectively.","Further down were the five kings of the continent’s southernmost region. Each commanded an army of hundreds of thousands of barbarian soldiers and possessed formidable tribal strength.","The dozens of other tribes, both large and small, were each allied with either the Great Monarch or one of the seven kings of the Barbarian Race.","Beyond that, the Barbarian Race also had Shamanism.","Its ranks were filled with countless masters who were nominally under the Great Monarch’s command but also stood apart from his authority, specializing in rituals, divination, medicine, and other such matters.","Some of the most powerful among them were said to possess world-shattering might, capable of moving mountains and filling seas.","However, the current Great Monarch of the Barbarian Race was old and near death, and several of his sons were locked in endless battle for the throne."]},{"number":410,"title":"Chapter 410 - 258: Fu... Isn’t Dead?","paragraphs":["It had even dragged the other seven kings into the conflict, leaving them with no time for anything else.","This was also the reason why Asutai had been abducted by Poshisu Country horse bandits.","After hearing the story, Chen Yi had a better understanding. He mulled it over for a moment before asking:","\"Have you ever heard the name ’Liu Hong’? Or do you know who your father, Mu Hage, is in contact with on the Wei Dynasty’s side?\"","Asutai said, \"I, not know.\"","\"I only, herd. Other things, not know.\"","Chen Yi nodded. He wasn’t surprised.","’This Asutai is just one of Mu Hage’s sons, and the one with the least influence at that. The things he knows must be limited.’","With that in mind, he mentally filed away these details and asked with a smile, \"Your Wei Language is quite good. You must have been studying for a long time, haven’t you?\"","\"Are there Wei People among the Barbarian Race too?\"","The expression on Asutai’s face shifted slightly. He turned his head to look at Chen Yi and said, \"In tribe, there is a Wei teacher.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"She was, from five years ago. War prize. Your Wei People’s, General.\"","Hearing this, the smile vanished from Chen Yi’s eyes. He frowned and asked, \"Do you know her name?\"","’Five years ago, the Barbarian Left King Mu Hage led a great army to attack Mengshui Pass.’","’The Wei Dynasty suffered heavy casualties, but very few people should have been taken captive.’","’He could ask who was so unlucky—and a General, no less.’","Asutai hesitated slightly before saying, \"Teacher... I not know her name. Only know her as, Ms. Fu.\"","\"Fu... Fu?\"","Chen Yi froze. ’If I remember correctly, my mother-in-law’s surname is Fu.’","’She wasn’t just Xiao Fengchun’s wife and the daughter of the Fu Family of Guangyuan County, but also a top disciple of the Celestial Sect.’","Chen Yi subconsciously asked, \"A woman?\"","Asutai nodded and asked in confusion, \"You know, Teacher?\"","A flash of astonishment crossed Chen Yi’s eyes. He said thoughtfully, \"I... hope I don’t.\"","’This was truly an unexpected twist.’","’If it really is Fu Wanqing, then this matter is serious.’","’Whether he tells the Xiao Family or not, it’s bound to cause a huge stir.’","’Especially Xiao Jinghong.’","’From what Chen Yi knew of Xiao Jinghong, if she learned that Fu Wanqing wasn’t dead, she would absolutely find a way to go rescue her from the Barbarian Race.’","’Even Elder Master Xiao might abandon his forbearance and do something reckless.’","Thinking of this, Chen Yi didn’t ask any more questions. Instead, he ordered Zhang Dabao outside to bring him a brush and ink.","He then began to paint in the quiet room.","Fortunately, he had seen portraits of Fu Wanqing a few times recently. As he sketched now, he managed to capture some of her essence.","In just a few moments, he finished the painting. Without waiting for the ink to dry, he held it up in front of Asutai.","\"Is this her?\"","Asutai’s big eyes widened. He looked it up and down, then pointed at the painting and said:","\"Is, and is not.\"","\"Teacher, white hair.\"","Chen Yi was speechless for a moment. ’...Then it’s her.’","’After all, five years had passed, and Fu Wanqing was deep in the heart of Barbarian territory. It would be normal for her to have aged.’","’This matter, however, was giving him a headache.’","As Chen Yi put the painting away, he asked, \"Besides this Ms. Fu, was there also a Mr. Xiao?\"","Asutai shook his head. \"No. I, not know.\"","Chen Yi sighed at his words. ’It seems Xiao Fengchun really is dead.’","’For a moment, he didn’t know if that was a good thing or a bad one.’","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi began asking about Fu Wanqing’s situation.","According to Asutai, Fu Wanqing was highly regarded by Left King Mu Hage among the Barbarian Race.","Not only was she assigned female Wei attendants, but she was also given her own private tent.","During festivals, Fu Wanqing would even receive various rewards.","Asutai finished by saying, \"But Teacher, her body not good. Very thin, like child.\"","Chen Yi said exasperatedly, \"...Compared to you Barbarians, she would indeed seem like a child who hasn’t grown up.\"","An average adult Barbarian was ten feet tall, so a Wei woman would naturally look like a child in their eyes.","Even the adolescent Asutai, though about the same height as Chen Yi, had a very sturdy build, in no way inferior to Wang Lixing and the others.","After asking about Fu Wanqing’s circumstances, Chen Yi let out a temporary sigh of relief.","’At least his mother-in-law’s life wasn’t in immediate danger. This would give him time to think about what to do next.’","After a moment of silence, Chen Yi made up his mind.","’He definitely had to tell the Xiao Family.’","’But when to tell them, and who to tell... he needed to consider that carefully.’","With his mind made up, Chen Yi no longer hesitated.","Then, under Asutai’s hateful gaze, he used his old trick, stimulating Zeng Zhifeng’s acupoints with a Silver Needle to wake him up.","\"Ugh, where am I...? Who are you?!\"","The moment Zeng Zhifeng woke up, he felt the weakness in his body. He glanced at Asutai to the side, then fixed his gaze on Chen Yi.","\"You... you dare cripple my cultivation!?\"","\"Do you have any idea whose man I am? Are you not afraid of death?\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but chuckle, shaking his head to himself.","\"People say the apple doesn’t fall far from the tree. But in your case, Liu Hong, who has no blood relation to you, seems more like your real father.\"","The false bravado on Zeng Zhifeng’s face faltered. He stared at him in utter astonishment.","\"You... you know I’m one of Master... Liu’s men?\"","\"If I didn’t know your identity, why would I have wasted my time abducting you?\"","Seeing Zeng Zhifeng was about to continue his defiant tirade, Chen Yi waved his hand and flicked out a wisp of Spear Intent, piercing straight through his thigh.","\"AHH... You... you cur, how dare you, how dare...\"","Zeng Zhifeng couldn’t finish his sentence.","He had thought that dropping Liu Hong’s name would save his life, but now that he knew his captor was fully aware of his identity, that line of reasoning fell apart.","Chen Yi couldn’t be bothered to waste words on him. \"Answer a few of my questions, and I’ll give you a quick death.\"","Zeng Zhifeng wasn’t an idiot. Enduring the intense pain, he grunted, \"In, in your dreams!\"","\"Even if I die, I won’t tell you a single thing!\"","\"No matter who you are, the Master will never let you go!\"","Chen Yi said dismissively, \"Your Master is practically a paranoid wreck right now. Even if he knew I existed, he’d have to come begging me.\"","He paused, then continued with a smirk, \"Begging me to hand over Lv Jiunan and Asutai.\"","\"Asu... Lv Jiunan?\"","Zeng Zhifeng noticed the Poshisu Country man lying on the other side. He took a closer look and his face filled with shock.","\"Lord Lv Jiunan?\"","\"You... are you really not afraid of death? Do you have any idea who he is? You dared to abduct him too?!\"","Chen Yi scoffed. \"Why is ’identity’ the only thing you talk about? Since I dared to do all this, what does anyone else’s identity matter?\"","\"Just like you...\"","Before his voice faded, he flicked out another wisp of Spear Intent, piercing Zeng Zhifeng’s other leg.","\"Killing you would be as easy as flipping my hand.\"","This time, Zeng Zhifeng gritted his teeth and didn’t scream. He glared at him with a savage expression.","\"Give up! I won’t tell you a single word!\"","\"Even if I die here today, you won’t live much longer! I’ll be waiting for you in hell!\"","Chen Yi shook his head and gestured to Asutai. \"He’s all yours.\"","This was the very sentence Asutai had been waiting for.","As fury surged through him, Asutai smashed a punch directly into Zeng Zhifeng’s face, then straddled his body, raining down punch after punch.","\"I, kill you!\"","\"Revenge!\"","\"Revenge!\"","\"...\"","With his cultivation gone, Zeng Zhifeng was powerless to fight back. He stopped struggling and forced out the words:","\"You just wait... all, ugh, you’ll all die!\"","\"The Master... the Master will definitely...\"","Before he could finish, Asutai’s furious fists had already beaten his face into a bloody mess, his eyes bursting early on.","He was clearly taking his last breaths.","「About fifteen minutes later.」","Only after Zeng Zhifeng had stopped breathing entirely did Chen Yi pat Asutai, who was still swinging his fists.","\"Alright, your revenge is complete.\"","\"Hah, hah...\"","Asutai stopped. Looking down at Zeng Zhifeng’s motionless body, the calm finally returned to his rugged face.","\"Many, thanks.\"","\"No need for thanks. I told you, this is a transaction between us.\"","\"I let you kill him, you do a few things for me.\"","\"Okay!\"","Seeing Asutai nod, Chen Yi said no more. He directly smashed a bottle of Immortal Drunk, its fumes spreading throughout the quiet room.","\"Remember your promise. When I need you, I will come and wake you again.\"","Asutai froze for a second, but before he could say anything, he fell unconscious once more.","Chen Yi used his Qi Observation Skill to check around. After confirming that both he and Lv Jiunan were deeply unconscious, he tidied up and returned to the main hall.","Pei Guanli adjusted the mask on her face and asked:","\"Brother-in-law, what were you just talking to them about? You...\"","Before she could finish, Chen Yi raised a hand to silence her. He turned his head to look outside the residence, his brow furrowed slightly.","\"Someone’s coming!\""]},{"number":411,"title":"Chapter 411 - 259: Middle Fifth Grade","paragraphs":["The sound of approaching footsteps was light as they circled the residence, closing in.","They moved in fits and starts.","As if trying to avoid detection while simultaneously tracking a trail.","If Chen Yi hadn’t left the quiet room, he might have already been discovered.","He listened for a moment.","Once he sensed the person had slipped into the front courtyard, Chen Yi motioned for Pei Guanli and Zhang Dabao to stay put.","But before he could even step out of the main hall, he heard Pei Guanli exclaim from behind him, \"Little Flower?\"","\"Sis... My lord, Little Flower says it’s my big brother. He’s here.\"","Chen Yi stopped in his tracks. \"Little Flower? Your brother?\"","Pei Guanli nodded eagerly, patting her chest. \"Little Flower is my Lifebound Gu. She smelled my brother’s scent.\"","With that, she rushed outside excitedly. \"I’ll go tell my brother to keep his distance.\"","Seeing this, Chen Yi didn’t stop her.","Pei Guanli’s brother, Pei Qian, was also Granny Shan’s grandson.","Also a member of the Mountain Race, his Martial Arts Cultivation and Techniques were formidable, having already reached the Middle Three Grades Realm.","Furthermore, his mastery of the Witchcraft and Gu Dao, a legacy of the Mountain Race he cultivated, made him far more powerful than Pei Guanli.","’He must have used his Gu Insect to follow Tiger Girl’s trail.’","Chen Yi watched Pei Guanli’s retreating figure, lost in thought.","’Fortunately, Asutai and Lv Jiunan are both in the quiet room. Pei Qian shouldn’t have detected them yet.’","’Unfortunately... I have to figure out how to deceive Pei Qian...’","But before he could give it much thought, he heard Pei Qian’s voice from the front courtyard. \"Little sister, why are you dressed like this?\"","\"I told you in my letter.\"","\"A lord saved my life. I... I’m repaying him now.\"","\"Is it that Spearman named Liu Wu?\"","\"Yes, yes, that’s him.\"","\"Brother, he’s a really good person.\"","\"He not only saved me, but he’s also teaching me Martial Arts. He was the one who helped me break through to the Eighth Grade Realm.\"","\"Take me to see him.\"","\"No, no, he... it’s not a good time... Hey, Brother? Wait for me!\"","Soon, Pei Qian burst into the inner residence and immediately saw Chen Yi standing in the doorway.","However, Chen Yi was still clad in his black cloak, his face obscured by a black iron mask, revealing only his eyes.","Pei Qian paused, sized him up for a moment, then cupped his fists and bowed.","\"I am Pei Qian of the Mountain Race. Greetings, Senior Liu Wu.\"","Just then, Pei Guanli caught up and tried to drag him back. \"Brother, my lord has important business! You need to leave, now...\"","Seeing this, Chen Yi spoke in an unrevealing tone, \"Never mind, Miss Pei. Since he’s here, let’s go inside and talk.\"","\"My lord?\"","Pei Guanli saw the signal in his eyes and reluctantly let go.","She didn’t forget to glare at Pei Qian. \"Brother, when we get back to the clan, I’m definitely telling Ah Ma you bullied me.\"","A wry smile appeared on Pei Qian’s face as he shook his head. \"Little sister, I’m your real brother.\"","\"I don’t care! It’s your fault for not listening to me...\"","Bickering, the two of them followed Chen Yi into the main hall.","Before this, he had already instructed Zhang Dabao to stay out of sight.","’My body is well-covered and my face is disguised, so Pei Qian won’t discover my identity.’","’But Dabao isn’t.’","’Until I’m certain of Pei Qian’s intentions, I can’t let my guard down.’","The three of them took their seats.","Pei Qian glanced at Pei Guanli, who had removed her mask. Seeing her completely different face, he couldn’t help but be curious.","\"Little sister, what’s with your face?\"","\"None of your business!\"","Pei Guanli pouted, turned away, and ignored him.","Chen Yi chuckled, mediating the situation. \"I imagine Brother Pei has heard about my activities in Shu State.\"","\"To avoid implicating your sister, I had her disguise herself to evade prying eyes.\"","Pei Qian’s expression cleared with understanding. \"I see.\"","\"I have indeed heard that you, Senior, killed two horse bandits from Poshisu Country, and that one of them was King Landu’s own brother.\"","\"Right now, the government offices in Shu State and various Jianghu people are all searching for you. You really should be careful.\"","Hearing this, Pei Guanli huffed, \"If you knew that, Brother, why did you come looking for us so recklessly?\"","Pei Qian gave an awkward laugh. \"We hadn’t heard from you for days. Third Grand-Uncle and the others were worried, so they sent me to find you.\"","\"I thought you were at the Xiao Family residence, but when I went over, Xiao Hei couldn’t find your scent. That’s why I ended up here.\"","Pei Guanli’s eyes glinted mischievously. \"Are you blaming Xiao Hei for that?\"","The expression on Pei Qian’s rough, dark-complexioned face changed instantly, and he waved his hands frantically. \"I’m not blaming Xiao Hei!\"","\"Hmph! Xiao Hei, bite him!\"","\"No, no, no...\"","Chen Yi watched them bicker with great interest. ’So the \"Xiao Hei\" they’re talking about is a Gu Insect,’ he realized.","’I didn’t expect Gu Insects could be so intelligent.’","A crystalline light then flashed in his eyes as he used his Qi Observation Skill on Pei Qian and Pei Guanli.","He discovered that inside each of them was a bizarrely-shaped Gu Insect.","It had the head of a bee with compound eyes, six spider-like legs, and a tail with a stinger like a scorpion’s.","It looked like a hybrid of several different insects.","But for all their bizarre appearances, the Gu Insects’ auras were not weak at all, only a sliver less powerful than their respective masters’.","After a bit more boisterous bickering, Pei Qian turned to Chen Yi. He didn’t seem to mind the disguise, smiling as he cupped his fists.","\"My sister and I have been like this since we were children. We’re used to teasing each other. Please excuse our foolish display, Senior.\"","Chen Yi waved his hand. \"It’s no trouble.\"","\"Although that girl Guanli can be impulsive, she has a kind heart. She’s been a great help to me in Shu State.\"","Pei Guanli beamed. \"Sis... Ahem, thank you for the praise, my lord. I’m not as good as you make me sound.\"","Pei Qian gave the two of them a strange look.","He knew his own sister best.","It was true that Pei Guanli was impulsive, but to say she had a kind heart was a bit of... an overstatement.","Fortunately, Pei Qian knew his sister’s temper well enough that he would only dare to think such a thing, never say it aloud."]},{"number":412,"title":"Chapter 412 - 259: Middle Fifth Grade","paragraphs":["After a few pleasantries, Pei Qian said, \"My sister should have already told you our purpose for coming to Shu State, Senior.\"","\"The clan received a letter from my sister some time ago. We were all furious to hear that the Five Poison Sect had reappeared in Shu State and even attacked her.\"","\"So Ah Ma sent me with some men to make the Five Poison Sect pay the price.\"","Chen Yi glanced at Pei Guanli and said with a smile, \"So I’ve heard.\"","\"The Five Poison Sect is plotting something big by coming to Shu State. It’s understandable that Granny Shan would make such arrangements.\"","\"Senior, do you know their intentions for coming to Shu State?\"","\"I haven’t yet identified their specific target, but I can confirm they’ve come to Shu State to align themselves with Liu Zhaoxue, the third young miss of the Jing State Liu Family.\"","\"The Jing State Liu Family... is that the same Liu Family as the current Consort Liu?\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"The very same.\"","\"Originally, after my friend Liu Lang and I joined forces to kill their Elder, Yan Fusha, Liu Zhaoxue had already returned to Jing State.\"","\"But five days ago, she came back to Shu State.\"","\"And members of the Five Poison Sect came with her. It’s said to be their Great Elder, along with several Altar Masters.\"","After listening, Pei Qian’s brow furrowed. \"So it really is him.\"","Before Chen Yi could ask, he continued, \"Years ago, before Ah Ma led our clansmen to annihilate the Five Poison Sect, their Great Elder, Yan Xuechen, was severely wounded by Ah Ma’s Lifebound Gu.\"","\"We all thought he had died from such a grievous injury, but to think he’s still alive.\"","\"Thinking about it now, the Five Poison Sect’s reemergence in the Jianghu must be Old Monster Yan’s handiwork.\"","Chen Yi silently committed the name \"Yan Xuechen\" to memory and asked, \"What is Old Monster Yan’s cultivation level?\"","He would have to deal with Liu Hong next, which meant he would inevitably clash with Liu Zhaoxue and the Five Poison Sect.","To be cautious, he asked a few more questions.","Pei Qian said thoughtfully, \"Decades ago, Old Monster Yan had already reached the Upper Three Grades Realm.\"","\"After so many years, I’m afraid his strength is even more terrifying.\"","\"Fortunately, my Mountain Race has a method for dealing with their potent poisons. As long as we’re careful, we should be able to take him down.\"","\"That’s good to hear...\"","Seeing the two men discussing serious matters, Pei Guanli sat quietly to the side.","But every time she heard her brother call him \"Senior, Senior,\" she couldn’t help but want to laugh.","’If my brother knew Brother-in-law’s true identity, he’d probably want to find a hole to crawl into.’","Pei Guanli was well aware of Pei Qian’s feelings for Xiao Jinghong.","She had originally come to Shu State under the pretext of getting even for her brother, claiming she was going to teach Sister Jinghong’s husband a lesson.","If not for that, she never would have met Chen Yi.","At this thought, Pei Guanli turned aside, covering her mouth to stifle a giggle, causing the bell on her necklace to tinkle incessantly.","Chen Yi naturally guessed her thoughts and cleared his throat. \"I have other matters to attend to today, so I won’t keep you any longer.\"","\"However, if the Mountain Race needs anything in the future, you can have Guanli inform me at any time.\"","Although Pei Qian was puzzled by Pei Guanli’s reaction, upon hearing Chen Yi’s polite dismissal, he had no intention of overstaying his welcome.","\"As it happens, this junior needs to return and inform the elders about my sister, so I won’t linger.\"","He then looked at Pei Guanli. \"Sister, are you coming back with me, or...\"","Before he could finish, Pei Guanli suppressed her laughter and said with a mock-serious expression, \"I’m not going back.\"","Pei Qian shook his head with a wry smile. \"Well, then I’ll have to trouble you to look after my sister for a while, Senior.\"","\"Of course.\"","With that, Chen Yi stood up to see him out.","Just as they left the inner residence, Pei Qian seemed to remember something and said, \"Before coming to Shu State, besides asking this junior to thank you for saving my sister, Ah Ma had one other matter for me to relay.\"","\"Feel free to speak.\"","\"Ah Ma asked me to tell you that Immortal Bai left the Wind and Rain Tower a few days ago.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. \"Immortal Bai? Gongye Bai?\"","Pei Qian nodded. \"That’s him.\"","\"Ah Ma said that after leaving the Wind and Rain Tower, Immortal Bai headed straight for Shu State.\"","\"Ah Ma specifically instructed that if you happen to run into him, Senior, it would be best to keep your distance.\"","Chen Yi let out a wry laugh. \"Immortal Bai and I have no history, no grievances between us. There should be no need to avoid him.\"","That’s what he said, anyway.","But upon hearing this news, he couldn’t help but feel a little puzzled.","’Immortal Bai has remained secluded in the Wind and Rain Tower for decades. Why would he head straight for Shu State the moment he emerges?’","Pei Qian, unaware of his thoughts, tried to persuade him, \"You may not know this, Senior.\"","\"While Immortal Bai isn’t a bloodthirsty killer, his tongue spares no one.\"","\"If you were to unfortunately cross paths with him and have him read your fate, I’m afraid...\"","Chen Yi had heard about this, but he still felt he wouldn’t be that unlucky.","Unless Immortal Bai’s target in Shu State was the Xiao Family, he wasn’t really worried.","’If I can’t beat him, can’t I at least avoid him?’","Before long, Pei Qian left.","Chen Yi watched him walk away before turning back to the main hall and calling for Zhang Dabao to help him remove his disguise.","Pei Guanli sidled up to him and said with a grin, \"Brother-in-law, I didn’t give the game away, did I?\"","\"You were clever enough.\"","\"It’s all because you taught me well, Brother-in-law. You just praised me for being pure and kind-hearted... Brother-in-law, now that my brother has found this place, should we relocate?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"No need.\"","The Mountain Race had close ties with the Xiao Family, and because of the Five Poison Sect, they were at odds with the Jing State Liu Family.","He wasn’t worried that Pei Qian would let word get out.","Besides, Pei Guanli was still here. For that reason alone, Pei Qian wouldn’t allow any danger to befall this place.","Soon, Chen Yi finished removing his makeup and asked, \"Has there been any word from Yan Hai?\"","Zhang Dabao carefully peeled the mask from his face as he replied:","\"Yesterday evening, Shopkeeper Yan sent a message back. He said he’s finished investigating the situation in Guangyuan County.\"","\"Oh? What did he say?\"","\"The letter wasn’t very detailed. It only said the situation there is rather complex.\"","\"There are many medicine halls, but they are all backed by Noble Families. In particular, Commander Zhu of the Capital Commandery’s medicine hall basically has a monopoly in Guangyuan County.\"","Chen Yi nodded impassively. \"And the others?\"","That man, Zhu Hao, was insatiably greedy and likely had some kind of partnership with Liu Hong.","He was bound to clash with him eventually, so this business with the medicine hall wasn’t a huge surprise.","Zhang Dabao continued, \"The other medicine halls are doing alright. Shopkeeper Yan tried to contact one of them.\"","\"He said they weren’t opposed to cooperating with Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","\"Which one?\"","\"Let me think... I think it was the Fu Family Medicine Hall. Yes, the Fu Family’s.\"","Chen Yi’s eyebrow twitched slightly.","As far as he knew, there was only one Fu Family in Guangyuan County—the family of Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Jinghong’s maternal grandfather.","What a coincidence. He had just learned that Fu Wanqing wasn’t dead...","Lost in thought, Chen Yi gave his instructions, \"Guanli, you stand guard here.\"","\"Dabao, you should also come here as little as possible for now. Stay at the residence behind the tailor shop. I’ll notify you in advance if I need you for anything.\"","Zhang Dabao bowed in acceptance, and Pei Guanli naturally had no objections.","She hadn’t found it boring or tedious guarding this place these past few days.","Zhang Dabao brought her everything she needed, and her days were spent doing nothing but cultivation. She was actually quite diligent.","Chen Yi glanced around to make sure nothing was amiss, then quietly left Chuansi Street and headed straight for the Xiao Family estate.","Now everything was in place. He was just waiting for the grain shipment from Lou Yuxue to arrive, and then he could set his plan in motion.","***","「Night fell quickly.」","The sky was exceptionally dim. Dark clouds had been gathering for a day or two, and a torrential downpour began just before nightfall.","Throughout Spring Lotus Garden, the roar of the downpour was audible everywhere.","In the wooden building, Xiaodie and Xiao Wuge had long since gone to sleep.","Only Chen Yi remained, sitting cross-legged on his bed, practicing the Four Symbols Skill.","In fact, ever since returning to the estate from Chuansi Street, he had given Xiao Wan’er a brief update on Hundred Herbs Hall’s progress and then spent his time cultivating in his room.","His cultivation was now progressing rapidly.","The next moment, Chen Yi opened his eyes and let out a long breath. \"Finally. Middle Fifth Grade.\"","It had taken him ten days in total to break through to the Middle Stage.","It might not seem long, but compared to his previous rate of advancement, taking ten days to break through a minor realm was already considered slow.","Fortunately, this one minor realm advancement at the Fifth Grade brought a significant increase in True Essence, nearly doubling the amount within his three great Seas of Qi.","This greatly increased his burst duration in combat.","Coupled with the amplification to his various techniques from the Four Symbols Skill’s Spiritual Essence Divine Position, the improvement was by no means small.","Just then, a golden light flashed:","[Daily Intelligence · Profound-rank Middle Grade: At the fifth quarter of the zishi hour, at the tailor shop in the West Market, the Hidden Guards—General, Lady Tiger, Simurgh Phoenix, and others—will retrieve intelligence. A very small amount of Opportunity can be obtained.]","Chen Yi scanned the message, and the moment he finished reading, he immediately stood up to change his clothes.","There wasn’t much time left until the fifth quarter of the zishi hour. He had to hurry.","Moreover, with several of the Hidden Guards present tonight, it was clear that the secret dispatch they were receiving was of the utmost importance.","’Lou Yuxue will be there too. This is a good chance to press her about the grain shipment.’","’I’ve already paid the deposit. She owes me an update...’"]},{"number":413,"title":"Chapter 413 - 260: The Pavilion Master Is Mad?","paragraphs":["The recent, crazy surge in Shu State’s grain prices was, for Chen Yi, nothing short of good news.","Or perhaps, it would be more accurate to say that from the moment he discovered the Ji State Trading Company, Lin Huai’an, and Liu Taofang were the \"financiers\" who hired Bright Moon Building to burn the summer grain in the Three Towns, he knew the rise in Shu State’s grain prices was irreversible.","Even with Lin Huai’an now dead, the various grain merchants hadn’t stopped their efforts.","Even with the public crying out in protest, even after their plan to frame the Xiao Family failed, they were still trying every method they could think of to drive up the price of grain.","All for the sake of a massive profit.","This alone revealed to Chen Yi the sheer greed of the people from the Ji State Trading Company.","But the greedy always get their comeuppance.","And if it didn’t happen naturally, he wouldn’t mind fanning the flames and giving them a spectacular \"funeral.\"","With that in mind, Chen Yi changed into night clothes, threw on a raincoat and a bamboo hat, and left the Xiao Family estate, venturing out into the rain.","The night was dark, and the rain was torrential.","Icy rain cascaded down, shrouding the surroundings in a thin layer of mist.","Fortunately, Chen Yi’s cultivation had now reached Middle Fifth Grade. As his True Essence circulated, his five senses became extremely sharp.","Even while using the Meteor Butterfly Step, he could travel without a sound while simultaneously surveying all movement within a two-li radius.","He only slowed his pace after passing through a deep, narrow alley near the West Market, concealing his aura as he approached the house behind the tailor shop.","By now, it was late into the night.","The wide main street of the West Market was deserted.","Only a few lavishly decorated shops showed a glimmer of candlelight, casting a faint, yellow halo through the torrential downpour.","Chen Yi scanned his surroundings. Once he confirmed no one was around, he slipped quietly into the house.","Chen Yi listened intently for a moment. After confirming there was no sound coming from the tailor shop, he gently woke Zhang Dabao.","\"Da—\"","Before Zhang Dabao could speak, Chen Yi clamped a hand over his mouth and gestured under the candlelight from the eaves:","\"Disguise me. And don’t make a sound.\"","Recognizing his face, Zhang Dabao breathed a sigh of relief. He nodded and went to get the necessary equipment.","Meanwhile, Chen Yi went to the window, his eyes fixed on the tailor shop ahead.","At this moment, the patter of rain on the roof tiles outside was quite loud.","He could only make out the faint sound of conversation coming from within.","\"...hasn’t she arrived...?\"","\"Lady Tiger is taking her sweet time. She... must need to be covert...\"","\"Simurgh Phoenix, calm yourself.\"","\"Lady Tiger’s status is unique. Give her some time. I’m sure she’ll be here soon.\"","’General.’","Chen Yi recognized the voice and silently mulled over the White Tiger Guard’s situation.","He had previously learned at the wonton shop that the White Tiger Guard’s Golden Banner Officer, General, wanted to meet with King Landu, and he’d intended to investigate the reason.","But things had taken an unexpected turn.","Because Lv Jiunan, Ge Muxiao, and the others were colluding with Liu Hong, he’d been forced to abduct them.","As far as Chen Yi was concerned, his actions were perfectly justified.","But from General’s perspective, his move had already interfered with the White Tiger Guard’s plans.","’I’d forgotten about that part.’","’If Lou Yuxue tells General about our previous cooperation, I probably won’t be able to get my hands on that grain.’","Chen Yi gazed thoughtfully out the window, mulling over his options.","It seemed he would have to find some way to get Lou Yuxue to make it happen.","He also needed to provide a reasonable explanation; otherwise, it would jeopardize his future plans.","’Silver coins?’","’Lou Yuxue certainly needs them, but she won’t take a bigger risk just for money.’","’Something else, then...’","An idea struck Chen Yi. He pulled up the sleeve on his left arm, revealing a corner of yellowed paper.","It was the secret letter Lin Huai’an had written to King Landu to arrange the sale of Zhu Hao’s ironware and ore to the King’s horse bandits.","’Perhaps Lou Yuxue would be interested in this.’","As things stood now, there was little point in Chen Yi holding onto the letter.","Lin Huai’an was dead and Lv Jiunan was his prisoner. No matter how desperately King Landu needed ironware, he wouldn’t choose this critical juncture to make a deal.","And even if he did...","Even if King Landu dared, the Ji State Trading Company and Zhu Hao would wait until the situation in Shu State stabilized before making their next move.","He might as well sell this information to Lou Yuxue. It might be enough to buy her help.","As he thought this, Chen Yi motioned for Zhang Dabao to start the disguise, all while keeping an ear on the activity in the tailor shop.","Just then, he heard a faint CREAK from the shop.","A door opened, then closed.","General asked, \"You’re here?\"","Lou Yuxue: \"Lord, this subordinate has arrived late. Please forgive me.\"","Cui Qingwu’s voice rose slightly as she scoffed, \"Lord Lady Tiger, you certainly put on airs. The Lord Golden Banner Officer summons you, and you still dare to dawdle?\"","\"The feeling is mutual.\"","\"I heard you and Lord General parted on bad terms last time. An outsider might even think Lord Simurgh Phoenix was the Golden Banner Officer in charge of Shu State.\"","\"Hah! A Golden... Don’t you try your little tricks to sow discord in front of me.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi’s expression turned strange. ’Lou Yuxue and Cui Qingwu don’t get along?’","’This is really... going to be a headache for General.’","And indeed it was.","Just as Chen Yi had guessed, General was feeling rather helpless.","Lady Tiger was about to be promoted to Golden Banner Officer, meaning she would soon be his equal. He couldn’t be overly critical of her.","As for Simurgh Phoenix, she was the treasured daughter of the Qinghe Cui Family.","Her status was so exceptional that even the Pavilion Master was wary of her, to say nothing of a mere Golden Banner Officer like himself.","General waved his hand in resignation. \"Enough idle talk.\"","\"I’ve called you here today to inform you all of an important matter.\"","At this, Lou Yuxue stopped paying Cui Qingwu any mind. She shook the rain from her raincoat and said, \"Lord, please speak.\"","Cui Qingwu, standing to the side, also fell silent. She turned slightly away, as if disgusted by the rainwater.","General took this in and sighed inwardly. He then asked, \"Are there any leads on the matter I had you investigate?\""]},{"number":414,"title":"Chapter 414 - 260: Pavilion Master, Gone Mad?","paragraphs":["\"Reporting, General. After arriving in Shu State, Liu Zhaoxue has been busy these past few days, moving between Xinglin Hall and several other Medicine Halls.\"","\"She made adjustments to the poorly performing ones and had the Medical Saint Hand who followed her from Jing State oversee them, which has had a considerable impact within Shu State City.\"","\"What about Liu Hong?\"","\"He hasn’t made any moves, but...\"","Lou Yuxue glanced at Cui Qingwu and said, \"It’s just that the whereabouts of his two sons have been somewhat unusual.\"","The General waved his hand, signaling for her to speak plainly.","Seeing this, Lou Yuxue began, \"His second son, Liu Taofang, has remained shut up at home.\"","\"It’s said that on the day the East Market Grain Storehouse was burned, he was punished by Liu Hong and placed under house arrest.\"","Cui Qingwu muttered upon hearing this, \"’How is that unusual?’\"","Lou Yuxue ignored her. \"I discovered that Liu Taofang was spotted in the East Market that night.\"","The General said thoughtfully, \"Are you suggesting Liu Taofang has connections to those grain businesses?\"","\"That is a distinct possibility.\"","\"Recently, those grain businesses have colluded to raise grain prices, and it’s connected to the burning of hundreds of thousands of bushels of grain.\"","\"I suspect Liu Taofang may be trying to take advantage of the situation for personal gain.\"","Seeing the General nod, Lou Yuxue continued, \"Then there’s the eldest son, Liu Taoyao.\"","\"According to reports from several Iron Banner Officers, he has rarely gone to the Government Office these past few days, spending most of his time at home.\"","\"Furthermore, suspicious individuals have been seen coming and going from his courtyard late at night.\"","\"After learning of this, I used Bright Moon Building’s informants to confirm that they are the same group of mysterious people who recently appeared in Shu State.\"","The General frowned slightly.","After a moment of thought, his brow smoothed, and a slight smile appeared on his face as he said:","\"It seems I’ve underestimated Liu Hong’s audacity. To think he’d dare raise a private army.\"","Lou Yuxue was taken aback for a moment. \"A private army? Not just retainers?\"","The General shook his head. \"Given Liu Hong’s current official position, why would he be so secretive if he were merely recruiting retainers?\"","\"Like Zhao Shichang, the proper way would be to do it openly.\"","Cui Qingwu crossed her arms. \"He’s planning to rebel.\"","The General glanced at her. \"We can’t jump to that conclusion just yet.\"","He then looked at Lou Yuxue and instructed, \"Later, pass this information to the Pavilion Master. Make the stakes clear.\"","Lou Yuxue acknowledged the order, then hesitated before saying, \"Forgive my incompetence, but I have not yet found any sign of ’Liu Wu’.\"","\"Although there are some new faces around Liu Zhaoxue, neither their physical builds nor their Cultivation levels come close to matching ’Liu Wu’.\"","The General nodded slightly. \"He just pulled off something big. It’s only normal for him to go into hiding.\"","\"From now on, however, just keep an eye on Liu Zhaoxue’s movements. As for Liu Wu...\"","He paused, took a secret missive from his robes, and continued, \"A secret missive from the Lord Pavilion Master.\"","\"His Lordship wishes for the two of you to work together and find a way to recruit Liu Wu into the White Tiger Guard.\"","Hearing the last part, Lou Yuxue stared at him in disbelief. \"Liu Wu? General, are you certain the Pavilion Master wants me... us... to recruit him?\"","Cui Qingwu, at her side, was equally astonished, and her expression soured as she said:","\"That Liu Wu previously used Poison to knock me unconscious. Making him a White Tiger Guard would be a slap in my own face, wouldn’t it?\"","Seeing their disbelief, the General unfurled the missive in his hand.","\"This is a secret missive, handwritten by the Pavilion Master himself. It did not pass through the White Tiger Guard’s Secretariat.\"","Lou Yuxue and Cui Qingwu leaned in to read the contents, then looked at each other, stunned.","Even though the two of them didn’t get along, this abrupt news left them both bewildered.","\"General, why would the Pavilion Master, why...\"","Before either could finish her question, the General raised a hand to cut them off. \"Have you forgotten the rules of the White Tiger Guard?\"","As he spoke, his expression turned cold.","\"The Pavilion Master’s orders are absolute. Even if His Lordship orders you to your deaths, you are to obey without question!\"","Lou Yuxue immediately bowed.","His words were incredibly severe.","Despite her countless questions, she knew this was not the time to probe the Pavilion Master’s reasons for recruiting Liu Wu.","Cui Qingwu, on the other hand, was not so easily intimidated. She pursed her lips and asked, \"And what if this Liu Wu doesn’t agree?\"","The General shot her a look, his tone icy. \"If he refuses to join the White Tiger Guard, then he is our mortal enemy.\"","\"In that case, we kill him!\"","Lou Yuxue wanted to point out that Liu Wu was already a major enemy.","However, she had her own agenda, so she swallowed the words before they could escape her lips.","’To be fair, even though Liu Wu has caused her trouble several times, his actions have a certain forthrightness to them. He isn’t some vicious, bloodthirsty follower of the Evil Demonic Dao.’","’That was why she had agreed to cooperate with him in the first place.’","’But...’","’Lou Yuxue felt she couldn’t come up with a way to persuade Liu Wu to join the White Tiger Guard, and what’s more, she didn’t particularly want him to.’","’From what she knew of him, the man was perpetually mysterious. There was no guarantee that once he became a White Tiger Guard, he wouldn’t turn all of Shu State upside down.’","’She just couldn’t fathom why the Pavilion Master had made such a decision...’","The same question also lingered in Chen Yi’s mind.","’The White Tiger Guard’s Pavilion Master... he actually wants me to join the White Tiger Guard?’","’Has he gone mad?’","Even though Chen Yi had several run-ins with the White Tiger Guard and had heard tales of their Pavilion Master, he couldn’t fathom the reasoning behind this arrangement.","’Surely he couldn’t have deduced that I’m working with Liu Zhaoxue and wants to use me to help her take down Liu Hong and the main branch of the Jing State Liu Family?’","’Or has that mysterious, high-ranking White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master devised some new scheme after learning that I \"killed\" Lv Jiunan?’","He racked his brain, but Chen Yi still couldn’t make heads or tails of it.","’If he wants me to join the White Tiger Guard, sending Lou Yuxue and Cui Qingwu isn’t enough.’","’If the Pavilion Master himself were to come in person, I might actually consider it.’","Of course, these were just Chen Yi’s fanciful thoughts.","Only a fool would give up his perfectly fine life as an idle, live-in son-in-law to go risk his life for the White Tiger Guard.","Just then, he heard the distant voice of the General continue, \"Alright, that’s all I have to say.\"","\"I will be departing for Poshisu Country shortly.\"","\"After I leave, Lady Tiger, you are to proceed as usual. Keep your identity concealed and continue investigating the situation at Bright Moon Building.\"","Lou Yuxue knew in her heart his purpose for going to Poshisu Country, so she simply nodded without asking any further questions.","The General then turned to Simurgh Phoenix and said, \"You should be aware that Lady Tiger is currently the only Silver Banner Officer left in Shu State. There are some matters where I must ask for your assistance.\"","Seeing his sincerity, Cui Qingwu nodded reluctantly. \"Go ahead, General.\"","\"Previously, Hawk and Gray Wolf were responsible for the Xiao Family matter.\"","\"But with one of them dead and the other having fled, the Xiao Family is now without a Silver Banner Officer overseeing things. I hope you will pay more attention to them during this time.\"","At this, the General’s tone grew a bit more serious. \"If the Iron Banner Officers over there seek you out, and it’s inconvenient for Lady Tiger to act, I want you to help resolve the situation.\"","Hearing this, Cui Qingwu’s heart stirred. \"The Xiao Family?\"","’In all this time, she had been in and out of the Xiao Family residence several times and had a lot of contact with Xiao Wan’er, yet she had never once contacted the Iron Banner Officers stationed there.’","’Looking back now, it was an oversight on her part.’","’Given the current situation in Shu State, if the White Tiger Guard wanted to accomplish *that matter*, they would inevitably have to stir up a storm in the state.’","’In that case, the Xiao Family was an unavoidable link in the chain.’","’Having two Silver Banner Officers responsible for the Xiao Family wasn’t unreasonable.’","Thinking of this, Cui Qingwu nodded and said, \"Rest assured, General. If I am needed, I will not refuse.\"","Beside her, Lou Yuxue said nothing more.","’She had been in Shu State longer and knew that Hawk’s only mission was the \"Fledgling\".’","’From what she knew of this \"Fledgling,\" she wasn’t worried about any major incidents happening with the Xiao Family.’","’There was no chance of trouble at all.’","Not long after, Lou Yuxue and Cui Qingwu left the tailor shop one after the other.","Having heard all this, Chen Yi signaled for Zhang Dabao to remain quiet. He put on his bamboo hat, preparing to follow Lou Yuxue.","But before he could make a move, he heard another faint sound from inside the tailor shop.","It seemed the General was opening the door to leave.","\"...After I’m gone, have the tailor shop keep an eye on Yunqing Building.\"","\"Lord Simurgh Phoenix?\"","\"Yes. Keep an eye on her movements for me.\"","\"But if you discover anything, don’t do anything extra. Just record it.\"","\"I understand...\"","Chen Yi sneered to himself upon hearing this. ’So, even within the White Tiger Guard, everyone is wary of everyone else.’","’No wonder Lou Yuxue agreed to cooperate with him before.’","’In a place where everyone has their own ulterior motives, what hope is there for genuine camaraderie?’","Soon, the tailor shop fell silent.","Chen Yi waited another moment, until a golden light flashed before his eyes:","[Witnessed Hidden Guard General and others receive a secret missive. Reward: \"Celestial Flower Flying Sword Technique\" [Profound Tier], Opportunity +30.]","[Remark: People were present, voices were heard, but the scene was not witnessed directly...]","Chen Yi glanced at the notification, and once he was sure the General and the others had all left, he quietly slipped into the rainy night, heading for the Spring Rain Building.","\"Heh, I wonder what kind of method Lou Yuxue will use to try and recruit me into the White Tiger Guard.\"","While there was no way he would agree, that didn’t mean he couldn’t have a little fun with the situation.","Right?"]},{"number":415,"title":"Chapter 415 - 261: Reckless Overconfidence","paragraphs":["Lou Yuxue, of course, had no idea that Chen Yi was hiding nearby, eavesdropping.","But right now, she was indeed thinking about Chen Yi.","To be precise, she was thinking of \"Liu Wu.\"","Of course, Lou Yuxue wasn’t thinking about questioning \"Liu Wu\" as to why he had killed Lv Jiunan, thereby delaying Lord General’s meeting with King Landu.","Instead, she was considering the deal she had discussed with him earlier.","’Since Lord Pavilion Master has decided to recruit him even after learning he killed Lv Jiunan, our cooperation can proceed.’","’It’s just... why now, of all times...’","In fact, after taking the deposit, Lou Yuxue had already used the Bright Moon Building’s channels to contact grain merchants in Jing State, You State, Yan State, and other regions.","She had preliminarily secured fifty thousand measures of grain.","But this was still a long way from the three hundred thousand measures of grain that \"Liu Wu\" wanted.","It wasn’t that Lou Yuxue couldn’t find more; rather, she knew the real culprit behind the rising grain prices in Shu State was the Ji State Trading Company.","Fifty thousand measures of grain was the absolute limit of what she could purchase through her channels.","If she tried to buy any more, word would likely get back to the people at the Ji State Trading Company.","At that point, even as a Chief Steward of the Bright Moon Building, and even if she used the excuse of making a little extra money on the side, she wouldn’t be able to get around the Ji State Trading Company.","They wouldn’t even need to show themselves. A single word from the leader of the Bright Moon Building would be enough to make her meekly hand over all that grain.","Or, she might be ordered to cooperate with the Ji State Trading Company’s operations in Shu State.","After all, the Ji State Trading Company was the real power behind the Bright Moon Building.","Therefore, after leaving the tailor’s shop, Lou Yuxue didn’t head straight back to the Spring Rain Building.","Instead, she took a detour and blocked Cui Qingwu’s carriage.","\"Simurgh Phoenix, let’s talk.\"","The driver, Huan’er, sized her up and frowned. \"Lord Lady Tiger, it’s late. My lady needs to rest.\"","Just then, Cui Qingwu, who had heard the voices, spoke from inside the carriage, \"It’s fine. Let’s hear what she has to say.\"","\"For Lord Lady Tiger, who is never one to give us the time of day, to come block our path in the rain... it must be something important.\"","Lou Yuxue gave a noncommittal nod. \"Let’s talk in private.\"","\"No need for all that trouble. Get in the carriage.\"","\"I don’t want your business to interfere with my rest.\"","Just as Lou Yuxue was about to climb aboard, she heard Cui Qingwu say with a hint of disdain:","\"Leave your raincoat, bamboo hat, and boots outside. I’d rather you didn’t dirty my carriage.\"","Lou Yuxue’s eyelid twitched. \"...Fine!\"","She promptly removed her raincoat, bamboo hat, and boots, placing them by the driver Huan’er’s feet before lifting the curtain and sitting inside the carriage.","A warm lamp hung from the ceiling, its candlelight illuminating the space.","Inside the small carriage, a carpet imported from the Western Regions was laid out. Threads of gold glittered within it, and it was as soft as a tiger’s pelt.","A far cry from her previous coldness in front of the General, Cui Qingwu was now lounging lazily against a jade pillow, her body veiled in light gauze, her hazy form faintly visible.","Lou Yuxue glanced over, then sat cross-legged near the entrance. \"I have a favor to ask.\"","Cui Qingwu propped her head up with one hand, her clear eyes gazing at Lou Yuxue with a half-smile.","\"Hearing the word ’ask’ come from your lips... that’s surprising.\"","\"You didn’t even use that word when you came to me looking for a hiding place before.\"","\"What’s the matter, Lord Lady Tiger? Hit a snag?\"","Lou Yuxue ignored her teasing and said bluntly, \"I need to buy two hundred thousand measures of grain.\"","Cui Qingwu paused, slightly stunned. \"Two hundred thousand measures? What are you doing buying so much grain?\"","\"Grain prices in Shu State have been rising lately. I want to take the opportunity to make a profit.\"","This was the most suitable reason Lou Yuxue could think of that wouldn’t expose her cooperation with \"Liu Wu.\"","Cui Qingwu asked thoughtfully, \"Is it really that simple?\"","She clearly didn’t believe it.","Just as she’d said—the Lady Tiger was never one to be pleasant with her and would never approach her without an important reason.","Just to make money... The reason felt a bit too flimsy.","\"It’s that simple!\"","Lou Yuxue said with finality, \"I’m still short seventy thousand of the silver coins I promised the Hawk. This is a good chance to make it up while Shu State is short on grain.\"","Cui Qingwu’s interest was piqued. \"I can agree, but I want twenty percent of the gross profit.\"","\"Ten percent, at most.\"","\"This price hike in Shu State won’t last long, so I’m just looking for a quick turnaround. The profit won’t be that high.\"","After a pause, Lou Yuxue snorted, \"If it weren’t for the Ji State Trading Company backing those other grain suppliers, I wouldn’t have come to you at all.\"","Hearing this, Cui Qingwu gave her a long, hard look.","’If that’s the case, then it’s a real possibility.’","The people from the Ji State Trading Company were the greediest of all. Causing such a disaster for the state and its people in Shu State was certainly in line with their style.","\"I agree.\"","\"The grain will be delivered to you within ten days.\"","\"My thanks.\"","Lou Yuxue was about to leave when Cui Qingwu stopped her. \"About Liu Wu, what are your plans?\"","\"Are you referring to ’inviting him to join the White Tiger Guard’?\"","\"You’re asking when you already know the answer. I refuse to believe that after he embarrassed you so badly, you’d be willing to let him join.\"","’It’s not entirely out of the question.’","Lou Yuxue thought to herself, her expression unchanging as she said, \"It’s an order from Lord Pavilion Master. Neither of us can refuse, can we?\"","\"That Liu Wu embarrassed me in front of Yunfan before. I don’t want him in the White Tiger Guard.\"","\"Are you thinking of disobeying an order?\"","\"It’s not entirely out of the question... Forget it. I can compromise.\"","\"How about you teach him a lesson for me?\"","Lou Yuxue said irritably, \"How about no.\"","\"I’d advise you to drop the idea. The loss would outweigh the gain.\"","’Has she gone mad?’","’Never mind that \"Liu Wu\" hasn’t even agreed to join the White Tiger Guard yet.’","’Even if he did, based on what I know of him, that bastard would never let anyone push him around.’","’Besides, what would I even use to teach \"Liu Wu\" a lesson?’"]},{"number":416,"title":"Chapter 416 - 261: Overestimating Oneself","paragraphs":["In terms of Martial Arts Cultivation, she was no match for him.","As for Poisoning or using poisonous Gu, it would be almost completely useless against a Medical Saint Hand.","’Or maybe use her status in the White Tiger Guard to pressure him?’","Not only would it be ineffective, it would invite his retaliation.","Besides, the Pavilion Master himself had ordered Liu Wu to be invited into the White Tiger Guard. Who knew what rank he would be given?","Iron Banner Officer, Silver Banner Officer, or Golden Banner Officer?","Any of them were possible.","Unless Lou Yuxue’s head had been kicked by a donkey, there was no way she would do something so foolish.","Cui Qingwu said, \"This won’t work, that won’t work. Do you still want that grain or not?\"","\"That’s a separate matter.\"","\"You...\"","Just then, Huan’er, who was driving the carriage, knocked on the carriage wall.","\"Miss, we’ve arrived at Tingyu Pavilion.\"","Hearing this, Cui Qingwu swallowed the words on the tip of her tongue, sat up, and said, \"You can go.\"","They were too close to Tingyu Pavilion.","She didn’t want to ruin her image in Chen Yunfan’s eyes over someone so insignificant.","Lou Yuxue, unaware of Cui Qingwu’s thoughts, got up and stepped out of the carriage. She straightened her clothes, leaped down, and vanished into the rainy night.","Huan’er watched her go, saying with some displeasure, \"Miss, that woman is truly tactless.\"","Cui Qingwu hummed in agreement and lifted a corner of the curtain to look out.","\"Later, inform Uncle Zhao to keep an eye on any movements from Bright Moon Building.\"","Although the reason Lou Yuxue gave was very reasonable, she remained skeptical.","After thinking it over, she decided to give one more instruction.","Huan’er agreed and drove the carriage into Tingyu Pavilion.","As they passed through the central courtyard, Cui Qingwu listened closely, and a slight smile appeared on her face.","\"Stop the carriage.\"","\"Miss?\"","\"It’s so late, and Brother Yunfan is still in his Cultivation. I’m going to go take a look.\"","\"Yes...\"","Holding an umbrella, Cui Qingwu gracefully walked into the Martial Arts Arena. She immediately saw Chen Yunfan cultivating in the rain, with Chun Ying and others standing nearby.","\"Brother Yunfan, how long have you been cultivating?\"","Ning Yu and Niu Mountain bowed but did not reply.","Chun Ying stepped forward, curtsied, and replied, \"Miss Cui, the Young Master has been cultivating ever since he returned from the Governor’s Office.\"","\"Six hours?\"","Cui Qingwu recalled for a moment. When she left earlier, Chen Yunfan was already cultivating.","’By now, he must have been cultivating for a continuous six hours.’","With this thought, she instructed, \"Chun Ying, please prepare a bowl of ginger tea for Brother Yunfan to warm him up.\"","Chun Ying hesitated for a moment before nodding and turning to leave.","Ning Yu glanced over, a strange expression on his face.","’If I remember correctly, Chun Ying already made ginger tea earlier.’","Beside him, Niu Mountain had the same doubt. \"Brother Ning, just now...\"","Before he could finish, Ning Yu clamped a hand over his mouth. \"Just watch the Young Master practice his swordplay and learn something.\"","’It’s a good thing Miss Cui is here, or I’d really teach Niu Mountain a lesson.’","Not long after, Chun Ying returned with the ginger tea. Cui Qingwu took it and called out to Chen Yunfan with a smile:","\"Brother Yunfan, it’s already past one in the morning. Why don’t you take a break?\"","Chen Yunfan’s form paused for a moment. With a wave of his hand, he sent out a flash of sword light, splitting the curtain of rain.","CRACK.","A steel-stone on the Martial Arts Arena snapped in two.","Seeing this, Cui Qingwu smiled in praise. \"Brother Yunfan, your Sword Dao is progressing at an incredible speed! I’m sure you’ll break through to the Realm of Perfection soon.\"","\"Perfection?\"","Chen Yunfan sheathed his sword, pursed his lips, and said, \"I’m still a long way off.\"","’It was obvious. Chen Yi reached the Spear Dao Perfection Realm ages ago.’","’After so much time has passed, his strength must be even greater now.’","Cui Qingwu didn’t understand why he was in such a hurry. After a moment’s thought, she picked up a towel and walked over to him.","\"Wipe yourself off, then drink this ginger tea.\"","Chen Yunfan didn’t refuse. He took the towel and wiped the rain and sweat from his face.","As he drank the ginger tea, he asked casually, \"Just get back?\"","Cui Qingwu smiled and said, \"The new batch of Lang Wine at Yunqing Building was being bottled, so I went to have a look.\"","Chen Yunfan gave a noncommittal nod. \"It’s late. You should get some rest.\"","\"Alright.\"","After Cui Qingwu left, Chen Yunfan washed up, leaned back on his bed, and called for Chun Ying.","\"Has there been a reply?\"","\"I was just about to report to you, Young Master. The White-robed Minister has already sent the letter to the Western Buddha Country. We estimate a reply should arrive in a few days.\"","\"Oh,\" Chen Yunfan murmured. He picked up a book and asked idly,","\"Has anything been happening in the city lately?\"","Chun Ying thought for a moment, then shook her head. \"Not much to report.\"","\"Ever since Liu Wu and Liu Lang killed those horse bandits from Poshisu Country, the Government Office has been searching the Prefecture City. So far, they haven’t made any progress.\"","\"It would be a miracle if those good-for-nothings could find anyone.\"","Chen Yunfan muttered as he read his book, \"So what if they do find him?\"","\"Can they even beat him?\"","\"A Spearman at the Perfection Realm of Martial Arts... how could they possibly deal with him?\"","’Hmph, the only one who can take down Brother Yi is me!’","Chun Ying looked at the expression on his face and felt that something was a little odd.","But after thinking about it carefully, she couldn’t pinpoint what was wrong, so she continued speaking:","\"Young Master, you should also rest soon.\"","\"First thing tomorrow morning, Lord Yang has invited you to his residence for a meeting.\"","Chen Yunfan put down his book and mused, \"Speaking of which, I really can’t figure out his reason for inviting me this time.\"","\"Young Master, have you forgotten? The Annual Examination.\"","\"The Annual Examination?\"","\"Yes. I heard that a few days ago, Mr. Yue Ming specifically went to Lord Yang to make a suggestion regarding the new rules for the Annual Examination.\"","\"I suspect he’s asking you to go, Young Master, to discuss this matter.\"","A look of realization dawned on Chen Yunfan’s face. \"So that’s why.\"","\"For that Academic Administrator to petition the Holy Emperor to change the new rules, he must have had Liu Hong’s approval.\"","\"Old Yang probably fears that if he brings it up himself, he’ll anger Liu Hong, so he wants me to be the one to stick my neck out.\"","Chun Ying nodded. \"Young Master, what do you plan to do?\"","\"I’ll agree, of course.\""]},{"number":417,"title":"Chapter 417 - 261: Overestimating Oneself","paragraphs":["\"The rules for this year’s Annual Examination are so strange. There’s no guarantee that old scoundrel Liu Hong isn’t up to something.\"","\"Besides...\"","Chen Yunfan stopped talking. He lay back on the bed and grumbled,","\"Besides, Brother Yi is also taking the Annual Examination this time.\"","\"If someone sets him up, he could even lose his Scholar title.\"","Chun Ying covered her mouth and chuckled. \"Wouldn’t that be for the best? Then Young Master Yi would have to bow to you, Young Master.\"","\"Hm? Are you looking down on me?\"","\"If I’m going to defeat Brother Yi, I’ll do it fair and square. How could I resort to such underhanded tactics?\"","\"You are right to scold me, Young Master. I was wrong.\"","\"It’s good that you know you were wrong. As punishment, you’ll finish all the paperwork in my study for me.\"","\"And you’re not allowed to rest until it’s done.\"","Chun Ying was both annoyed and amused, but seeing that he had already pulled the covers over himself, she could only agree and turn to leave the room.","She took a few steps, then paused, a strange look flickering in her eyes.","’Defeat him?’","’In what way is Young Master Yi stronger than the Young Master?’","’The Young Master isn’t planning to compete with Young Master Yi in the Calligraphy Dao, is he?’","’That would be... truly overestimating himself...’","...","「Spring Rain Building.」","Lou Yuxue made her way back to her private chamber. Just as she was about to shut the door, a figure abruptly appeared before her.","\"You... Liu Wu?!\"","The visitor was none other than Chen Yi, dressed in a black cloak. He stood outside the chamber, looked at the surprised Lou Yuxue, and said with a smile,","\"We meet again, Miss Yuxue.\"","Lou Yuxue let go of the door and huffed, \"I had no desire to see you, you bastard.\"","She had long grown accustomed to Chen Yi’s habit of appearing and disappearing like a ghost, so seeing him now wasn’t entirely a surprise.","Chen Yi walked into the chamber unconcerned and closed the door. \"If you truly didn’t want to see me, why would you seek out that Miss Cui to purchase grain?\"","Lou Yuxue’s brow furrowed. \"You followed me?\"","The words had barely left her mouth when she suddenly pointed at Chen Yi and demanded, \"Did you go to the tailor shop again?!\"","Chen Yi sat down calmly at the table and waved his hand. \"Don’t be so surprised. Didn’t you already know that I have some knowledge of your White Tiger Guard?\"","\"So, you already know the Lord Pavilion Master wants to invite you to join the White Tiger Guard?\"","\"Of course.\"","\"Then you...\"","\"I refuse.\"","Chen Yi looked at her with a half-smile, then changed the subject. \"However, I am curious to hear how you plan to persuade me.\"","Lou Yuxue rolled her eyes at him and sat down opposite him.","\"Since you don’t want to join, nothing I say will be of any use.\"","\"How do you know if you don’t try? Maybe I’ll change my mind.\"","\"Joining the White Tiger Guard means pledging loyalty to the Pavilion Master and the Holy Emperor. You also have to accept deployments, many of which are life-threatening...\"","Before Lou Yuxue could finish, Chen Yi waved his hands dismissively.","\"Never mind, never mind. The requirements for your White Tiger Guard are too steep. I’m not worthy.\"","’Pledging loyalty and all that is one thing; it’s just words.’","’But things like deployments would only add a ton of trouble to my leisurely life.’","’Besides, there’s nothing in the White Tiger Guard that I want. Joining would be more trouble than it’s worth.’","With this in mind, Chen Yi said, \"Enough chatter.\"","\"I came to find you this time not only to ask when that shipment of grain will arrive in Shu State, but also because I need your help with something.\"","Lou Yuxue’s expression eased slightly. \"Before we talk business, shouldn’t you explain why you killed Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao?\"","\"Do you have any idea how many things their deaths have affected?\"","\"If the Lord General finds out about this, do you know what kind of punishment I’ll face?\"","Chen Yi took off his mask, looking completely shameless as he said with a smile,","\"If you were so worried about all that, why did you cover for me?\"","\"You... Hmph!\"","Lou Yuxue fumed.","’She never should have covered for this bastard. Even more, she shouldn’t have taken the initiative to discuss buying grain with Cui Qingwu before he showed up.’","Chen Yi knew she had indeed taken some risks for him, so he said with a serious expression,","\"I promise you, once the grain arrives, I’ll tell you everything about Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao.\"","\"Before that, I need you to spread some rumors.\"","Lou Yuxue’s expression improved. \"What kind of rumors?\"","\"Not many. Just two.\"","\"First, that King Landu intends to lead the Peacock King Banner in an attack on Shu State.\"","\"And second, that the son of the Barbarian Left King Mu Hage is currently in Shu State...\""]},{"number":418,"title":"Chapter 418 - 262: People’s Hearts Can Be Overturned","paragraphs":["\"...Asutai, the son of the Barbarian Left King Mu Hage, was captured by horse bandits from Poshisu Country and made into a barbarian slave. Right now, he’s in Shu State!\"","Chen Yi finished, looking at the wide-eyed Lou Yuxue. He chuckled lightly and said, \"That’s all.\"","Lou Yuxue stared at him blankly.","After a long moment, she finally spoke.","\"Th-that’s all?\"","\"Do you have any idea what you’re saying?\"","\"King Landu is marching east to raid the border, and the Left King’s son is in Shu State. If these two pieces of news get out, it will undoubtedly cause chaos.\"","\"All of Shu State, and even the entirety of Great Wei’s Nine State and Three Prefectures, will be thrown into a panic.\"","\"I, you... Why would you do this?\"","Hearing this, a faint smile appeared on Chen Yi’s face. \"I’m very satisfied with your reaction.\"","\"If someone as sharp as you can lose their composure like this, I imagine no one else in Shu State will be an exception, will they?\"","Lou Yuxue couldn’t help but curse, \"Satisfied my ass!\"","\"Tell me, what are you really planning?!\"","Chen Yi let out a short, incredulous laugh. \"Relax, relax. I’m just asking you to play along with me.\"","Seeing that Lou Yuxue was still glaring at him, he had to explain further, \"The news is fake.\"","\"Fake... It’s all fake?\"","\"Not entirely.\"","Lou Yuxue, who had just started to relax, instantly tensed up again. She nearly choked on her own spit.","\"Explain everything!\"","’To think that I’m a distinguished White Tiger Guard Silver Banner Officer—and one on the verge of becoming a Golden Banner Officer at that. I’ve been through things ordinary people can’t even fathom. I should be able to stay calm even if a mountain collapsed in front of me.’","’Yet here I am, losing my composure and blurting things out again and again because of Chen Yi.’","’It’s truly embarrassing for a Silver Banner Officer like me.’","Chen Yi naturally noticed, but he didn’t point it out, lest Lou Yuxue pounce on him and bite him.","\"As King Landu’s biological younger brother, it’s not entirely impossible that Lv Jiunan would lead the Peacock King Banner here, but the idea doesn’t hold up to scrutiny.\"","\"Horse bandits are horse bandits, after all. Their weapons, equipment, and their soldiers’ Cultivation are all inferior to the Dingyuan Army. They’d have no chance of victory in a large-scale attack.\"","\"So that piece of news is just a ’rumor.’\"","\"As for the son of the Barbarian Left King... he really is in Shu State.\"","Before Lou Yuxue could speak, Chen Yi preempted her, asking, \"You remember the incident with the East Market Grain Storehouse being burned down, don’t you?\"","A flicker of understanding crossed Lou Yuxue’s mind as she realized, \"Are you saying that one of those barbarian slaves is Mu Hage’s son?\"","\"Have those bumpkins from Poshisu Country lost their minds? They even dared to go after the Black Bear Tribe?\"","\"Aren’t they afraid Mu Hage will lead the Barbarian Race’s army to slaughter everyone along the Ancient Tea-Horse Road?\"","Chen Yi shook his head, not explaining further. \"It’s a long story. I’ll tell you when I have time.\"","\"You just need to know that Asutai... Mu Hage’s son... is currently in Shu State.\"","Lou Yuxue gritted her teeth. She really wanted to punch him.","But she knew that if Chen Yi didn’t want to talk, there was nothing she could do. She could only press on, asking:","\"Then where is he now?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","\"Then how can I be sure that what you’re saying is true?\"","Chen Yi spread his hands. \"If both pieces of news were fake, wouldn’t that be even better for you?\"","Lou Yuxue said helplessly, \"I still need to understand what the impact will be after the news gets out.\"","\"Otherwise, I can’t possibly help you with this.\"","Seeing this, Chen Yi thought for a moment and nodded. \"There’s no harm in telling you.\"","\"After these two pieces of news spread, grain prices in Shu State will skyrocket.\"","\"You... You’re doing all this just for that?\"","\"Of course. It’s not like I’m actually crazy. Why would I joke about such matters for no reason?\"","Lou Yuxue was beginning to understand Chen Yi’s intentions for releasing these two rumors.","The two rumors—\"King Landu is attacking\" and \"The Barbarian Left King’s son is in Shu State\"—would have only one effect.","—To create panic among the people of Shu State.","Even if the news couldn’t be confirmed, and even if many people weren’t foolish, there would still be some who adopted a \"better safe than sorry\" attitude.","It wouldn’t take many.","If even one percent of the population believed it, they would do everything in their power to buy grain, causing prices to soar.","At this thought, Lou Yuxue snorted, \"Deceiving the common people... aren’t you afraid of retribution?\"","Chen Yi smiled and shook his head. \"You’re using the wrong word, and you’re blaming the wrong person.\"","\"I’m not the one deceiving the common people. It’s the few grain distributors in Shu State, and the Ji State Trading Company.\"","\"Manipulating people, then. That’s right, isn’t it?\"","\"’Manipulating’... I suppose you could call it that. But my targets have never been the common people.\"","At this point, Chen Yi paused, toying with the black iron mask in his hands before changing the subject.","\"Do you remember the question for this year’s metropolitan examination?\"","Lou Yuxue thought for a moment before saying hesitantly, \"Was it ’A boat is on the water, why does it capsize’?\"","\"That’s right. Why does it capsize?\"","\"The common people are like the water. The boat is like ’Shu State,’ like the Great Wei’s Nine State and Three Prefectures, like the Court Officials.\"","\"Tell me, if the boat capsizes, is it the fault of the people in the boat, or the fault of the water beneath it?\"","Lou Yuxue looked at him, displeased. \"I haven’t read many books...\"","Chen Yi shook his head and said, \"What I’m trying to say is, the water that bears the boat is the same that swallows it up.\"","\"Since they want to plot against the people of Shu State, I don’t mind teaching them what real pain feels like.\"","Hearing this, Lou Yuxue gave him a deep, long look.","She might not be well-read, but she understood the meaning behind the phrase \"the water that bears the boat is the same that swallows it up.\"","’Since the people from the Ji State Trading Company don’t care about the common folk, manipulating grain prices and forcing them to buy at exorbitant rates to make a massive profit...’","’He, \"Liu Wu,\" was going to end this farce as soon as possible.’","\"Two questions.\"","\"First, aren’t you afraid of the situation spiraling out of control? Those people from the Ji State Trading Company are no pushovers.\"","Chen Yi smiled and said, \"Simple.\"","\"Before the news is released, all we have to do is find a way to buy up all the grain they’re holding, right?\"","\"You... Where are you going to get that much silver?\"","\"I have my ways.\"","Lou Yuxue was momentarily stunned. After a moment’s thought, she couldn’t help but remind him, \"Whatever you’re planning, you still owe me the silver for the grain I bought from Simurgh Phoenix.\""]},{"number":419,"title":"Chapter 419 - 262: People’s Hearts Can Be Overturned","paragraphs":["\"Don’t worry. Once the grain arrives, I’ll give it to you.\"","\"But if you try any more tricks, the Cui Family won’t let you off either.\"","Seeing Chen Yi nod, Lou Yuxue continued, \"Second question.\"","\"These two pieces of news can only fool people for a short time. As soon as the Government Office issues a notice to clarify things, your little scheme will fall apart, won’t it?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly and praised her, \"As expected of Lord Lady Tiger of the White Tiger Guard. It’s impressive you thought of this. Very impressive.\"","\"Cut the crap. Tell me your plan.\"","\"The Buddha said, ’It cannot be spoken.’\"","Lou Yuxue slammed her hand on the table, her beautiful eyes glaring at him. \"You won’t talk about this, you won’t talk about that. Are you planning to screw me over again?\"","Chen Yi didn’t know whether to laugh or cry. \"Lord Lady Tiger, this matter is like a nocked arrow. It must be fired.\"","\"If I were planning to swindle you at a time like this, wouldn’t I be shooting myself in the foot?\"","\"The only reason I’m not telling you is because I don’t want the White Tiger Guard to have me on their radar.\"","Lou Yuxue was still skeptical. \"I doubt you’d dare...\"","The two then discussed more details, such as when to spread the two rumors and when that shipment of grain would arrive in Shu State.","It wasn’t until the sixth mark of the Hour of the Ox that Chen Yi finally stood up, preparing to leave Spring Rain Building.","Before leaving, he took the letter handwritten by Lin Huai’an from his robes and handed it to Lou Yuxue.","\"Here, this is for you. Consider it a thank-you gift.\"","Since Lou Yuxue had already made a deal with Cui Qingwu without any persuasion from him, he didn’t mind returning the favor and throwing in this letter as a little bonus.","Lou Yuxue was initially unconcerned, but after a quick glance, her expression suddenly turned serious.","\"Lin Huai’an... King Landu... ironware trade?\"","\"This thing... where did you get it?!\"","As the Chief Steward of Bright Moon Building and having been in Shu State for many years, Lou Yuxue naturally knew Lin Huai’an’s identity.","But she never imagined that a secret letter between Lin Huai’an and King Landu would so blatantly mention the word \"ironware.\"","She couldn’t help but recall what Lord General had said earlier—that his meeting with King Landu was to find concrete evidence of his trades with certain courtiers in Shu State.","’This letter should be it. The number of people in Shu State who can provide ironware is very small. No matter who it is, Lord General will surely be pleased.’","Unfortunately, Lin Huai’an was already dead. For this letter to be effective, further investigation would be needed.","Chen Yi, naturally unaware of these things, raised an eyebrow. \"Is it useful?\"","\"Never you mind. Just tell me where this letter came from.\"","\"I was there the night Lin Huai’an died.\"","Lou Yuxue was taken aback. \"You killed him?\"","Chen Yi pursed his lips. \"Someone else did.\"","After a moment’s thought, he added a few more words.","\"The supplier of the ’ironware’ mentioned in this letter is Zhu Hao of the Shu State Capital Commandery.\"","\"Zhu Hao?\"","Lou Yuxue had a flash of realization. \"So it was him.\"","After a moment of thought, she asked, \"Who else knows about the contents of this letter?\"","\"No one.\"","Chen Yi replied, and seeing Lou Yuxue’s evasiveness, he understood that the White Tiger Guard must need this letter.","Naturally, he wasn’t about to reveal Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao.","Lou Yuxue nodded slightly. \"I’ll take this letter. Thank you.\"","Chen Yi said nonchalantly, \"Glad it could help. I’m leaving.\"","This time, his targets weren’t the likes of King Landu and Zhu Hao, but the far more important Liu Hong.","Even the few grain trading companies in Shu State were just something he was dealing with on the side.","He didn’t much care about a letter that could prove Zhu Hao’s guilt.","After a bit more small talk, Chen Yi repeatedly warned Lou Yuxue not to leak the information—not even to the White Tiger Guard ahead of time—before finally leaving.","Lou Yuxue didn’t refuse.","’If I know, it means the White Tiger Guard knows. Whether or not I keep it a secret will depend on the repercussions of this whole affair.’","After all, she hadn’t been promoted to Golden Banner Officer yet. There were many things she couldn’t decide on her own, so it was inevitable she’d have reservations.","If the plan succeeded, everyone would be happy.","If it failed... she couldn’t possibly take the fall alone.","She might just have to let \"Liu Wu\" take the blame.","Thinking this, Lou Yuxue didn’t hesitate for long. After putting the letter away safely, she summoned her subordinates and gave them their instructions.","Although she was still wary of \"Liu Wu,\" compared to the money-grubbing people from the Ji State Trading Company, she was more willing to trust him.","At the same time, she also wanted to see just how \"Liu Wu\" planned to make the Ji State Trading Company suffer a loss in Shu State.","’Hmph. Those people have already made so much in the north, yet they still want a piece of Shu State. Truly insatiable. This is a perfect chance for \"Liu Wu\" to teach them a lesson...’","「Not long after.」","Chen Yi returned to the residence behind the tailor shop and called for Zhang Dabao to remove his disguise.","He gazed at the night outside the window, listening to the patter of the rain, as the Go board in his mind constantly had pieces placed and removed.","Black stones were swapped back and forth.","They included people like King Landu of Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Left King, Mu Hage.","On the side of the white stones, however, there were only Lou Yuxue and Pei Qian of the Mountain Race.","In the end, Chen Yi picked up the white stone that represented himself and sighed inwardly.","’To make those people fall into the trap, I’m afraid Wang Ji alone won’t be enough.’","After much thought, he concluded that the only way to make this play more convincing was for him to personally enter the fray.","’Fortunately, I have another identity.’","None other than Chen Yu.","Thinking of this, Chen Yi changed his clothes and instructed, \"Wait for me here tomorrow.\"","Zhang Dabao acknowledged with a \"Yes, sir,\" and didn’t ask a single question.","Chen Yi didn’t say much either. He slipped silently into the rain and returned directly to Spring Lotus Garden.","Once he had changed into a set of dry, casual clothes, he went to his study and lit an oil lamp.","He sat quietly for a moment.","Chen Yi cleared his mind slightly, took out a brush and paper, and began to write and sketch.","His trip tonight had been quite fruitful.","Not only had he gained Asutai’s trust, but he had also consulted with Lou Yuxue to confirm their subsequent plans.","On top of that, he had unexpectedly received a piece of news—Fu Wanqing was currently deep within the Barbarian Race’s territory, in Left King Mu Hage’s tribe.","This trip could only be described as a success.","However, although he had made his moves and many things were proceeding according to his plan, he still needed a bit of luck.","Although he often touted the saying \"man can conquer fate,\" when push came to shove, a certain degree of caution was unavoidable.","Especially since he was now facing not fools like Liu Wen and Liu Jing, but the likes of Liu Hong, King Landu, and the people from the Ji State Trading Company.","If word got out, or if any mishap occurred along the way, the entire plan could be overturned.","He had no choice but to handle it with extreme care.","’Now, it all depends on the Xiao Family’s luck.’","As Chen Yi thought this, he focused his mind and began painting portraits of Xiao Wan’er, Xiao Jinghong, and others on a wide sheet of Yunsong Paper.","It had been a long time; he really did need to hand over two paintings to fulfill his obligation.","Why two paintings?","Because his wife, Xiao Jinghong, had to have a portrait too, of course.","So, Chen Yi shamelessly painted himself into the picture, depicting himself with a handsome face and a dashing posture, the very image of a graceful young master.","’A family should be complete and proper, after all.’","And as one painting was completed, Chen Yi’s True Essence flowed, and he used the Mental Realm of his Painting Dao to connect with the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","The next moment, he saw the portraits of the people on the Yunsong Paper seem to come alive.","Not only could they move, but they could also make various expressions.","Chen Yi looked at the figures in the painting with a strange expression. ’The Painting Dao has such a miraculous ability?’","Then, with a slight shift in his thoughts, the Four Great Divine Beasts Spiritual Essence shifted position within the Sea of Qi in his Forehead Acupoint, and strands of True Essence flowed into the painting.","The next moment, a figure walked straight out of the painting.","It was none other than \"Xiao Wan’er\" in a long dress.","The figure of \"Xiao Wan’er\" was solid, her face flushed with a healthy blush, and she smiled at him as if she were a living person.","Chen Yi sized her up, then reached out a hand to test it. Confirming that it was just a shadow formed from the ambient Spiritual Mechanism, he finally relaxed.","’An unexpected surprise. Not bad.’","Right now, his Painting Dao was only at the Minor Success Realm, so this illusion wasn’t of much help to him.","Perhaps when his Painting Dao advanced to Great Success or even Perfection, it would have other uses.","Thinking this, Chen Yi painted another one, a slight smile appearing on his face.","’Lord Ye’s love of dragons... It really is a wondrous thing.’","...","「The next day.」","Just as the sky began to brighten, Chen Yi, already dressed neatly, came into the living room and sat down at the dining table.","Xiaodie asked, slightly surprised, \"Young Master, are you going out today? I thought you didn’t have classes at the academy until tomorrow.\"","While telling her to prepare breakfast, Chen Yi looked at the fine drizzle outside the window and said:","\"I have some business at Hundred Herbs Hall...\""]},{"number":420,"title":"Chapter 420 - 263: An Autumn Cleansing","paragraphs":["Although Chen Yi had no intention of appearing in Shu State as \"Chen Yu\" anytime soon, he simply had no suitable subordinates for the task.","Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao were adequate for following orders, but they were not fit for important tasks.","Liu Lang, on the other hand, was capable of handling major affairs, but his ability to improvise was too poor. If he ran into people from the Ji State Trading Company, he would almost certainly be exposed.","As for the remaining disciples of the Celestial Sect, Chen Yi had yet to discover anyone who possessed both excellent character and ability.","Thus, he had no choice but to resort to this suboptimal plan.","’Now that \"Chen Yu\" has made an appearance, I wonder how the old master and the others will react.’","Of course, Chen Yi wasn’t particularly worried about the Xiao Family coming to find him.","The ones he needed to be wary of were the people inside Yunqing Building, across from Hundred Herbs Hall—Cui Qingwu and Chen Yunfan.","The two of them had previously sensed that \"Liu Wu\" was in the West Market, so there was no guarantee they wouldn’t make the connection to \"Chen Yu.\"","’Things have already come to this. I can only take it one step at a time.’","Though a million thoughts raced through his mind, Chen Yi’s expression remained impassive as he told Xiaodie, \"Let’s have breakfast.\"","\"Yes, Young Master! As it happens, the kitchen made your favorite steamed pork with rice flour today. I’ll go bring it over right now.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. As he watched Xiaodie trot away, his gaze naturally shifted toward the courtyard.","Overcast clouds obscured the sun, making the courtyard seem a little dim.","The wet bluestone slabs were clean and smooth. Drops of rain pattered lightly against them.","A distant pavilion stood by the pond, shrouded in a thin mist born from the mingling rain and water, giving it a hazy appearance.","It was like a living painting titled \"Misty Rain over Jiangnan.\"","\"The endless evening rain sprinkles river and sky, washing the clear autumn clean...\"","’It may be a pond instead of a river, but the sentiment fits.’","Chen Yi muttered to himself, the phrase \"a golden-scaled fish is no creature of the pond\" inevitably coming to mind.","This seemed to reflect the Xiao Family’s current circumstances.","’Heh, whether it fits or not, it will have to...’","Just then, Xiaodie came in carrying his bowl and chopsticks. Urging him to eat, she asked with a smile,","\"Young Master, what were you saying about whether something fits?\"","Chen Yi collected himself and sat down at the table. Shaking his head without answering, he asked a different question instead:","\"The Double Ninth Festival is almost here. Does the household have any arrangements?\"","The ninth day of the ninth month was the Double Ninth Festival.","Back in Jiangnan Prefecture, grand events were held every year on this day, such as dharma assemblies by the Buddhist Sect, poetry gatherings for scholars, or performances by the courtesans of the Qin Building.","He wasn’t sure what to expect here in Shu State.","A smile spread across Xiaodie’s face. She spread her hands wide and gestured as she said, \"Lots and lots... of fun things.\"","\"But here in the Prefecture City, it’s more or less the same every year—poetry gatherings, temple fairs, and that sort of thing.\"","\"But many of the Mountain Race people have all kinds of different festivities. The most interesting are the horse races and the sacrifices to the Road God.\"","\"The Road God?\"","A look of realization dawned on Chen Yi’s face. \"You mean the people from the Horse Gangs, right?\"","Horse Gangs were similar to the Cao Gang.","The only difference between the two was that the former traveled the Ancient Tea-Horse Road from Great Wei to the Western Buddha Country, while the latter traveled by water, navigating ships along rivers and lakes.","The Road God was the deity worshipped by the Horse Gangs.","Seeing that he understood, Xiaodie nodded eagerly. \"Every year, people ride piebald horses through the streets and alleys, followed by lots of floats made from colorful paper. They’re so beautiful.\"","\"I remember the year before last, the Eldest Miss had Sister Huatang take us out to enjoy the festivities. I ate so many Double Ninth cakes...\"","Chen Yi’s expression relaxed as he ate his breakfast and listened to her chatter.","It wasn’t that he wanted to attend poetry gatherings or celebrate the festival. He was merely asking about the household’s arrangements to avoid any scheduling conflicts.","After all, the task ahead of him allowed for no carelessness. Since he couldn’t be in two places at once, caution was paramount.","A short while later, he finished his breakfast.","Chen Yi retrieved a painting from his study, gave Xiaodie a few instructions, and went straight to Jiaxing Garden.","At this time, Xiao Wan’er had also just finished her meal and was in the middle of drinking her medicinal soup.","Seeing Chen Yi arrive, she rose to greet him with a gentle smile. \"I was just about to send Huatang to find you.\"","Chen Yi looked at her, slightly surprised. \"Is there news from Tonglin Town already?\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded, her pale face wreathed in a smile.","\"Uncle Kang just sent word. After the people from the Prefecture City arrived yesterday, they finished surveying the academy grounds on the very same day and adjusted the blueprints.\"","\"These are the new blueprints. Have a look.\"","Chen Yi placed the painting scroll he was carrying on the table, took the blueprints, and gave them a quick scan. He then shook his head with a smile.","\"This is a job for professionals.\"","\"With these adjustments, the whole academy’s layout is much more logical, especially with the new addition of the Observatory Platform.\"","Chen Yi himself was blessed by his Medical Dao’s Mental Realm and had the highest principles of the medical arts etched into his heart. He could determine the solar terms and the positions of stars without relying on external tools.","His Qi Observation Skill was a Medical Skill he had honed on this very foundation.","However, students new to the Medical Dao, or even those whose Medical Skills were still unrefined, would need to learn some fundamentals when first studying the \"Five Qi and Six Cycles.\"","The Observatory Platform was an essential structure to help them survey solar terms and celestial alignments.","Xiao Wan’er hummed in agreement. \"Once I send my reply, they’ll begin construction.\"","\"With Uncle Kang overseeing it, I’m confident it can be completed before spring.\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"The preparations took a while, but the actual construction will proceed much faster than the work on the Mutual Market.\"","The Wu Mountain Mutual Market, after all, was a marketplace in the middle of nowhere. Plus, it would hold all sorts of valuable goods, so its structures needed to be sturdier.","Once the storefronts and warehouses were built, they might even need to erect a defensive wall to facilitate protection and management.","But the Medical Dao Academy was a different matter.","Aside from buildings with specific functions—such as the Observatory Platform, the library, and the herb storage—the remaining structures merely needed to provide shelter from the elements.","Xiao Wan’er put the blueprints away. Her eyes fell on the painting scroll on the table, and she couldn’t help but ask, \"What’s this?\""]},{"number":421,"title":"Chapter 421 - 263: A Thorough Autumn Cleansing","paragraphs":["Chen Yi said with a smile, \"I’ve fulfilled my promise. The painting I said I’d make for you is complete.\"","\"Really?\"","Xiao Wan’er’s heart skipped a beat. She quickly handed the blueprints to Shen Huatang and carefully unrolled the painting.","Six figures seemed to leap off the paper.","There was Xiao Fengchun, imposing without being angry, and the elegant Fu Wanqing, both seated on chairs. Squatting beside them was Xiao Wuge, grinning from ear to ear.","Behind them stood a valiant and heroic-looking Xiao Jinghong, a gentle and delicate Xiao Wan’er, and, standing between the two women, Chen Yi.","—Just as he had painted himself the night before, he was dressed in black brocade robes, his features strikingly handsome.","As Xiao Wan’er looked at the portrait in her hands, the images of Xiao Fengchun and Fu Wanqing reflected in her eyes, which began to mist over.","\"Fa-Father... Mother...\"","Chen Yi watched Xiao Wan’er, who was on the verge of tears, and sighed internally. He decided not to mention the other uses for his Minor Achievement Painting Dao.","He didn’t want her worries to fester into a sickness of the heart.","It was a pity he couldn’t yet reveal that Fu Wanqing was deep in the territory of the Barbarian Race; otherwise, he could have given Xiao Wan’er something to be happy about.","Beside them, Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun glanced at the portrait and naturally sensed a trace of Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism emanating from it.","While marveling inwardly, they didn’t dare say much.","After a long while, Xiao Wan’er finally came back to her senses, turning to the side to wipe the corners of her eyes.","\"You... Brother-in-law, please forgive me. I... You... Your painting is just too good. For a moment, it made me think of Father and Mother.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment and said comfortingly with a smile, \"As long as you’re not blaming me for taking the liberty of painting myself in.\"","Only then did Xiao Wan’er notice Chen Yi in the painting. After a brief look, a blush inexplicably appeared on her face.","\"You... You are Jinghong’s husband. Of course, that also makes you my... our family.\"","’But why did this scoundrel paint himself with both arms outstretched?’","’It looked as if he had his arms around both of us sisters.’","Chen Yi, of course, was aware of that little \"flaw.\" He said nonchalantly, \"As long as you’re satisfied, Eldest Sister.\"","\"I also painted an extra one for my wife. In a few days, I’ll have someone deliver it to her.\"","While carefully putting the portrait away, Xiao Wan’er nodded. \"Calculating the time, Second Sister’s reply should be on its way.\"","\"After you and I have read her letter, we can write a reply and send it along with the painting.\"","Once Xiao Wan’er had calmed down, Chen Yi explained the reason for his visit.","\"Yesterday, I heard from Wang Ji that Boss Chen Yu is returning today. I’m going to head over and check on things later.\"","\"If everything goes smoothly, Guangyuan County should be the first stop for Hundred Herbs Hall’s expansion.\"","Xiao Wan’er thought for a moment. \"You can make the decision.\"","She then explained apologetically, \"Right now, I’m spread too thin. All my attention is on the Medical Dao Academy.\"","\"If you don’t mind, could you help me by checking in on Hundred Herbs Hall more often?\"","This was exactly what he wanted.","Chen Yi, of course, wouldn’t refuse. \"The partnership between Hundred Herbs Hall and the other medicine halls has already taken shape, so there isn’t much to do.\"","\"Of course, this ultimately concerns the Xiao Mansion’s finances. After I see Boss Chen Yu, I’ll ask about his plans and let you know.\"","Xiao Wan’er gazed at him with limpid eyes and nodded gently. \"Thank you.\"","\"There’s no need for thanks...\"","Watching the two of them, Xie Tingyun had an \"I knew it\" expression all over her face.","In her eyes, the way they were acting right now could only be described as \"lovey-dovey.\"","So, after watching a moment longer, she couldn’t resist nudging Shen Huatang with her elbow.","’Junior Sister, I was right, wasn’t I? The relationship between these two... is unusual.’","Shen Huatang shot her a sidelong glance and mouthed silently, \"Don’t be ridiculous.\"","But still, Shen Huatang recalled what she had seen and heard that day in Tonglin Town and had to admit to herself that Xie Tingyun was right.","’The Eldest Miss and the Second Sister’s husband are just... This is beyond me!’","After a few more lighthearted words, Chen Yi stood up to leave.","Xiao Wan’er saw him out of Jiaxing Garden, handing him an oil-paper umbrella as she reminded him:","\"When you see Boss Chen Yu, say hello for me.\"","Chen Yi nodded in agreement, then opened the umbrella and left the Xiao Mansion.","This time, without Cui Qingwu’s meddling, he had no desire to let Liu Si’er and the others follow him.","He disappeared alone into the rainy crowd, doing his best not to attract attention.","However, just as he rounded Chuansi Street, Chen Yi surveyed the surrounding pedestrians and couldn’t help but frown slightly.","He wasn’t sure if it was his imagination.","But he had a feeling that there were far more Wandering Martial Artists on the streets today than usual.","Moreover, based on their accents, it wasn’t hard to tell they were all from outside Shu State.","Chen Yi scanned the area, then slightly relaxed his Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, revealing his Eighth Grade Realm cultivation.","He infused his ears with True Essence to listen carefully to their conversations.","\"I never expected a place like Shu State, so far from the Central Plains, to be this prosperous.\"","\"It is a State Capital, after all. Even on the frontier, the Imperial Court and the powerful nobles still have their reach.\"","\"Besides, there are many Noble Families here. Naturally, they benefit the region by building bridges, paving roads, developing the local economy, and so on.\"","\"That’s true... As I recall, the family with the longest legacy in Shu State is the Xiao Family of Duke Dingyuan, right?\"","\"That’s them.\"","\"But that was in the past. Ever since the previous Patriarch, Duke Dingyuan Xiao Fengchun, died on the battlefield, the current Xiao Family’s old are old and its young are young. They’re already in decline.\"","Chen Yi glanced at the few Wandering Martial Artists with obvious Jiangnan accents, then turned his head to listen elsewhere.","\"...Immortal Bai appeared in Xiangyang City, north of Jing State, the day before yesterday. And he performed a divination for someone.\"","\"Who was so unlucky?\"","\"They say it was someone from the Evil Demonic Dao. No one knows their name, but the prophecy got out.\"","\"What did it say?\"","\"A fate of wealth and status; if not rich, then noble.\"","\"HISS! Doesn’t that mean that person is going to die a horrible death?\"","\"Isn’t that the truth? We’ll see what becomes of them in a few days. We’d better be careful, too.\"","\"Yeah, Immortal Bai unintentionally revealed he’s coming to Shu State. We’re just here to watch the show, we can’t afford to lose our lives here...\"","After listening to a few more idle conversations, Chen Yi finally understood why all these Wandering Martial Artists had come to Shu State.","—It was all because of Immortal Bai of the Wind and Rain Tower!","Realizing this, Chen Yi didn’t know whether to laugh or cry.","Yesterday, when he’d heard the news from Pei Qian, he hadn’t thought much of it. But now, it seemed the influence of Immortal Bai—the number one figure in Martial Arts who had dominated the Jianghu for decades—far exceeded his imagination.","’I wonder what his purpose is for coming to Shu State.’","’It couldn’t possibly be to deal with the Xiao Family, could it?’","The moment the thought appeared in Chen Yi’s mind, he quickly shook his head to banish it.","The Jing State Liu Family, the White Tiger Guard, and the Ji State Trading Company were already enough of a headache for him.","If Immortal Bai was added to the mix, he’d really just throw in the towel.","With these thoughts, Chen Yi walked straight to the residence behind the tailor shop in the West Market.","Zhang Dabao had been waiting there for a long time.","Chen Yi didn’t linger. He sat down in a chair and had the man apply his disguise.","As Zhang Dabao worked quickly on him, he reported, \"The Shopkeeper came by first thing this morning.\"","\"What was it about?\"","\"He told me to tell you that suspicious people have been seen outside that residence in the East Market recently.\"","\"That residence?\"","Chen Yi frowned slightly. The residence in the East Market was the very place where he had tricked Xiao Dongchen into signing the contract.","He hadn’t been back there since. He had even specifically instructed Wang Ji to send the seller out of Shu State and have him watched.","He never thought that after all this time, someone had actually found the place.","After a moment of thought, a pensive look crossed Chen Yi’s face. \"It can only be one of two parties.\"","’First, the White Tiger Guard. After all, Xiao Dongchen is one of their Silver Banner Officers, so it’s reasonable they’d follow the clues he left behind.’","’Second, the Liu Family.’","’Or more specifically, Liu Hong.’","’Comparatively, the latter is more likely.’","’After all, after Liu Wen’s death, interested parties have investigated his affairs quite thoroughly.’","’The three hundred thousand taels of silver that ended up in the Xiao Family’s hands is a clear clue in itself.’","Thinking of this, Chen Yi gave an order: \"A while ago, didn’t you get in touch with some beggars? Just have them keep an eye on the place.\"","Just as Zhang Dabao was about to agree, he suddenly remembered something and said with an embarrassed expression:","\"My lord, I’m afraid those men won’t dare to help me anymore.\"","\"Oh? And why is that?\"","\"You’ve forgotten, my lord. That day, they followed those two horse bandits from Poshisu Country to Heiyu Lane, and afterward... a lot of them died.\"","Zhang Dabao gave a bitter smile. \"Afterward, the Shopkeeper had to give them a lot of silver coins to keep them quiet.\"","Chen Yi chuckled in spite of himself. \"In that case, just have someone else watch it.\"","’Aside from Liu Lang, only the Guards from the Celestial Sect have the necessary strength right now.’","After some thought, Chen Yi continued his instructions, \"Later, go to Hundred Herbs Hall and summon Wang Ji, Liu Lang, and a few disciples from the Celestial Sect. Tell them... that I want to see them.\"","\"As... who?\"","\"Chen Yu!\"","Chen Yi pointed to his face—now handsome and serene—and said, \"This will do.\"","Zhang Dabao understood. He quickly put down another mask and replied while tidying up:","\"Please wait a moment, my lord. I’ll go right away.\""]},{"number":422,"title":"Chapter 422 - 264: The East Wind Has Come","paragraphs":["Zhang Dabao didn’t keep Chen Yi waiting for long.","About an hour later, Wang Ji and Liu Lang arrived one after the other.","Three other young men, dressed in fitted blue attire with blades and swords at their waists, followed them.","Liu Lang caught sight of Chen Yi and greeted him with a grin. \"Greetings, Boss. It’s been a while since you’ve shown your face.\"","Wang Ji and the others, however, were not as casual. They bowed in unison and said, \"Boss.\"","Chen Yi regarded them with a calm expression and said faintly, \"Sit and talk.\"","Liu Lang was the first to sit down beside him. Looking at the expression on his face, he chuckled inwardly.","’When I first met Boss Chen,’ he thought, ’he’d always put on a stern face unless we were meeting in private.’","’But after getting to know him, I realized—Boss Chen has a thousand faces.’","’Besides using the identity of Liu Wu when he’s out and about, he’s also impersonated Black Tooth.’","’Not only are his demeanor and tone of voice perfect imitations, but even his aura changes to match. Few people can ever discern his true identity.’","Liu Lang couldn’t help but feel a little smug. ’I’m the only... no, one of only two people who knows Boss Chen’s true identity.’","He had, after all, remembered Wang Ji.","Too bad Wang Ji didn’t know what he was thinking, or he would have surely looked at him with pity.","But Wang Ji clearly had no time for Liu Lang at the moment. After taking his seat, he turned to Chen Yi and began his report.","\"Sir, as you instructed, after consulting with Senior Disciple-Sister Xie Tingyun of the Celestial Sect, I have made arrangements for her junior disciples.\"","With that, he gestured to the three young men sitting at the far end. \"Why don’t you introduce yourselves.\"","The eldest of the group nodded and clasped his fist. \"I am Xue Duanyun of the Celestial Sect.\"","The other two young men followed suit. \"Celestial Sect, Zhang Sanhu.\"","\"Celestial Sect, Zhang Sihu. A pleasure to meet you, Boss.\"","Chen Yi sized them up, a faint glint in his eyes.","The auras of the three Celestial Sect disciples then appeared before him.","Their auras, a faint white, were not particularly strong. They were all Fifth Grade Realm Swordsmen, just one minor realm weaker than Shen Huatang.","However, the aura of Xue Duanyun, the first to speak, was faintly connected to the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","Clearly, his Sword Dao had already reached Minor Success, allowing him to empower his Swordsmanship with a wisp of Sword Intent.","After observing each of them, Chen Yi nodded, his expression unchanged. \"Welcome.\"","Xue Duanyun and the other two were slightly taken aback. They glanced at each other, a strange feeling in their hearts.","Before coming, they hadn’t thought much of it when they learned they were going to meet the boss of Hundred Herbs Hall. Now, it seemed they had been too optimistic.","This Boss Chen’s stern and unsmiling demeanor made them uneasy.","Chen Yi, of course, didn’t dwell on their thoughts. After signaling for Zhang Dabao to guard the door, he got straight to the point.","\"Word from Guangyuan County has come back. The situation is better than I expected.\"","\"Later, Wang Ji, send a message to Yan Sea. Tell him to begin preparations for opening a Hundred Herbs Hall branch on-site. You will also send people with the necessary silver coins and medicinal herbs.\"","A look of joy spread across Wang Ji’s face. He immediately stood and agreed.","His hard work for the past two months hadn’t been in vain. Hundred Herbs Hall finally had a chance to grow.","Chen Yi reminded him in a level tone, \"Don’t get careless.\"","\"This is the first step in Hundred Herbs Hall’s expansion. I will not tolerate any mistakes.\"","The joy on Wang Ji’s face faded slightly, replaced by a serious expression. \"Rest assured, Sir. I will arrange everything properly.\"","Chen Yi nodded slightly. \"How are the medicinal herb preparations coming along with Boss Jia Yuzhi?\"","Wang Ji, who was about to sit back down, froze. He hesitated. \"To be honest, Sir, he’s run into some trouble.\"","Before Chen Yi could ask, he continued, speaking a little faster, \"It’s not that Boss Jia is intentionally dragging his feet. Xinglin Hall is interfering.\"","\"Ever since I... and Mr. Qingzhou confronted Boss Jia, he has been trying to procure the medicinal herbs.\"","\"But for three straight days, he hasn’t been able to acquire a single stalk, let alone the thousand jin we need.\"","Wang Ji glanced at Chen Yi and saw that his expression was still impassive. He gritted his teeth and continued.","\"After investigating, we discovered that Xinglin Hall had already signed contracts with all the major medicinal herb merchants.\"","\"They... they bought up all the medicinal herbs.\"","For the first time, a slight change flickered in Chen Yi’s eyes. He asked with a hint of surprise, \"Except for Boss Jia?\"","Wang Ji nodded. \"Jia Yuzhi and three other herb merchants have always worked with our Hundred Herbs Hall, so of course they wouldn’t sign a contract with Xinglin Hall.\"","Chen Yi frowned to himself.","’Xinglin Hall’s move to cut off our supply at the source really did catch me off guard.’","’At the same time, what I previously thought was just an accident at Lin’s Grain Store—the burning of the medicinal herbs—now seems to have a whiff of conspiracy.’","’Could it be that Liu Hong’s target wasn’t just the grain store’s warehouse, but also Hundred Herbs Hall’s batch of medicinal herbs?’","Chen Yi pondered for a moment, still unable to determine if it was a coincidence or if Liu Hong had done it intentionally.","So he asked thoughtfully, \"How much silver and how many tea drinks do we have on hand?\"","Wang Ji hurriedly replied, \"After paying out the shares to our partners and the taxes to the Government Office, we have one hundred fifty-four thousand taels of silver remaining.\"","\"As for the five types of tea drinks, we only have three warehouses’ worth left. I estimate it’ll last ten days at most.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment and began calculating silently.","Last month, because of the Yunqing Building’s grand opening, other restaurants in Shu State had rushed to purchase the tea drinks, allowing Hundred Herbs Hall to make a huge profit.","But with the planned supply of medicinal herbs cut off, the workshop had nearly ground to a halt. Now, for every jar of tea drink Hundred Herbs Hall sold, they had one less in stock.","\"In that case, we’ll limit sales.\"","Wang Ji asked hesitantly, \"Sir, what... what kind of limit did you have in mind?\"","\"We need to make our supply last until September 20th at the latest. Until then, sell an equal, limited amount of tea drinks each day.\"","\"But... but if we do that, won’t we be unable to supply the restaurants and the Qin Building?\""]},{"number":423,"title":"Chapter 423 - 264: The East Wind Has Come","paragraphs":["Chen Yi glanced at him and said coolly, \"Spread the word. Tell everyone Xinglin Hall has all the medicinal herbs. We can’t make something from nothing.\"","\"And add that if anyone is in a hurry, they can supply the herbs themselves.\"","After listening, Wang Ji thought for a moment before it dawned on him, and a smile instantly spread across his face.","\"Brilliant, my lord. This is sure to cause a major headache for Xinglin Hall.\"","After all, Hundred Herbs Hall was no longer the destitute, fledgling business it had been at its grand opening.","Thanks to its five signature teas, Hundred Herbs Hall had firmly established itself in Shu State.","To say it was a household name would be no exaggeration.","Especially in the Qin Building, the carousing, hungover gentlemen adored the Divine Bull Tea. It was the perfect choice, whether for their own consumption or for treating their companions.","Wang Ji could just imagine the reaction of those gentlemen, young and old, who prided themselves on their freewheeling lifestyles, once Hundred Herbs Hall started limiting its tea sales.","Either way, it meant trouble for Xinglin Hall.","Chen Yi, well aware of this, continued, \"Have Yan Hai start gathering the medicinal herbs from Guangyuan ahead of time.\"","\"And here in the Prefecture City, you need to find other herb suppliers as quickly as possible.\"","He paused, a thought occurring to him. \"The Mountain Race has the Wumeng Mountains at their back. They must have plenty of medicinal herbs, wouldn’t you say?\"","Wang Ji nodded. \"As far as I know, most of the major suppliers get their herbs from the Mountain Race.\"","\"It’s just that the Mountain Race has always been wary of outsiders, and they place great importance on loyalty and personal connections. It’ll be very difficult to convince them to sell to us at Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","Chen Yi chuckled inwardly. ’With Pei Guanli in the picture,’ he thought, ’it’s debatable who the real outsider is.’","Despite this thought, he didn’t reveal his hand just yet, merely telling Wang Ji to try other avenues first.","\"Also, get all the silver from the shop’s coffers ready. I have a major use for it shortly.\"","Wang Ji nodded in acknowledgment.","Now that Hundred Herbs Hall was about to limit its tea sales, there wasn’t much point in holding on to all that silver anyway.","Besides, the boss needed the money. How could he, a mere shopkeeper, dare to object?","A short while later, Wang Ji departed.","Those remaining in the room—Liu Lang, Xue Duanyun, and the others—all turned to Chen Yi, awaiting his orders.","Chen Yi didn’t hesitate. \"I have a task for you,\" he said directly.","\"This is of the utmost importance. Until I give the word, no one else can know about it.\"","Liu Lang cracked a grin. \"Boss, just give the order. I guarantee I’ll get it done right.\"","He had previously promised to complete thirty tasks for Chen Yi and hadn’t even finished ten, so of course he wouldn’t refuse.","Xue Duanyun and the other two Celestial Sect disciples, however, were not as quick to accept. Xue Duanyun asked,","\"May we ask what this task is?\"","Chen Yi glanced at them, then had Liu Lang bring out a brush and paper. He wrote a few lines.","When he was finished, he paused for a moment, then tore off two more sheets of paper. He wrote something on each before folding them.","Once everything was prepared, he handed the first sheet of paper to Liu Lang. \"Take them and follow the instructions on this.\"","Liu Lang took the paper and glanced at it, looking slightly stunned. \"Boss, so all that silver you had Shopkeeper Wang prepare... it was for us?\"","There wasn’t much on the paper, just a single instruction: disguise yourselves and buy up as much grain in Shu State as possible.","Chen Yi grunted in affirmation. He held up one of the other two folded notes and instructed,","\"If the granaries stop selling to you, read this one.\"","\"If anyone catches on and tries to stop you, read the other.\"","Liu Lang nodded, smiling as he promised there would be no mistakes this time.","He didn’t ask any questions, as he might have in the past.","After all this time, he had gained a deep appreciation for Chen Yi’s seemingly flawless strategies. He trusted that Chen Yi wasn’t acting without reason.","Xue Duanyun, on the other hand, couldn’t help but ask, \"May I inform my other martial brothers?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"The more people involved, the more prying eyes there will be. It’ll be too easy to get discovered.\"","\"For now, just follow Guard Liu’s orders. He’ll tell you what to do.\"","Xue Duanyun and the other two exchanged glances and asked no further questions.","With the serious business concluded, Chen Yi’s expression relaxed slightly.","\"A lot of Wandering Martial Artists have shown up in the Prefecture City today. Rumor has it Immortal Bai is coming to Shu State, so they’ve come to see the spectacle.\"","He had barely finished speaking when Liu Lang shot to his feet.","\"Who? Boss, who did you just say?\"","Even Xue Duanyun and the other two were stunned.","Such was the power of his reputation.","Their reaction was hardly surprising.","Chen Yi, of course, didn’t mind. He repeated, \"Immortal Bai.\"","Then he added a word of caution. \"We don’t yet know why he’s coming to Shu State, but those Wandering Martial Artists are a motley crew. Be careful when you’re out and about.\"","It took Liu Lang a long moment to snap out of his stupor. Far from being worried, his face was alight with manic fervor.","\"Immortal Bai... the greatest master of Martial Arts in all of Great Wei! The Immortal Bai who has dominated the Jianghu for decades! Hahaha...\"","\"He’s coming to Shu State! This is absolutely incredible news! I...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi held up a hand to stop him. \"You what?\"","\"With your level of Martial Arts Cultivation and Technique, what good would it do you to meet him? You’re not actually thinking of running over and challenging him, are you?\"","While Liu Lang only had a superficial understanding of him, Chen Yi knew Liu Lang through and through.","As the saying goes, a name can be a mistake, but a nickname never is.","Liu Lang embodied the \"madman\" part of his \"Sword Madman\" moniker to a T.","Never mind the things he’d done in the Northern Desert; the fact that he’d dared to challenge Xiao Jinghong, knowing full well he was no match, spoke volumes about the confidence he had in his own Saber Dao.","\"Boss, you know me. An opportunity like this...\"","\"If you want to get yourself killed, I won’t stop you. But you’ll have to win our duel first.\"","Liu Lang froze, realizing Chen Yi was referring to their duel in five days. A bitter look crossed his face.","No matter how much of a madman he was, he knew he was no match for Chen Yi.","Seeing him fall silent in disappointment, Chen Yi snorted. \"Finish the task I gave you first. We can talk about everything else after Immortal Bai actually arrives in Shu State.\"","\"Thank you for your generosity, Boss...\"","After giving a few more instructions, Chen Yi dismissed them.","Zhang Dabao saw them out, then returned and bowed. \"Sir, shall I help you...\"","He made a gesture as if to remove a mask.","Chen Yi shook his head and gazed outside.","The rain had eased, leaving only a light drizzle drifting down.","From the nearby West Market, the constant sounds of hawking and laughter indicated a large crowd.","In an even closer tailor’s shop, several women were chattering away in the local Shu State dialect.","They seemed to be discussing which fabric was best.","Chen Yi watched and listened in silence, running through all his plans in his mind one last time.","Once he was certain nothing had been overlooked, he gave his order, \"Prepare the carriage. We’re going to check on those Xinglin Hall branches.\"","\"Yes...\"","...","「For three consecutive days.」","Aside from teaching at Guiyun Academy, Chen Yi spent the rest of his time out and about under the guise of \"Chen Yu,\" not returning home until nightfall.","His absence became so conspicuous that Xiao Wuge mentioned it to Xiao Wan’er on two separate occasions.","Fortunately, Xiao Wan’er knew he was busy with \"Hundred Herbs Hall matters\" and didn’t give it much thought.","She simply urged Chen Yi to be careful, worrying aloud about the many Wandering Martial Artists who had come to Shu State and the fact that the killer of the Poshisu Country horse bandits still hadn’t been caught.","This, of course, was nothing Chen Yi couldn’t handle.","He dispelled Xiao Wan’er’s worries with just a few sentences.","Then, he went right back to his old ways, appearing all over Shu State Prefecture City as \"Chen Yu.\"","During this time, he naturally learned everything he needed to know.","The first piece of news was that Mr. Yue Ming’s attempt to mediate with Yang Ye had been largely ineffective.","The Lord Academic Administrator was dead set on implementing the new regulations for the Annual Examination.","Fortunately, Yang Ye had given Liu Hong some suggestions, which led Ma Shuhan to give his word that the new rules were not deliberately targeting the scholars of Shu State.","The second piece of news concerned Xinglin Hall.","Or more accurately, Liu Zhaoxue.","She had been making moves nonstop since her return to Shu State.","First, she signed contracts with all the herb suppliers, using a massive sum to corner the market on medicinal herbs and ensure her monopoly.","Then, she invited two Medical Saint Hands from Jing State to hold court at her hall, offering three days of free medical consultations to the people of Shu State.","Instantly, business at all the other major Medicine Halls took a hit.","Her actions even overshadowed the news of Hundred Herbs Hall limiting its tea sales.","The third piece of news came from Liu Lang.","The price of grain in Shu State had recently risen again. With his 150,000 taels of silver, he had only managed to buy 50,000 dan of grain.","Fortunately, the granaries hadn’t noticed anything amiss, and none of them had stopped selling their grain.","As for the final piece of news... it had only just arrived that evening, coming from the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.","\"After learning of Lv Jiunan’s death, King Landu of the Poshisu Country flew into a thunderous rage and slaughtered several merchant caravans along the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.\"","\"There are even rumors that he intends to lead a horde of horse bandits to Shu State to demand justice!\""]},{"number":424,"title":"Chapter 424 - 265: A Practiced Hand","paragraphs":["「In a small courtyard by Quchi.」","Days of overcast rain had washed clean the soil in the cracks of the stone-paved path.","A cool breeze drifted through the fine rain.","Brilliantly blooming hibiscus lined both sides of the small path, their fragrance mingling with the scent of the earth to fill the entire courtyard.","Chen Yi sat quietly in the main hall sipping tea, while Wang Ji sat respectfully to the side, recounting the news from the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.","\"Sir, those horse bandits are truly terrifying.\"","\"Every Wei Dynasty merchant returning from the Western Buddha Country has been killed by him and his men. Not a single one has been spared.\"","\"If the Wan Family Trading Team from Shu State hadn’t sensed something was amiss from a distance and managed to escape with their lives, who knows how many more would have died.\"","Chen Yi hummed in acknowledgment but did not speak, his mind racing.","As the one who had personally arranged for Lv Jiunan to fake his death, he had long expected that King Landu would not remain indifferent to the matter.","Even if King Landu didn’t dare lead the Pirate Alliance’s main army to Shu State, he would still take some predictable actions.","Such as slaughtering passing merchants, or spreading rumors about seeking revenge on \"Liu Wu.\"","Of course, this wasn’t necessarily a bad thing.","At least, not for Chen Yi.","At this thought, he asked impassively, \"What has been the reaction in Shu State Prefecture City?\"","As he asked the question, he already knew the answer. ’Chaos has broken out.’","And indeed, that was the case.","Wang Ji’s next words confirmed it. \"To be honest, Sir, after the news arrived, the price of grain in the East and West Markets shot up from three silver taels per stone to six.\"","\"Even so, some of the Noble Families who heard the news early are still sending people to buy it all up, and the city’s residents are following suit.\"","\"On top of that, the prices of medicinal herbs, silk, tea, and other goods have all gone up as well.\"","He knew Chen Yi had been focusing on the East and West Markets lately, so he reported on that situation first before continuing:","\"The Governor’s Office just issued a proclamation: the entire city is under martial law.\"","\"All leave for the City Guard Army has been canceled. They are now guarding the city walls, the streets, and the nearby post stations.\"","\"The Prefectural Magistrate’s Office has also sprung into action, mostly patrolling the streets. Anyone caught acting suspiciously or spreading rumors is being arrested on the spot.\"","\"The Imprisonment Department, on the other hand, seems to be business as usual. I heard they’ve been busy hunting for ’Liu Wu,’ the one who supposedly killed Lv Jiunan.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. \"What? Do the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office and the Imprisonment Department plan to hand him over to King Landu in exchange for peace on the border?\"","’If that’s the case, then those few Thousand Households from the Imprisonment Department are truly spineless.’","Wang Ji gave a wry smile. \"It’s not out of the question.\"","\"You’ll recall the great war from five years ago. Shu State is still feeling its effects, especially the Dingyuan Army.\"","\"Although the soldiers of the Three Towns are at full roster strength, their quality is mixed. Over half of the New Army’s troops are far lacking in cultivation, strength, and combat experience.\"","Chen Yi knew all this, of course. He was also well aware that before the Dingyuan Army was a force to be reckoned with again, ninety percent of the people in Shu State did not want to rashly start a war.","After thinking for a moment, he asked, \"Any news from the Xiao Family?\"","Wang Ji thought for a moment. \"The Old Marquis hasn’t said anything for now.\"","\"However, I heard that after settling affairs at the Governor’s Office, Governor Liu Hong rushed over to the Xiao Family estate without a moment’s delay.\"","\"Sir, do you think he wants to ask the Old Marquis to come out of retirement?\"","Chen Yi laughed at this and shook his head. \"Quite the opposite.\"","\"If I’m not mistaken, Liu Hong’s purpose in going to the Xiao Family was to persuade the Old Marquis to remain calm and not act rashly.\"","He could even imagine the kinds of things Liu Hong would say.","’Marquis, right now these are just rumors. We still need to ascertain the situation with the Peacock King Banner.’","’Marquis, the soldiers garrisoned at the border are more than enough to handle those horse bandits. Even if they throw their lives away in an attack, there’s no need for the Dingyuan Army to get involved.’","’Your Lordship is unwell. You should wait a while longer.’","’Besides, this is a grave matter. We must send word to the Imperial Court and let the Holy Emperor himself decide. It will not be too late for you to act once the situation is confirmed.’","’And so on and so forth.’","Chen Yi sneered inwardly. He was certain that the moment Liu Hong learned of this, he would send a letter to King Landu, also urging those horse bandits to remain calm and not act rashly.","Based on his understanding of Liu Hong, although the old fox was anxious, he still knew how to prioritize.","Especially since he was also preparing to abuse his authority, using the upcoming Annual Examination as a pretext to both win over and suppress the Noble Families of Shu State.","Wang Ji, who naturally didn’t understand these subtleties, looked a little awkward. \"If you say so, Sir, it must be true.\"","He hadn’t considered that Liu Hong would try to persuade the Old Marquis not to act rashly.","After all, his position was too low for him to be aware of the true intentions of the Imperial Court and the Shu State administration toward the Xiao Family.","To put it bluntly—unless it was a matter of last resort, no one from the Holy Emperor and the Imperial Court of the Great Wei Dynasty, down to the various ministers of Shu State and even some of the Noble Families, wanted the Xiao Family to regain the authority to command troops.","Once the Tiger Talisman was brought out, the Xiao Family would have true command over the three hundred thousand soldiers of the Dingyuan Army.","’At that point, what could those with ulterior motives possibly use to contend with the Xiao Family?’","Chen Yi understood this situation perfectly, but he didn’t explain it to Wang Ji.","He tapped his fingers on the table, thought for a moment, then said, \"There should still be some silver in the coffers from the last few days. Give it all to Guard Liu.\"","\"But...\"","Wang Ji nodded hesitantly and said, \"I’ll go do that shortly.\"","In truth, he said this against his better judgment.","In the past three days, because Hundred Herbs Hall had been limiting its sales of tea drinks, they had earned a total of less than five thousand silver taels.","This hadn’t just affected places like the Qin Building and other taverns; even the supply of tea drinks to the Xiao Family’s several Medicine Halls had been severely impacted.","To be precise, Hundred Herbs Hall was now only supplying one hundred jars of the tea drink to each of the Xiao Family’s Medicine Halls per day.","No more than that.","Chen Yi could naturally see Wang Ji’s reservations, but he still didn’t offer an explanation, simply continuing with his instructions:"]},{"number":425,"title":"Chapter 425 - 265: Merely a Matter of Practice","paragraphs":["\"Also, go find Boss Jia and find a way to get all the silver he has.\"","\"Whether you tell him it’s to compensate for losses or you’re just borrowing it, it doesn’t matter. Just get your hands on that silver and send it all to Liu Lang.\"","Wang Ji nodded in agreement.","He had no choice. All of Hundred Herbs Hall’s silver was gone, so he might as well take Jia Yuzhi’s too.","Once he calmed down, another matter came to mind.","\"It’s just that, milord, I’m afraid we won’t be getting the silver from Yan Sea over in Guangyuan County.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment. His gaze drifted to the hibiscus outside, a rare look of hesitation on his face.","Lately, while investigating the situation across Shu State, his greatest concern had shifted from Liu Hong to the Xiao Family.","Or more precisely, Old Marquis Xiao.","For one, he had appeared in Shu State as \"Chen Yu,\" yet the Xiao Family had shown no reaction, which made him suspicious.","He couldn’t help but worry about what the Old Marquis might be planning.","For another, he was running out of silver.","Aside from the hundred-thousand-plus taels of silver for Liu Lang, the rest was earmarked for Lou Yuxue.","If he used all his funds to buy out the grain from the major Trading Companies, it would certainly impact his subsequent plans.","After a moment of silence, Chen Yi sighed inwardly. ’Given the current situation, I’m afraid I’ll have to take a few more risks.’","Of course, the \"risk\" he was considering had nothing to do with his life; it was purely the possibility of Old Marquis Xiao seeing through his ruse.","This was precisely why he had always intentionally avoided any direct confrontation with the Xiao Family while carrying out his secret operations.","’It seems a confrontation is unavoidable this time.’","\"Tomorrow morning, deliver a visiting card to the Xiao Family on my behalf.\"","Wang Ji paused. \"The Xiao Family? Are you going to visit the young lady?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"Deliver it to Old Marquis Xiao. See when he might be free to meet with me.\"","\"Understood.\"","Given how business was booming at Hundred Herbs Hall, Wang Ji wasn’t worried that Old Marquis Xiao would refuse the request.","A short while later, Wang Ji took his leave.","Without hesitation, Chen Yi summoned Zhang Dabao. \"Are the men you found ready?\"","Zhang Dabao nodded vigorously, a hint of excitement visible on his youthful, inexperienced face.","\"Rest assured, milord. I will put my all into the task you’ve given me.\"","\"Good. Have them make their move tonight.\"","\"Yes, sir!\"","Zhang Dabao affirmed the order. Just as he stepped forward to remove the disguise from Chen Yi’s face, Chen Yi spoke.","\"You may go. I’ll handle it myself this time.\"","\"But... milord, should I at least explain the key techniques to you?\"","Chen Yi shook his head with a smile. \"You’ve applied my disguise so many times. Even without paying close attention, I’ve picked up a thing or two.\"","He paused, then waved him off. \"Business comes first. Have them get into position before nightfall.\"","Hearing this, Zhang Dabao hesitated no longer. He bowed and turned to leave.","Chen Yi watched him disappear beyond the courtyard gate, the smile on his face slowly vanishing.","’By my calculations, Lou Yuxue’s people should be making their move by now.’","’With Zhang Dabao’s people added to the mix, it will be enough to quickly spread the news that King Landu is leading an army to attack Shu State throughout all of Shu State.’","That’s right.","After his discussion with Lou Yuxue, Chen Yi still felt uneasy, so he had arranged for Zhang Dabao to be his backup plan.","His goal was simple: he wanted to make the grain prices in Shu State skyrocket in the shortest time possible.","’Those whom the gods would destroy, they first make mad.’","’The Ji State Trading Company... heh. Ultimately, they’re too small-minded...’","With these thoughts, Chen Yi took out Zhang Dabao’s kit—a rattan-woven box—and pulled out a palm-sized dagger.","He made a few practice motions with it before turning to the Copper Mirror and methodically removing the disguise from his face.","As Chen Yi watched his own features reappear bit by bit, he was left holding a thin mask, and a thought came to him.","’The Disguise Skill truly is a marvelous thing.’","’But this Skill is merely a matter of manual dexterity. It doesn’t involve the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism. No matter how masterful one becomes, it’s only a matter of crafting a more exquisite mask.’","Compared to this Skill, pursuits like Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting, or the Martial Arts, were the true paths to the Great Dao.","Chen Yi wiped his face, packed the rattan box, and left the courtyard under his umbrella.","Zhang Dabao had his own assignments for the next few days, which meant Chen Yi would have to apply his own disguises.","’That’s fine. This way, I won’t have to keep running back and forth.’","...","Meanwhile, Liu Lang, Xue Duanyun, and the others were guarding a two-courtyard residence deep within the West Market.","Unlike a few days ago, when it was sparsely furnished with old furniture, every room in the residence was now piled high with grain.","Each sack held two bushels of grain, and a full thirty thousand of them were piled up here.","If it hadn’t been raining for days on end, Liu Lang would have just stacked them all in the courtyard to save the trouble of moving them around.","Fortunately, aside from the physical labor, they hadn’t run into any trouble over the past few days.","It was a stroke of luck amidst their misfortune.","At that moment, Liu Lang was sitting sprawled in a Grandmaster’s Chair, guarding the entrance to the main hall.","He looked at the inner hall, so packed with grain it was difficult to even get through the doorway, and couldn’t help but mutter:","\"Has the boss calculated that grain prices will keep rising? Is that why he had us hoard all this, to make a huge profit?\"","He had spent the last few days in various disguises, rushing between the East and West Markets, so he was well aware of the daily price of grain.","Before today, it hadn’t been too bad.","The price of grain was only rising by a mace or two of silver each day.","But now, with news from the Ancient Tea-Horse Road spreading, every Trading Company in Shu State had adjusted their prices, citing all sorts of reasons.","Fine grain was six taels a bushel.","Coarse grain was three taels a bushel.","Other staples that could substitute for grain, like sweet potatoes and yams, had also seen price hikes of varying degrees.","This couldn’t help but make Liu Lang question the motives of his boss, a man whose plans were always flawless.","After all, they had spent over a hundred thousand taels of silver to acquire this grain, at an average price of about three taels and two mace per bushel.","If they sold it now, their profit in silver coins would nearly double their investment.","\"Three hundred thousand taels of silver... I have to say, a mind like the boss’s is wasted at Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","Hearing this, Xue Duanyun, Zhang Sanhu, and Zhang Sihu, who were standing nearby, all showed looks of admiration.","Even though their Celestial Sect was famous in the Jianghu, it was a fame built on Martial Arts alone.","When it came to making money, they couldn’t hold a candle to what they’d witnessed over the past three days.","Zhang Sihu counted on his fingers for a while before scratching his head. \"Senior Brother, how much silver did we make?\"","Xue Duanyun shook his head, exasperated. \"Junior Brother Sihu, *we* didn’t earn anything. The boss earned the silver.\"","They were just following orders. They couldn’t let themselves get greedy at the sight of money and give someone the wrong idea for no reason.","Especially not with their leader, Guard \"Liu Qing,\" right in front of them.","Zhang Sihu chuckled sheepishly. Realizing he had misspoken, he didn’t ask any more questions.","Zhang Sanhu, however, chimed in, \"Senior Brother, what do you think the boss is going to do with all this grain?\"","Xue Duanyun hesitated. \"Now that the price of grain in Shu State has risen so much, the next step must be to sell it, right?\"","Liu Lang overheard their conversation, glanced at the three of them, and shook his head with a smile.","\"If you ask me, there’s more to what the boss is doing than meets the eye.\"","\"Oh? Does Guard Liu know the boss’s plan?\"","\"I don’t.\"","Liu Lang explained, \"I may not know the boss’s specific intentions, but I know the kind of man he is.\"","’With the boss’s style of always being three steps ahead, there’s no way this is just about making a bit of silver.’","’Remember when he burned the summer grain in the Three Towns? The boss made six hundred thousand taels of silver then.’","’Even though he gave three hundred thousand taels to the Xiao Family and left a portion with Lou Yuxue at the Spring Rain Building, it just goes to show he doesn’t really care about silver coins.’","’At least he’s not like Black Tooth, who’s only in it for the profit.’","\"Then... the boss...\"","Before Zhang Sanhu could finish, Liu Lang raised a hand. \"Someone’s coming!\"","Xue Duanyun froze, quickly signaling for Zhang Sanhu and Zhang Sihu to spread out and scout the courtyard’s perimeter.","Liu Lang, however, remained in place, concentrating on the sounds from outside.","After confirming that three suspicious individuals about half a mile away were headed for their location, he couldn’t help but mutter to himself.","\"The boss was right. Someone really has come to scout us out...\"","The words had barely left his mouth when Liu Lang pulled two pieces of paper from his robes. He looked at them, and his face went blank.","\"Huh?\"","\"What was it the boss said?\"","\"If there’s trouble with someone scouting, do I use this note, or that one?\"","Damn it, the two pieces of paper look exactly the same, and I put them together. Not even a god could tell which is which now."]},{"number":426,"title":"Chapter 426 - 266: That’s the Dragon Spear","paragraphs":["Liu Lang looked at the two slips of paper in his hand. He hesitated for only two breaths before opening them one after the other.","The two slips of paper read—","[Kill anyone who comes. Quickly move the stored grain to a new location. Absolutely no leaks!]","[Find the warehouses of the several grain stores, especially Lin’s Grain Store! Burn them!]","Liu Lang glanced left and right, a look of realization dawning on his face. ’I get it.’","’If the grain stores won’t sell, we’ll just burn them down.’","’If someone comes to investigate, then we kill them all.’","’It’s that simple, he should have just said so. The boss... how did he guess someone would follow us?’","For the past few days, Liu Lang, Xue Duanyun, and the others had bought grain separately, all in disguise and using different names.","And to ensure they weren’t discovered, they had even intentionally stored it in other locations first.","Only at the end did they consolidate and move the grain to this residence.","’To think we were so careful, yet they still tracked us here.’","’Fortunately, the boss was thorough in his thinking. In that case, we can let loose.’","As Liu Lang muttered to himself, he patted the scabbard at his waist and chuckled.","\"The last time I failed to let you taste blood was my mistake.\"","\"This time... Duanyun, Sanhu, Sihu, the boss said everyone who comes is an enemy. Kill!\"","\"Remember, keep it quiet. Don’t want to alert the neighbors!\"","Over on the other side, Xue Duanyun was taken aback. \"Kill people?\"","As a Guard for Hundred Herbs Hall, it was indeed his duty to ensure their safety here.","But right now, he didn’t know if the people outside were friend or foe. To attack directly seemed somewhat rash.","Zhang Sanhu and Zhang Sihu, however, did not hesitate. They each picked a target and silently slipped out of the residence.","Seeing this, Liu Lang glanced at Xue Duanyun and said with a chuckle, \"Those from prestigious backgrounds sure do have a lot of hang-ups.\"","\"But I can guarantee you, anyone the boss wants dead is definitely not a good person.\"","Before his voice had faded, he too disappeared from the courtyard.","Xue Duanyun hesitated for a moment. He thought about how Eldest Senior Sister Xie Tingyun had been the one to bring them down from the mountain and place them at Hundred Herbs Hall. With that, he hesitated no longer.","When he reached Zhang Sihu, he saw that he was already fighting a man in black clothes and a bamboo hat.","Sizing up the situation with a glance, Xue Duanyun could tell the man’s Cultivation was only at the Sixth Grade. Although his Saber Technique was fierce, it was merely entry-level in the Saber Dao.","Without the enhancement of Sword Intent, he posed little threat to Zhang Sihu.","Zhang Sihu noticed him approach and stopped holding back. \"You damn thief!\"","He was about to add ’since you’re here, don’t even think about leaving,’ but he suddenly recalled Liu Lang telling them to keep it quiet. Instead, he swung his massive Heavy Sword in a horizontal slash.","Seeing this, the man in black’s expression turned grim.","\"Do you have any idea who I am?!\"","\"A dead man!\"","Zhang Sihu’s Heavy Sword was blunt, his movements wide and powerful.","Although the black-clothed Swordman’s Cultivation and Technique were weaker than his, he had the advantage of a nimble Step Technique.","Thus, for a time, the two were evenly matched.","Xue Duanyun had intended to watch from the side and wait.","But when he heard the sounds from the other two fights die down, he knew Liu Lang and Zhang Sanhu had already taken care of their opponents, so he had no choice but to step forward.","\"Sihu, move aside.\"","As he spoke, Xue Duanyun advanced with a sword Step and directly blocked the black-clothed Swordman from behind.","SHING!","The moment his Long Sword left its sheath, a faint glint of light flashed past.","A hint of terror appeared in the black-clothed Swordman’s eyes, but caught off guard, he was completely unable to block.","Before he could turn and block with his Blade, Xue Duanyun’s sword had already pierced his chest.","The black-clothed Swordman’s body froze. He looked down at the sword tip protruding from his chest as blood trickled from the corner of his mouth. \"You... you... ambushed me...\"","Xue Duanyun slowly withdrew his Long Sword. \"I’m paid to solve problems for people. My apologies.\"","\"However, I know my limits. This strike only grazed your heart meridian.\"","\"If you don’t want to die, don’t move.\"","Who would have thought that after he finished speaking, a tragic smile would appear on the young black-clothed Swordman’s face.","\"Hehehe... someone like... someone like me... what meaning is there... in living...\"","Xue Duanyun was stunned for a moment. He watched as the man crumpled to the ground, his body beginning to emit a green smoke.","A foul, pungent stench spread through the air.","Soon, all that was left of the Swordman was a set of black clothes and a bamboo hat.","Zhang Sihu stared at the pool of blood being gradually washed away by the raindrops and couldn’t help but swallow hard.","\"Bone-Dissolving Powder... Senior Brother, what’s this person’s background? To think he’d hide such a potent poison in his teeth.\"","Xue Duanyun shook his head lightly. \"Regardless of his identity, I’m afraid we’ve been drawn into some major trouble.\"","Although he didn’t know why Hundred Herbs Hall wanted these people dead, he could deduce that there was surely a secret behind it all.","Both Hundred Herbs Hall and the person behind this black-clothed Swordman resorted to taking lives at a moment’s notice, which showed just how dangerous the conflict between them was.","Zhang Sihu asked, \"Then... should we tell Eldest Senior Sister about this?\"","Xue Duanyun hesitated slightly. \"Let’s not tell Senior Sister Xie for now.\"","After a brief pause, he continued to explain, \"Before we came, Senior Sister already instructed us to follow all of Hundred Herbs Hall’s orders.\"","\"Plus, she clarified the relationship between Hundred Herbs Hall and the Xiao Family. I think Senior Sister must have known some things in advance to have sent us here.\"","Zhang Sihu nodded, slinging his Heavy Sword onto his back as he agreed, \"Senior Brother is right.\"","\"On Tian Mountain, everyone knows Eldest Senior Sister is chivalrous and righteous. A place she approves of can’t possibly have any problems.\"","They then cleaned up all traces in the surrounding area and returned to the residence where the grain was stored.","Liu Lang and Zhang Sanhu had already returned a step ahead of them.","The four of them gathered, looked at the clothes in each other’s hands, and understood everything without a word.","Liu Lang casually tossed the bloody black clothes and bamboo hat onto the ground and sighed.","\"These people would rather use Bone-Dissolving Powder than live in disgrace. It seems their origins are not so simple.\"","\"But the boss must be aware of their identities, or he wouldn’t have given us a countermeasure in advance.\""]},{"number":427,"title":"Chapter 427 - 266: But That’s the Dragon Spear","paragraphs":["Xue Duanyun’s heart stirred. \"Brother Liu, I wonder if you would allow us to see those notes?\"","Hearing this, Zhang Sanhu and Zhang Sihu also looked at Liu Lang, their curiosity piqued.","After all, they had received their orders alongside Liu Lang and had personally witnessed the handsome young Boss Chen Yu write the two notes.","Naturally, they were incredibly curious about what was written on them.","Seeing the looks on their faces, Liu Lang thought for a moment before complying, taking out both notes and handing them over.","As he did, he added with a smile, \"The boss is a master strategist. When he sets his mind to something, he never comes out on the losing end.\"","Xue Duanyun listened to his praise for Boss Chen Yu while reading the notes in his hand.","The content was brief and simple, but every line exuded the writer’s absolute certainty.","After finishing, he passed the notes to his two junior brothers beside him and said thoughtfully,","\"We naturally believe what you say, Brother Liu. It’s just...\"","\"How exactly did Boss Chen deduce all of this for today?\"","Although he claimed to believe Liu Lang, he was actually half-convinced and half-skeptical.","After all, the contents of the notes were stated with such certainty, as if... as if Boss Chen had orchestrated these events himself.","Liu Lang was taken aback for a moment. He pointed to himself and said, dumbfounded, \"Brother Xue, you give me too much credit.\"","\"If I could deduce things like that, I never would have come to Shu State.\"","’If I had known I’d run into so many freakishly talented powerhouses here, there’s no way I would have come at this time.’","’I would have at least waited until my Saber Dao broke through to the Perfection Realm.’","\"You three... you just haven’t been at Hundred Herbs Hall long enough.\"","\"Once you’ve been here for a while, you’ll understand just how formidable he is.\"","At this, Liu Lang looked at the three of them, then leaned in and continued in a deliberately mysterious, low voice,","\"I’m sure you’ve heard about the murders that happened a few days ago.\"","Xue Duanyun’s interest was piqued. \"Are you referring to what happened here in the West Market? The incident with the Poshisu Country horse bandits?\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"I don’t mind telling you, our boss is actually—the ’Dragon Spear,’ Liu Wu!\"","\"It’s him?!\"","Xue Duanyun was stunned, as were Zhang Sanhu and Zhang Sihu.","The three of them then turned to Liu Lang. \"Then, that... that would make you the ’Sword Madman’ of the Northern Desert, wouldn’t it?\"","Seeing the expressions on their faces, Liu Lang nodded, quite pleased with himself.","\"The one and only.\"","But as soon as he said it, a pang of regret hit him.","’After all, I revealed ’Liu Wu’s’ identity to Xue Duanyun and the others on my own. I haven’t even told ’Chen Yu’ yet!’","But on second thought, he comforted himself.","’The boss probably won’t blame me.’","’Since he had these guys work with me, he must have been prepared for them to find out his identity.’","’Yes, that’s right...’","Of course, Xue Duanyun and the others were oblivious to these internal calculations.","They just stared at Liu Lang in astonishment.","A man’s reputation precedes him.","Forget about \"Dragon Spear\" Liu Wu.","The \"Sword Madman of the Northern Desert,\" Liu Lang, alone was a figure they had to look up to.","And this was the \"Dragon Spear\" they were talking about.","—The legendary figure from the Jianghu whose Spear Dao was said to have reached the Perfection Realm.","It was impossible for them not to be shocked.","After a long moment, Xue Duanyun finally came to his senses. He shook his head with a wry smile. \"So the boss is ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu. We were truly blind to not recognize a great man in our midst.\"","Zhang Sanhu nodded in agreement. \"I really didn’t expect that.\"","\"I always thought that for ’Liu Wu’s’ Spear Dao Realm to be so terrifying, he must be a Jianghu senior who has cultivated for many years. I never imagined he’d be so young.\"","Zhang Sihu scratched his head. \"He looks even younger than me, doesn’t he?\"","Hearing this, Xue Duanyun was filled with a sense of admiration.","It was true he was from the Celestial Sect, but aside from a few Sect elders, Xie Tingyun was the most talented and had the highest cultivation among his peers.","But even Xie Tingyun was a far cry from \"Liu Wu.\"","What did that say about him, a second-rate Wandering Martial Artist whose Sword Dao was only at Minor Success?","\"Junior Brothers, do not be disrespectful.\"","\"Even if Boss Chen is young, his cultivation is not low. He is still our senior.\"","\"Yes, Senior Brother.\"","\"Understood...\"","Seeing this, Liu Lang couldn’t help but add a warning. \"I revealed all this without the boss’s permission.\"","\"I hope you three will keep it a secret for now. We can talk more after I’ve asked the boss.\"","Xue Duanyun nodded. \"You’re too kind, Senior Sword Madman. You don’t need to remind us; we will keep our lips sealed.\"","Zhang Sanhu and Zhang Sihu chimed in with their own promises.","Just as a smile returned to Liu Lang’s face, he heard Xue Duanyun ask,","\"Brother Liu, do my senior sisters know the boss’s identity?\"","\"Your senior sisters... Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang?\"","Liu Lang shook his head. \"They shouldn’t know about this yet.\"","Xue Duanyun was stunned for a moment. \"But our Eldest Senior Sister told us it was the boss’s approval that allowed us to stay at Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","\"How... how could she not know his identity?\"","Hearing this, Liu Lang grimaced as if he had a toothache. This time, he truly regretted speaking.","But if he didn’t explain, it would be even worse if these guys ran off and told Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang.","—He’d probably be run through by Boss Chen’s spear.","After some thought, Liu Lang had no choice but to say, \"The boss is doing this for the Xiao Family.\"","\"The Xiao Family?\"","\"It’s a long story. You just need to know that the Xiao Family is in a difficult situation right now, and the boss doesn’t want to get too involved.\"","\"That’s why he’s hiding his identity and helping the Xiao Family from the shadows.\"","Hearing this, Xue Duanyun, Zhang Sanhu, and Zhang Sihu exchanged a look, as if they’d all realized something.","\"Senior Brother Xue, do you remember what Eldest Senior Sister told us back then?\"","\"She said Senior Sister Shen wrote a letter asking for help, telling her to hurry to Shu State.\"","Xue Duanyun nodded. \"Eldest Senior Sister and the others are also here to help the Xiao Family.\"","Hearing this, Zhang Sihu scratched his head and grinned. \"So, it seems the boss really is a good person. I was just saying...\"","Before he could finish, Zhang Sanhu smacked him.","\"What are you talking about? The boss was willing to kill the Poshisu Country horse bandits. There’s no way he’s part of the Evil Demonic Dao.\"","\"Oh...\"","Seeing that their doubts were dispelled, Liu Lang finally breathed a sigh of relief.","\"Enough talk. This place isn’t safe anymore. Let’s hurry and move the grain to the other residence, just as the boss ordered.\"","\"Alright...\"","...","Xiao Family, Spring Lotus Garden.","Chen Yi had no idea that Liu Lang had already sold out one of his disguises.","But even if he did know, he probably wouldn’t have said anything.","It was just as Liu Lang had thought—since he had allowed the Celestial Sect disciples to get involved, he had never intended to hide his identity as \"Liu Wu.\"","At that moment, Chen Yi finished his two-hour cultivation session.","He glanced out the window.","At some point, the dark clouds in the sky had dispersed.","Amidst the countless stars, a crescent moon hung in the night sky, casting down a silvery glow.","Fallen leaves dotted the courtyard, and from time to time, a drop of water would hit one, making a soft PITTER-PATTER sound.","The sound carried far in the silence.","’By my calculations, it’s about time I heard from Lou Yuxue about the grain she promised.’","Chen Yi muttered to himself, then rose without hesitation and changed into a black robe.","He then retrieved a rattan case from under his bed and began to put on a disguise.","He had to admit, Zhang Dabao’s case was full of treasures.","Besides the little trinkets for disguise, it also contained various tools for practicing lockpicking and pickpocketing.","It was a diverse collection with a little bit of everything.","Chen Yi had fiddled with them before, and he had only one assessment: every trade has its master.","Zhang Dabao’s master, \"One Finger,\" was clearly a man of considerable skill.","In no time, Chen Yi had applied two masks to his face: the inner one was for \"Chen Yu,\" and the outer one was for \"Liu Wu.\"","Once he had carefully eliminated any minute flaws on his face, he packed up the rattan case and slipped out of Spring Lotus Garden.","He followed South Street south, all the way to the depths of Yanhua Lane in South City—the Spring Rain Building.","It was now close to the Hour of the Boar.","Except for places like Yanhua Lane, where one went to seek pleasure, most of the surrounding households had already gone to bed.","From time to time, one could even hear sounds like cats in heat.","Chen Yi had no desire to listen to such noise, but as his cultivation and techniques improved, his five senses were far beyond what they used to be.","Even without connecting to the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, he could hear every movement within a three-li radius.","Nothing to be done about it. After waiting for a moment to confirm there were no unusual movements nearby, Chen Yi zipped onto the roof of the Spring Rain Building and quietly entered a private room.","He looked around, then strained his ears, trying to locate Lou Yuxue.","But before he could find her, the side door was pushed open.","And who should it be but Lou Yuxue?","Their eyes met, both of them a little surprised.","Just as Chen Yi was about to greet her, he saw Lou Yuxue repeatedly giving him meaningful glances, which he found rather strange.","He strained his ears again.","He immediately detected a faint presence outside the private room.","Sure enough, the next moment, the side door opened again.","Standing calmly outside the door was Cui Qingwu, dressed in a simple white gauze dress.","When Chen Yi saw her face, he understood the meaning behind Lou Yuxue’s glances.","His thoughts raced, and he broke into a smile. \"Miss Yuxue, Miss Cui, it’s good to see you’re both well.\"","Cui Qingwu started. \"It’s you!?\""]},{"number":428,"title":"Chapter 428 - 267: Shattering Their Invincibility","paragraphs":["\"So ’Dragon Spear’ really is you, Liu Wu!\"","Cui Qingwu knew \"Liu Wu.\"","She’d know him even if he were burned to ash.","Not long after she first arrived in Shu State, \"Liu Wu\" had knocked her out with a vile poison, causing her to lose all face in front of Chen Yunfan. How could she possibly forget?","Of course, at the time, she didn’t yet know the man was \"Liu Wu.\"","It wasn’t until after the Three Towns’ summer grain was set ablaze and reports on the situation in Shu State trickled into the White Tiger Guard that she finally confirmed her attacker that night was indeed \"Liu Wu.\"","However...","As the name \"Dragon Spear\" resounded throughout the Shu State Jianghu, she grew uncertain again.","’How could a man whose Cultivation and Fist Dao were inferior to hers just two months ago possibly elevate his Spear Dao to the Perfection Realm in such a short time?’","Even when Lou Yuxue had told her this before they came to the Spring Rain Building, she had remained skeptical.","But now, with \"Liu Wu\" standing right before her, Cui Qingwu had no choice but to believe.","With that thought, she took a deep breath. \"Since it’s you, this deal is off!\"","Chen Yi smiled. He wasn’t surprised by Cui Qingwu’s attitude.","Their previous encounter had led to a bit of a misunderstanding.","Both had suffered some damage.","Originally, Chen Yi hadn’t planned on letting her go. Unfortunately for him, she was Chen Yunfan’s betrothed.","His \"sister-in-law,\" in name at least.","With no other choice, he could only act as if their previous encounter had never happened.","’What could he do? He and Chen Yunfan were two peas in a pod.’","\"Miss Cui, you’re worrying needlessly. This deal was struck with Miss Yuxue.\"","\"Lou Yuxue is buying the grain from me! Without me, you won’t get a single kernel!\"","\"Miss Cui...\"","Before Chen Yi could speak, Lou Yuxue, who was beside them, rubbed her brow and said, \"Simurgh Phoenix, you’ll get thirty percent of the profits from this deal.\"","The moment she said it, the displeasure vanished from Cui Qingwu’s face.","She tilted her chin up slightly. \"You should have said so from the start. I accept.\"","Next, she looked at Chen Yi and snorted. \"Don’t think I’m just going to forget how you humiliated me.\"","\"If the Lord Pavilion Master didn’t value you so highly, I would never have forgiven you, not even if Lady Tiger had pleaded until she was blue in the face.\"","Chen Yi gave a wry laugh and shook his head. \"Then I thank Miss Cui for her forgiveness.\"","’The Pavilion Master again.’","’I can’t believe it. The White Tiger Guard’s Pavilion Master has put me in his debt twice without even showing his face.’","’Luckily, I still have my ’Fledgling’ identity.’","’—When you weigh the two, the White Tiger Guard owes me more!’","Seeing that the tension had eased, Lou Yuxue invited them both to sit.","She then caught Chen Yi’s eye and said, \"You needed that batch of grain rather urgently.\"","\"Plus, the grain inside Shu State has already been snapped up by the major trading companies. I had no choice but to ask Miss Cui for help.\"","Chen Yi was inwardly amused.","’He already knew from their last meeting that Lou Yuxue had to buy the grain through Cui Qingwu.’","’Lou Yuxue bringing it up again now was clearly a reminder not to let the cat out of the bag.’","’Looks like these two Silver Banner Officers from the White Tiger Guard really are at odds with each other.’","With that thought, Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"Thank you, Miss Yuxue.\"","He paused, then looked to Cui Qingwu. \"And thank you as well, Miss Cui.\"","Cui Qingwu glanced between the two of them. Suspecting something fishy was going on, she said with feigned annoyance:","\"We’re all in the same boat now. Why the need for all this secrecy?\"","Chen Yi smiled but said nothing.","Lou Yuxue remained unfazed. \"You’re exaggerating, Miss Cui.\"","\"My partnership with Liu Wu is simply to take advantage of the major trading companies’ price manipulation and make a profit.\"","\"I haven’t hidden anything from you.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi inwardly shook his head.","’It would have been better if she hadn’t tried to explain. This would only make things worse.’","Sure enough, a breathtaking smile spread across Cui Qingwu’s slightly haughty face.","\"Lady Tiger, don’t forget... I’m a Silver Banner Officer too.\"","\"If it were just a small matter of making money, would you have sought my help so readily?\"","Lou Yuxue realized her mistake and inwardly cursed her own shortsightedness.","But before she could salvage the situation, Cui Qingwu cut her off.","\"Think carefully before you speak again. If I’m not satisfied with what you say, I won’t take thirty percent of the silver. I’ll take all of it.\"","With the grain as her leverage, she had both Lou Yuxue and Chen Yi right where she wanted them.","They were stuck.","Lou Yuxue had no choice but to look at Chen Yi.","When he gave a slight nod, she sighed and said resignedly, \"This matter involves a mission from the Lord General. I can only tell you the part I discussed with Liu Wu.\"","Cui Qingwu had no objections. \"Do tell,\" she said, her interest piqued. \"I’m dying to know what you two are planning.\"","\"A word of warning first: this is no small matter. You must not breathe a word of this to anyone.\"","\"Alright.\"","Once Cui Qingwu agreed, Lou Yuxue began to selectively recount the information she’d gotten from Chen Yi.","She mentioned the Ji State Trading Company’s various schemes—burning the Three Towns’ summer grain, manipulating grain prices, framing the Xiao Family, and the like.","However, she completely omitted any mention of matters involving Commander-in-Chief Zhu Hao and Lin Huai’an.","After she finished, Cui Qingwu looked at the two of them with an unreadable smile.","\"So, your target is the Ji State Trading Company? This isn’t just about making money, is it?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"Not at all. Dealing with the Ji State Trading Company is also about earning some silver.\"","\"Heh. If it’s all about making money, wouldn’t it be easier to take it from the common folk?\"","\"You’re mistaken again, Miss Cui.\"","\"A gentleman loves wealth, but he acquires it through righteous means.\"","\"It’s easy enough to take money from the people of Shu State, true. But wouldn’t you agree it’s far more interesting to take it from the Ji State Trading Company?\"","Chen Yi paused, then added meaningfully, \"Besides, it’s not like your White Tiger Guard is fond of the Ji State Trading Company either.\"","Cui Qingwu’s gaze flickered. She turned her head and fixed her eyes on Lou Yuxue."]},{"number":429,"title":"Chapter 429 - 267: Shattering Their Golden Body","paragraphs":["\"Aren’t you afraid of being discovered by the Ji State Trading Company?\"","\"I am. That’s why I came to you to buy grain.\"","Lou Yuxue’s reply was terse. Before Cui Qingwu could retort, she waved a hand and said, \"If you have no other questions, let’s move on to the next few matters.\"","Cui Qingwu’s smile froze. She shot Lou Yuxue an annoyed glance but said nothing more.","’Although I have no interest in the White Tiger Guard or the Ji State Trading Company, that doesn’t mean I can’t enjoy the show.’","’Especially with Liu Wu present.’","’I’m curious to see what abilities this man possesses to have earned the Pavilion Master’s high regard.’","But the first thing Lou Yuxue said left her stunned.","\"Liu Wu, things are going more smoothly than anticipated.\"","\"The grain shipment is still on its way, but news from King Landu has already arrived, which works even more in our favor.\"","\"First thing tomorrow morning, my people will start a rumor—that Asutai, son of the Left King, is currently in Shu State.\"","Chen Yi nodded. Just as he was about to speak, Cui Qingwu stared at them and shouted, \"Wait.\"","\"You... The ’Left King’ you mentioned... you mean *the* Left King of the Barbarian Race?\"","Seeing the expression on her face, Lou Yuxue felt a great sense of satisfaction.","’So much for putting on the airs of a young miss from the Cui Family. Look how shocked you are now, huh?’","\"Who else in this world besides Mu Hage bears the title ’Left King’?\"","\"You ask Lord Simurgh Phoenix such an obvious question.\"","Cui Qingwu ignored her taunt. Composing herself, she asked with a peculiar expression,","\"This is a huge matter. How could you dare to keep it from the Lord General?\"","\"And what makes you so sure I didn’t?\"","\"But earlier...\"","Lou Yuxue cut her off. \"I didn’t know then.\"","At that, Cui Qingwu frowned. \"Then why didn’t you say anything just now?\"","\"I’m telling you now, so I’m not keeping it from you...\"","Seeing the two Silver Banner Officers bickering endlessly, Chen Yi didn’t know whether to laugh or cry.","\"Ladies,\" he interjected, \"if you two keep arguing, it’ll be morning.\"","Lou Yuxue acted as if she hadn’t heard him and continued, \"In any case, you understand the stakes. If you want to back out, I won’t stop you.\"","At these words, the displeasure on Cui Qingwu’s face vanished instantly. She rested her hands on her crossed knees, assuming the perfect posture of a well-bred lady.","\"Who said I want to back out?\"","\"I most certainly intend to take part in something this interesting.\"","’No matter how big of an uproar the news of the Left King’s son in Shu State might cause, I only know one thing: he must end up in my hands.’","’No, to be precise, I need to deliver him into Chen Yunfan’s hands.’","’Then, with the credit for capturing the Left King’s son, Chen Yunfan is certain to receive a commendation from the Holy Emperor.’","’A promotion and a title will be well within his grasp.’","Chen Yi, of course, had no idea what Cui Qingwu was thinking. He just found the situation amusing.","’As the saying goes, three women are enough for a drama.’","’It’s a good thing there are only two of them, Cui Qingwu and Lou Yuxue. If there were one more, I’m afraid they’d tear this room apart.’","\"Let’s get back to the plan.\"","\"After the news gets out tomorrow, those grain companies will definitely adjust their prices again. I estimate it will rise to ten taels of silver per shi.\"","Lou Yuxue frowned. \"Ten taels?\"","\"Aren’t they afraid the Government Office will open its granaries and release grain to suppress the price?\"","Cui Qingwu smiled. \"With the Ji State Trading Company’s methods, they’re more than capable of convincing the Government Office to delay its intervention.\"","\"After all, those guys have pulled this stunt more than once at the northern Mutual Markets. They’re old hands at it.\"","Chen Yi chimed in with a smile, \"And if the Government Office does intervene, it won’t hurt us either.\"","He was certain Liu Hong wouldn’t take the initiative to become a thorn in the Ji State Trading Company’s side.","At least, not anytime soon.","Lou Yuxue took a deep breath and gestured for him to continue. \"Go on.\"","Chen Yi gave a slight nod. \"Then, after three to five days, they’ll inevitably start liquidating their stock in large quantities to avoid eating into their profits.\"","\"Which is why I’ve prepared two plans.\"","Originally, he had only one plan, but after Cui Qingwu confirmed she was in, he added a second one on the fly.","\"The first plan is to release a new piece of information every two days. This will make the grain companies postpone their plans to cash in.\"","Lou Yuxue couldn’t help but ask, \"You have more information?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"I don’t.\"","\"But once we release the information about Asutai tomorrow, any subsequent rumor connected to King Landu or the Barbarian Mu Hage will seem plausible.\"","Cui Qingwu couldn’t help but applaud. \"A brilliant move.\"","\"I never thought that on top of your astonishing talent in Martial Arts, you’d also have such a thorough understanding of human nature.\"","\"This move of yours seems simple, but you’ve actually got both the Ji State Trading Company and the people of Shu State eating out of the palm of your hand.\"","\"For one, it makes the Ji State Trading Company unwilling to part with the profits that seem so close at hand.\"","\"And for another, you can use the mouths of the Shu State populace to turn fiction into fact.\"","\"By the time anyone learns the truth, it’ll be too late to turn back.\"","She paused, then shot Lou Yuxue a disdainful look. \"And to think you’re a Silver Banner Officer of the White Tiger Guard. You don’t even understand the concept of fishing in troubled waters.\"","Lou Yuxue, knowing her own reaction had been a bit slow, simply turned her head and ignored her.","Chen Yi, on the other hand, nodded in admiration. \"When the tide turns, anyone standing in its way will be swept away.\"","\"Let alone those insatiably greedy merchants.\"","\"I predict they won’t just refuse to stop; they’ll add fuel to the fire themselves. It wouldn’t be impossible for the price to rise from ten taels of silver per shi to twenty.\"","Here, Chen Yi’s tone shifted.","\"I assume you have no objections to the first plan. In that case, let me tell you about the second.\"","Lou Yuxue pursed her lips. \"Go on.\"","\"This second plan is a bit risky, but the rewards are immense.\"","\"I want to proactively contact those grain companies and purchase a large quantity of grain from them directly.\"","Cui Qingwu’s eyes lit up when she heard this. \"You mean, pulling the rug out from under them?\"","But as soon as she said it, she recanted.","\"No, that’s not it. If we just intercept their deal, at most the Ji State Trading Company would lose face. It wouldn’t damage their foundation.\"","\"Tell me, what are you really planning?\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"I can tell you, but I have one condition, which I hope Miss Cui will accept.\"","Cui Qingwu’s gut told her he was trying to set a trap, but after a moment’s thought, she didn’t believe she’d be the one to fall into it.","She nodded at once. \"Let’s hear it.\"","Chen Yi’s smile widened. \"I want you, Miss Cui, to be the one who purchases the grain.\"","Cui Qingwu was taken aback. She pointed to herself. \"Me?\"","When Chen Yi nodded, her expression immediately soured.","\"Liu Wu, I haven’t even settled our old scores, and you’re already scheming against me.\"","Chen Yi’s expression didn’t change as he looked at her. \"Doesn’t Miss Cui want to personally shatter the Ji State Trading Company’s invincible image?\"","\"I...\"","Just as Cui Qingwu was about to argue further, a thought suddenly surfaced in her mind.","’Shattering the Ji State Trading Company’s invincible image would be beneficial to me, to the Cui Family, and to Chen Yunfan.’","’Even though I know that the true nature of the Ji State Trading Company is a secret only circulated among a few Noble Families and Ministers of the Court... if I pull this off, my prestige in Shu State will soar, which would be a great help to my future plans.’","At this thought, Cui Qingwu cleared her throat. \"Lord Dragon Spear, I accept your condition.\"","Lou Yuxue was stunned for a second, then let out a derisive laugh.","\"Weren’t you so righteously refusing just a moment ago, Miss Cui? What made you change your mind so quickly?\"","Cui Qingwu ignored the jibe, her gaze fixed on Chen Yi, waiting for him to continue.","Seeing this, Chen Yi didn’t keep her in suspense any longer and explained the rest in a low voice.","After listening, Cui Qingwu’s beautiful eyes instantly lit up. \"Excellent!\"","\"I never expected you to be so strategic! If this plan succeeds, I will be sure to give you a magnificent gift!\"","Lou Yuxue, listening from the side, was also amazed. She was truly stunned by the scale of Chen Yi’s plan.","\"It’s one interlocking scheme after another. If I were part of the Ji State Trading Company, this would give me nightmares.\"","Chen Yi just smiled, paying no mind to their praise. He waved his hand and said,","\"In that case, let’s proceed with the second plan.\"","\"Once the news is out, we’ll be counting on Miss Cui to work her magic.\"","A rare look of excitement appeared on Cui Qingwu’s face. Instead of the harsh words she’d used before, she spoke with a touch of arrogance.","\"When my Cui Family makes a move, how could a few mere grain merchants dare to refuse?\"","\"True enough...\"","The three then fleshed out the rest of the plan’s details before going their separate ways.","Whether by forgetfulness or by design,","none of the three mentioned the silver coins for the earlier grain purchase.","Chen Yi: ’I came up with the strategy, I gathered the intelligence, and I’m the one who’ll have to fight when things get dangerous. It would be pretty shameless of them to ask me for money.’","Lou Yuxue: ’She’s taking most of the credit, so what’s wrong with me getting a little silver out of her?’","Cui Qingwu: ’Good thing I left quickly. Otherwise, I’d owe them a favor, and wouldn’t they just take advantage of me then?’","The three of them had their own schemes, yet each got what they wanted.","This was especially true for Chen Yi.","The moment he left the Spring Rain Building, he headed straight for Liu Lang and the others.","He was still carrying nearly three hundred thousand taels of silver, and it needed to be spent.","Just then, a brilliant golden light flared before his eyes—","[Daily Intelligence: Earth-level Lower Grade...]"]},{"number":430,"title":"Chapter 430 - 268: Impressive Prowess","paragraphs":["[Daily Intelligence - Earth-level Lower Grade: At high noon, Gongye Bai will be telling fortunes at the East Market Entrance. Reward: A large amount of Opportunity.]","Chen Yi glanced at it, his calm expression shifting in an instant. Even the Meteor Butterfly Step he was performing faltered.","\"Gongye Bai?\"","\"Immortal Bai?\"","\"Telling fortunes at a stall?\"","\"This is... I never would have expected this...\"","Even though Chen Yi already knew Immortal Bai was coming to Shu State, he hadn’t expected him to parade through the market so brazenly.","It didn’t fit the image of a transcendent master, \"the greatest in Martial Arts.\"","Instead, it was more like... like...","Chen Yi pondered for a moment before two words escaped his lips: \"An immortal.\"","Come to think of it.","Wasn’t Gongye Bai always this unorthodox?","For someone like Immortal Bai, setting up a fortune-telling stall right after arriving in Shu State wasn’t really that out of character.","It was just that.","Immortal Bai’s \"Ironclad Judgment\" was far too \"perilous\"—even more so than his world-shaking Martial Arts Cultivation.","As Chen Yi mulled this over, he started to consider whether or not he should go take a look.","His rational mind told him not to go.","But his eyes kept drifting to the words [Earth-level Lower Grade].","Finally, after seeing [Opportunity: 768], he made his decision. He would go!","He had to go, if only for the sake of that much Opportunity.","’The last Earth Level intelligence, about burning the summer grain in the Three Towns, netted me four hundred Opportunity.’","’And I had to plan for days to get that Opportunity.’","’Immortal Bai’s appearance this time is also Earth Level.’","’Even if I just watch him from afar, I should be able to gain a considerable amount of Opportunity.’","’Perhaps by tomorrow, I’ll have enough Opportunity to raise one of my Daos to the Perfection stage.’","But that was just a thought.","Chen Yi knew that Immortal Bai’s purpose in coming to Shu State was unclear, and it was best to be cautious.","Besides, there was something deeply uncanny about Immortal Bai.","If he got too close and was noticed, or worse, if he was unlucky enough to be on the receiving end of one of his \"judgments,\" the loss would far outweigh the gain.","He had no desire to test his own luck and Opportunity against Immortal Bai’s cursed mouth.","Therefore, his plan for this trip was simple: watch from afar.","With that thought, Chen Yi let out a long breath. After calming himself, he headed straight for the house just outside West Market Heiyu Lane.","By now, it was late at night.","The stars and moon hung high in a silent world.","Not even the crow of a rooster or the bark of a dog could be heard.","The only sign of life came from the government officials on night watch, stationed in key streets and alleys due to the threat of King Landu’s impending border raid.","It was currently the changing of the guard.","The officials finishing the first half of the night stretched their stiff limbs while joking around with those taking over for the second half.","They were mostly talking about the local goings-on.","For instance, which shop had a troublesome customer, who was having a loud argument at home, or who was acting suspiciously.","Although this information was fragmented and mostly useless, they carried out their duty meticulously.","\"I wonder if that news is even true. Logically, that band of horse bandits is a motley crew. They wouldn’t dare invade our Great Wei Dynasty.\"","\"Other horse bandits might not, but King Landu is different.\"","\"His master is the National Preceptor of Poshisu Country, and he’s a nobleman himself. His followers might be called horse bandits, but they’re more like soldiers.\"","\"Plus, they’ve spent years traveling the Ancient Tea-Horse Road, so their skills on horseback are incredible.\"","\"Ordinary foot soldiers and Armored Warriors are no match for them. Only the White Armored Cavalry from our Dingyuan Army can deal with them.\"","\"Unfortunately, after the great battle five years ago, barely one in ten of the veteran White Armored Cavalry survived, and the current generation isn’t ready yet.\"","\"Does that mean no one will be able to stop King Landu when he attacks?\"","\"If he dares to come, General Jinghong will make sure he never goes back!\"","The voices of the government officials carried a long way.","Chen Yi turned to look, a faint smile on his face.","’My lady isn’t even in the Prefecture City, yet so many people are thinking of her.’","’Come to think of it, it’s been half a month since her last letter. I wonder how things are going for her over there.’","Chen Yi muttered to himself, shook his head, and walked straight through the West Market.","But when he reached the house, he found it completely deserted.","Chen Yi scanned his surroundings, his gaze landing on a mound of earth in the courtyard.","Faint wisps of smoke were rising from it.","He walked over, kicked aside a clod of earth, and carefully examined the ashes within, a thoughtful look flashing in his eyes.","According to the instructions he had given Liu Lang.","This was the first location for hiding the grain. If anyone discovered it, the grain was to be moved elsewhere.","Clearly, Liu Lang and the others had followed his orders.","’Three days... and our tracks were still discovered...’","’The people from the Ji State Trading Company certainly have some skill.’","With this thought, Chen Yi pushed the earth back into place to prevent the smoke and dust from attracting unwanted attention.","He then turned and headed for the East Market.","That was the second grain storage location he had instructed Wang Ji to prepare.","Chen Yi headed due east, passing the offices of the Prefect of Shu State, the Governor’s Office, the Inspectorate Office, and other government buildings, until he arrived outside the East Market.","Once he was certain he hadn’t been noticed, he turned into a dark alley and headed south.","Before long.","Chen Yi arrived outside a residence enclosed by high walls and pressed his ear against one to listen.","He could faintly hear voices from within the residence.","\"...Elder Liu Lang, we’re all done.\"","\"Alright. You’ve been working hard all afternoon. Go get some rest. I’ll stand watch tonight.\"","\"Don’t worry, Elder. We’re not tired...\"","A strange expression crossed Chen Yi’s face. ’Elder Liu Lang?’","’Was this guy so careless that he actually let his identity slip?’","Just as he was thinking this, he heard Zhang Sihu say, \"I wonder where Elder Liu Wu is right now.\"","Liu Lang replied in a lazy tone, \"Him? He comes and goes like a ghost. For all we know, he could be watching us from nearby right now...\"","He didn’t finish his sentence. As if realizing something, he quickly spat a few times.","\"Don’t want to jinx it. Why would the boss come all the way out here?\""]},{"number":431,"title":"Chapter 431 - 268: Fine Prowess","paragraphs":["\"You’re right, Elder. We just finished moving everything over. The boss won’t know until tomorrow.\"","\"I hope so...\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi knew instantly that Liu Lang had sold out his identity as well.","’That damned Sword Madman.’","’Always doing these ridiculous things.’","Chen Yi’s eye twitched. ’Just you wait. I’ll beat you to a pulp tomorrow night!’","With that thought, he no longer hesitated and appeared inside the residence in a flash.","\"I’m afraid I have to disappoint you, Brother Liu.\"","Liu Lang froze for a moment. When he realized what was happening, he leaped to his feet and bowed.","\"Boss, my profound respects.\"","\"It’s so late. Why aren’t you resting? What brings you here?\"","\"If you had an order, you only needed to send a messenger. I would have walked through fire and water for you.\"","Speak of the devil...","It was almost enough to make Liu Lang, a man who had seen his share of storms, turn and flee.","The others—Xue Duanyun, Zhang Sanhu, and Zhang Sihu—looked at Chen Yi with some hesitation.","For one simple reason.","Chen Yi still wore the handsome face of \"Liu Wu.\"","But after seeing Liu Lang bow repeatedly, they followed suit with a grand salute.","\"Greetings, Elder.\"","Chen Yi scanned the group. He considered reprimanding them but decided against it, simply waving a hand. \"All of you, rise.\"","But when Liu Lang rose and met his eyes, he obediently lowered his head again.","\"Boss, I didn’t mean to.\"","Chen Yi shot him a look and huffed, \"Just stay here and keep bowing for now. I’ll deal with you later.\"","With that, he strode into the main hall, gesturing for Xue Duanyun and the others to follow and report.","Xue Duanyun glanced at the back of the man walking ahead, then at Liu Lang’s sheepish grin, and it seemed he understood something.","Before Zhang Sanhu or Zhang Sihu could speak, he quickly pulled them into the hall with him.","Leaving Liu Lang alone outside.","’Boss, I’m a renowned Jianghu elder with years of fame to my name, and you...’","’If you’re going to punish me, how can it be this simple?’","But simple was simple, and Liu Lang couldn’t help but breathe a sigh of relief.","At least it proved his earlier assumption was correct—even if the boss found out he had revealed his identity, he wouldn’t do much about it.","A blessing in disguise.","He knew just how formidable Chen Yi could be.","If Chen Yi had kept his anger hidden without letting it out, that would have been truly terrible.","’Alright then, I’ll just keep bowing...’","Chen Yi, for his part, paid no mind to Liu Lang’s thoughts.","Arriving in the main hall, he stood with his hands clasped behind his back, gazing at the sacks piled high all around him.","\"You’ve all worked hard.\"","Xue Duanyun bowed. \"Eld— You are too kind, sir.\"","\"My martial brothers and I are the Guards you hired. It’s only natural that we do our part.\"","Zhang Sanhu added, \"You can rest assured, sir. We know what’s at stake and will absolutely not breathe a word of this.\"","Zhang Sihu, who only half-understood, nodded and grinned.","\"Elder Liu Lang told us a few things earlier. We know that you are the famous ’Dragon Spear,’ who’s recently made a name for himself in Shu State.\"","\"Say no more. From now on, whatever you tell us to do, we’ll do it.\"","\"...\"","Xue Duanyun and Zhang Sanhu exchanged a look, both knowing exactly what the other was feeling.","’Our junior brother Sihu still has no grasp of social graces.’","’Forgive him, Senior Brother. My brother is simple-minded. It’s a miracle he can string a coherent sentence together.’","Chen Yi watched the trio’s subtle exchange and a smile suddenly touched his lips. He waved his hand.","\"Tell me what happened today.\"","’It seems Liu Lang revealing my identity ahead of time wasn’t such a bad thing after all.’","’At least, with their background as disciples of the prestigious Celestial Sect, Xue Duanyun and the others are showing me, their boss, proper respect.’","After a brief conversation, Chen Yi had a rough idea of what had happened during the day. He asked thoughtfully,","\"Do you know who typically has access to Bone-Dissolving Powder?\"","Xue Duanyun thought for a moment before replying respectfully, \"Bone-Dissolving Powder is a potent poison formula from a past dynasty. It’s widely circulated in the Jianghu.\"","\"All sorts of unsavory characters use it to dispose of bodies and erase evidence. Some Death Warriors from the Noble Families also carry it for self-defense.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment and sat back in his chair, not asking any more questions.","’I had previously assumed the intruders were from the Ji State Trading Company.’","’But after hearing the three men’s description, I’ve overturned that conclusion.’","It was obvious. If the Ji State Trading Company had discovered someone buying such large quantities of grain, they wouldn’t have sent only three people.","And it was even more unlikely that no one would have gone to investigate the residence when those three failed to report back for so long.","’Death Warriors from the Noble Families...’","An image of Liu Hong surfaced in Chen Yi’s mind. ’Even if they weren’t his men,’ he thought silently, ’they must be connected to him somehow.’","He knew, after all, that Liu Hong was using Zhu Lingchuan to secretly spy on the Ji State Trading Company.","’Perhaps the people who came to investigate during the day were his.’","Xue Duanyun and the others were, of course, oblivious to his thoughts.","Seeing him silent for a long time, Xue Duanyun asked hesitantly, \"Do you have any further instructions for us, sir?\"","Chen Yi returned to the present. After a moment’s thought, he said, \"I do have a few things for you to do, but...\"","Before he could finish, he turned his head toward Liu Lang outside and called out with a half-joking, half-scolding tone, \"What are you still doing standing out there like a post? Get in here.\"","\"Coming!\"","Liu Lang had been keenly listening to the activity inside. The moment he heard the summons, he appeared before them in a flash.","\"Boss, what are your orders?\"","\"I will spare no effort and shrink from no sacrifice.\"","Chen Yi gave him an exasperated glare. \"I’ll let it slide this time. But if there’s a next time, you’ll see how I deal with you.\"","’Thankfully, there’s still one identity he doesn’t know about.’","’Otherwise, it wouldn’t be long before I’d be hearing Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang calling me ’Elder Liu Wu’ at the Spring Lotus Garden.’","Still, this whole affair served as a wake-up call for Chen Yi. ’Unless it’s absolutely necessary, I’ll have to make sure that fellow Liu Lang works alone from now on.’","’Lest he get me into trouble and sell me out in the process.’","Seeing this, Liu Lang knew Chen Yi wasn’t truly angry. He gave a sheepish chuckle and nodded. \"Rest assured, Boss. There won’t be a next time.\"","Chen Yi shook his head at that and waved his hand dismissively. \"Let’s get down to business.\"","He then took a thick stack of silver notes from his robes and handed it to Liu Lang. \"I don’t care how you do it, but spend all of these by tomorrow.\"","Liu Lang took the notes and counted them, his eyes wide with surprise. \"All of this... to buy grain?\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"Coarse or fine grain, it doesn’t matter. It also doesn’t matter if you buy it from a grain merchant or not.\"","\"I recall there are quite a few farming estates belonging to the great families outside the city. You can go ask if they’re willing to sell.\"","Chen Yi knew full well that the rising grain prices in the Prefecture City mostly affected the common folk.","In the short term, the Noble Families wouldn’t be affected in the slightest.","Take the Xiao Family, for example.","With the people of Tonglin Town to work their lands, the family estate sealed away grain in its storehouses every year. They were in no danger of running out.","The other Noble Families all had their own grain reserves, to one degree or another.","Even if only some of the Noble Families were willing to sell, he was confident they could acquire another large batch of grain.","Liu Lang understood after listening. He put away the silver notes and promised,","\"Rest assured, Boss. If I have to, I’ll steal the grain for you by tomorrow.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment. Seeing the darkness outside the window, he decided not to stay any longer.","As he rose and walked toward the door, he gave his final instructions, \"I’ll have Wang Ji find another place to store the grain you buy tomorrow.\"","\"As for what’s here...\"","Chen Yi paused, his gaze sweeping across the room. \"Seal up the grain here for now.\"","’Once the news about Asutai gets out tomorrow, grain prices are bound to skyrocket.’","’At that point, this grain—purchased at a relatively low price—will become my trump card.’","\"You can make a big show of purchasing the grain tomorrow.\"","\"But remember, you can’t use the name of Hundred Herbs Hall, nor can you use your own.\"","Liu Lang nodded in understanding and watched him leave the residence.","After a moment of silence, he spun around to face Xue Duanyun and his brothers, the fawning expression on his face completely gone.","\"We’ll worry about tomorrow’s business tomorrow. No rest for us tonight, either. Let’s have a few drinks...\"","If nothing else, he had to maintain his status as a Jianghu elder.","...","Chen Yi, of course, paid no mind to Liu Lang’s \"remedial\" actions. After leaving, he quietly returned to the Xiao Family estate.","What he didn’t know, however, was that as he passed the East Market Entrance, a figure was standing silently under the eaves, watching his retreating form.","The man was slender, dressed in a worn Daoist robe. Despite his graying hair, his face was surprisingly young.","At this moment, his eyes, fixed on Chen Yi, held a hint of appraisal.","’This young man... what impressive skills.’","After a pause, he averted his gaze to the night sky, his hands clasped behind his back.","’This Shu State is truly a land of heroes and wonders. It might be worth staying for a few days to have a closer look...’"]},{"number":432,"title":"Chapter 432 - 269: General A Little Cold Plum Is Coming","paragraphs":["Chen Yi, of course, was unaware that someone was spying on him from the shadows.","After all, with his current cultivation and mastery over the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, the slightest disturbance within a five-li radius could hardly escape his notice.","He ambled along.","Returning to Spring Lotus Garden, he shed his black clothes, removed the disguise from his face, and changed into a light robe.","Only then did he let out a long breath.","’The plot against the Ji State Trading Company is mostly complete. If everything goes smoothly, they’ll soon be backed into a corner.’","’At that point, whether they choose to take a desperate risk or simply give up and lie low... it’s hard to say for now.’","Of course.","Chen Yi would rather the Ji State Trading Company act more frantically, more arrogantly.","Only then would he get to see more of the dirty dealings hidden beneath the surface of Shu State.","Besides, if the people from the Ji State Trading Company chose to just swallow this loss, it would affect his subsequent plans.","Fortunately...","Fortunately, Lin Huai’an was dead.","A smile touched Chen Yi’s lips, likely at the thought of the chagrined looks on certain people’s faces when they learned they had been outmaneuvered.","He looked out the window at the night sky, a hint of mockery in his eyes.","The Great Wei Dynasty has held power for over two hundred years. The Noble Families and Clans have formed factions for their own selfish interests, creating a truly tangled web of relationships.","It’s not just in the Imperial Court or the Jianghu; it even reaches down to the common folk in the markets.","There’s a saying that goes, \"Taken from the people, used for the people.\"","But for those Noble Families that have stood for hundreds, even thousands of years, their creed is \"Taken from the people, used for ourselves.\"","Which one of them isn’t sucking the blood of the common people?","Just like that Ji State Trading Company. Behind them, there’s no doubt a group of the rich and powerful.","’Since you’ve come, you should at least leave something behind.’","Chen Yi murmured softly, then rose to close the window before turning back and sitting cross-legged on his bed.","Originally, those dirty dealings had nothing to do with him.","But as the saying goes, the tree may want peace, but the wind will not cease.","With the Xiao Family besieged on all sides, how could he, their son-in-law, possibly stay out of it?","First, there was the \"Fledgling\" identity given to him by the White Tiger Guard. Then came one scheme after another targeting the Xiao Family.","Every single one of them disrupted his peaceful life.","It couldn’t be helped.","’I hope Shu State can find some peace after this.’","’I’ve had my eye on that \"A Little Cold Plum\" for a long time.’","...","「It was now nearly one in the morning.」","But Elder Master Xiao was still awake.","And not just him.","Xiao Shen, Xiao Xuanshuo, and the others were also gathered in the Qingjing Residence.","Each wore a grave expression, all of them looking at the Elder Master at the head of the room.","\"Eldest Brother, weren’t Liu Hong’s words today a bit biased?\"","Xiao Shen, his usual amiability gone, rested his hands on the arms of his chair and grumbled in a displeased tone:","\"As the Governor of Shu State, how can he side with outsiders?\"","The Elder Master seemed not to have heard, his gaze lowered to the Jade Ring on his thumb.","Xiao Shen was about to say more, but he saw Xiao Xuanshuo across from him shake his head, so he could only sit there and fume in silence.","Seeing this, Xiao Xuanshuo glanced at the Elder Master and sighed inwardly.","It was no wonder even a good-natured man like Xiao Shen was angry.","Liu Hong had come to persuade them to \"remain calm,\" which was tantamount to asking them to give up a chance to improve the Xiao Family’s situation.","One had to understand that although the Xiao Family, as Marquis Wu, controlled the Dingyuan Army, they could not mobilize it at will.","The Tiger Talismans of the Great Wei’s Vermilion Bird Guard, the Commander-in-Chief of Shu State, and the Xiao Family all had to be brought together before the army could be deployed.","Unless the Xiao Family was planning a rebellion, not a single soldier from the Three Towns would move.","This was especially true for matters like \"the Poshisu Country’s Peacock King Banner violating the border.\"","Therefore, Liu Hong had come today to persuade the Elder Master to be patient and wait for definitive news from the Ancient Tea-Horse Road before reporting to the Imperial Court.","His reasoning was grand enough—to avoid \"disturbing the Holy Emperor\" over a minor stir.","After a moment of silence.","The Elder Master’s drooping eyelids lifted slightly. He glanced at the sky outside and said in an even tone:","\"It’s late. All of you go back and rest. It seems no news has come from the Capital Commandery today.\"","\"Eldest Brother...\"","Before Xiao Shen could persuade him further, the Elder Master waved his hand. \"Third Brother, I know what you mean.\"","\"But... Liu Hong has a point.\"","\"Right now, we’ve only heard some news from the Wan Family’s merchant caravan. We haven’t yet seen any sign of King Landu and his forces advancing east to violate our border.\"","\"To petition the Holy Emperor and deploy the Dingyuan Army at this time would indeed be premature.\"","The Elder Master’s words were as placid as an old well, yet they were also resolute.","This caused Xiao Shen, who had wanted to say more, to give up completely. He rose and left without another word.","Xiao Xuanshuo and the others exchanged glances, then also bowed in salute.","\"Father, you should also rest early.\"","\"My Lord...\"","In a short while, the Qingjing Residence lived up to its name and fell completely silent.","In truth, what kept him so quiet at this moment were Liu Hong’s last few words before he left.","\"Marquis, the Xiao Family has lain dormant for five years. Anyone with eyes can see it, and they are all wary.\"","\"If you rush to mobilize the Dingyuan Army now, you’ll inevitably give those with ill intentions an opportunity to attack the Xiao Family.\"","\"You can’t be hasty.\"","Although Elder Master Xiao knew Liu Hong’s persuasion stemmed from his own selfish motives, his words had indeed hit home.","He had endured for so many years.","’Why be hasty now?’","Moreover, King Landu’s Peacock King Banner was still lingering on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road, showing no signs of advancing east.","If it was later confirmed that those horse bandits weren’t coming, his petition to the Imperial Court now to request the Tiger Talisman would become a joke.","It would be a classic case of lifting a rock only to drop it on his own foot.","As Elder Master Xiao thought about these things, his cloudy eyes gazed at the moonlight outside the hall, and he let out a long sigh.","’The Capital Commandery probably thinks the same way.’","’Li Fu and Zhu Hao... those two are even more composed than I expected.’","Just then, Xiao Jing appeared in a flash. \"My Lord.\""]},{"number":433,"title":"Chapter 433 - 269: General ’A Little Cold Plum’ is Coming","paragraphs":["Elder Master Xiao’s gaze fell upon him, his expression softening slightly. He leaned back in his chair and asked,","\"Have you found out?\"","Xiao Jing bowed and replied, \"Yes, I have.\"","\"The news did indeed come from the Wan Family. The person’s name is Wan Hui, and he is Wan Hongzhang’s maternal grandson.\"","\"He was leading a group to the Western Buddha Country, traveling along the first half of the Ancient Tea-Horse Road. A guard in his caravan spotted the Peacock King Banner ahead of time, which is how they managed to escape with their lives.\"","Elder Master Xiao frowned slightly. \"And how did they find out that King Landu intends to march east?\"","\"My Lord, I’ve investigated that as well.\"","\"Apparently, while they were fleeing, they rescued a merchant who had narrowly escaped from King Landu’s men. That’s how they learned of the situation over there.\"","\"So, you’re saying there’s a chance this is... false?\"","Xiao Jing nodded. \"That’s correct.\"","After a pause, he continued his report. \"However, one thing can be confirmed.\"","\"Within a thousand li west of the border, there have indeed been sightings of the Peacock King Banner. This has been corroborated by Fenghuo Castle.\"","Elder Master Xiao nodded slightly, his fingers subconsciously tapping on the armrest of his chair. A thoughtful expression appeared on his old, wrinkled face.","\"Fenghuo Castle serves as our outpost. Their intelligence comes from military scouts, so what they say should be reliable.\"","\"Right now, we just need to confirm the movements of the Peacock King Banner to deduce their direction of travel.\"","At this, Elder Master Xiao paused for a moment.","\"If we could also get intelligence on King Landu, that would be even better, of course.\"","Xiao Jing’s expression turned troubled. He hesitated before saying, \"Marquis, please forgive this subordinate, but that is beyond my capabilities.\"","Elder Master Xiao shot him an annoyed glare. \"This old man knows I can’t count on you for that. If you could lead the Hidden Guards deep into Poshisu Country, wouldn’t that make you as capable as that lot from the White Tiger Guard?\"","Xiao Jing gave an awkward laugh. He would never dare compare his Hidden Guards, who could only operate within Shu State, to the White Tiger Guard of the Great Wei Dynasty.","It wasn’t just a matter of strength.","To achieve the same level of infiltration as the White Tiger Guard, the preparation and planning involved were not something that could be accomplished overnight.","Financial resources, connections, channels—not a single one could be lacking.","Take the Xiao Family’s current Hidden Guards, for example.","It had taken the full power of the family two hundred years just to establish coverage over the entirety of Shu State.","Even so, the monthly expenditure of silver was beyond what an ordinary person could imagine.","Fortunately, the Xiao Family wasn’t short on silver at the moment, which allowed him to plant some people deep within several of the great Noble Families.","Such as the Wan Family, the Liu Family, and even the various Government Offices.","After a moment of silence, Xiao Jing thought for a bit and asked, \"Marquis, should we inform the Second Miss about this matter?\"","Upon hearing this, Elder Master Xiao straightened up slightly and mused, \"This is a grave matter. Jinghong should indeed be informed ahead of time.\"","\"However...\"","\"Never mind. Wait two more days. The morning after tomorrow, you will gather all intelligence on the situation in Shu State and pass it to Jinghong.\"","Xiao Jing nodded in agreement.","’That’s good too. In two days, the situation in Shu State will be clearer.’","’Perhaps there will be new intelligence on King Landu and his Peacock King Banner.’","Elder Master Xiao was thinking the same thing.","But while he knew this, he also felt a little resentful.","If King Landu truly did invade the border with his Peacock King Banner, he could mobilize the Dingyuan Army.","Then, the decision of whether or not to defend the frontier against the Peacock King Banner would be his alone to make.","At that point, even if it wouldn’t solve all of the Xiao Family’s problems once and for all, it would make most people think twice before acting against them.","At the very least, within Shu State Prefecture City, those great Noble Families wouldn’t dare to have any more ideas.","After thinking for a long while, Elder Master Xiao pushed himself up with his cane and walked toward the side room.","As he walked, he gave his instructions, \"The Wu Mountain Mutual Market is on the verge of completion. It is of the utmost importance.\"","\"As for everything else... just wait and see how things develop.\"","Xiao Jing bowed. \"Rest assured, Marquis. This subordinate will devote all his efforts to investigating this matter in the coming days.\"","\"Don’t forget about Liu Hong...\"","Hearing Elder Master Xiao’s final words, Xiao Jing stood up and watched his retreating back, a wry smile appearing on his face.","’Liu Hong.’","’He’s the Left Governor of Shu State, after all, and also the Chief Steward of the third branch of the Jing State Liu Family. His men aren’t so easy to bribe.’","’Even after using every trick in the book, I’ve only managed to insert two Hidden Guards so far, and they’re just Household Servants who can’t move freely in the rear residence.’","’How could I possibly investigate Liu Hong’s activities?’","With this thought, Xiao Jing composed himself and slipped away from the Xiao residence.","Regardless, he had to do his best.","...","「The next day, before dawn.」","The side gate of the Xiao Family’s residence was already open.","Third Steward Lu Tong sat just inside the gate, glancing outside.","Seeing two or three carriages already waiting, he straightened his long robe and strolled out the gate.","\"All unauthorized personnel, stand back.\"","\"If you have a calling card, present it now.\"","\"No gifts will be accepted.\"","Clearly, the people waiting here all knew the rules.","After hearing his voice, they disembarked from their carriages one by one and handed their calling cards to Lu Tong.","Among them was Wang Ji.","After handing over a card, he smiled and cupped his fist. \"I’ll have to trouble Steward Lu to deliver this to the Marquis for me.\"","Lu Tong glanced at him and asked, a hint of surprise in his voice, \"Shopkeeper Wang, why so formal today?\"","He recognized Wang Ji, of course, and knew that Wang Ji’s many visits to the Xiao Family were to see the Eldest Miss.","He either came to discuss matters of the Medicine Hall with the Eldest Miss or to deliver their share of the silver.","He rarely presented a calling card.","Wang Ji smiled. \"This time, I’m not here to see the Eldest Miss. I’m delivering a calling card to the Marquis on behalf of my master.\"","He paused, then added, \"My master knows the Marquis is extremely busy, so he did not specify a time for the visit.\"","\"He also specifically instructed me to say that everything depends on the Marquis’s wishes. Whether he will see him or not, and when, we only hope His Lordship will give us an answer.\"","Lu Tong’s eyes lit with understanding. He nodded and asked, \"Your master is the one from Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","\"That’s him. His surname is Chen, and his given name is Yu.\"","\"I remember now. He came to the residence once before to visit the Eldest Miss. I was the one who led him to Jiaxing Garden.\"","Wang Ji, his face wreathed in smiles, chimed in, \"Steward Lu has an excellent memory.\"","Lu Tong grunted in acknowledgment and then asked, \"I heard he left Shu State for a while. When did he return?\"","\"My master has been back for some time but has been tied up with trivial matters.\"","\"See? He sent me with this calling card as soon as he was free.\"","\"Oh...\"","After a few more pleasantries, Wang Ji had his carriage depart, but his eyes remained fixed on the Xiao Family’s residence.","He couldn’t help but feel a little emotional.","’I wonder what the Xiao Family will think of the Master in the future, after all he’s done.’","’But on second thought, these things aren’t for me to worry about.’","Right now, the Xiao Family still didn’t know that Mr. Qingzhou was Chen Yu, the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall.","’Who knows when the Master will let the Xiao Family find out?’","With these thoughts, Wang Ji calmed himself, tapped the side of the carriage, and ordered, \"To East Market Jia’s Medicine Shop.\"","\"After all, we’re going there to collect silver. If we’re late, it will inevitably displease them.\"","Of course, Jia Yuzhi probably wouldn’t be displeased if they were early, either.","Steward Lu watched the carriage depart, then looked down and shuffled through the calling cards in his hand.","He finished looking through them, getting a sense of the day’s visitors. Just as he was about to leave, he heard a frantic set of footsteps from outside the gate.","\"Old Lu, Old Lu...!\"","Seeing that it was the residence’s Chief Steward, Bao Tong, Lu Tong couldn’t help but frown. \"What is it? Why are you in such a panic?\"","Bao Tong didn’t wait to answer, simply grabbing him and pulling him toward the central courtyard.","\"No time to explain! Come on, we need to see the Elder Master!\"","Realizing something major must have happened, Lu Tong obediently followed him.","After the two of them had gone, a hunched-backed old man slowly emerged from the gatehouse and glanced in their direction.","\"What could have happened to make Bao Tong so flustered?\"","After a moment’s thought, he picked up a broom, grabbed a wicker basket, and ambled after them.","「Inside Jiaxing Garden.」","Chen Yi had woken up early and washed up, then brought Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie here to enjoy breakfast.","He didn’t know if it was his imagination, but Xiao Wan’er seemed to be in an exceptionally good mood today.","Not only had she changed into a brightly colored red cloak, but her hair and hair ornaments were also meticulously styled.","Chen Yi couldn’t help but take a second look.","Xiao Wan’er seemed to notice and shot him a playful look of reproach. \"Do you have something to say, Brother-in-law?\"","Chen Yi met her gaze and smiled. \"Are you going out today, Eldest Sister?\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er looked down at her clothes, and upon realizing what he meant, a faint blush crept onto her cheeks. She lowered her head and said,","\"Nothing important today. It’s just that Little Sister Qingwu said yesterday that she would come to the residence for a visit. She said she had something to discuss with me.\"","Chen Yi was slightly taken aback. \"Miss Cui?\"","’That’s strange.’","’I just saw Cui Qingwu last night and specifically told her to go see those grain merchants.’","’How could she possibly have time to come to the Xiao Family’s residence?’"]},{"number":434,"title":"Chapter 434 - 270: Trying to Steal a Chicken, But Losing the Rice","paragraphs":["Xiao Wan’er, of course, had no idea what Chen Yi was thinking. She simply gave a slight nod.","After a moment’s thought, she spoke in a gentle voice.","\"Little Sister Qingwu has probably heard about my plan to establish the Medical Dao Academy. She must be here to learn a few things about it.\"","An expression of understanding dawned on Chen Yi’s face. \"She wants in on it too?\"","Xiao Wan’er hesitated slightly. \"You mean, she wants to partner with me?\"","\"I just thought she was asking about the specific procedures so her family could build one in Qinghe.\"","\"After all, she isn’t likely to stay in Shu State for long. Partnering with me... I don’t think so.\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"It’s just speculation. Who knows what that Miss Cui is really thinking.\"","’Though I’m not a hundred percent certain,’ he thought, ’based on what I’ve learned of Cui Qingwu recently, she won’t be leaving Shu State anytime soon.’","The reason was simple.","The Yunqing Building she opened in the West Market alone didn’t seem like a casual undertaking.","’Of course, it’s also possible this great lady of the Cui Family is so wealthy she doesn’t care about such a ’small-time’ business.’","’Hard to say for sure.’","Xiao Wan’er hummed in acknowledgment, lowering her head to take a spoonful of congee. Her pale cheeks, tinged with a faint blush, puffed out slightly.","After a moment of silence,","Xiao Wan’er looked up at Chen Yi again. \"If she is truly interested, should I turn her down?\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment. \"To consider this, I need to know: would you mind her getting involved with the Medical Dao Academy?\"","\"I... a little,\" she admitted. \"I’m just worried she might...\"","\"Ruin it?\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded, a little embarrassed. \"If the Medical Dao Academy is done well, it will benefit the state and its people, so I want to do the best job I possibly can.\"","\"Besides, I’ve never done anything like this before, but I have you to help me.\"","\"She has no experience with it either, so I’m just afraid...\"","Chen Yi smiled. ’This was indeed what Xiao Wan’er truly thought.’","’Her first thought wasn’t that Cui Qingwu might try to take the Medical Dao Academy for herself, nor was she being possessive of the idea.’","’She was simply worried that Cui Qingwu might unintentionally make mistakes, preventing the Medical Dao Academy from being as perfect as it could be.’","\"If that’s all, then I think you should let Miss Cui join in.\"","Xiao Wan’er froze for a second, her beautiful eyes fixed on him, unblinking.","Her gaze held a trace of confusion.","Chen Yi explained with a smile, \"There are two reasons.\"","\"Miss Cui is from the Qinghe Cui Family. They have money and they have manpower. If the academy runs into difficulties in the future, she’ll naturally have a responsibility to lend a hand.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but pat him lightly on the arm, chiding him.","\"I would never think of that.\"","\"If the academy is truly in trouble, it should be my responsibility to find a solution.\"","\"If I let Little Sister Qingwu join me for that reason, wouldn’t that be taking advantage of her?\"","Chen Yi feigned injury, rubbing the back of his hand with a pained expression. \"You are too kind-hearted, my lady. Of course you wouldn’t think that way. I was the one overthinking things.\"","\"N-no, I...\"","Noticing the gazes from Xiao Wuge, Shen Huatang, and the others, Xiao Wan’er gestured for him to continue.","\"Y-you, just continue... In any case, I had no such intention.\"","Chen Yi chuckled, unable to help himself. He decided it was best not to tease her further and continued.","\"As for the second point, it’s quite simple. By working with you, Miss Cui will be able to see the entire process of the Medical Dao Academy being built from the ground up.\"","\"If she’s able to open another Medical Dao Academy somewhere else in the future, that would align with your wishes, wouldn’t it?\"","’Of course, there was a more crucial point—Cui Qingwu being on good terms with Xiao Wan’er would, to a certain extent, represent an alliance between the Cui Family and the Xiao Family.’","’After all, Cui Qingwu’s Qinghe Cui Family was in no way weaker than the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family, the Jing State Liu Family, or the Shu State Xiao Family.’","’In fact, with the head of their family, Cui Mao, ranked among the Nine Ministers, they could make most outsiders who were unaware of the full picture hesitate to act against them.’","’The reason Chen Yi didn’t mention this was likely because he worried Xiao Wan’er would find it too ’utilitarian’.’","’So, he had to at least ensure the Medical Dao Academy remained pure on the surface.’","When Xiao Wan’er heard his explanation, a smile graced her face. The second point had clearly resonated with her.","\"If Little Sister Qingwu is interested, I certainly won’t refuse.\"","She paused, then added, \"But I should still ask her clearly to be sure.\"","\"This isn’t a venture for earning silver, after all. If Little Sister Qingwu is merely curious, I won’t pressure her.\"","Chen Yi grunted in agreement and said no more.","’Still, he was fairly certain Cui Qingwu had already set her sights on the Medical Dao Academy.’","’Otherwise, with her ’great lady’ airs, she wouldn’t have even bothered to ask a single question if she weren’t interested.’","’At most, she would have offered a few words of perfunctory praise after hearing Xiao Wan’er’s idea, and left it at that.’","Seeing him agree, Xiao Wan’er’s smile widened. She ate a few pastries, then took a letter from Cui’er at her side and placed it on the table.","\"There’s more good news. We received a reply today to one of the letters we sent to the Medical Saint Hands.\"","Chen Yi put down his bowl and chopsticks, raising an eyebrow. \"Which one?\"","\"A Medical Saint Hand from Guangyue Prefecture, an heir to the Fuyang Sect, by the name of Lv Chunle.\"","\"He wrote back saying he will bring his people to Shu State shortly to diagnose Grandfather’s illness.\"","As Xiao Wan’er spoke, she couldn’t help but feel a new wave of worry.","\"Do you think a Medical Saint Hand like him would be willing to serve as the dean of the academy?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"It’s hard to say.\"","\"As long as he has a physician’s integrity, he should be interested. At the very least, he’ll leave something of value behind.\"","’He had, of course, heard of the Fuyang Sect.’","’It was a major school of thought within the Medical Dao. They believed that ’all illnesses under the heavens are caused by damage to one’s yang energy,’ and that ’primordial energy and true yang are the very foundation of life.’’","’Therefore, physicians from this sect primarily focused their diagnoses and prescriptions on warming a patient’s yang energy. They were skilled in using pungent and hot-natured herbs and relied heavily on classical formulas.’","\"But don’t worry too much, my lady. After they arrive in Shu State and have a look at the Old Master, we can still think of other methods.\"","\"If one path doesn’t work out, another one will. We’re bound to gain something.\"","\"Mmm...\"","Not long after, they finished their breakfast."]},{"number":435,"title":"Chapter 435 - 270: Trying to Steal a Chicken, Only to Lose the Rice","paragraphs":["Shen Huatang cleared the table with Xiaodie, Cui’er, and the others.","Chen Yi, meanwhile, sat in the living room chatting with Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Wuge.","Today, Xiao Xuanshuo was busy, giving Xiao Wuge a rare day off, so he didn’t go to the Martial Arts Arena.","However, Xiao Wuge had gotten up before dawn to practice his Pile Skill in the courtyard.","He could certainly be called diligent.","So now, Xiao Wuge was recounting in great detail everything he did at the Martial Arts Arena.","It wasn’t exactly boasting, but there were definitely things worthy of praise.","At least, Xiao Wan’er looked gratified after hearing his story.","\"Wuge, Second Uncle is teaching you so diligently. You must not let him down in the future.\"","\"Don’t worry, Big Sister. I’ll definitely work hard.\"","Xiao Wuge puffed out his chest and promised, then turned to look at Chen Yi.","\"Brother-in-law, when is Sister Guanli coming back? She promised to teach me her Step Technique. She hasn’t forgotten, has she?\"","Chen Yi smiled and shook his head. \"Her? She’s probably been held up by something.\"","\"But don’t worry. I’ll go ask her about it later. I’ll make sure she teaches you her best moves.\"","\"That’s good...\"","Just as he spoke, Xiaodie hurried back, a panicked look on her face.","\"Young Miss, Young Master-in-law, Young Master, something’s happened outside...\"","Xiao Wan’er froze, raising a hand to signal for her to slow down.","Without catching her breath, Xiaodie quickly said, \"Just now, word came from the central courtyard... they said... they said...\"","\"Said what?\"","\"They said the Barbarian Race might be massing troops at Mengshui Pass!\"","Upon hearing this, Xiao Wan’er’s expression changed. Her eyes couldn’t hide the confusion, sorrow, and unease that surfaced.","\"How could that be... Xiaodie, who did you hear this from?\"","\"Young Miss, a few Armored Warriors said it. They also said... they also said the Old Master has already given the order to place our mansion under lockdown.\"","After hearing Xiaodie’s words, Xiao Wan’er’s face paled, causing that trace of gentle, sunny warmth about her to dim.","Seeing this, Chen Yi naturally knew the reason. He asked in a calm, gentle voice:","\"Xiaodie, was it an urgent report from Mengshui Pass?\"","Xiaodie shook her head. \"No, it wasn’t.\"","\"They said it’s the son of some Barbarian Left King. He’s in Shu State right now, and he’s even been branded as a slave.\"","\"So, many people in the mansion are guessing that the Barbarian Race might launch a full-scale invasion to get revenge for that ’Crown Prince’.\"","\"Crown Prince?\"","’Since when did a lowly barbarian slave who herded cattle and sheep on the fringes of the Black Bear Tribe become a Crown Prince?’ Chen Yi chuckled to himself.","At this thought, he let out a laugh, drawing the gazes of the others.","\"If that’s the case, I believe this matter requires further investigation.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s beautiful eyes were fixed on him, her hands clasped at her chest, her expression unable to hide her worry.","She truly did not want to see war break out in Shu State again, especially a large-scale barbarian invasion from the north.","Never mind the long history of Xiao Family members who had died on the barbarian battlefields.","In the last great war alone, she had personally witnessed the deaths of many relatives.","Her father, her mother, her Fourth Grand-uncle Xiao Zhan, her Third Uncle Xiao Rui, and many, many other elders from the branch families.","Most of them had died in battle.","\"Is that so?\"","\"Mm, as far as I know, the Barbarian Race is currently embroiled in internal strife over the position of Barbarian King.\"","\"The several heirs are each fighting for themselves, and all have numerous supporters. Even the Barbarian Left King, Mu Hage, is not exempt.\"","Chen Yi gently patted Xiao Wan’er’s hand and said comfortingly, \"Sister Wan’er, please try not to worry. Believe me, we haven’t reached the worst-case scenario yet.\"","Meeting his gaze, the anxiety that had just gripped Xiao Wan’er’s heart was soothed by a wave of warmth.","She nodded gently, slowly pulling herself away from the scars of her past memories. \"You’re right.\"","Composing herself, she looked at Xiao Wuge, Xiaodie, and the others, forcing a smile.","To reassure herself, and to reassure them.","\"We haven’t reached the worst point yet. We should wait until Grandfather and the others have investigated clearly.\"","Xiao Wuge, for his part, showed no signs of fear.","He even seemed eager for a fight. \"If they dare to invade again, Second Sister will surely beat them so badly that not a single piece of armor remains!\"","Xiao Wan’er smacked him lightly and chided, \"Don’t talk such nonsense.\"","\"On the battlefield, blades have no eyes. Even someone as powerful as a Grandmaster faces the risk of falling, let alone your Second Sister.\"","Xiao Wuge clutched his head and muttered an \"oh,\" then sullenly fell silent.","They chatted idly for a few more moments.","Seeing that they had calmed down a bit, Chen Yi stood up to leave.","Hearing that he was leaving the mansion, Xiao Wan’er instinctively followed him. \"You... you should still take some Guards with you.\"","\"Even if the horse bandits from the Barbarian Race and Poshisu Country don’t attack, I’m afraid the city isn’t safe either.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"Don’t worry. Even if they do invade, nothing will happen here in the Prefecture City.\"","\"Take some Armored Warriors with you. Only then will I... I be at ease.\"","\"Alright, I’ll listen to you.\"","As Chen Yi spoke and was about to leave Jiaxing Garden, he saw two figures approaching the gate.","It was none other than Cui Qingwu, whom he had just met last night, and her Maid, Huan’er.","’What a coincidence,’ Chen Yi thought. He then said smoothly, \"Sister Wan’er, Miss Cui is here.\"","He didn’t forget to add, \"This is a good chance for you to ask her for news from outside.\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in agreement, reminding him to be careful, then stepped forward to greet them.","\"Little Sister Qingwu, please don’t be offended. I was just held up by something and couldn’t greet you at the main gate.\"","Cui Qingwu quickened her pace and said with a smile, \"Sister Wan’er, what are you saying? I wouldn’t dare have you come out to greet me.\"","After speaking, she noticed Chen Yi looked like he was about to head out, so she greeted him and asked,","\"Is Mr. Qingzhou heading out?\"","Chen Yi nodded, calmly said, \"I’ll let you two talk,\" and walked away.","’This woman... instead of handling her proper business, she comes running here. She’s really...’","’Forget it. It was my suggestion, anyway.’","’There’s not much I can say about it now.’","’Besides, even without Cui Qingwu, I have other plans in place. It doesn’t really affect the outcome.’","Meanwhile, Cui Qingwu watched his expression and felt a flicker of displeasure herself.","’She was, by all rights, Chen Yi’s nominal sister-in-law. Why did he still have that \"can’t be bothered with you\" look on his face?’","With that in mind, her eyes darted, and she said, \"Sister Wan’er, isn’t it a bit inappropriate for Mr. Qingzhou to be going out at a time like this?\"","Xiao Wan’er was taken aback. \"What’s wrong?\"","\"It’s almost chaos outside right now.\"","\"Because of the Left King’s son?\"","\"Oh, Sister Wan’er already knows. Yes, that’s it.\"","\"I also heard that the Barbarian Left King, Mu Hage, has learned that his son is in Shu State and is already amassing his forces.\"","\"Really?\"","\"I...\"","Chen Yi, who hadn’t gone far, couldn’t stand to listen anymore. He turned back and interrupted them.","\"Miss Cui, I was wondering, where might my elder brother be at present?\"","Cui Qingwu paused, looking at him with a half-smile. \"Mr. Qingzhou still acknowledges Brother Yunfan as his elder brother? How could you not know his whereabouts?\"","Chen Yi knew she was trying to stir up trouble for him. He calmly clasped his hands in a salute and said,","\"If my brother is willing to acknowledge me, I am naturally grateful.\"","\"It’s just that he is, after all, an Advisor to the Governor’s Office. I wouldn’t want to disturb him. I hope Miss Cui can inform me.\"","’Now that’s more like it,’ Cui Qingwu thought. She looked up at the sky and said, \"Brother Yunfan will be going to the East Market at noon.\"","Chen Yi faltered. ’The East Market?’","\"Is he going there... on official business?\"","\"Mm. I heard Lord Yang asked him to go keep an eye on those grain stores. I’m sure Mr. Qingzhou has heard that the price of grain in the Prefecture City is too high right now.\"","After hearing Cui Qingwu’s words, Chen Yi’s heart gave a strange leap.","But he looked up at the sky, saw that it was still a while before noon, and breathed a sigh of relief.","’It makes no sense.’","’It can’t be such a coincidence.’","’Even if Immortal Bai is going to read someone’s fortune, it shouldn’t be Chen Yunfan, of all people.’","Thinking this, Chen Yi bid farewell to the group and left Jiaxing Garden directly.","Cui Qingwu watched his retreating figure, feeling that his actions just now were a bit baffling.","But after hearing what Xiao Wan’er said next, she understood.","\"Little Sister Qingwu, quickly, tell me more. What other news is spreading outside? Are the barbarians really coming?\"","\"Oh, Sister Wan’er, I was just making things up...\"","Cui Qingwu wasn’t stupid. The moment she realized what was happening, she understood Chen Yi’s intention.","She certainly couldn’t keep making Xiao Wan’er worry.","But as she thought about this, Cui Qingwu couldn’t help but have some strange thoughts about Chen Yi.","’After coming to Shu State, how did this Chen Yi become so frivolous?’","’Isn’t it enough for him to be the husband of the Xiao Family’s second daughter? Does he want Xiao Wan’er as well?’","’Isn’t he afraid of trying to steal the chicken, only to lose the rice?’","...","Chen Yi, of course, had no idea what Cui Qingwu was thinking.","After arriving at the front courtyard, he followed Xiao Wan’er’s instructions and found Liu Si’er to drive him to Jishi Medicine Hall.","Originally, he had planned to go to Hundred Herbs Hall first.","But hearing that Chen Yunfan would be at the East Market at noon made him feel a little uneasy.","After all, that Immortal Bai had quite a reputation.","’What if he were to tell Chen Yunfan something like \"Your official career will be smooth sailing,\" or \"You are destined for wealth and honor\"? Who knows what the consequences would be?’","Not long after.","Liu Si’er brought the horse-drawn carriage, and they departed from the Marquis’s Mansion with Chen Yi inside.","\"Huh?\"","\"Why is he here again?\"","Hearing Liu Si’er’s mutter, Chen Yi lifted the curtain to look and also raised an eyebrow slightly.","’Liu Hong?’"]},{"number":436,"title":"Chapter 436 - 271: Young Master, Care for a Divination?","paragraphs":["The visitor was Liu Hong, Liu Gongmo, the Left Governor of the Shu State Governor’s Office.","As Chen Yi lifted the carriage curtain, he happened to see the man stepping down from his own carriage.","Beside him was a man in the long robes of a Scholar—it was Zhao Liuan.","What a coincidence.","As Liu Hong turned, his gaze met Chen Yi’s. The serious expression on his face instantly gave way to a smile.","The two then exchanged greetings.","One gave a gentle nod, while the other clasped his hands in a brief, apologetic gesture.","Their carriages then passed each other.","Liu Hong watched the carriage turn onto South Street before looking away. He then dispatched an older, middle-aged man to present his calling card.","He, meanwhile, adjusted his sleeves pensively. \"Chen Qingzhou...\"","Hearing his voice, Zhao Liuan looked belatedly toward South Street and said in a low voice,","\"Sir, was that Chen Yi in the carriage just now?\"","Liu Hong nodded slightly. \"It was.\"","\"Strange. Why would he choose to leave the Marquis’s Mansion at a time like this?\"","Upon hearing this, Zhao Liuan raised his head slightly, glanced at his superior, and answered cautiously,","\"Perhaps he’s off to teach the Calligraphy Dao at Guiyun Academy?\"","It was meant as a perfectly ordinary suggestion, but to his surprise, Liu Hong simply shook his head. \"Not today.\"","Zhao Liuan froze for a moment, nearly blurting out, ’How do you know for sure?’","Once he caught himself, he chose his words carefully. \"I was not aware.\"","Liu Hong hummed in acknowledgment and turned to look at the gates of the Xiao Mansion, instructing in a low voice,","\"From now on, I want you to pay closer attention to this Chen Qingzhou.\"","Zhao Liuan was about to ask why when Liu Hong continued,","\"The Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family has been greatly favored by the Holy Emperor in recent years. If the brothers Chen Xuanji and Chen Xuandu were without considerable skill, how could they possibly have remained unshaken in the Imperial Court?\"","\"And do you really believe two men like that would allow their own descendant to marry into the Xiao Family, let alone for such a pathetic reason as being pushed out by the first wife of the Liu Family?\"","It dawned on Zhao Liuan. \"Sir, are you saying that... Mr. Qingzhou came here because...\"","He pointed toward the northeast. \"He was sent by... them?\"","Liu Hong gave a noncommittal nod. \"Chen Qingzhou’s recent actions would seem to confirm it.\"","\"However...\"","He saw the head steward of the Marquis’s Mansion appear at the gate, paused for a moment, and then quickly finished his thought.","\"It’s just... his behavior feels somewhat contrived. It doesn’t align with the interests of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family at all.\"","For the great Noble Families, \"interest\" came first, followed by the growth and prosperity of the family, and finally, the continuation of their lineage.","Marriage alliances, political factions, scholarly achievements, commerce, and even farming—all served these ends.","So, in Liu Hong’s view, once Chen Yi joined the Xiao Family, he should have been single-mindedly focused on climbing the social ladder.","But the reality was that after more than half a year, he remained a peripheral figure in the Xiao Family.","This was true even though he was an Instructor at Guiyun Academy.","He avoided official circles and military service, living like a carefree hermit, unconcerned with worldly matters.","How could such a person not make Liu Hong suspicious?","After listening, Zhao Liuan quietly assented and followed Liu Hong into the Xiao Mansion.","He silently filed away the matter of Chen Yi and focused his mind on the upcoming visit with Old Marquis Xiao.","’Yesterday’s incident with the horse bandits from Poshisu Country was one thing...’","’...but now with this business involving Asutai, I’m afraid even Sir will have a hard time convincing the Old Marquis to do nothing.’","...","Meanwhile.","Liu Si’er drove the carriage, chattering away as he went.","\"That Governor Liu came by yesterday, and now he’s back again today. He must be terrified the Marquis will petition the Imperial Court to release the Tiger Talisman.\"","\"Mr. Qingzhou, don’t you think he’s overstepping his bounds?\"","Chen Yi gave a noncommittal hum, his eyes fixed on the pedestrians outside the window, offering no real response.","’Who in the entire Xiao Mansion didn’t know what Liu Hong was after?’","’There was no need for him to add anything.’","There was one thing, however, that concerned him.","Would the Old Marquis use this as a legitimate reason to mobilize the Dingyuan Army?","’Probably... not likely.’","Chen Yi sighed inwardly.","The Old Marquis was, after all, a man who cherished his reputation, too constrained by rules and conventions. Unless his hand was forced, he would find it very difficult to strike first.","It was just like the time he’d gone to Liu Hong to discuss the matter of Liu Wen.","Seeing he wasn’t going to get a response, Liu Si’er muttered inwardly that this \"Fledgling\" was getting harder and harder to figure out.","There was a time.","Back then, looking at the \"Fledgling\" was like looking at a naked child; he could see right through him.","But now, when he looked at the \"Fledgling,\" he felt as if a layer of rice paper separated them, obscuring his view.","It had only been two or three months, and the \"Fledgling\" clearly had no Cultivation whatsoever.","After much thought.","Liu Si’er could only attribute it to the growth in the \"Fledgling’s\" character that came after achieving Perfection in the Calligraphy Dao.","After all, the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism was full of inexplicable Profound Mysteries, so it was only natural he couldn’t fully comprehend it.","As Liu Si’er mulled this over, he glanced at the pedestrians on either side and, just to make conversation, said, \"Young Master, do the streets seem more crowded than usual today?\"","Chen Yi replied offhandedly, \"They’re probably rushing to buy grain.\"","Even without actively listening, he could tell the surrounding pedestrians were all talking about Poshisu Country and the son of the Barbarian Left King.","He heard surprise, agitation, and fear in their voices.","Most, however, were preparing for a rainy day.","For the common folk, the coming of war meant their first thought was to ensure their own survival and stability.","Notions like \"dying on the battlefield\" or \"a warrior’s burial\" were for scholars and those who practiced Martial Arts.","Their primary concerns were always food, clothing, medicine, and other necessities of life.","\"Damn those profiteers!\"","\"A single stone of fine grain is selling for as much as ten taels! They’re... they’re committing highway robbery!\"","\"Come on, let’s report them to the Government Office!\"","\"If those scoundrels won’t let us live, we can’t let them get away with this lawlessness!\""]},{"number":437,"title":"Chapter 437 - 271: Young Master, Care for a Divination?","paragraphs":["As the carriage neared the East Market, Chen Yi could faintly hear a clamor coming from that direction.","Amidst the noise, some people were trying to mediate or plead, lamenting how helpless the situation in Shu State had become.","Many others ignored these voices, busy haggling with the grain merchants and calculating how much grain their silver coins could buy.","Amidst the tumult, Chen Yi saw a surging crowd of people outside the East Market Entrance, even from a great distance.","They were practically packed shoulder to shoulder.","Even the carriage driven by Liu Si’er struggled to push through, much to his embarrassment.","\"Carriage of the Xiao Mansion! Make way!\"","\"Don’t block the road!\"","Having been blocked several times, an embarrassed Liu Si’er raised his whip, about to strike the horse’s rump.","Chen Yi spoke up just in time to stop him. \"Stop the carriage, Brother Si.\"","Liu Si’er paused, hesitating. \"Young Master, we’re still a short distance from Jishi Medicine Hall. You... you could wait a little longer?\"","\"Besides, there are too many people here. What if there’s danger...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi had already lifted the curtain and stepped down from the carriage beside him, saying with a smile, \"It’s fine.\"","He glanced at a few people nearby, saw the fearful looks on their faces, and then waved his hand.","\"You can head back first. I’ll return to the mansion on my own later.\"","Liu Si’er was taken aback for a moment, but seeing his firm expression, he could only say:","\"Young Master, please be careful. If anything happens to you, the mansion will surely not spare me.\"","Chen Yi nodded, gave a gentle gesture to the startled people, and then squeezed into the crowd.","The short distance of one li took him a full quarter of an hour to cover, with all the stopping and starting, before he finally reached Jishi Medicine Hall.","By now, the entrance to the Medicine Hall was also packed with people.","However, most of them weren’t sick. They were just people who had come to buy medicinal herbs to stock up at home.","Many more were there for the medicinal teas.","Even with the entire staff of Jishi Medicine Hall out front, it was still difficult to maintain order at the entrance.","It made the accountant, Liu Quan, so agitated that he stood at the door shouting, \"Everyone, everyone! This Medicine Hall is running out of herbs! Please, go to other shops!\"","\"The Wan Family Medicine Shop, the Fang Family Medicine Hall...\"","Even so, the crowd continued to surge.","Watching the scene before him, Chen Yi couldn’t help but feel a strange sense of unease.","Although he had anticipated before setting these events in motion that his plan would affect the people of Shu State, he hadn’t truly expected the impact to be this great.","Or rather, he had underestimated the influence that the Barbarian Left King, Mu Hage, had on the people within Shu State.","After all, when the news about King Landu of Poshisu Country spread yesterday, it hadn’t caused this level of panic.","But on second thought, it made sense.","Even Xiao Wan’er had lost her composure the moment she heard Mu Hage’s name, so it was only natural for these ordinary people to react this way.","Thinking of this, Chen Yi sighed.","’I did not kill Boren, yet Boren died because of me.’","This time, he would inevitably have to let the people of Shu State suffer for a while.","To achieve his goal and solve this problem once and for all, he had to harden his heart.","’Better to suffer a sharp, short pain than a long, dull one. I’ll find a way to compensate these people later.’","As he thought this, Chen Yi scanned the area, his gaze falling on a place a little farther from the East Market Entrance.","To be precise, it was a medicine hall there—Xinglin Hall.","It was identical to the Xinglin Hall on South Street; the plaque above its entrance was also written with the Minor Achievement Calligraphy Dao.","Amidst shimmering wisps of brilliance, the two large words \"Xinglin Hall\" were clearly visible, illuminating the crowd constantly entering and leaving below.","Vaguely, Chen Yi could make out a familiar figure in the inner hall—Liu Zhaoxue.","Behind her were several busy servants.","One of them, a petite and pretty Maid, made him look twice.","’Ling’er of the Five Poison Sect? Liu Zhaoxue?’","’I didn’t expect them to be here today...’","Chen Yi subconsciously used his Qi Observation Skill and scanned the area again.","The auras of those few people were displayed before his eyes.","’Martial Arts Upper Fifth Grade, Middle Fifth Grade, Middle Sixth Grade, Fourth Grade, Fourth Grade... Upper Stage?’","Chen Yi’s gaze landed on a middle-aged Swordman dressed as a Guard at the entrance of Xinglin Hall.","An Upper Fourth Grade Cultivation, two minor realms higher than even Yan Fusha’s.","’Is he an Elder of the Five Poison Sect? Or one of those so-called Altar Masters I heard about before?’","Chen Yi had no way of knowing, and now was not the time for him to investigate such things.","After a quick scan, he pushed through the noisy, congested crowd and entered Jishi Medicine Hall.","Liu Quan was about to start cursing when he suddenly caught sight of Chen Yi and quickly swallowed his words.","\"Shopkeeper, you’re finally here!\"","\"Please, tell them! The Medicine Hall is really out of medicinal herbs.\"","\"I don’t know if those medicine merchants have gone crazy, but they’ve taken all their herbs to Xinglin Hall!\"","Chen Yi waved his hand, signaling for him to be quiet, before turning to the people outside and announcing in a clear voice:","\"My apologies, everyone. Jishi Medicine Hall has few herbs left today. If you are not a patient, I ask that you please disperse for now.\"","Seeing the people around him hesitate, Chen Yi smiled and pointed toward the nearby Xinglin Hall.","\"Right now, the only place in the entire Prefecture City with an ample supply of medicinal herbs is Xinglin Hall. You can all go take a look there.\"","\"Moreover, I’ve heard that the Physician presiding over Xinglin Hall is a Medical Saint Hand, a truly rare talent.\"","\"Regardless of whether you need to treat an illness or simply wish to buy herbs, you can go there.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, someone in the crowd muttered under their breath.","\"Who doesn’t know they have herbs there? But their prices are so high.\"","\"Mr. Qingzhou, that Xinglin Hall is from Jing State. They’re unscrupulous and can’t be trusted.\"","\"The herbs at Xinglin Hall are ten percent more expensive than at Jishi Medicine Hall. We... we really don’t want to go there.\"","Chen Yi fell silent for a moment upon hearing this, then offered a gentle smile and began to patiently persuade them.","\"Today it’s ten percent. Tomorrow it might be twenty.\"","\"Never mind the future, just look at the grain prices here in the East Market...\"","He left it at that.","The people who were prudent enough to buy herbs in advance were certainly no fools.","Almost as soon as Chen Yi finished speaking, the people in line began heading toward Xinglin Hall.","\"That’s right. The price of grain has already increased more than tenfold. If herbs start being sold like that too, how are we supposed to survive?\"","\"Let’s go, let’s all go...\"","In just a short while, the people who had come to buy herbs dispersed.","The only ones who remained were the sick and a few casual customers who wanted to buy medicinal tea.","Chen Yi didn’t concern himself with them further. He instructed Liu Quan to watch over the front and turned to enter the inner hall.","At this time, however, all the Physicians in the Medicine Hall were busy.","This was especially true for Ma Liangcai, whose Medical Skill was becoming more and more refined.","There were always two or three people gathered around him.","One person would be receiving treatment while two others waited, with a dedicated apprentice behind them asking others to wait their turn.","At a glance, it was a pocket of tranquility amidst the chaos.","Listening to the noise outside, Chen Yi simply sat calmly in his chair.","This incident also served as a wake-up call for him.","’The enemy is the enemy, but to implicate innocent people in the process is truly an offense against natural justice.’","Fortunately, he had always acted in secret.","Aside from himself, Liu Lang, and a few others, it was nearly impossible for the common people to know he was behind it.","Therefore, it was only his own conscience that suffered...","So be it.","...","Just past noon, the chaotic and noisy crowd at the East Market finally dispersed.","Although those who had and hadn’t managed to buy grain were all resentful, by now, no matter how anxious they were, they had no better options.","The Medicine Hall was short on herbs.","The grain shops were hoarding grain and restricting sales.","The prices of other goods were also rising, and their availability was limited.","However, after staying for half the day and getting a better understanding of the situation, Chen Yi proceeded with his plan.","The sword was already drawn; he could no longer afford to hesitate.","But right now, he had something more important to do.","Chen Yi calculated the time, calmly walked out of the inner hall, and instructed Liu Quan and the others to prepare lunch.","He then went to the entrance and began scanning the nearby East Market Entrance.","As far as his eyes could see, most of the people were from poor families.","Even those dressed in fine silks arrived and departed swiftly in their carriages, like the wind.","The artisans who usually made a living here were all waiting at their stalls.","Performers performed, and hawkers hawked their wares.","Just as Chen Yi finished scanning the area and was wondering where Immortal Bai could be, he suddenly heard a voice tinged with a smile right by his ear.","\"This... young master, care for a divination?\"","Slightly stunned, Chen Yi turned his head to look at the person beside him.","He saw a man with black hair and a pale, preternaturally handsome face. He wore a tattered Daoist Robe with patches and held a cloth banner in his hand.","The man was beaming at him.","’When did he get here... He...’","’Immortal Bai?’","For some reason,","even though the young man before him was a far cry from the legendary Immortal Bai, Chen Yi was certain that this was him.","The young Daoist priest noticed his daze. A flicker of suspicion crossed his eyes as he asked again,","\"Young master, care for a divination?\"","Chen Yi snapped back to his senses, pressed his lips together, and turned to walk back into Jishi Medicine Hall.","’Divination?’","’Divination my ass!’"]},{"number":438,"title":"Chapter 438 - 272: A Gentleman Inquires of Woe, Not Weal","paragraphs":["The young Daoist...","Or, more accurately, Immortal Bai watched as Chen Yi walked into Jishi Medicine Hall, a hint of interest on his handsome face.","\"Interesting.\"","He naturally recognized Chen Yi as the rather talented Martial Arts prodigy who had appeared in the East Market the night before.","He also saw through Chen Yi’s disguise and attempts at concealment.","That was why he had sought him out. Beyond their chance encounter the previous night and the thought of \"offering some guidance\" to this Martial Arts prodigy, he was also somewhat curious.","He wanted to see the man’s origins, to learn of his master.","He hadn’t expected the young man to be so unreceptive.","\"Fine, so be it.\"","\"Enter a mountain but refuse to greet the immortal, enter a temple but refuse to bow to the Buddha... you’re the only one who loses out.\"","\"My... this humble Daoist’s fated connection with you has come to an end.\"","Immortal Bai coughed once, then carried his cloth banner toward the East Market Entrance. He planted the banner beside him and gave his sleeves a couple of flicks.","He truly looked the part of a transcendent immortal.","\"To know your past and foretell your future, just listen to a word or two from this humble Daoist.\"","\"I divine life and death, fortune and ruin. I can eliminate your worldly obstacles and guarantee a future of endless peace.\"","\"You there... my good sir. I see your forehead is full and bright. You must have some happy occasion coming up?\"","A burly man in hemp clothes and a white head wrap shot him a mournful look and grumbled,","\"Piss off! Can’t you see I’m on my way to a funeral?\"","\"Right, right...\"","Inside Jishi Medicine Hall, Chen Yi stood by the door, furtively observing the young Daoist’s distant antics. He couldn’t help but feel that something was strange.","’This is... Immortal Bai?’","Aside from his exceptional good looks, the young Daoist seemed no different from an ordinary person.","He looked frail, as if a gust of wind could blow him over, and gave off no fluctuations of the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","His every move had nothing in common with a ’revered master’.","If his intelligence hadn’t indicated otherwise, he never would have connected this young Daoist with \"Immortal Bai.\"","Chen Yi muttered to himself for a moment, then discreetly circulated his True Essence and cast his Qi Observation Skill in the man’s direction.","The very instant his gaze fell upon the young Daoist...","A blinding, silvery-white light filled his entire field of vision, followed by a searing heat that stabbed into his eyes.","HISS.","Chen Yi reflexively squeezed his eyes shut as tears streamed from the corners.","’What was that?’","He had only managed a single glance, just enough to see what looked like a phantom silhouette overlaying the young Daoist’s body.","It was the silhouette of a figure with a blurred face, wearing a formal headpiece and a long, violet-gold robe, a small jade seal hanging from its waist.","It was this violet-gold figure that had sensed his gaze, causing the seal at its waist to erupt with that dazzling light.","The light had traced his Qi Observation Skill back to its source and injured his eyes.","’Is this the aura of the number one expert in Martial Arts?’","’Truly terrifying!’","Though inwardly horrified, Chen Yi did not make any sudden moves. Instead, he drew True Essence from his Forehead Acupoint Sea of Qi to repair the meridians around his eyes.","Fortunately, he had sensed something was wrong and closed his eyes just in time.","Otherwise, that one strike from the young Daoist... from Immortal Bai, would have been enough to severely injure his eyes.","’I wonder what Realm his Cultivation has reached.’","’The First Grade Realm? Or even higher?’","Chen Yi had no way of knowing.","But he was certain of one thing—Immortal Bai had discovered his probing gaze.","A wry smile inevitably touched his lips.","For the longest time, he had relied on his Qi Observation Skill to probe others’ auras, using it to judge their Cultivation and Technique Realm.","He never imagined it would be the very thing that exposed him today.","’Immortal Bai... I suppose it’s acceptable that the number one expert in the Great Wei Martial World would have such an ability.’","As he mulled this over, Chen Yi raised a hand to wipe the moisture from the corners of his eyes. He slowly opened them and looked toward Immortal Bai again.","But having learned his lesson, this time he was careful to use only his naked eyes.","Chen Yi expected to meet Immortal Bai’s gaze.","But to his surprise, Immortal Bai seemed completely oblivious, and was earnestly pulling someone aside, chattering incessantly.","Chen Yi was about to breathe a sigh of relief when he suddenly noticed the person at Immortal Bai’s side.","—Dressed in a lavish Official Robe and Official Hat, with a Jade Belt fastened at his waist. He carried himself with a magnificent air, and his face...","His face...","Who else could it be but Chen Yunfan!?","Immortal Bai paid no mind to Chen Yi’s spying. He tugged on Chen Yunfan’s sleeve and said with a smile,","\"Sir Official, this humble Daoist sees your forehead is full and your bearing is extraordinary. Might I be permitted to perform a divination for you?\"","Chen Yunfan was initially displeased, but his interest was piqued by the man’s words.","\"Seeing as your handsome face is only a tiny bit inferior to my own, I’m sure you wouldn’t dare spin lies to deceive me.\"","\"In that case, you can just give me a—\"","Before Chen Yunfan could finish, a voice tinged with a mixture of delight and alarm called out from the side, \"Brother!\"","Hearing the voice, Chen Yunfan turned his head. \"Brother Yi?\"","\"What are you doing in the East Market? I didn’t think you’d have the time.\"","\"Oh, right, I remember. You managed to land a job as the Xiao Family’s Medicine Hall Master.\"","With that, Chen Yunfan left Immortal Bai behind and walked over to Chen Yi, beginning to lecture him.","\"Look at you. For goodness’ sake, you’re an Instructor at Guiyun Academy, one of the Great Wei Dynasty’s most renowned masters of the Calligraphy Dao and Poetry. Why must you involve yourself in something as unseemly as commerce?\"","Chen Yi nodded, his smile stiff. Out of the corner of his eye, he saw that Immortal Bai wore an equally rigid smile.","\"Your lecture is sound, Brother. Why don’t you come inside the Medicine Hall and sit for a while?\"","’Damn it.’","’Immortal Bai almost got what he wanted, all because I used my Qi Observation Skill.’","’Good thing I got here in time. Otherwise, if he’d delivered one of his prophecies... I don’t care if Chen Yunfan lives or dies, but I absolutely cannot get dragged into it!’","It wasn’t that Chen Yi was \"superstitious.\"","It was just that all the stories he’d heard about Immortal Bai were simply too bizarre.","That, coupled with the phantom silhouette he had just witnessed...","He had no choice but to believe there was something to it.","Chen Yunfan froze at his words, looking him up and down suspiciously. \"What’s this? Have you... had a change of heart?\"","\"You usually argue with me every step of the way. Why are you so agreeable today?\"","Chen Yi didn’t respond, simply grabbing him and starting to pull him toward Jishi Medicine Hall."]},{"number":439,"title":"Chapter 439 - 272: A Gentleman Inquires About Calamity, Not Fortune","paragraphs":["He was afraid that if he walked too slowly, he’d be tainted by the jinx.","But he had only taken two Steps when Immortal Bai from behind caught up and appeared right in front of him.","\"You two, ahem... fellow Daoists, don’t be in such a hurry to leave. I can see that you are both dragons among men. How about you let me tell your fortune?\"","Seeing this, Chen Yi cursed inwardly but forced a smile and said politely, \"We wouldn’t want to trouble you, Daoist Master. We have other matters to attend to.\"","But before he could take a step, Immortal Bai closed the distance and blocked his path, asking with a faint, unreadable smile:","\"Young Daoist friend, do you know me?\"","\"I... don’t believe I do?\"","\"You don’t?\"","\"I don’t!\"","Seeing the two of them trading cryptic remarks, Chen Yunfan looked back and forth before interrupting:","\"Brother Yi, there’s no harm in letting this Daoist Master tell our fortunes.\"","\"He looks honest enough. I doubt he’ll spout nonsense. Of course, if he dares to fool us, just watch how I’ll deal with him.\"","Chen Yi shot him an exasperated glare. \"Brother, as the saying goes, ’a gentleman asks of misfortune, not of fortune.’\"","\"Why would an upright gentleman like you seek out trouble for yourself?\"","\"Then let’s ask about misfortune...\"","\"Misfortune? What misfortune?\"","\"Brother, you come from a renowned family and are this year’s top scholar. Your future is bound to be filled with official success, boundless blessings, great wealth, and high status...\"","\"You truly are a hero, Brother!\"","Chen Yi gave Chen Yunfan no chance to speak, and even less of a chance for Immortal Bai to read his fate.","He just spouted a string of auspicious predictions, forcibly applying them to Chen Yunfan.","Chen Yunfan stared at him, stunned. \"Brother Yi, you... do you really think so?\"","Chen Yi gave a firm \"Mhm\" then nodded to Immortal Bai. \"We’ll be on our way.\"","This time, Immortal Bai didn’t stop him.","But after seeing Chen Yi and Chen Yunfan enter Jishi Medicine Hall, a thoughtful expression crossed his face.","He then pinched his fingers together a few times in calculation, his expression turning to one of suspicion.","’He... has the look of one destined for an early death.’","’Yet now he possesses so much Dao Realm... Who could have the power to defy the heavens and alter his fate?’","The figures of a few certain individuals appeared in Immortal Bai’s mind, but he dismissed them one by one, muttering to himself:","’Those wandering cranes wouldn’t so easily sacrifice their own lifespan and Cultivation for such a thankless task.’","’Besides, even if they did intervene, it’s impossible for a person’s destiny to change so drastically.’","’How strange, how bizarre.’","For the moment, Immortal Bai couldn’t figure it out, so he simply made a mental note of the matter to investigate another day.","He glanced again toward Jishi Medicine Hall, the corner of his mouth hooking into a smile.","’This junior recognizes me, though. He has some skill.’","After all, he hadn’t roamed the Jianghu for decades. Even if he intentionally revealed his whereabouts, an ordinary person would have a hard time discerning his identity.","To think that he had just arrived in Shu State only to be recognized by a junior.","With these thoughts, Immortal Bai returned to his original spot and continued to wait for the next fated person.","’Li Wudang was right. The Jianghu produces new talents in every generation. Even I can’t dominate this Jianghu forever.’","’Just like this junior before me... His Martial Arts talent might be even greater than that Hetong kid’s.’","’Hehe, this trip was not in vain. Not in vain at all.’","Just then, two figures walked straight up to him.","One was dressed in a pink long skirt, her face coolly beautiful, while the other was petite and delicate.","It was none other than Liu Zhaoxue and her maid, Ling’er.","Immortal Bai sized them up, an eager smile returning to his face.","\"Young ladies, are you looking for me to tell your fortune?\"","Before Liu Zhaoxue could speak, Ling’er behind her cut in, \"Of course we want our fortunes told.\"","\"But I’m warning you, if you do a good job, there’s a reward. If you do a bad job, HMPH HMPH HMPH, you can watch that raggedy banner of yours burn.\"","Immortal Bai was taken aback, then chuckled and shook his head. \"I can foresee some things, but I can’t say whether they are good or bad.\"","\"I don’t care about that...\"","At that moment, Liu Zhaoxue raised a hand to interrupt her, bowed, and said, \"I’ll have to trouble you to read my fortune, Daoist Master.\"","Ling’er glanced at her, a hint of displeasure on her face, but she didn’t act out. She just added to Immortal Bai, \"And me.\"","Immortal Bai had no objection. After nodding, he adopted the manner of a typical Jianghu fortune-teller and said:","\"Your birth date and time.\"","Without hesitation, Liu Zhaoxue took out a handkerchief with the information already written on it and handed it over.","Ling’er followed suit.","Immortal Bai took their handkerchiefs, opened them for a look, and began to chant while pinching his fingers in calculation:","\"I see from your chart, young lady, that your frame is one of jade and gold, with a heart of orchid.\"","\"The benefit of your destiny lies in the word ’noble,’ but its key is in the word ’hidden.’ It is the image of a colored phoenix resting on a golden parasol tree.\"","\"The phoenix, king of all birds, is incomparably noble. The golden parasol tree is the foundation of your family, exceptionally stable. But...\"","Immortal Bai paused, then looked at Liu Zhaoxue and said:","\"But the phoenix is proud. It drinks only the morning dew and eats only the finest fruits. Thus, your standards are exceedingly high, leading easily to a sense of loneliness.\"","Liu Zhaoxue listened with a calm expression, weighing his words in her heart.","\"Daoist Master, I must ask, is there a way to break this fate?\"","\"It is not about ’breaking,’ but about ’dissolving.’\"","Immortal Bai shook his head and pointed to the clouds in the sky. \"When the attachments in your heart dissipate like those clouds, your troubles will vanish as well.\"","Liu Zhaoxue looked at him thoughtfully, murmuring the word \"dissolve.\"","The past few years flashed through her mind, and she couldn’t help but sigh inwardly.","’Easier said than done.’","Thinking this, Liu Zhaoxue waved a hand to the person behind her. \"Give him his reward.\"","Ling’er gave a perfunctory acknowledgment, then stood before Immortal Bai with the silver. \"My turn, my turn.\"","Immortal Bai gave her an unreadable smile and didn’t refuse.","He pinched his fingers and calculated.","\"Young lady, your life will be smooth sailing. Your parents will be healthy and well. You are a person of boundless fortune.\"","Ling’er froze for a second, then turned and pointed at Liu Zhaoxue, asking suspiciously:","\"That’s not what you said when you were reading her... my lady’s fortune just now.\"","\"Aren’t you supposed to mention my destiny’s structure, and how to resolve it?\"","Immortal Bai smiled faintly. \"Your destiny is far too noble, young lady. How could I dare sully your ears with such vulgar words?\"","’A junior from the Five Poison Sect. The aura of blood is practically written on her forehead, and she doesn’t even know it.’","’Sigh, I am a kind old man. I can’t bring myself to say such vicious things.’","Ling’er was relentless. \"No, no way. You have to tell me something specific, or I won’t let you off...\"","Seeing this, Liu Zhaoxue didn’t wait any longer and turned to leave.","When she reached the entrance of Jishi Medicine Hall, she saw Chen Yi and Chen Yunfan at the door and her steps faltered.","This time, however, she didn’t approach to exchange a few words as she had before. She simply bowed and walked toward Xinglin Hall.","A moment ago, she had seen Chen Yi and Chen Yunfan from a distance, which gave her the idea to have her fortune told.","Since it was a spur-of-the-moment decision, she naturally wouldn’t do anything extra.","Besides... she was well aware of the current situation in Shu State. She kept her distance from anyone related to the Xiao Family.","Chen Yi glanced over, his gaze returning to Immortal Bai and the girl from the Five Poison Sect named Ling’er.","He couldn’t help but wonder.","’Immortal Bai just gave two fortunes.’","’One involved a reversal of fortune, while the other was all wealth and nobility.’","’Does that mean both Liu Zhaoxue and that Ling’er girl will meet bad ends?’","’Or is there a difference?’","Just as Chen Yi was pondering this, Chen Yunfan beside him suddenly let out a laugh.","\"That girl... she’s no good.\"","Chen Yi followed the sound with his eyes and saw the girl, Ling’er, secretly sprinkling some kind of powder.","He almost burst out laughing.","’Do people from the Five Poison Sect really resort to Poisoning at the slightest disagreement?’","’Savage. Truly savage!’","Stifling his laughter, Chen Yi said nonchalantly, \"Did you see something, Brother?\"","Chen Yunfan turned his head to look at him, the smile vanishing from his face in an instant. He said irritably:","\"I didn’t see anything.\"","’This Brother Yi really treats me like an outsider.’","’His Martial Arts Cultivation is clearly so high, yet he acts like a frail scholar in front of me all day.’","’Just you wait!’","Chen Yunfan grumbled to himself, then took a letter from his robes and handed it over:","\"A few days ago, I corresponded with Father.\"","\"This one is for you, from him.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi withdrew his gaze, looked at him, then at the letter in his hand.","\"Father?\""]},{"number":440,"title":"Chapter 440 - 273: Dragon and Phoenix Among Men","paragraphs":["Father...","Chen Xuanji...","It had been a long time since Chen Yi had heard that title.","The last time had been in the letter from the Chen Family’s matriarch, Cui Yu.","He hadn’t expected Chen Xuanji’s reply to Chen Yunfan to include a letter for him as well.","Chen Yi was silent for a moment before taking the letter. \"Chen... Father, has he returned from the Western Regions?\"","Chen Yunfan nodded, then shook his head. \"His letter says he plans to return.\"","\"But he hasn’t departed yet, so there’s no telling when he’ll make it back to the Capital Prefecture.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment and opened the letter to read.","It was two pages long, filled to the brim with writing.","[For the eyes of my son, Yi, only.]","[I, your father, have heard of your marriage into the Xiao Family. My heart is filled with a measure of regret. I regret that I should not have entrusted all family matters, large and small, entirely to your mother’s care, which led to her making this grave error...]","Reading this, Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly.","’What’s this? A little late for that, isn’t it?’","’He’s the Patriarch of the great Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family. If he had truly cared, how could he not have arranged everything properly before he left?’","[...However, a man born into this world must be able to stand on his own two feet.]","[I trust that even while living with the Xiao Family, my son has not forgotten the patriotic heart of his youth.]","[Therefore, I shall write a memorial to the Holy Emperor to petition on your behalf, allowing you to participate in the next imperial examination, or to arrange an official post for you.]","[What do you say to a position in the Shu State Capital Commandery or the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office? Indulge me this, and ease the mind of this worried father of yours...]","By the end of the letter, a strange expression had crept onto Chen Yi’s face.","’The imperial exams, being granted a post...’","In his memory, Chen Xuanji had never been a kind or affectionate father.","Most of the time, he was stern and unsmiling—calm, composed, and possessed of a powerful aura.","So Chen Yi reread the letter before looking up suspiciously at Chen Yunfan.","\"Are you certain Father wrote this, Brother?\"","At these words, Chen Yunfan gave him a stern look. \"Brother Yi, you mustn’t be disrespectful toward Father.\"","Chen Yi offered no explanation, simply handing him the letter. \"See for yourself.\"","Chen Yunfan froze, muttering something about how he’d be in for it if their father found out, before quickly reading through the letter.","The expression on his face instantly became a picture of utter bewilderment.","\"This... Father wrote this?\"","\"When... when did he become so kind and approachable?\"","\"This can’t be right. Shouldn’t he be sternly warning you to behave yourself at the Xiao Family’s home and not bring shame upon our name?\"","Hearing Chen Yunfan say the same, Chen Yi felt his suspicions confirmed.","Based on his memories of Chen Xuanji, even if their father felt guilty about him marrying into the Xiao Family, he would never be this gentle and magnanimous.","’So something must have happened to cause such a shift in Chen Xuanji’s attitude toward me.’","Just then, as if he’d suffered a terrible blow, Chen Yunfan pulled out another letter and handed it over.","\"You should see the one Father wrote to me. He’s just... he’s just...\"","Chen Yi didn’t refuse. He took the letter and began to read it carefully.","[For the eyes of my son, Yunfan, only.]","[I have heard that my son placed first in the imperial examinations. I am deeply grateful to the Holy Emperor for allowing such an ignorant and unskilled rascal as yourself... ]","[As your father, I expect you to remember three things. First, you must take responsibility for the country and its people; this is not a game, so do not act foolishly... ]","[I will soon depart for my return to Great Wei. When that time comes, if I hear that you have been causing trouble in Shu State, you will face the full force of our family’s discipline!]","A small smile appeared on Chen Yi’s face after he finished reading. \"Father has high hopes for you, Brother. This is to be expected.\"","Chen Yunfan shot him a resentful look. \"You tell me, doesn’t he favor you more?\"","\"If you hadn’t come to Shu State, he probably would have secured a post for you in the Capital Prefecture by the time he got back.\"","Chen Yi waved a dismissive hand. \"It’s enough that I have you to toil for the common good, Brother. I just want to be a man of leisure.\"","\"Brother Yi, you’re really something else...\"","Chen Yunfan nearly called his bluff, but a thought to his own current Cultivation and Technique Realm made him hold his tongue for the time being.","\"In any case, now that Father has made an offer, you should think about your next steps.\"","\"I’m not interested, I’m not listening, and I’m not doing it.\"","Chen Yi’s reply was blunt.","He was now a live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family—a \"husband married out,\" so to speak.","His priority had to be the Xiao Family in all matters.","Naturally, he couldn’t possibly follow Chen Xuanji’s arrangements—either by taking the imperial exams or by serving in some government office in Shu State.","After a moment of silence, Chen Yunfan clapped him on the shoulder. \"Just what I’d expect from you.\"","\"Even though Father has been gone for so many years, I still hold him in reverent fear.\"","He wasn’t just saying that to flatter Chen Yi.","It was a testament to the influence Chen Xuanji had held over him since childhood.","Even though he lived a wild and dissolute life in Shu State, fearing neither heaven nor earth, he would never dare act out of line in front of Chen Xuanji.","Much less would he dare to defy one of his father’s decisions.","Take the three rules from the letter, for instance. Chen Yunfan had them memorized, front to back, after a single read-through.","He couldn’t help it.","The letter had promised he would \"face the full force of our family’s discipline,\" and if he dared step out of line, he truly would be punished as such.","Chen Yi, who was unaware of all this, simply shook his head. \"It’s not that I lack reverence for Father, but...\"","He paused, then looked at Chen Yunfan and continued, \"It’s that I intend to stay in Shu State for the rest of my life.\"","\"Unless absolutely necessary, I’m afraid I won’t see him again in this lifetime.\"","Chen Yunfan froze at his words.","Hearing this couldn’t help but make him a little sad.","\"I wrote to Father about this before, asking if he knew in advance about your marriage.\"","\"But in his reply, he never gave a clear answer.\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"Thank you, Brother.\"","\"However, in his letter to me, Father already made it clear he only learned about it after the fact.\"","’The letter was full of pretty words about guilt and regret, but it never once mentioned punishing the Chen Family’s matriarch.’","’It was all just a pretense.’","’Still, getting the ever-stern Chen Xuanji to use such \"soft words\" could be considered a form of closure for this body’s original owner.’"]},{"number":441,"title":"Chapter 441 - 273: Dragons and Phoenixes Among Men","paragraphs":["Chen Yunfan nodded and sighed, \"I hope Father doesn’t regret this in the future.\"","’He probably will.’","If Chen Xuanji knew about Chen Yi’s current Martial Arts Cultivation, Technique Realm, and his achievements in the other Daos, he would surely be filled with regret.","What’s more, he might even redirect his anger toward Cui Yu.","This was also why Chen Yunfan didn’t explicitly mention Chen Yi’s achievements in his last letter.","Chen Yi smiled, put the letter away, and changed the subject.","They mostly talked about recent events at the Governor’s Office.","Chen Yunfan collected himself and began rambling about his own situation and matters concerning the Governor’s Office.","Especially the matter of the fluctuating grain prices in Shu State.","\"Damn it, I submitted a petition to Liu Hong five days ago, asking him to issue an order to stabilize grain prices, but he just keeps sitting on it and won’t agree.\"","\"Even Lord Yang can’t do anything about it.\"","\"With no other choice, I had to come over myself to knock some sense into those bastards at the grain suppliers.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"Did it work?\"","Chen Yunfan snorted, his tone resentful. \"None of them agreed.\"","\"What? Don’t they know who you are? They’re just going to disregard the reputation of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family like that?\"","\"My reach doesn’t extend that far. Jiangnan Prefecture is Jiangnan Prefecture, and Shu State is Shu State. At the end of the day, Liu Hong is the one in charge here.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded, comforting him. \"Since you know all this, just take a step back for now.\"","\"Perhaps things will take a turn for the better in a few days.\"","Chen Yunfan grunted in acknowledgment. Just as he was about to say more, something occurred to him and he asked with a pointed look:","\"Brother Yi, have you been busy with the academy and that Medical Dao Academy recently?\"","\"You’ve heard about it, Brother?\"","\"Mhm, I’ve been helping the young lady of the Xiao Family with preparations for the Medical Dao Academy these past few days.\"","\"Is that so?\"","\"Then have you heard that Asutai, son of the Barbarian Left King Mu Hage, has appeared in Shu State?\"","Meeting Chen Yunfan’s gaze, Chen Yi nodded slightly. \"I just heard about it this morning.\"","\"You must be quite troubled by it, Brother.\"","\"I am. And I don’t even know if the rumor is true or not.\"","Seeing no change in his expression, Chen Yunfan turned his head to watch Immortal Bai and Ling’er bickering.","He knew that Chen Yi had killed Lv Jiunan.","That’s why he was asking about \"Asutai\" so indirectly.","His intuition told him that this matter might also be related to Chen Yi.","’Sigh, Brother Yi is becoming more and more inscrutable.’","’As his older brother, I really can’t understand the things he does anymore.’","Fortunately, Chen Yunfan trusted that Chen Yi wouldn’t act without reason; he must have his motives for doing what he did.","’Perhaps... it’s related to the Xiao Family?’","’It must be.’","After a bit more small talk, Immortal Bai had sent Ling’er away. Though the smile on his handsome face remained, his mood had clearly been affected.","Even his previously skilled hawking cries had stopped.","’No wonder the Five Poison Sect is still so second-rate after all these years. With a successor like that, how could they possibly contend with the renowned orthodox sects?’","Immortal Bai glanced unhappily in the direction of Xinglin Hall, then listlessly packed up his cloth banner.","Just as he was about to leave, he heard a familiar voice from beside him.","\"Master?\"","A young man dressed in black brocade was looking at Immortal Bai with suspicion.","That was one thing.","The crucial part was that, aside from his clothes, the newcomer was identical to the current Immortal Bai in both build and appearance.","Immortal Bai, who of course knew the newcomer’s identity, glanced over and grumbled, \"What ’Master’? Can’t you see I’m wearing your face right now?\"","The newcomer didn’t know whether to laugh or cry. \"Master, you... you haven’t been telling fortunes for people again, have you?\"","\"So what if I have?\"","\"Shu State is a land of great people. What’s wrong with me offering some guidance to the people here?\"","\"But you, Shui Hetong... why aren’t you back at the Wind and Rain Tower? What are you doing chasing me all the way here?\"","Seeing Immortal Bai turn the tables on him, Shui Hetong repeatedly cupped his fist and bowed. \"Master, this disciple came to deliver a letter to you.\"","\"A letter? Whose letter?\"","\"A letter from Junior Master Li.\"","\"Li Wudang?\"","Seeing Shui Hetong nod, Immortal Bai held out his hand. \"Give it to me.\"","Once the letter was in his hand, Immortal Bai waved impatiently. \"I’ve got the letter. Hurry up and get back to the Wind and Rain Tower.\"","\"Yes...\"","But before Shui Hetong could get far, Immortal Bai called out to him again.","\"Forget it, forget it. I’m traveling, and it just so happens I could use someone to serve me.\"","Shui Hetong beamed and agreed, falling into step beside him.","Immortal Bai paid him no mind, taking out the letter and reading it to himself.","After finishing it, a smile appeared on his face. \"Li Wudang, oh, Li Wudang. So you have a time when you need to ask me for a favor.\"","Shui Hetong heard this and glanced sideways at him. \"Junior Master Li is asking a favor of you?\"","\"Heh, your Junior Master Li asked me to give his disciple some pointers when I pass through Shu State.\"","\"His disciple... Junior Sister Xiao?\"","Shui Hetong understood now. He said thoughtfully, \"I remember Junior Sister Xiao is now a General in the Shu State’s Dingyuan Army, and she’s already married?\"","\"Are you asking me?\"","\"I wouldn’t dare...\"","\"That is indeed the case. And as it happens, I know exactly where her husband is.\"","Hearing this, Shui Hetong looked at him and saw that he was staring meaningfully in another direction.","Shui Hetong followed his gaze.","Not far away, under the entrance of a building with a sign that read \"Jishi Medicine Hall,\" stood two young men.","Moreover, those two were also looking their way.","\"Them?\"","Immortal Bai nodded slightly and, speaking to himself, waved at Chen Yi and Chen Yunfan. \"Both are dragons among men.\"","Shui Hetong fell silent for a moment, and a sharp aura began to emanate from him.","It was like a treasured sword, long-sealed, that dazzled with brilliant light the moment it was unsheathed.","His entire disposition underwent an earth-shattering transformation—he radiated an air of looking down upon the world.","\"To earn Master’s approval, they must be extraordinary. What’s more, one of them is Junior Sister Xiao’s husband.\"","\"So, Master, may this disciple go and make their acquaintance?\"","Immortal Bai shook his head, chuckling. \"There will be plenty of opportunities in the future. Let’s go.\"","At his words, Shui Hetong nodded, and the aura around him quietly dissipated.","\"Master, where are we going now?\"","\"Wumeng Mountain...\"","The two of them, talking and laughing, vanished into the crowd in an instant, as if they had never been there at all.","And what was even stranger—","No one in the surrounding crowd seemed to have noticed.","Even though Shui Hetong and Immortal Bai had the same face, not a single person had stopped to stare.","Except for Chen Yi and Chen Yunfan...","The two of them stared at the spot where Immortal Bai and Shui Hetong had disappeared, their expressions shifting.","After a long silence, Chen Yunfan let out a slow breath and spoke. \"Brother Yi, do you know who they are?\"","Chen Yi was tempted to say he didn’t know, but after witnessing Immortal Bai’s extraordinary abilities, he could only nod.","\"Some time ago, the Mountain Race brought news that Immortal Bai was re-emerging in the Jianghu and would soon arrive in Shu State.\"","\"If my guess is correct, the young Daoist who wanted to tell our fortunes earlier was Immortal Bai.\"","Chen Yunfan’s face filled with shock. \"You’re saying... Immortal Bai? Gongye Bai??\"","\"Holy hell, it’s a good thing you stopped me just now.\"","\"Otherwise, once he opened that ruinous mouth of his, I wouldn’t even know what hit me before I died.\"","Chen Yi grunted in agreement and said with a smile, \"It was just a guess. I didn’t expect it was really him.\"","Chen Yunfan grimaced, still shaken. \"Some guess you made...\"","He trailed off, then let out a long breath, forcing down the tremor in his heart and squeezing out a smile.","\"Looks like it’s not a good day for me to be out. I’m going back to my residence and locking the doors.\"","Chen Yi gave him a look, a ghost of a smile on his face. \"Are you scared, Brother?\"","Chen Yunfan snorted. \"I am.\"","With anyone else, he might have tried to act tough.","But Immortal Bai...","Setting aside the rumors about him, his Cultivation and Technique Realm alone were not something he could ignore.","\"Brother Yi, who was the person who came later?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","\"You don’t know either?\"","Chen Yi spread his hands. \"I’d guess he’s some kind of disciple or servant of Immortal Bai.\"","\"A disciple... Shui Hetong?\"","Chen Yunfan muttered that it was no wonder he had such an imposing aura, then shook his head.","\"The affairs of the Jianghu are too far removed from you and me. It’s best not to get involved.\"","\"You’re right, Brother, but...\"","Chen Yi paused, feigning curiosity. \"What were those two talking about just now?\"","\"How come we couldn’t hear anything?\"","Chen Yunfan rolled his eyes inwardly. ’There Brother Yi goes again, asking the obvious.’","\"For someone like Immortal Bai, if he doesn’t want his words to be overheard, then no one will be able to hear them.\"","\"I see...\"","Chen Yi looked toward the East Market Entrance and nodded lightly. \"Truly a godlike figure.\"","The moment he finished speaking, a flash of golden light appeared before his eyes.","[Witnessed Immortal Bai performing divination at the Shu State East Market Entrance. Reward: Mountain Shattering Fist Technique tier increased to Celestial Tier, Opportunity +253.]","[Evaluation: Arrival confirmed. Voice heard. Scene witnessed.]","[Rejected Immortal Bai’s guidance for yourself; disrupted Immortal Bai’s guidance for Chen Yunfan...","Performance—barely satisfactory.]","After reading it, a strange look appeared in Chen Yi’s eyes.","’Guidance?’","’Are you sure it wasn’t \"open his ruinous mouth and bring disaster\"?’"]},{"number":442,"title":"Chapter 442 - 274: Why Does He Hide","paragraphs":["Chen Yi, of course, had no idea that Immortal Bai had seen him out and about last night. Still, he wouldn’t doubt the accuracy of his intelligence prompts.","And so,","he was left with a sense of regret, like someone who could have taken both the watermelon and the sesame seeds but ended up with only one.","Even if Immortal Bai offered him no guidance, simply being on good terms with the man would be of great benefit to his future.","It was a matter of timing and fate.","Chen Yi shook his head to himself and put the matter out of his mind.","He glanced over at Chen Yunfan, thought for a moment, and asked, \"Brother, you haven’t had lunch yet, have you?\"","Chen Yunfan raised an eyebrow. \"What, you finally remembered that I’m standing here under the eaves of your Jishi Medicine Hall?\"","Chen Yi let out a surprised laugh. Without another word, he greeted Liu Quan and the others, then led his brother to the tavern next door.","It was the very same tavern Xiao Wan’er had brought him to before.","The shop was small, and the air thick with the heat and aroma from the kitchen.","The place was filled with smoke and heat, and packed to the brim with wandering martial artists.","People from all corners of the land were gathered together, and even the most reserved person couldn’t help but be swept up in the ordinary, bustling atmosphere.","They would exchange a few words, boast a little, then raise their cups with a hearty, \"I’ve long admired your name!\"","Evidently, these wandering martial artists, who had originally come hoping to catch a glimpse of Immortal Bai, were completely unaware of his arrival.","\"Shu State has been really bustling lately.\"","\"Immortal Bai is coming, and so are those horse bandits and barbarians.\"","\"Don’t talk nonsense. If the Barbarian Race really invades Great Wei again, it’ll be a catastrophe for everyone.\"","\"Right, let’s just talk about Immortal Bai instead...\"","The two brothers, Chen Yi and Chen Yunfan, naturally had no interest in joining such gossip.","They had already met Immortal Bai.","And they had already discussed the matter of King Landu of Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race.","So, for once, they set aside their usual playful bickering and ate in peace, only speaking a few words from time to time.","Though it was just small talk, with their combined insight and perspective, they could clarify a whole matter in just a few sentences.","After three rounds of drinks,","Chen Yunfan set down his cup and smiled. \"Before I came to Shu State, the last time you and I sat at the same table was five years ago.\"","\"Back then, Father had just departed for the Western Regions.\"","\"You had just returned from Jinling.\"","\"Mother had a full banquet prepared and invited you, me, Old Four, Old Six, and the others.\"","At this, Chen Yunfan looked at Chen Yi and continued, a touch of wistful emotion in his voice:","\"To be honest, I thought our reunion would be in the Capital Prefecture. I even imagined seeing both our names on the imperial honor roll.\"","\"I never imagined that after that dinner, I’d go off to pursue my studies, and the next time we met would be here, in Shu State of all places.\"","Chen Yi met his gaze with a smile. \"It was a matter of timing and fate.\"","The scene from that night surfaced in his mind—","Cui Yu’s smile was gentle; she looked at him and his brothers without a hint of judgment.","Chen Yunfan was his usual boisterous self, constantly teasing \"Chen Yi\" about the farewell poem he’d written for their father, Chen Xuanji.","Old Four, Chen He, was half a year older than Chen Yi, born to another of Chen Xuanji’s concubines.","He had been strong and powerful since childhood, with an exceptional talent for the Martial Arts. By the age of fifteen, he had already reached Seventh Grade cultivation.","At every meal, he spoke the least and ate the most.","Old Six, Chen Yu, was a year younger than Chen Yi and Chen Yunfan’s full-blooded brother.","He had no interest in the Martial Arts or his studies, preferring to spend his time having fun.","It had been an ordinary dinner, yet unexpectedly, the very next day, the previous owner of his body was locked in the woodshed.","’Now that he thought about it, Chen Yi did recall something odd.’","’It seemed there was more to that incident than met the eye.’","Chen Yunfan, unaware of his brother’s thoughts, poured two more cups of wine, raised his, and said:","\"Since things are as they are, there’s no point in me saying more. It’s all in this cup.\"","Chen Yi returned to the present, raising his cup to clink it against his brother’s.","CLINK.","They both downed their cups, met each other’s eyes with a smile, and then picked up their chopsticks to eat.","\"I hear that ever since you married into the Xiao Family, Xiao Jinghong has been away?\"","\"Yes, she has military duties and can’t get away.\"","\"Can she really not get away, or is she deliberately avoiding you?\"","\"Perhaps... a bit of both?\"","\"So, what’s your impression of her?\"","\"Wait, don’t tell me. Let me guess—you quite like her, don’t you?\"","Chen Yi froze at his words, uncharacteristically hesitant.","After a moment’s thought, he admitted frankly, \"I do.\"","Though he and Xiao Jinghong had only met a few times, he still remembered the first time he saw her one afternoon.","He had been standing by a pond, holding an earthworm in his hand.","And there, in the faintly golden sunlight, he saw a beautiful figure.","Valiant and striking, she was truly extraordinary.","’Even if he never said it aloud, the marriage was a done deal. Xiao Jinghong was his destiny in this life.’","’Besides, as carefree as his personality was, he wasn’t the type to repay kindness with malice.’","’At least, as long as the Xiao Family didn’t wrong him, he wouldn’t think of leaving.’","’Call him someone who just muddled through life, perhaps.’","’But this place was, after all, his home now.’","At that thought, Chen Yi looked at Chen Yunfan and changed the subject. \"Enough about me. What about you and Miss Cui?\"","Any thought Chen Yunfan had of continuing his teasing vanished. His voice grew wistful. \"I don’t know.\"","He paused, then said with a serious expression, \"Thinking about it, I don’t actually hate Qingwu. What I hate is the marriage alliance between the Chen Family and the Cui Family.\"","’A marriage alliance...’","Chen Yi suddenly understood. He had a good idea of what his brother was feeling.","’Perhaps in Chen Yunfan’s mind, a relationship tainted by family interests couldn’t be pure.’","\"So, you don’t actually dislike Miss Cui?\"","\"I do! Of course I do.\"","Chen Yunfan said stubbornly, \"You have no idea how annoying she is, pestering me all day.\"","\"Like this trip to Shu State. I have no idea how she found out, but she followed me here. It’s just...\"","Just then, a figure walked in from outside, shot Chen Yunfan a sideways glance, and asked:"]},{"number":443,"title":"Chapter 443 - 274: Why He Hides","paragraphs":["\"She’s truly what?\"","Chen Yunfan flinched when he heard the voice. But upon seeing Chen Yi’s teasing smile, he suddenly stiffened his neck and declared:","\"Truly graceful and intelligent, empathetic and understanding, dignified and courteous... Huh? Qingwu, what are you doing here?\"","\"I was just praising you to Brother Yi.\"","The newcomer was none other than Cui Qingwu. Seeing Chen Yunfan’s expression, she chuckled.","She walked over and sat down beside him, chiding playfully, \"If I hadn’t come, how would I ever have known Brother Yunfan finds me so tiresome?\"","\"Haha... I don’t think I said that. It was, it was Brother Yi.\"","\"Right?\"","Chen Yi chuckled, at a loss for words. He gave a fist-and-palm salute and said, \"Miss Cui, please forgive him. My brother has had a little to drink and misspoke.\"","\"Yes, that’s right... I’ve had too much to drink.\"","\"Is that so?\"","\"Of course...\"","Chen Yi was both surprised and not surprised by Cui Qingwu’s arrival.","He was surprised that she had finished her lunch with Xiao Wan’er so quickly; it also seemed that the two of them had gotten along very well.","What was not surprising was that Cui Qingwu, after all, remembered what they had discussed the previous night.","After some idle chatter, the three of them paid the bill and left the small tavern.","Before they parted ways, Chen Yunfan looked at Chen Yi, tilting his head up slightly as he spoke:","\"I’ve been here in Shu State for so long, and you’ve finally played the part of a proper host.\"","\"But I won’t let you be on the losing end. Once things calm down, I’ll...\"","He glanced at Cui Qingwu, who was standing to the side. \"I’ll have Qingwu treat you to a meal at the Yunqing Building.\"","Cui Qingwu, of course, did not refuse. \"Perfect timing. We’ve just opened a new vintage, and it has a unique sweetness.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"It would be my pleasure.\"","Not long after, Chen Yunfan took a carriage back to the Government Office, while Cui Qingwu and Huan’er headed for the East Market.","Chen Yi watched them go, then smiled and returned to Jishi Medicine Hall.","The afternoon sun was at its peak.","But at this time of year, the weather had already turned cold.","As a cool breeze swept by, Chen Yi’s mood gradually settled.","He’d had a pleasant conversation with Chen Yunfan today.","Reminiscing about the past, discussing the present, and talking about the future had relaxed him considerably.","Ever since he had arrived in this world, he had been burdened by so many things that he rarely made small talk with anyone in the Xiao Family.","He rarely did so even with those he knew well, like Xiao Wan’er, Xiaodie, and Pei Guanli.","It wasn’t that there was no need; rather, he knew that saying too much would only cause them to worry.","So it was better not to speak of it at all.","But Chen Yunfan was different.","Even though Chen Yi didn’t reveal his secrets, he could still talk around the heavier topics, allowing him to confirm some of his own speculations and deductions.","’Chen Yunfan... I wonder why he hides his true self...’","...","For the entire afternoon, Chen Yi remained in the Medicine Hall. Aside from occasionally helping Ma Liangcai with a few difficult cases, he spent most of his time monitoring the situation in the East Market.","Or to be more precise, the price of grain.","At first, rumors spread like wildfire that the price of grain was skyrocketing, jumping from ten taels of silver per dan to twelve.","By mid-afternoon, it had already climbed to fifteen taels per dan.","But just past the middle of the afternoon, several graineries collectively dropped their prices to a level even lower than that morning.","—Nine taels of silver per dan.","\"I can’t believe I bought so early! How could the price drop so much in such a short time?\"","\"If I’d bought now, couldn’t I... couldn’t I have bought twice as much grain?\"","\"I heard it was the young lady from the Qinghe Cui Family. They say she has her own supply of grain, and that’s what brought the price down.\"","\"Anyone who can afford it should buy some now. Otherwise, once Miss Cui’s grain sells out, the price will probably shoot up again.\"","\"You’ve got a point...\"","After half a day of fluctuations, even those who had originally found the prices exorbitant were now willing to accept nine taels per dan.","There were many buyers.","Even Liu Quan and the others in the Medicine Hall were tempted.","Liu Quan, however, was a quick thinker. Even if he wanted to buy, he’d still try to be clever about it.","\"Shopkeeper, do you think the horse bandits from Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race will really attack again?\"","Chen Yi glanced at him and shook his head. \"I don’t know.\"","Liu Quan pressed on, \"But the rumors are all over the place, and they sound so detailed and convincing. Could they be true?\"","\"Until the Government Office makes an official announcement, it’s all just speculation.\"","\"But...\"","Seeing his persistence, Chen Yi naturally guessed what he was thinking. He tossed the account book aside and started walking out.","\"If you want to buy grain, then go buy it. It’s not like you’re short on a little silver.\"","\"Shopkeeper?\"","\"I’m heading home. You all watch the shop.\"","Without looking back, Chen Yi gave a wave of his hand and departed.","He, of course, knew the reason for the afternoon’s fluctuating grain prices.","First, Liu Lang, Wang Ji, and their people had been secretly buying up grain. Then, Cui Qingwu had made her powerful entry.","The owners of the graineries naturally had to respond.","They could either sell off their stock in large quantities now, or they could try to win over Cui Qingwu and offer her a piece of the pie.","Clearly, the grainery owners were still greedy—they chose to hold their noses and accept Cui Qingwu’s entry into the market.","’Good.’","’If they were to give up now, wouldn’t all my planning have been for nothing?’","Musing on this, Chen Yi headed straight for the West Market Hundred Herbs Hall.","Wang Ji had been waiting for some time and led him upstairs to a private room.","Chen Yi got straight to the point. \"Any word from the Marquis?\"","Wang Ji bowed. \"Sir, a messenger just arrived from Steward Lu of the Marquis’s Mansion.\"","\"The Marquis has been feeling unwell recently, so he would like to schedule a meeting with you five days from now.\"","As he said this, he felt a flicker of inexplicable amusement.","How could Chen Yi, the renowned Mr. Qingzhou, not know whether the Old Marquis was actually unwell?","This reply was merely a pretext.","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgement, not at all surprised.","\"With news of the Barbarian Race marching north spreading through Shu State today, it’s perfectly normal for the Old Marquis to be concerned.\"","Fortunately, he only wanted to confirm a time with the Old Marquis on this occasion, so he wasn’t in a rush.","Besides, five days was the perfect amount of time."]},{"number":444,"title":"Chapter 444 - 274: Why Is He Hiding","paragraphs":["It was enough time for him to tie up some loose ends.","With this in mind, Chen Yi asked, \"Did you give Boss Jia’s silver to Guard Liu?\"","Wang Ji nodded. \"I delivered it as soon as I got it this morning. I also led them to the other storehouse.\"","\"It’s just that...\"","He hesitated. \"It seems things aren’t going so well for Guard Liu. He went to several manors outside the city but couldn’t procure any grain.\"","Chen Yi frowned slightly, but his expression quickly smoothed over. \"It seems these Noble families of Shu State are quite selfish.\"","There were only two reasons not to sell grain at a time like this.","One, their families were too large, and they didn’t have enough surplus grain.","Two, they thought the selling price was too low and wanted to wait for it to rise further.","Obviously, the latter was more likely.","\"Let them be.\"","\"Next, I need you to do one more thing for me...\"","After listening, Wang Ji stared at him in stunned silence for a long moment, his expression a mixture of shock and confusion.","\"My lord, you... if this gets discovered, then...\"","Chen Yi waved his hand dismissively. \"Just put on a show.\"","\"Of course, this matter must be handled as secretly as possible.\"","Wang Ji nodded hesitantly, suppressing the panic in his heart and accepting the task.","\"Rest assured, my lord. I will handle it for you.\"","\"Mm, if you’re not sure, contact Zhang Dabao. He’ll tell you what to do.\"","\"Yes...\"","Having given his instructions, Chen Yi didn’t linger. He got up and headed back to the Xiao Family residence.","Wang Ji saw him out of Hundred Herbs Hall. After a moment of contemplation, he gritted his teeth, summoned two guards, and left with them.","Everything he had now was thanks to Chen Yi.","He couldn’t possibly disobey an order.","Besides, after all this time, he was well aware of how formidable Chen Yi could be and wouldn’t dare do anything unnecessary.","’I just hope my lord doesn’t go too far.’","’If this really gets discovered, then... then we’re doomed...’","Chen Yi, of course, knew why Wang Ji was hesitant.","But to achieve his goals, he had to use both open strategies and secret schemes.","Only by using a two-pronged approach could he make this whole act more convincing.","’By my calculations, it should be about time for Zhang Dabao to set off.’","’Heh, I hope they can withstand it...’","...","「Before nightfall.」","Chen Yi leisurely returned to Spring Lotus Garden.","Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie were in the courtyard.","One was practicing his Pile Skill, while the other was clapping and cheering him on.","\"Young Master, you’re improving so fast! Your stance for this Pile Skill is amazing.\"","\"Second Uncle said so too, hehe...\"","As they were laughing, the two saw Chen Yi approaching and went to greet him.","\"Brother-in-law, you’re finally back! Come and see how my Pile Skill stance is!\"","\"Young Master-in-law, the Eldest Miss just sent someone to say that you’ll be having dinner over there tonight.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment, then patted Xiao Wuge on the shoulder and said with a smile, \"This Pile Skill of yours isn’t something just anyone can learn.\"","The Pile Skill, called the *Little Yellow Court*, was clearly a secret art of the Xiao Family.","Even if he could spot some flaws in it, he wouldn’t be so brazen as to point them out.","However, seeing Xiao Wuge’s slight disappointment, Chen Yi added with a smile:","\"Since Second Uncle praised you, it means you’ve been doing well recently.\"","\"I think so too.\"","\"What do you mean, ’you think so too’? It’s just a compliment. Don’t get arrogant.\"","\"Don’t worry, Brother-in-law...\"","Before long, Chen Yi had washed up and changed into some comfortable clothes, then led Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie to Jiaxing Garden.","The moment he saw Xiao Wan’er, she walked over with a letter in her hand and said with a smile:","\"Second Sister has sent a letter.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly, taking the letter as he asked, \"What does it say?\"","\"Second Sister said that things at the Mutual Market are wrapping up, and she’ll be returning to Shu State soon.\"","\"Returning?\"","Chen Yi opened the letter and began to read.","[For my husband’s eyes only.]","[Jinghong has been busy with the Wu Mountain Mutual Market lately and has not written back often. I hope my husband can forgive me.]","[Fortunately, with the help of the Mountain Race, the Mutual Market is not far from completion. In about ten days to half a month, Jinghong will set out to inspect the Three Towns...]","Reading up to this point, Chen Yi glanced sideways at Xiao Wan’er.","\"Returning soon?\"","\"Probably. She might come back when she passes through the Prefecture City during her inspection of the Three Towns...\""]},{"number":445,"title":"Chapter 445 - 275: Martial Arts Body, Perfection","paragraphs":["Xiao Jinghong’s letter didn’t mention the recent major events in Shu State.","Either the news was delayed and she hadn’t yet heard about Lv Jiunan’s death and King Landu of Poshisu Country’s impending arrival.","Or she was intentionally omitting them to avoid worrying the family back home.","As Chen Yi speculated, a gentle smile touched his face.","Even without her saying so, he knew what her days were like at the Wu Mountain Mutual Market.","Allocating lumber and stone, finishing construction on various buildings, assigning manpower, contacting nearby merchants who wanted to trade at the mutual market, and so on.","And on top of all that, there were the military affairs of the Three Towns.","Xiao Jinghong was anything but idle.","’She’s working so hard. I really should apply myself more.’","Just as the thought crossed his mind, Chen Yi heard Xiao Wan’er speak.","\"Brother-in-law, you’ve been out every day lately. I haven’t had a chance to ask how you’re preparing for your studies.\"","Chen Yi blinked. \"What studies?\"","\"The Annual Examination, of course.\"","Xiao Wan’er set the letter down, her crystal-clear eyes reflecting his figure.","\"The Annual Examination is at the end of the month. That’s only half a month away.\"","\"Oh, right, the Annual Examination. I’ve been preparing.\"","’By \"preparing,\" I’m really just getting ready to use my sharp eyes and ears,’ Chen Yi thought to himself.","He had been so preoccupied with manipulating grain prices lately that he truly hadn’t touched a single book.","Not suspecting a thing, Xiao Wan’er breathed a sigh of relief.","\"That’s good.\"","\"I was just thinking I’d mention in my reply to our sister that you were studying hard at home, just to put her mind at ease.\"","Chen Yi chuckled. ’I suppose I should get on that,’ he thought.","Even people like Mr. Yue Ming were vexed by the new Annual Examination rules that Liu Hong and Ma Shuhan had concocted.","He would indeed have to tread carefully.","\"I’ll write a reply to Jinghong later and bring it over first thing in the morning.\"","\"And your painting.\"","\"Mm...\"","After a few more pleasantries, dinner was served.","The group ate and chatted, the atmosphere turning quite cheerful.","Xiao Wuge mentioned he was going to the Martial Arts Arena tomorrow, and also brought up that his second uncle, Xiao Xuanshuo, hadn’t really rested at all that day.","\"I heard from the staff that Grandfather and Third Master were up very late last night.\"","\"Apparently, it was because of that King Landu, who’s planning to lead an invasion of Great Wei’s eastern frontier.\"","Xiao Wuge continued, clenching his fists in frustration, \"And then today, word comes that the Barbarian Left King is heading north.\"","\"Grandfather had barely fallen asleep when some villain came and disturbed him.\"","Xiao Wan’er tapped him lightly on the arm, chiding, \"He’s not a villain. That was Lord Liu Hong from the Governor’s Office.\"","Xiao Wuge pouted and muttered, \"He’s still not a good person.\"","\"Everyone in the manor is talking about it. He came to persuade Grandfather to delay his petition to the Imperial Court for troops.\"","\"What are we going to do if there are enemies to the west and the south?\"","After a moment’s hesitation, Xiao Wan’er looked to Chen Yi, her gaze speaking volumes.","She clearly wanted him to say a few words.","Chen Yi nodded, understanding her unspoken request. He put down his bowl and chopsticks and said with a smile, \"We’ll meet soldiers with generals and floods with dams.\"","\"Wuge, the most important thing for you right now is to hone your skills. The Old Master will take care of any border incursions.\"","Xiao Wuge grunted in acknowledgment, then shoveled down a few bites of rice before continuing.","\"When I grow up, I’m going to lead an army and wipe out all those barbarian tribes! And I won’t spare Poshisu Country, either!\"","Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er exchanged a smile at his words.","\"Your sister and I will be waiting for the day you ride down the Barbarian Race.\"","\"I will!\"","He might have been young, but Xiao Wuge had seen and understood a great deal over the years.","Especially after spending so much time under Chen Yi’s influence, Xiao Wuge had become far more mature than others his age.","He understood, therefore, that many people in the Xiao Family were waiting for him to come of age.","Chen Yi gave Xiao Wuge a thumbs-up. \"You will.\"","Xiao Wan’er smiled and nodded, though the corners of her eyes glistened with unshed tears.","It was as if she could see the figures of their father and mother in him.","And yet, more than anything, she just wanted him to be safe.","After a moment of silence, Xiao Wan’er rose and went to the study. She returned with a painting and handed it to Xiao Wuge.","\"Your brother-in-law painted this,\" she said. \"Take it and hang it in your room.\"","She had originally intended to keep it for herself.","But after hearing Wuge’s impassioned words, she felt the painting belonged with him more.","Xiao Wuge eagerly unrolled it for a look and saw several figures emerging from the canvas.","Xiao Fengchun, Fu Wanqing, Xiao Wan’er, Xiao Jinghong, Chen Yi... and himself.","\"This is...?\"","Xiao Wan’er gave a slight nod. \"Father... Mother...\"","Xiao Wuge froze, his eyes staring blankly at the figures that seemed to materialize from the painting.","There was the tall and sturdy Xiao Fengchun, and the gentle but heroic Fu Wanqing.","\"Father... Mother...\"","Xiao Wuge murmured their names, tears welling in his eyes. \"Father... Mother... Your son... your son... I can finally see you...\"","He had only just been born when Xiao Fengchun and Fu Wanqing had \"died on the battlefield.\"","He’d never even had the chance to meet them.","Now, thanks to Chen Yi’s Painting Dao, the sight of those two vivid, lifelike figures overwhelmed him with a tide of emotion.","Clutching the painting, he began to cry his heart out.","Xiao Wan’er wept silently beside him.","Xiaodie, Cui’er, Juan’er, and the other servants were the same, dabbing at the corners of their eyes from time to time.","Even Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang tilted their heads back, unable to bear watching the scene.","Only Chen Yi watched them, a faint, constant smile on his face.","He wished he could feel what they were feeling.","But he already knew that Fu Wanqing wasn’t actually dead. The most he felt was a pang of sadness out of concern for Xiao Wuge.","But beyond that, his mind was mostly occupied by the endless string of troubles he faced.","After all, he had to face what needed to be faced, and solve what needed to be solved."]},{"number":446,"title":"Chapter 446 - 275: Martial Arts Body, Perfection","paragraphs":["Wasn’t it?","The night was star-strewn and brilliant, the moon a silver hook.","A cool breeze stirred.","Withered leaves drifted down, one by one.","Brightly lit lanterns swayed gently, casting a splash of red light.","Xiao Wan’er saw Chen Yi and Xiao Wuge to the door, her eyes slightly red but also filled with relief.","\"You two should get some rest.\"","\"You too, Big Sister.\"","Chen Yi bowed. Just as he was about to lead Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie back to Spring Lotus Garden, he heard Xiao Wan’er continue:","\"Brother-in-law, I’ve decided to have Little Sister Qingwu help manage the Medical Dao Academy’s affairs.\"","Chen Yi paused for a moment, then realized after a moment’s thought that she had taken his two earlier suggestions to heart.","\"Miss Cui comes from an extraordinary family. With her involvement, things with the Medical Dao Academy will go much more smoothly.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded lightly. \"So tomorrow, I’ll go find her to discuss the matter of the academy’s headmaster.\"","\"Y-you don’t think this is inappropriate, do you?\"","Meeting her slightly apprehensive gaze, Chen Yi smiled faintly.","\"Whatever you decide is fine, Big Sister.\"","Just as he had said before, bringing Cui Qingwu into the fold gave Xiao Wan’er and the Xiao Family much more room to maneuver.","At the very least, she would be far more useful than him, a live-in son-in-law on the fringes of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family.","\"That’s good...\"","Before long, Chen Yi returned to Spring Lotus Garden with Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie.","Perhaps because of the painting, Xiao Wuge didn’t linger and followed Xiaodie back to his room.","\"Young Master, shall I hang this painting up for you?\"","\"No, no, I’ll do it myself.\"","\"Then, please be careful, Young Master. Calligraphy and paintings are fragile.\"","\"Don’t worry, I’ll be careful and put it away properly...\"","Hearing the faint sounds of their conversation from upstairs, Chen Yi couldn’t help but smile.","It seemed that once his Painting Dao improved further, he would need to paint another one for Xiao Wan’er.","Not for any other reason.","Just so he could paint himself to look even more dashing and handsome.","After washing up, Chen Yi returned to his room and sat cross-legged on the bed.","He rested for a moment.","Then, he opened the glowing screen and began to look it over.","Today, because of the incident with Immortal Bai, his Opportunity had increased by 253 points.","Furthermore, the grade of his Mountain Shattering Fist had been raised to the Celestial Tier, the same as his Dragon-Falling Spear Technique.","[Opportunity: 1021]","Chen Yi gazed at the contents of the glowing screen, a thoughtful expression on his face.","’In terms of maximizing returns, raising my Fist Dao to Perfection would be the most suitable choice.’","’That way, I’d have the Celestial Tier Mountain Shattering Fist for close combat and the Celestial Tier Dragon-Falling Spear Technique for long-range attacks.’","’And with both Daos at Perfection, the combined power from the overlapping Heaven and Earth Spiritual Mechanism Realms would be far greater than before.’","’At that point, very few within the same realm would be able to match me.’","But even though Chen Yi knew this, he still hesitated.","The reason was simple.","Fist Technique and Spear Technique were both methods of combat. While their upper limits were high, the improvements they offered were singular in focus.","Therefore, Chen Yi was more inclined to choose between Martial Arts·Body and Step.","Improving the former’s realm would enhance the effects of his Big Spear Pile Skill, Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, and Four Symbols Skill.","The latter would make his two step techniques, the Meteor Butterfly Step and the Wandering Dragon and Phoenix, even faster.","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi’s gaze landed on [Martial Arts·Body]. ’In all of martial arts, nothing is indestructible. Only speed is unbeatable.’","’But that requires sufficient cultivation and physique to support it.’","Therefore—","[Opportunity consumed. The realm of Martial Arts·Body has been upgraded from Great Success to Perfection.]","A golden light flared.","A roar echoed through Chen Yi’s mind.","The vast, ocean-like Profound Mysteries of the Martial Arts Body surged into him, nearly causing him to lose consciousness and fall into a coma.","Even so, Chen Yi’s head was splitting.","He had no choice but to rapidly digest some of the Profound Mysteries while circulating the Four Symbols Skill, using his True Essence to slowly recover his spent mental energy.","About an hour passed.","Only then did Chen Yi begin to feel refreshed. He got up, stretched his arms and legs, and let out a long breath.","Compared to his previous breakthrough to Spear Dao Perfection through epiphany, his senses felt slightly different this time, having relied on Opportunity to raise his realm.","After all, when he’d had his epiphany in the Spear Dao, he had been in a life-or-death battle with Yan Fusha, making his comprehension of the Spear Dao far more profound.","Chen Yi checked the sky. Seeing that it was still three hours until midnight, he wasn’t in a hurry to head to the Chishui Riverbank for his appointment.","’I’m meeting Liu Lang for a duel tonight. It’s a good chance to ask him about his progress over there.’","With this in mind, Chen Yi went to the study.","He began writing a letter to Xiao Jinghong while simultaneously absorbing the Profound Mysteries in his mind.","He had to admit.","His choice had been the right one.","After his Martial Arts·Body reached the Perfection Realm, the effects of his Pile Skill and Heart Method had indeed multiplied.","This was especially true for the Big Spear Pile Skill.","Originally, after his Martial Arts Cultivation broke through to the Ninth Grade, the Pile Skill had become almost useless to him.","His body’s Power had stagnated.","But now, he could find a way to raise the grade of the Big Spear Pile Skill and continue to strengthen his body.","The same was true for the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique and the Four Symbols Skill.","However, the grades of these two cultivation techniques were already high. He just needed to finish absorbing all the Profound Mysteries to make significant progress.","The Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, for one, would be better at hiding his cultivation and Technique Realm.","Even if it couldn’t fool the likes of Immortal Bai, he believed it would be better at dispelling the suspicions of Xiao Jinghong and the others.","As for the Four Symbols Skill, the improvement from raising its realm was the most direct—it would allow his cultivation to advance faster.","Of course, the enhancement effect of the Four Symbols Spiritual Essence on his techniques would also be more formidable.","The specific effects remained to be discovered.","’All in all, I’ve taken another step forward.’","’A good thing, a very good thing...’","As he mused on these things, the wolf hair brush in his hand moved ceaselessly. Under the power of his Perfect Calligraphy Dao, every word was like an Illusion Realm.","In the end, they merged into an Illusory Chain.","These illusions were not grand or magnificent, not like the ones that appeared during the Mid-Autumn Festival with the \"Song of the Water Melody.\"","They were confined to a single study.","The desk was opulent, the candlelight flickering.","Chen Yi sat upright before the desk, a wide smile on his face, narrating the letter’s contents:","\"My dear wife,\"","\"Nothing much has happened in the mansion lately, so you needn’t worry.\"","\"As for me, I’ve been busy preparing for the Annual Examination...\"","\"Wuge is busy with his cultivation and is progressing at an incredible speed...\"","\"There’s also the matter of the Medical Dao Academy... and Hundred Herbs Hall...\"","As if he were standing right in front of Xiao Jinghong, Chen Yi’s figure recounted all the recent events in Shu State.","At the end, he tilted his head up slightly and asked, as if quite pleased with himself:","\"My wife, what do you think? Is your husband’s use of the Calligraphy Dao to write a family letter pleasing to the eye?\"","How could it not be?","Chen Yi felt that using the Perfection Realm of the Calligraphy Dao to write a letter to someone was an absolute rarity in the Great Wei Dynasty.","It wasn’t that others couldn’t do it, but that they probably couldn’t bring themselves to do so.","It had the distinct air of showing off.","And what’s more, hadn’t he \"shamelessly\" pointed it out himself?","Imagining Xiao Jinghong’s expression when she saw this letter, Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh out loud.","\"The wife manages the outside world, the husband manages the home... Quite nice, quite nice...\"","...","「Meanwhile, at the Wu Mountain Mutual Market.」","Amidst the mountains, the dense forests made the area seem even more profound in the darkness of night.","Only the surrounding bonfires provided any light.","The faint outlines of structures of varying heights could be seen, showing that it was already beginning to take shape.","On a nearby hillside.","Xiao Jinghong stood on a rooftop overlooking the entire Mutual Market, but her eyes held no joy for its impending completion.","Instead, they were filled with anxiety and worry.","Although it took some time for news from the Prefecture City to arrive, she was, after all, a Commander of the Dingyuan Army.","She would receive word of any major events at the first opportunity.","Such as the death of Lv Jiunan and the attack by King Landu.","Such as the abnormal grain prices in Shu State, and the fact that the Marquis’s Mansion had to borrow grain from Guangyue Prefecture to fill the supply gap in Iron Wall Town.","And also the appearance of the Five Poison Sect in Shu State, Immortal Bai’s journey to Shu State, and so on.","All this inevitably made Xiao Jinghong anxious.","’The Mutual Market is on the verge of completion, yet it has to be at a time like this...’","’And that \"Liu Wu\"... he helped my Xiao Family before, so why would he act so impulsively this time?’","’He killed Lv Jiunan, provoking King Landu into action. For Shu State, this does far more harm than good.’","Xiao Jinghong couldn’t understand \"Liu Wu’s\" intentions, but because of that previous letter, she subconsciously stopped herself from assuming the worst.","At least, not before confirming King Landu’s movements.","’I wonder what Grandfather will do.’","’If we report this to the Imperial Court now and request the Tiger Talisman, I’m afraid...’","Having been in the army for many years, Xiao Jinghong naturally understood the importance of the Dingyuan Army to the Xiao Family.","But she knew even better that now was absolutely not the best time to deploy the troops of the Three Towns.","First, those horse bandits from Poshisu Country come and go like the wind. If the Dingyuan Army were to fight them, they would need cavalry.","This would disrupt the training of the soldiers in the Three Towns.","Second, if the Dingyuan Army mobilized, it would inevitably trigger a great upheaval in Shu State.","Xiao Jinghong had no confidence she could foresee what was to come.","Mulling this over, she called down, \"Zhenyue, send two more letters. One to inquire with Grandfather, and the other to the Capital Commandery...\"","Before she could finish.","Xiao Jinghong’s gaze snapped northward, her expression turning grave.","\"Who’s there?!\"","After two or three breaths of silence, a slightly aged, laughing voice rang out.","\"Haha, was I not right? Hetong, your Junior Sister Xiao’s Martial Arts Cultivation is no worse than yours, is it?\"","\"Jinghong girl, don’t be so tense...\""]},{"number":447,"title":"Chapter 447 - 276: That Husband of Yours... Is Quite Good","paragraphs":["The light of the waning moon was like frost.","Amidst the scattered stars, two figures hung high in the night sky.","One had white hair that fell nearly to his knees and wore a purple Daoist Robe. Though his face was weathered and his beard sparse, he had a somewhat cavalier air.","The other had long, flowing hair and was as handsome as a demon, dressed in black robes with a three-foot green-edged sword at his waist.","His long, narrow eyes looked down at Xiao Jinghong below, a hint of inquiry within them.","They were none other than \"Immortal Bai\" Gongye Bai and his disciple, Shui Hetong, who had just rushed from Shu State Prefecture City to the Wu Mountain Mutual Market.","Xiao Jinghong looked up, studying the two. A thoughtful look flashed from behind her half-armor mask, and she suddenly spoke:","\"You... are you Master Bai?\"","\"Jinghong, I’m surprised you still recognize me.\"","Immortal Bai let out a hearty laugh. His white hair swayed, and he landed beside her.","Shui Hetong followed close behind, bowing in salute. \"Wind and Rain Tower, Shui Hetong, greets Junior Sister Xiao.\"","Seeing their friendly smiles, the wary Su Zhenyue, who stood to the side, finally relaxed.","Without waiting for Xiao Jinghong to speak, she quietly withdrew to prepare tea for the three of them.","Xiao Jinghong paid this no mind. Her gaze swept over Immortal Bai and Shui Hetong, and she cupped her fist in salute.","\"Jinghong pays her respects to Master Bai and Senior Brother Shui.\"","Immortal Bai waved his hand. \"No need for such formalities.\"","\"My arrival was rather abrupt. I hope you don’t find it rude.\"","\"You jest, Master Bai. Jinghong wouldn’t dare.\"","As she spoke, Xiao Jinghong gestured with her hand and led the way, saying, \"Please.\"","\"Master Bai, Senior Brother Shui, please follow me to the meditation room so we can talk.\"","Previously, when she had learned from Granny Shan that Immortal Bai had re-emerged in the Jianghu, she hadn’t thought much of it.","But when Pei Qian passed through the Wu Mountain Mutual Market and told her that Immortal Bai would be coming to Shu State, she had a faint premonition that she would meet him.","It was for no other reason than the relationship between her master, Li Wudang, and Immortal Bai.","「A short while later.」","The three of them arrived at a wooden house.","It was called a \"meditation room,\" but it was even more spartan than Xiao Jinghong’s own quarters.","One table, five chairs.","An oil lamp hung from a roof beam, casting a dim yellow glow. A few flickering shadows filled the entire room.","The three of them sat down.","Su Zhenyue brought in tea and placed it before them, then withdrew from the room to stand guard at the door.","After a moment of silence, Xiao Jinghong spoke calmly, \"Forgive me, Master Bai. The Mutual Market is not yet complete, so the accommodations are simple.\"","Immortal Bai smiled and shook his head. \"It’s no matter.\"","\"Hetong and I were just passing through. Don’t you worry about it.\"","\"Besides, your master sent a message the other day, asking me to look after you a bit while I was in Shu State.\"","He paused, studying Xiao Jinghong, then shook his head again. \"Li the Scoundrel isn’t very honest, is he?\"","\"A young woman like you, with your Cultivation and Technique already so advanced, why would you need anyone else’s guidance?\"","Xiao Jinghong, of course, paid little mind to such praise.","She was more interested in the name \"Li the Scoundrel.\"","’It seems Immortal Bai’s relationship with my master, Li Wudang, is closer than I thought.’","\"You flatter me, Master Bai. In recent years, I have been busy with military affairs and have neglected my Cultivation. I feel I haven’t lived up to my master’s high hopes.\"","\"At your age, you’ve reached the Lower Stage of the Second Grade and achieved Sword Dao Perfection and Spear Dao Perfection. How can you call that ’neglecting your Cultivation’?\"","Immortal Bai saw through to Xiao Jinghong’s true strength with a single glance. He chuckled and pointed to Shui Hetong beside him.","\"This worthless disciple of mine is about your age, and after ten years of Cultivation, he has only managed to cultivate his Fist Dao to the Perfection Realm.\"","\"Compared to yours, his Sword Dao is a whole Chishui River behind.\"","Shui Hetong lowered his head slightly, his tone full of admiration. \"Junior Sister Xiao’s talent is extraordinary. I am truly impressed.\"","\"If you weren’t burdened by military service and practicing Spear Dao at the same time, I’m afraid your mastery of the Sword Dao would already rival Junior Master Li’s.\"","Xiao Jinghong’s eyes fell on him. \"You overpraise me, Senior Brother Shui.\"","\"My master’s Sword Dao is already approaching the true ’Dao.’ Even if I were to cultivate for another ten years, I would still find it hard to even glimpse his back.\"","Hearing this, Shui Hetong just smiled, taking it as mere humility.","Immortal Bai, on the other hand, nodded. \"What Jinghong says is true.\"","\"Li the Scoundrel may be a scoundrel, but his talent for the Sword Dao is a rarity in this world. Few can ever hope to match him.\"","\"But you don’t need to sell yourself short, Jinghong Girl. Give it ten years, and it wouldn’t be impossible for you to surpass your master.\"","Xiao Jinghong lowered her head slightly in tacit agreement.","’One knows one’s own business best. She was well aware of just how strong her own talent for the Sword Dao was.’","’Never mind ten years; give her just five, and she was confident she could achieve a breakthrough in her Sword Dao.’","’Unfortunately, in the military, the Spear Dao was better suited for killing. By dividing her focus, her progress in both would naturally be slower.’","After a few more pleasantries, Xiao Jinghong inquired, \"Master Bai, for what purpose have you come down from the mountain this time?\"","Immortal Bai had expected this question. He smiled and replied, \"Lately, I’ve been observing the celestial signs at night. The Ziwei Yuan is stirring over Shu State, so I thought I’d come have a look.\"","’The Ziwei Yuan is stirring over Shu State?’","’Does this mean the threat of war in the west?’","Xiao Jinghong knew a little about divination, so she naturally understood the Alchemist’s terminology.","’The term `兵燹` referred to the ravages of war, a conflict that spreads like wildfire, consuming everything in its path.’","’Does this mean... war will break out again in Shu State?’","Xiao Jinghong frowned slightly as several major events she had recently learned of came to mind.","’Could it be that the band of horse bandits from the Poshisu Country really intends to push eastward?’","\"Master Bai, is a great change truly coming to Shu State?\"","Immortal Bai waved his hand dismissively. \"I’ve never been very accurate with my readings. You needn’t take it so seriously, girl.\"","\"But...\"","Seeing Xiao Jinghong’s hesitation, Shui Hetong, who was beside them, chimed in with a smile:","\"On the way here, Master looked at the celestial signs again. He said that the land of Shu State is full of outstanding people and blessed with spiritual energy, so it will surely turn misfortune into good fortune.\"","...","Xiao Jinghong looked between the two of them, then pursed her lips. \"Please don’t be offended, Master Bai. I was being too impulsive.\"","’Anxiety leads to confusion.’","’I really did overthink things.’","Immortal Bai, however, shot a glance at Shui Hetong and snorted, \"Did I, your master, ask you to butt in?\""]},{"number":448,"title":"Chapter 448 - 276: That Husband of Yours... Is Pretty Good","paragraphs":["Shui Hetong gave a bitter smile. \"Master, you... why must you worry Junior Sister Xiao like that?\"","\"What do you know?\"","\"Divination and numerology are a grand Dao—seventy percent truth, thirty percent falsehood. I wasn’t finished speaking, but you had to butt in. Aren’t you turning all my words into lies?\"","\"Yes... This disciple was wrong...\"","Watching the master and disciple bicker, Xiao Jinghong couldn’t help but smile wryly.","Immortal Bai was just as the rumors described: a bit of a scoundrel, with none of the airs of a lofty grandmaster.","Fortunately, he and Li Wudang were the closest of friends, so he wouldn’t hold any ill intentions toward a junior like her.","After a moment’s thought, Xiao Jinghong spoke up, \"Master Bai, a few days ago, Granny Shan mentioned you. She said that when you arrived in Shu State, she...\"","Before she could finish, Immortal Bai raised a hand to cut her off. \"That old hag wishes I would never set foot in Shu State. Pay her no mind.\"","\"But I’m going to do the exact opposite of what she wants and come here openly and honorably.\"","The moment the words left his mouth, he seemed to realize that Shu State was the territory of the Mountain Race. He quickly changed his tune.","\"However, I do have important business to attend to on Wumeng Mountain this time. Jinghong Girl, don’t you dare reveal my whereabouts to her.\"","\"To prevent... ah... to prevent her from sabotaging me in secret.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Jinghong and Shui Hetong glanced at each other, both clearly sensing the strangeness in Immortal Bai’s words.","It seemed there was a deep and complicated history between Immortal Bai and Granny Shan.","Shui Hetong asked cautiously, \"Master, did you and Granny Shan know each other in the past?\"","\"That’s all ancient history.\"","\"Back when I first entered the Jianghu, my fame was second to none. Naturally, I attracted some people with ulterior motives...\"","Immortal Bai noticed the looks from the two juniors and cleared his throat.","\"It’s all in the past. No need to bring it up.\"","\"But as for you, Jinghong Girl, I’ve been holed up in the Wind and Rain Tower all these years and have only heard about you from Li the Scoundrel.\"","\"I didn’t even prepare a gift for your wedding, which was truly improper of me.\"","Xiao Jinghong smiled and shook her head. \"Master Bai, you’ve been in seclusion for so long. How could I possibly disturb you with such a worldly matter?\"","\"Nonsense. Don’t talk about ’disturbing’ me. I’ll just...\"","As Immortal Bai spoke, he patted himself down, his old face flushing red. He immediately looked at Shui Hetong and gestured.","\"My good disciple, why don’t you represent your master and give her something?\"","\"...\"","Shui Hetong gave a helpless smile. After a moment’s thought, he took a White Jade Square Seal from his robes and placed it on the table.","\"This is a token of the Wind and Rain Tower. In the future, if Junior Sister Xiao encounters an urgent matter, you can use this to command the disciples of the Wind and Rain Tower.\"","Xiao Jinghong looked at him and Immortal Bai, then at the White Jade Square Seal on the table, and didn’t refuse this time.","Although she had spent all these years in the Dingyuan Army, she was still knowledgeable about the affairs of the Jianghu.","Thanks to Immortal Bai, the Wind and Rain Tower had long been one of the most prominent powers in the Jianghu.","Even with Immortal Bai in seclusion for so long, under the management of his few disciples, the Wind and Rain Tower’s influence had spread throughout the Great Wei’s Nine State and Three Prefectures.","There was no shortage of powerful Martial Arts experts among its members.","Just like Shui Hetong before her—two years ago, he had made a name for himself as the \"Punch that Topples a Thousand Leagues of Mountains and Rivers.\"","If she could gain the help of the Wind and Rain Tower, Xiao Jinghong would have a powerful ally in the Jianghu from now on.","\"Thank you, Master Bai, Senior Brother Shui.\"","Seeing her accept it, a smile appeared on Immortal Bai’s face.","\"I knew you weren’t as stubborn as your master, girl. Years ago, I tried to persuade him to come keep me company at the Wind and Rain Tower, but he refused no matter what.\"","\"If it weren’t for his letter a few days ago, I would’ve thought he’d died in some forgotten corner of the world.\"","Xiao Jinghong put away the seal and dared not say a word.","Seeing this, Immortal Bai grew even more animated, listing the \"sins\" of the \"Sword Master\" Li Wudang one by one.","He went from their time roaming the Jianghu together as youths to their duel thirty years ago.","There was nostalgia, reminiscence, and plenty of cursing.","Getting worked up, Immortal Bai looked at Xiao Jinghong and was about to start pinching his fingers for a divination. \"Come, come! I’m in a good mood today. I’ll read your fortune, girl.\"","Xiao Jinghong froze for a second, then quickly coughed twice once she realized what was happening.","\"Master Bai, please wait. The tea is gone. I’ll have someone refill it for you.\"","As she spoke, Su Zhenyue \"burst\" in and refilled the tea for the three of them.","This naturally interrupted Immortal Bai’s \"fortune-telling.\"","After Su Zhenyue left, Immortal Bai lowered his hands and smacked his lips. \"Boring, so boring.\"","\"You’re just like your husband, girl. You’re both prejudiced against my divination skills.\"","\"My husband?\"","Xiao Jinghong’s heart skipped a beat. \"Master Bai, you’ve met my husband?\"","Immortal Bai nodded and snorted. \"He’s a slippery one, too. Not only did he refuse to let me read his fortune, but he also stopped me from divining his older brother’s.\"","Xiao Jinghong’s heart relaxed. She smiled and said, \"Please forgive him, Master Bai.\"","\"My husband is a scholar who has never practiced Martial Arts. Furthermore, he rarely leaves home and doesn’t understand the ways of the Jianghu.\"","\"If he was discourteous to you, Master Bai, I apologize on his behalf.\"","Upon hearing this, a strange look appeared on Immortal Bai’s face. He asked, \"Your husband has never practiced Martial Arts?\"","Xiao Jinghong simply thought he was blaming her for choosing such a husband, so she nodded and explained:","\"My husband is from the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family. He has loved reading since he was a child and has indeed never practiced Martial Arts.\"","\"But after coming to Shu State, the family did teach him some Pile Skill, just to keep him fit and healthy.\"","Xiao Jinghong added a few more words, praising Chen Yi. \"Fortunately, my husband has an extremely high aptitude for scholarship.\"","\"Not only has his Calligraphy Dao reached the Realm of Perfection, but he also used it to become an Instructor at Guiyun Academy. Even his poetry is quite accomplished.\"","\"Perhaps you’ve heard of it, Master Bai. The recent ’Song of the Water Melody’ was written by my husband.\"","Immortal Bai and Shui Hetong, who was beside him, exchanged another glance, their expressions growing even stranger.","\"Sounds like your husband is... quite something, hehe...\"","\"So, he can’t heal the sick and save lives? And he can’t wield blades or brandish spears?\""]},{"number":449,"title":"Chapter 449 - 276: That Husband of Yours... Is Pretty Good","paragraphs":["Xiao Jinghong didn’t suspect a thing. Shaking her head, she said, \"My apologies, Martial Uncle, but my husband truly doesn’t know martial arts. However...\"","After a brief pause, she met their gazes and said, \"But I am very satisfied with my husband.\"","\"Whether he practices the Martial Arts or not, he is still my husband.\"","Her voice was calm, but for some reason, she felt a wave of heat rise to her face.","Fortunately, neither Immortal Bai nor Shui Hetong noticed her expression. They were both smiling faintly.","Immortal Bai nodded, his smile radiant. \"Excellent, excellent.\"","\"That husband of yours is a scholar, he has his Calligraphy Dao, and... well, he’ll be able to help you one way or another.\"","Upon hearing this, Shui Hetong turned his head slightly to look elsewhere, the corner of his mouth twitching.","\"Master is right.\"","\"Previously, Master even praised Junior Sister Xiao’s husband as a dragon among men.\"","At this, Xiao Jinghong looked at Immortal Bai again. \"Martial Uncle, you... you didn’t...\"","Immortal Bai, of course, knew what she was worried about. Leaning back in his chair, he waved a dismissive hand.","\"I don’t need to waste my energy on divination for this. One look is all it takes to see he’s no ordinary man.\"","Xiao Jinghong breathed a sigh of relief and nodded. \"On my husband’s behalf, I thank you for the praise, Martial Uncle.\"","\"Praise or not... Jinghong Girl, with a husband as outstanding as yours, you’ll have to be careful in the future.\"","\"Be careful?\"","\"As the saying goes, scholars are the trickiest sort. Be careful he doesn’t fool you.\"","\"Don’t worry, Martial Uncle. My husband is no devious scoundrel.\"","\"That’s good...\"","Immortal Bai gave a noncommittal reply, though his mind was already turning. ’That kid looks completely harmless, yet he’s hiding things so deeply.’","’To think that even Xiao Jinghong hasn’t discovered he knows the Martial Arts.’","’How strange. How very strange.’","’The kid is obviously skilled, so why hide it?’","’Fortunately, he seems righteous enough. Otherwise, I’d have to expose his little act.’","Shui Hetong was also confused, but since this was ultimately a family matter for Xiao Jinghong, it wasn’t his place to say more.","「Not long after.」","The three of them rose.","Xiao Jinghong instructed someone to prepare two wooden cabins for Immortal Bai and Shui Hetong as temporary lodging.","Only after everything was arranged did she and Su Zhenyue go to rest.","\"General, about Senior Bai’s trip to Shu State this time... is it possible that...\"","Su Zhenyue gestured cautiously to the south and west. \"...it’s related to them?\"","Xiao Jinghong pondered for a moment, then shook her head. \"For now, we should wait for news from the Prefecture City and the Capital Commandery.\"","Su Zhenyue nodded. \"I’ll dispatch two letters at once,\" she said immediately.","As Su Zhenyue bustled off to her task, Xiao Jinghong recalled her conversation with Immortal Bai from earlier that evening. Her curiosity about his purpose in coming to Shu State was secondary. She found herself thinking more about Chen Yi instead.","’Why do Martial Uncle and the others seem so interested in my husband?’","...","「9:45 PM.」","「Two hundred li outside Shu State Prefecture City, on the banks of the Chishui River.」","Dressed in black and wearing a bamboo hat, Liu Lang finally arrived after a hurried journey.","He scanned his surroundings.","Peering through the darkness, he spotted a figure sitting by the distant riverbank, and his tense expression eased.","\"Ah, Boss, so you were already here.\"","Chen Yi glanced back at him and waved a hand. \"Haven’t been here long.\"","He then turned back around, his eyes fixed unblinkingly on the float in the distance.","Liu Lang walked over, saw what he was doing, and asked in surprise, \"Boss, are you fishing?\"","Chen Yi grunted. \"Keep it down. You’ll scare the fish.\"","Liu Lang was taken aback for a moment. He looked at the schools of fish circling lazily beneath the float; they didn’t look like they would scare easily.","But seeing how serious Chen Yi was, he sat down beside him and waited quietly for a fish to bite.","’With so many fish here, I’m sure one will bite soon.’","But to his surprise, Liu Lang waited for a full hour. As midnight approached, Chen Yi’s fishing rod hadn’t so much as twitched.","He couldn’t help but say, \"Boss, why don’t you jiggle the line a little? Maybe that’ll get the fish to bite.\"","Without moving, Chen Yi shot him a sideways glance. \"Are you questioning my fishing skills?\"","\"Huh?\"","For some reason, a chill ran down Liu Lang’s spine.","\"I...\"","Before he could say anything more, Chen Yi flicked his line out of the water, packed up his rod, and stood.","\"Since you’re so impatient, we can begin.\"","\"?\""]},{"number":450,"title":"Chapter 450 - 277: Ghost Blade, Radiant Sun","paragraphs":["An angler’s dignity is not to be trifled with!","A fishing rod, a bit of bait, sitting quietly by the river, waiting for that moment a fish takes the hook.","What kind of joy is this?","What kind of bliss is this?","This is the happiest, most satisfying thing in the world!","Therefore, even though Chen Yi saw the school of fish swarming around his hook, he disdained to use his True Essence to pull them onto it.","Someone like Liu Lang, who didn’t fish, would never understand such broad-minded magnanimity.","Of course, Chen Yi had no intention of lecturing him about it.","Actions would speak louder than words.","Might makes right.","Liu Lang, of course, knew none of this. He only felt that Chen Yi had changed the moment he put away his fishing rod.","His originally calm and tranquil aura instantly erupted into a tempestuous storm.","Like a vortex, it sucked in all the surrounding Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","As he watched, Liu Lang’s expression gradually grew excited. Suppressing the tremor in his heart, he took off his bamboo hat and tossed it aside.","\"Boss, in our duel today, I hope you will use your full strength!\"","\"I would be deeply grateful!\"","Chen Yi noncommittally set down his fishing rod. With a flick of his wrist, a plain, unadorned Steel Blade appeared in his hand.","\"First, you’ll have to get past my Saber Dao.\"","The moment he finished speaking, his Sword Intent unfurled.","The Brocade Spring Saber Technique couldn’t be simply categorized as fierce and domineering or nimble and agile. Instead, it emphasized simple and direct moves.","Steady, precise, and fast.","Thus, Chen Yi’s Sword Intent was the same—beneath its domineering presence lay a pervasive killing intent.","In contrast, spurred on by that Sword Intent, Liu Lang subconsciously gripped his blade’s hilt with a reverse \"Yin Hand\" grip.","He drew it slowly.","Then, he lowered his stance, resting the spine of the blade across the crook of his left arm.","A violent Sword Intent blossomed forth.","As the saying goes, there are wrongly given names, but never wrongly earned \"titles.\"","Liu Lang’s blade, just like his title \"Sword Madman,\" was domineering, sharp, and relentlessly pressed forward.","\"Besides my master, when it comes to blades, I fear no one!\"","Chen Yi watched his posture, gave his blade a flourish, and strode forward.","As he closed the distance, he said calmly, \"Today, I’ll teach you that what is too rigid is easily broken.\"","The next moment, he was already at Liu Lang’s side.","As he arrived, his blade fell.","Liu Lang let out a low roar of approval, swinging his blade horizontally to parry.","CLANG.","The powerful, heavy strike landed squarely on the Treasure Blade in Liu Lang’s hands.","Two beams of blade light shot out, slicing through the trees hundreds of yards away at their trunks.","Liu Lang seemed not to have expected the power of Chen Yi’s strike. His straight back suddenly buckled, forcing him to one knee.","But not only did he show no sign of defeat, he even shouted in excitement:","\"That’s got some kick!\"","Then, he swung his blade upward in a horizontal arc, forcing Chen Yi back a step.","In the same motion, he gripped the hilt with both hands, twisted his wrist, and brought the blade down in a diagonal slash.","Chen Yi sidestepped to dodge, tapped Liu Lang’s blade with his own, and said unhurriedly:","\"Your blade isn’t fast enough, hard enough, or wild enough.\"","A fierce look appeared on Liu Lang’s face. \"Again!\"","As he spoke, he used the force from Chen Yi’s tap on his long blade to spin rapidly and execute two crossing slashes.","A cross of brilliant light flashed into existence.","Chen Yi was unmoved. With one hand behind his back, he thrust his blade straight forward.","His Sword Intent solidified into a silvery-white blade of light.","With just one move, he shattered the cross-shaped Sword Intent.","His attack having missed, Liu Lang was not discouraged. He closed the distance, hiding his long blade behind his body.","In a half-turn, he drew back and swung upward.","Chen Yi had already anticipated it. Staring at him without blinking, he precisely tapped the edge of the long blade with his own Steel Blade.","His Sword Intent, wrapped in the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, collided with Liu Lang’s Sword Intent.","CLANG.","The scattered Sword Intent lashed out at the surroundings.","Earth and stone shattered, trees were sent flying, and the top two feet of soil within a hundred-foot radius was stripped away.","This time, however, Liu Lang didn’t pause at all. Gripping his blade with both hands, he began to circle Chen Yi, attacking relentlessly.","Every strike aimed for a vital point.","Chen Yi’s stance remained fixed, still holding his blade with one hand.","No matter how Liu Lang’s blade flashed and flickered, he shattered the assault with a single strike.","After all, the two were at the same Realm in the Saber Dao, and their Saber Technique realms were also similar.","Although their Sword Intents differed, in a duel, it made almost no difference.","Liu Lang, who was inferior in Power, True Essence, and Sword Intent, was naturally no match for Chen Yi.","Especially since they differed in other aspects as well.","Chen Yi’s advantage was his comprehensiveness. With the boon from the Profound Mysteries of [Martial Arts: Blade], he could see through the secrets of Liu Lang’s Saber Technique and Sword Intent at a glance.","He could even see through its flaws.","He could always strike Liu Lang’s weak points with minimal effort, restricting him at every turn.","It was utterly suffocating.","But Liu Lang had, after all, roamed the Jianghu for several years and had rich combat experience.","Moreover, his resilience was excellent; he wasn’t bogged down by temporary gains or losses.","After discovering that his usual moves were useless against Chen Yi, he began to employ a variety of Saber Techniques.","Sometimes domineering, sometimes nimble, sometimes bizarre—the styles were ever-changing.","However, after the duel had gone on for about a quarter of an hour, Liu Lang realized he could hardly pose a threat to Chen Yi.","\"Boss, you’re forcing my hand.\"","After that, Liu Lang no longer aimed to defeat Chen Yi. Instead, he resolved not to lose in the Saber Dao, which he considered his greatest strength.","Even if it meant using some dirty tricks, he was determined to force Chen Yi to use his terrifying Spear Dao.","After three to five moves, Chen Yi saw that Liu Lang’s techniques hadn’t changed and couldn’t help but chuckle.","\"And so?\"","\"Here it comes!\"","Liu Lang’s strike was blocked by Chen Yi, but a triumphant expression appeared on his face, as if his scheme had succeeded.","Then, his wrists trembled slightly, and he rapidly vibrated his blade, unleashing several more strikes with minimal movement.","’Heh, relying on the sharpness of your Treasure Blade to bully my Steel Blade?’","But just as he was about to withdraw his blade, a golden light flashed before his eyes—","[Daily Intelligence · Profound-rank Top Grade: At the first quarter of the Zi hour, the Peacock King Banner Horse Bandits of Poshisu Country will have a secret night meeting with Liu Hong of the Shu State Governor’s Office. A small amount of Opportunity may be obtained.]","Chen Yi froze for a moment when he read the contents, and his hand movements slowed by a fraction."]},{"number":451,"title":"Chapter 451 - 277: Ghost Blade, Radiant Sun","paragraphs":["CLANG! The Steel Blade in his hand was severed by Liu Lang.","A single strike was all it took.","Liu Lang instantly retreated ten zhang, straightened up, and exhaled before saying with a smile,","\"Boss, your blade is gone.\"","Chen Yi didn’t respond, instead looking up to read the contents on the light screen one more time.","Then, his gaze shifted toward the Prefecture City as he said thoughtfully,","\"What’s coming will come.\"","\"That’s right, that’s right. How could you possibly be my opponent using just an ordinary long blade?\"","Seeing Liu Lang’s misunderstanding, Chen Yi glanced down, tossed away the Broken Blade, and pulled back his left sleeve.","\"As you wish. However...\"","He paused, then whipped out his Long Spear. His eyes fixed on Liu Lang as he tilted his head up slightly and asked,","\"You couldn’t even get past my blade. Why insist on seeing my Spear Dao?\"","But Liu Lang just shook his head, his tone laced with excitement. \"No, it’s different.\"","\"When you use a blade, I can’t use my full strength. I’d end up hurting you and myself.\"","\"But if you use that spear, I won’t have to hold anything back.\"","As Liu Lang spoke, he took a deep breath. His posture straightened, and his aura intensified with it.","Even his Sword Intent, bolstered by the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, grew more solid and substantial.","The almost-tangible Sword Intent coiled around his body, layer after layer.","It twisted and morphed like a serpent.","It trembled wildly, causing the surrounding Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism to fluctuate.","After this, Liu Lang’s eyes turned completely black. \"Be careful, Boss,\" he said, his voice hoarse.","\"I didn’t even use this move when I went to challenge General Jinghong.\"","\"Back then, I felt I couldn’t control it and was worried I would injure the General.\"","\"But now... this move should be enough to make you use your Spear Dao, Boss.\"","In the distorting Sword Intent, his figure seemed to stretch and shrink, to widen and narrow.","He truly looked like a vicious ghost.","Chen Yi sized him up. \"This move... is it a true teaching from your master, the Sword Ghost?\"","\"It is!\"","Liu Lang nodded emphatically, gripping the Treasure Blade with both hands as the Sword Intent around him coiled onto the blade itself.","\"My master once said that the Ghost Blade is tyrannical, like a procession of a hundred ghosts in the night, and that using it harms the natural harmony of the world.\"","\"He forbade me from using it lightly.\"","\"But with your level of Martial Arts Cultivation, Boss, I have no such reservations.\"","Chen Yi let out a dry laugh and shook his head. \"You really overestimate me.\"","Then, his expression turned serious, and a brilliant golden light erupted from his body.","An incomparably sharp Spear Intent, as if wanting to shatter the heavens, shot straight into the clouds.","Dark clouds gathered in the sky at a speed visible to the naked eye.","BOOM.","RUMBLE.","Amidst the roar of thunder, golden lightning twisted and coiled within the clouds, illuminating a ten-li radius.","But there was only thunder and lightning; not a single drop of rain fell.","Instead, on the nearby Chishui River, fierce winds whipped the water into ceaseless waves.","Seeing this, a smile spread across Liu Lang’s face, made grotesque by the surrounding Sword Intent.","\"Thank you for granting my wish, Boss!\"","The next moment, Liu Lang’s entire body transformed into a ghostly afterimage.","His body and blade became one.","One after another, ghostly apparitions began to manifest.","Each one was hideous and terrifying, howling like the wind, like a thousand ghost-shadows blotting out the sky and covering the earth.","They completely enveloped Chen Yi.","Furthermore, the incredibly tyrannical Sword Intent began to tear at the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism around him.","It squeezed out a gale that blew furiously in all directions.","Trees toppled, stones were sent flying, and even the previously calm Chishui River nearby was churned into waves.","\"Ghost Blade: Thousand Kill!\"","At this, Chen Yi’s expression grew even more serious as he stared at the hazy figures before him.","After a quick scan, his gaze landed on one of the ghost-shadows, and he shook his head.","\"This move of yours... you haven’t mastered it yet.\"","The Sword Intent is sharp, to be sure, but if the user cannot conceal themselves without a trace, they become the move’s greatest flaw.","’But... if I use this to break your technique, you probably won’t be satisfied, heh...’","As he thought this, Chen Yi stepped on the air, soaring straight up.","His hand moved with his will. He held the tail of the Long Spear with one hand, pointing it straight at the heavens.","CRACK!","A golden thunderbolt instantly descended from the dark clouds.","It struck the spear’s tip, dyeing the Long Spear gold and bathing Chen Yi in a layer of golden brilliance.","Immediately, the golden light around him intensified.","It not only submerged his entire figure but also devoured the swarming \"ghostly apparitions\" that were attacking him.","Everything happened in complete silence.","A long while later.","When the golden brilliance finally began to fade, the surrounding ghost-shadows were gone.","The dark clouds had scattered, and the wind was calm.","Chen Yi stood in mid-air, one hand behind his back, the other holding his spear angled toward the Chishui River. His eyes, however, were looking down on Liu Lang below.","Liu Lang, in contrast, was half-kneeling on the ground, staring up at him in a daze.","His clothes were tattered, his upper body bare.","\"Boss, what’s the name of that spear technique?\"","\"Dragon-slaying Spear, Radiant Sun.\"","It was also the greatest of his four ultimate moves after his Spear Technique broke through to the Celestial Tier.","\"Radiant Sun... I am thoroughly impressed...\"","A satisfied smile appeared on Liu Lang’s face before he collapsed to the ground.","Chen Yi glanced at him, shook his head, put away his Long Spear, and landed at his side.","Just as he was about to take out the Silver Needles he had specially prepared to treat his injuries, he suddenly heard a commotion in the distance.","He had no choice but to hoist Liu Lang onto his shoulder and dash downstream along the Chishui River, planning to take a wide detour back to the Prefecture City.","’If you die, don’t blame me for not holding back.’","’No other choice.’","The commotion from his Radiant Sun Spear Technique just now had been too great.","Even though they were two hundred li from the Prefecture City, it had already attracted many people.","Aside from the garrison stationed in the camp outside the city, who were closer, there were also the Jianghu People who had come to Shu State to wait for Immortal Bai.","Among them were many with profound cultivation.","In less than a quarter of an hour, several figures arrived, speeding toward the location.","There was an old man covered in wrinkles, a beggar dressed in ragged clothes, and a handsome young Swordsman.","They arrived one after another, sized each other up, and then all looked toward the same spot.","—Just beyond the Chishui River’s channel, there was a deep crater a hundred zhang wide.","Gurgling river water was seeping in from a hole on one side of the crater.","In moments, several chi of water had already filled it.","The old man stared at the crater, his brow furrowed. \"Spear Intent...\"","The beggar in ragged clothes picked his nose and glanced around. \"In all of Shu State, the only person with such Spear Dao we’ve heard about recently is that one from the other day, right?\"","The handsome Swordsman nodded. \"’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu.\"","But his attention was clearly not on that. Instead, he was looking at the residual Sword Intent within the crater.","Using the fluctuations of the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, he carefully extended his own Sword Intent to touch it.","TING.","After the crisp sound, a wisp of black blade qi slashed out.","The handsome Swordsman tilted his head slightly, but still failed to completely dodge the blade qi.","A clear gash appeared on his cheek.","Droplets of fresh blood oozed out.","\"What treacherous Sword Intent... I feel like I’ve heard of it somewhere...\"","The beggar glanced at him and grinned. \"How strange. You’re a Swordsman, yet you can’t recognize this move?\"","The handsome Swordsman thought for a moment before a look of realization dawned on his face. \"Ah, it’s him.\"","\"Senior ’Sword Ghost’!\"","The old man nodded slightly and, looking at the Swordsman’s face, said, \"Ever since ’Sword Ghost’ Chu Xiudao was defeated by ’Sword Master’ Li Wudang over a decade ago, he has not been seen in the Jianghu.\"","\"The one who used this move must be his successor.\"","\"’Sword Madman’ Liu Lang. I have heard his name.\"","The handsome Swordsman looked at the crater below and sighed. \"A pity I’ve never had the chance to meet him.\"","The beggar shot him a look and sneered, \"And what if you did meet him?\"","\"Could you block that move?\"","Hearing this, the handsome Swordsman pressed his lips together and, after a long moment, shook his head.","\"I couldn’t...\"","...","「Outside South Street, Shu State Prefecture City. Liu Mansion.」","In the quiet rear courtyard, only two lanterns provided light.","The Guards who had been standing watch here were all silent, lying scattered on the ground.","In the study.","Liu Hong sat at his desk, his expression grim as he looked at the person before him.","\"I didn’t expect King Landu to send you this time.\"","The visitor was dressed in black and had a small, thin frame.","Beneath a head of short, graying hair was a face that was practically skin and bones. The pupils in his triangular eyes were red.","He grinned, revealing a mouth full of pitch-black teeth, and spoke in a sinister voice,","\"Your Majesty’s brother has died. He sent this old one to investigate, and I hope Lord Liu will lend a hand.\"","Just as Liu Hong was about to answer, the study suddenly brightened for a moment.","He turned his head slightly to look out the window and saw the golden lightning in the distant sky, a thoughtful look on his face.","\"You should know that Lv Jiunan was killed by ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu.\"","The visitor followed his gaze, and the crimson in his triangular eyes deepened.","\"Now that I am here, that ’Dragon Spear’ will surely die.\"","\"It’s just that Your Majesty sent me here for another matter...\"","He looked at Liu Hong, his expression turning ice-cold. \"Lord Liu Hong, you promised to hand Asutai over to the Barbarian Race...\"","\"Where is he?!\""]},{"number":452,"title":"Chapter 452 - 278: You’re Insane","paragraphs":["Where is Asutai?","Liu Hong wanted to know, too.","All this time, he had not only been pressuring the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office and the City Guard Army to scour the city, but had also ordered his personal Death Warriors to investigate in secret.","And the result?","There was no trace of him, dead or alive.","It was as if Asutai had vanished into thin air.","Even the Guard Commander he had sent, Zeng Zhifeng, had also disappeared.","This made him increasingly suspect that Zeng Zhifeng had pulled an inside job—hiding Asutai away or selling him for his own benefit.","But Liu Hong obviously couldn’t say any of this out loud.","He looked at the small, thin old man before him and said in a low voice, \"Has the other side put pressure on your king?\"","The small, thin old man snorted. \"What do you think?\"","\"This whole thing was an accident. Who would have thought a routine shakedown would end up netting the prince of the Black Bear Tribe?\"","\"But it’s already happened.\"","\"Even if my king and the rest of the Pirate Alliance don’t want this outcome, we have to deal with it.\"","His expression turned grim as he stared at Liu Hong and continued, \"You are our king’s only ally in Great Wei.\"","\"Furthermore, you’ve dealt with the Barbarian Race before, which is why His Majesty entrusted this matter to you.\"","\"You agreed. You took your payment. So why haven’t we seen Asutai yet?\"","Liu Hong fell silent at his words.","After a moment, he sighed. \"Everything was going smoothly. My men had already secured the prince.\"","\"But there was an incident. He was abducted.\"","He paused, then looked at the small, thin old man and said gravely, \"Du Cang, since I agreed to this, I will see it through to the end.\"","\"Just give me some more time...\"","Before he could finish, the small, thin man, Du Cang, raised a hand to cut him off. \"There is no more time.\"","\"My king only gave me ten days.\"","\"And I am only giving you ten days.\"","\"If you cannot give me an answer before I leave, then I’m afraid I’ll have no choice but to apologize for what comes next.\"","Liu Hong’s brow furrowed, and he asked with a hint of displeasure, \"Does your king truly intend to be so ruthless?\"","\"Hmph. It is not our king who wishes to be harsh with you. The Left King’s emissary has already arrived at the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.\"","\"If we cannot bring Asutai back this time, those barbarians will slaughter everyone along the entire Ancient Tea-Horse Road.\"","\"An emissary? Who?\"","\"Wen Kela’s first disciple, Yuan Jingxuan.\"","Du Cang spoke, letting out a cold laugh. He looked at Liu Hong, his tone dripping with amusement.","\"I imagine Lord Liu is no stranger to him. During that great war years ago, you...\"","Liu Hong’s face paled. He slammed his hand on the table. \"Silence!\"","Du Cang stopped talking, but his face retained its cold, unapproachable expression as he stared fixedly at him.","The two stared at each other for a long moment.","Liu Hong took a deep breath and slowly leaned back in his chair, his face tinged with exhaustion.","\"Go back and wait for news.\"","\"I promise you. Within ten days, I will deliver Asutai.\"","Hearing this, Du Cang laughed. He gave Liu Hong a long, meaningful look and said, \"Very good.\"","\"I trust that Lord Liu is a man of his word. I will wait in the city for ten days.\"","Liu Hong glanced at him. \"And Liu Wu?\"","\"You needn’t worry about him. I will take care of it myself.\"","\"Are you sure?\"","\"Hah. What’s so difficult about a Spearman at the Perfection Realm of the Middle Three Grades of Cultivation?\"","Du Cang continued as he walked toward the door, \"Instead of worrying about other things, you had better focus on finding Asutai.\"","\"That outcome would be best for you, and for my king.\"","As he reached the doorway, he paused. He turned his head to look back at Liu Hong with a very strange smile.","\"I will give you one more piece of news, free of charge—that old friend of yours is not far from Shu State now.\"","The moment he finished speaking, Du Cang vanished from the study.","Liu Hong quietly watched him leave. He sat there, stunned, for a long time before finally rising and going to the window.","He looked up at the bright moon in the night sky, a harsh, cold look slowly appearing on his face.","’King Landu...’","...","[Opportunity +12.]","[Evaluation: Confrontation between Du Cang, Grand General of the Poshisu Country’s Peacock King Banner Horse Bandits, and Liu Hong, Left Governor of the Governor’s Office, concludes with the latter yielding.]","[To not be present, to not hear, to not witness—to let an Opportunity sent from heaven pass by untaken is the mark of a truly lazy person.]","Elsewhere, Chen Yi’s eyebrows twitched as a screen of light materialized before him.","’A confrontation, and he yielded?’","’It seems Du Cang, the Grand General King Landu sent this time, has a rather unusual attitude toward Liu Hong.’","’If King Landu himself had come and forced Liu Hong to yield, that would be one thing.’","’That could be understood as King Landu and Liu Hong being equals.’","’But for just a General to come—someone whose status is not equal to Liu Hong’s—and still force him to yield...’","That gave Chen Yi a lot to think about.","’Does King Landu have some leverage on Liu Hong?’","’That must be it.’","’If not for some deep-seated fear, Liu Hong, with his current status and hidden trump cards, would have no reason to be afraid of King Landu.’","’The ironware trade?’","Chen Yi inwardly shook his head. The ironware deals were handled by the Ji State Trading Company, with Liu Hong operating from the shadows. King Landu’s horse bandits shouldn’t know about his involvement.","Beyond that, the only other thing he could think of were the deals Lv Jiunan had mentioned previously.","Or perhaps...","’Asutai?’","The name surfaced in Chen Yi’s mind. His expression shifted as he quickly considered the possibility.","’From what I understood before, Liu Hong had entrusted Lv Jiunan with rescuing Asutai so he could be returned to the Barbarian Race.’","’This was Liu Hong’s way of currying favor with the Barbarian Race.’","’And for King Landu and his horse bandits, the reason for wanting Asutai rescued also seemed simple.’","’Fear of incurring the Barbarian Race’s wrath?’","’That would make sense.’","’It seems the Barbarian Race has already made its move... Good...’","At this thought, a smile spread across Chen Yi’s face, and his mood inexplicably brightened.","He looked down at Liu Lang, who was lying on the floor of the ruined temple, and chuckled. \"You’re a lucky one.\"","\"If you had delayed me from collecting my Opportunity, I would have definitely left a needle inside you.\""]},{"number":453,"title":"Chapter 453 - 278: You’re Really Crazy","paragraphs":["Be that as it may, Chen Yi wasn’t about to joke with Liu Lang’s life.","After all, Liu Lang had done a lot for him recently. Even if it wasn’t distinguished service, it was still hard work.","After a short rest,","Chen Yi took out his Silver Needles to repair the ruptured meridians in Liu Lang’s body and sort out his chaotic True Essence.","He spent nearly two hours before he managed to get the injuries inside Liu Lang’s body completely under control.","\"Luckily, I treated him in time. There shouldn’t be any lasting effects.\"","Chen Yi put away his Silver Needles and flicked a Qi Blade at Liu Lang’s face.","SLAP.","The Qi Blade landed on the ground.","Liu Lang, who had been lying there peacefully, suddenly dodged to a corner of the ruined temple. He looked at Chen Yi and gave a sheepish laugh.","\"Thank you for saving my life, Boss.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, then turned to walk out. \"Stop fooling around. It’s getting late. We’ll talk as we walk.\"","\"You got it.\"","\"Try not to fight with anyone for a while. You don’t want to rupture those fragile meridians again.\"","\"But I have you, don’t I, Boss?\"","\"Heh, you’ll die.\"","\"...I’ll be more careful, then.\"","After some idle banter,","Chen Yi led Liu Lang back toward Shu State Prefecture City, getting down to business. \"What did you accomplish today?\"","At his words, Liu Lang’s face soured. \"Boss, you have no idea how shrewd those people from the Noble Families are.\"","\"When they heard I was there to buy grain, some quoted me exorbitant prices, some turned me away at the door, and some even cursed me out.\"","\"It was like I was trying to dig up their ancestral graves...\"","Chen Yi knew full well that while the Noble Families of Shu State couldn’t compare to the Xiao Family or the Jing State Liu Family, they weren’t shortsighted people.","However, most of the grain in the Prefecture City was still in the hands of a few trading companies. If he couldn’t find a way to make them part with some of it, it would be detrimental to his plans.","Liu Lang rambled on for a bit before finally saying, \"But I did have some success.\"","\"Two families sold me grain at a price of fifteen taels of silver per dan.\"","Chen Yi hummed in surprise. \"Which two families?\"","\"One was the Wan Family from East City, and the other was the Sun Family from North City.\"","\"The Wan Family... of the Wan Family Medicine Hall?\"","\"You know them?\"","Before he could answer, Liu Lang said with a smile, \"I don’t know what happened to the Wan Family, but they seem to be very short on money lately.\"","\"Besides the grain they sold us, they’ve also sold off many family assets. I heard they even sold two of their medicine halls.\"","Chen Yi murmured, \"Is that so,\" then mused for a moment before saying, \"Perhaps they’ve sensed something.\"","He didn’t know much about the Wan Family.","But a few previous incidents had led him to suspect that their relationship with the Xiao Family was very close.","Most notably, the \"culprit\" who had taken his place as Liu Jing’s killer was from the Wan Family.","That alone was reason enough for him to suspect the Wan Family was likely acting on Elder Master Xiao’s instructions.","Otherwise, he couldn’t understand why the Wan Family would voluntarily take the blame for this \"unsolved case.\"","On top of that, Miss Wan Rourou had visited Xiao Wan’er time and again, far more frequently than the women from other families.","Therefore, Chen Yi deduced that the Wan Family was one of the Xiao Family’s contingency plans.","Perhaps the Wan Family’s selling of their assets was also related to the Xiao Family.","’Are they raising silver coins for grain and provisions?’","’If so, the Wan Family is truly loyal to Elder Master Xiao.’","As Chen Yi considered this, he asked about the Sun Family from North City.","Unexpectedly, it was another family he had heard of before—the second young miss of the Sun Family was the wife of Bai Yelin, the Grain and Grass Supervisor for the Shu State Capital Commandery.","A long time ago, this Madam Sun had visited Xiao Wan’er, hoping to ask her to persuade Chen Yi to take her son, Bai Yutang, as his student.","However, because Chen Yi never agreed, the matter was dropped.","\"Is there anything unusual about this Sun Family?\"","Liu Lang thought for a moment. \"Unusual... I don’t think so.\"","\"But the Sun Family has a lot of grain. When I went over and offered thirteen taels of silver per dan, they agreed to sell without even haggling.\"","\"A lot?\"","\"Yes, a full ten thousand dan.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi laughed and shook his head. \"When a man gets to the top, all his friends and relations get there with him.\"","Seeing Liu Lang’s confusion, he explained the relationship between the Sun Family and the Bai Family.","Given Bai Yelin’s position as the Grain and Grass Supervisor, there was bound to be something fishy about the Sun Family’s grain supply.","The Capital Commandery was responsible for managing the supply and distribution of provisions for Shu State’s Three Towns and even Mengshui Pass.","Skimming just a little off the top could allow many people to live a lifetime of wealth and luxury.","After listening, Liu Lang said with a look of disdain, \"So they’re a bunch of parasites. No wonder they could produce so much grain.\"","He paused, then looked at Chen Yi. \"Boss, we have over fifty thousand dan of grain on hand now. What’s your plan?\"","\"Let’s hold onto it for now.\"","\"It’s not the right time to make a move yet.\"","Chen Yi gazed at the distant Shu State Prefecture City, a playful smile on his face.","\"This time, I’ll make them shoot themselves in the foot.\"","When Liu Lang saw his smile, he couldn’t help but shiver.","He mourned silently, ’I wonder who’s so unlucky as to be targeted by the Boss. Sigh.’","Of course, Chen Yi had no idea what he was thinking.","After they snuck back into the Prefecture City, he gave further instructions. \"Once you’ve spent all the silver coins from Wang Ji, just guard the grain with Xue Duanyun and the others.\"","\"If there’s a development, I’ll have someone come and inform you.\"","\"Alright...\"","...","「Four days passed in the blink of an eye.」","Public resentment in Shu State City had reached a boiling point.","The price of grain, which had dropped to nine taels per dan, had once again risen to twelve taels.","Even so, the grain trading companies in the East and West Markets still had long lines of people crowded in front of them.","Up to twenty thousand dan of grain were sold each day.","Fortunately, it had only been half a month since the price hike, so even the poorest families could hold on for a little longer.","The tragedy of people selling their sons and daughters had not yet occurred.","\"Is that damn Barbarian Prince in Shu State or not?\"","\"The Government Office officials have searched house-to-house three times recently, how have they not found him yet?\"","\"And those horse bandits from Poshisu Country! If you’re coming, then come. If not, fine, but at least give us a clear answer!\"","\"If this grain price keeps rising, whether the war happens or not will be the least of our worries. I’m afraid we won’t be able to afford to eat!\"","\"Isn’t that the truth?\"","It wasn’t just the common folk; even some of the Noble Families with fewer landholdings couldn’t withstand such a drain on their resources.","When grain prices rose, other goods like medicinal herbs and meat would follow suit.","The larger the household, the more staggering the daily expenditure of silver coins became.","Take the Xiao Family, for example.","Even though they weren’t short on grain, their daily purchases for each residence cost dozens of taels of silver.","Who could bear such an expense?","Chen Yi saw all of this and knew he needed to move his plan forward.","Otherwise, his sins would be great.","Therefore, that night, he disguised himself and went to the Spring Rain Building alone.","Cui Qingwu and Lou Yuxue had been waiting for a long time. When they saw him arrive, both looked displeased.","\"You’ve got some nerve, Liu Wu! After setting things up, you just washed your hands of it all?\"","\"Do you really think the White Tiger Guard are your subordinates?\"","Chen Yi smiled and cupped his fists. \"My apologies, you two. My absence was purely a sign of my faith in your abilities.\"","Cui Qingwu snorted. \"I think you’re just pushing your luck!\"","Lou Yuxue was about to chime in, but she had dealt with \"Liu Wu\" several times before and knew he must have come with a purpose. Instead, she said:","\"According to the plan, Simurgh Phoenix has already started cooperating with those few grain trading companies. A portion of the grain sold recently came from her.\"","\"And the price of grain has already reached the previous twelve taels. What’s next?\"","\"Next, of course, it’s Miss Cui’s turn to shine.\"","Chen Yi said as if it were obvious, \"I’ve received word that the horse bandits from Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race are already approaching the Prefecture City.\"","Cui Qingwu and Lou Yuxue were shocked. \"What?!\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"It’s fake.\"","Cui Qingwu and Lou Yuxue glanced at each other, then frowned and asked, \"What’s fake? What’s real? Tell us the truth.\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"You’ll find out soon enough.\"","Lou Yuxue couldn’t help but remind him, \"I know you’re a master of schemes, but the matter of Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race is serious. You can’t be reckless.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi thought for a moment, then revealed a few details before concluding:","\"In short, Miss Cui just needs to wait for those grain trading companies to come knocking.\"","\"When the time comes, all you have to do is sell them the grain you have at a high price.\"","Cui Qingwu roughly understood what he was planning. She gave him a deep look and said:","\"If the Pavilion Master hadn’t personally invited you to join the White Tiger Guard, we definitely wouldn’t be going along with this madness.\"","Lou Yuxue nodded in deep agreement. \"You actually dared to find people to pose as horse bandits from Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race to attack passing merchants. You...\"","She looked at Chen Yi and asked, \"Aren’t you afraid of being arrested by the Imperial Court?\"","Chen Yi gave a deliberately mysterious smile. \"Truth and lies... who can really tell the difference?\"","If those grain trading companies didn’t suffer a huge loss, how would they become desperate enough to take drastic measures?","The name of the Ji State Trading Company still inspires a certain amount of fear in Shu State.","\"Enough idle talk.\"","\"I came here for another reason. I need you two to help me with something...\""]},{"number":454,"title":"Chapter 454 - 279: Upper Fifth Grade","paragraphs":["The person Chen Yi was looking for was none other than Du Cang, the Grand General of the Poshisu Country’s Peacock King Banner who had previously met with Liu Hong.","For the past few days, he had been trying to find the man.","To that end, he had even snuck into Liu Hong’s mansion.","But the man named Du Cang seemed to have vanished into thin air.","He hadn’t shown his face anywhere in Shu State Prefecture City, nor had he met with anyone else from Poshisu Country.","Chen Yi was somewhat worried.","\"Your White Tiger Guard has an extensive network in Shu State Prefecture City. Help me find him.\"","Lou Yuxue and Cui Qingwu exchanged a glance, their brows furrowing slightly.","\"The Grand General of the Peacock King Banner, Du Cang... He’s actually in Shu State?\"","\"Liu Wu, is your information reliable?\"","Chen Yi grunted in affirmation. Seeing their expressions, he couldn’t help but ask, \"You know of him?\"","Lou Yuxue nodded, her expression growing serious.","\"Du Cang is a very low-profile individual and seldom appears on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.\"","\"But within the Peacock King Banner, he’s King Landu’s right-hand man.\"","\"His status is even higher than Lv Jiunan’s.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"You mean he’s very powerful?\"","Lou Yuxue shook her head. \"It’s not as simple as being powerful.\"","\"He’s infamous within the Peacock King Banner for his viciousness. He’ll stop at nothing to achieve his goals.\"","\"It is said that when the Peacock King Banner was just starting to rise, Du Cang led his men to slaughter several of Poshisu Country’s small city-states in order to expand their power.\"","\"They killed every adult, man or woman, and only spared the children under ten.\"","Lou Yuxue paused for a moment before Cui Qingwu added, \"And he used a Black Magic Master’s Secret Technique to wipe the children’s minds.\"","\"Those children have since grown up to become the core of the Peacock King Banner, known as the ’Jackal Army.’\"","\"Although Du Cang doesn’t personally lead the Jackal Army, I’ve heard they obey him implicitly.\"","\"That’s why Du Cang was able to become King Landu’s right-hand man.\"","After listening, Chen Yi frowned slightly. ’Du Cang...’","’No wonder he was able to force Liu Hong to back down.’","’So it wasn’t just because King Landu had leverage over Liu Hong.’","\"That name doesn’t sound like it’s from Poshisu Country, does it?\"","Lou Yuxue nodded. \"You’re right. Du Cang is from Great Wei.\"","\"Oh? Then why would he follow King Landu?\"","\"His specific origins can no longer be traced.\"","\"Our White Tiger Guard spies over there have only sent back fragmented information.\"","\"Supposedly, Du Cang was once a stablehand for a family merchant caravan. He was seriously injured in an attack by horse bandits and was saved by King Landu.\"","\"After that, he became the disciple of a Black Magic Master. It turned out he had an incredible talent for Black Magic, and in just fifteen years, he became a Black Magic Master of the Upper Three Grades.\"","’Upper Three Grades...’","Chen Yi nodded thoughtfully. \"Sounds like he won’t be easy to deal with.\"","’Of course, that just means he won’t be easy to deal with.’","’The Black Magic that Black Magic Masters specialized in certainly had its merits, but it also had glaring weaknesses.’","’At least, that was true for him.’","’But if Du Cang had other plans, things could get complicated.’","\"Then I’ll leave it to you two to track him down.\"","\"If you find any trace of him, please let me know. I’ll go pay him a visit.\"","Hearing this, Lou Yuxue hesitated before saying, \"I know your Cultivation and Techniques aren’t weak.\"","\"But Du Cang has been famous for years, and he has the Jackal Army to back him up. I’m afraid you won’t have an easy time facing him alone.\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"Don’t worry, Miss Yuxue. I never do anything I’m not sure of.\"","\"You...\"","Before Lou Yuxue could finish, Cui Qingwu cut her off with a raised hand. \"Instead of worrying about him, you should be worrying about yourself.\"","\"Don’t forget, we still haven’t reported what we’ve been doing recently to the Lord General.\"","At this, she shot Lou Yuxue a sideways glance before turning to Chen Yi with a pointed remark:","\"Or have you taken a fancy to this fellow? Want to run off and live happily ever after with him?\"","Lou Yuxue froze, then her face flushed with anger. She glared at her. \"Simurgh Phoenix, stop spouting nonsense!\"","\"If I’m wrong, why are you getting so flustered?\"","\"When did I get flustered? You—you’re being ridiculous!\"","\"Cat got your tongue? Heh...\"","\"To be fair, your taste isn’t half bad. ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu is one of the most notable Spearmen in Shu State in recent years.\"","\"You’re still talking?!\"","\"I...\"","Watching them bicker, Chen Yi shook his head helplessly, then rose and walked toward the door.","\"I’ll leave these two matters to you, then.\"","\"If you get any news on Du Cang, you can have someone post a notice in front of the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office. Just leave the line: *Where in this vast world can a soulmate be found?*\"","\"I’ll come find you when I see it.\"","As his voice faded, Chen Yi vanished from the meditation room.","Leaving Cui Qingwu and Lou Yuxue alone, glaring at each other.","「A moment later.」","Cui Qingwu was the first to look away, her gaze following the direction Chen Yi had vanished. \"He’s gone. Sit down, let’s talk.\"","Lou Yuxue shot her a glare, then took a deep breath and sat down across from her.","\"Whatever you want to say, just say it.\"","\"Don’t you think Liu Wu’s plan is a bit too audacious?\"","\"Dealing with Lv Jiunan and Left King Mu Hage’s son was one thing; after all, they weren’t here for him.\"","\"But everything that followed—framing the Ji State Trading Company, impersonating horse bandits from Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race—every single one is a capital offense.\"","Cui Qingwu paused, looking at Lou Yuxue. \"Why exactly do you value him so highly?\"","\"Or are you really planning to run off with him?\"","Lou Yuxue snorted. \"The fact that he was personally chosen by the Lord Pavilion Master is enough reason for me to take a few risks.\"","\"That’s not enough.\"","\"The Pavilion Master is far away in the Capital Prefecture. Any news he receives is already two or three days behind what we know.\""]},{"number":455,"title":"Chapter 455 - 279: Upper Fifth Grade","paragraphs":["\"Just because he valued Liu Wu before doesn’t mean he does now.\"","Cui Qingwu’s expression grew more serious. \"How can you be so sure his actions won’t bring disaster to Shu State?\"","\"Think about it. If horse bandits from the Poshisu Country and soldiers from the Barbarian Race show up in Shu State, the entire Great Wei Dynasty will be shaken.\"","\"You and I know it’s a sham, but others won’t. In fact...\"","She glanced north of the Spring Rain Building, her words loaded with meaning. \"In fact, a certain someone might even seize this opportunity to take complete control of the Dingyuan Army!\"","Lou Yuxue’s expression wavered. \"I... I trust him!\"","Seeing her reluctance to elaborate, Cui Qingwu gave her a long, hard look and didn’t press the matter further.","She rose and walked toward the door. \"I’ve said my piece. The rest is for you to consider.\"","Just as she reached the door, she paused, turned back, and broke into a smile.","\"Of course, I do hope what he’s doing is truly just to take the Ji State Trading Company down a notch.\"","\"If that’s the case, it would be a great service to you, to me, and to our White Tiger Guard.\"","With that, Cui Qingwu glanced at Lou Yuxue, gave a wave and a quick \"I’m off,\" then vanished through the doorway.","Lou Yuxue watched her disappear, mouthing a name.","\"Simurgh Phoenix...\"","\"Bastard!\"","As she cursed, an inexplicable mix of vexation and embarrassment crept onto Lou Yuxue’s face.","It was unclear whether she was flustered for having lost their verbal spar with Cui Qingwu, or for some other reason.","In any case, she was in a foul mood.","She sat in silence for a long while.","Finally, Lou Yuxue let out a long sigh.","She still held firm to her judgment: ’This man, Liu Wu, can be trusted!’","Even if the Lord Pavilion Master hadn’t invited Liu Wu to join the White Tiger Guard, she would still believe him to be trustworthy.","The reason was simple.","A man who would kill Lv Jiunan and take on the Ji State Trading Company could hardly be an enemy of the White Tiger Guard.","She judged him by her own standards.","If it were her, she would have killed Lv Jiunan given the chance, as the Great Wei Dynasty and the Poshisu Country were already enemies.","By the same token, she wished for nothing more than the destruction of the Ji State Trading Company.","Therefore, based on these two actions alone, she trusted Liu Wu.","His true identity was a secondary concern.","With these thoughts in mind, Lou Yuxue summoned a subordinate. \"Send word to investigate any suspicious individuals entering or leaving Shu State.\"","\"Their description is as follows: short in stature, with a treacherous face and vicious eyes.\"","The subordinate acknowledged the order and departed.","Just as Lou Yuxue began to relax, another voice called from outside the door.","\"The Lord General requests your presence.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"One moment.\"","Lou Yuxue’s expression flickered. She rose, put on her bamboo hat, draped a black cloak over her shoulders, and left her private room.","After a moment’s thought, she asked the messenger to wait again, returned to her quarters, and retrieved a letter to bring with her.","「Not long after.」","The two of them left the Spring Rain Building and made their way to a tailor’s shop in the West Market, one following the other.","The General, dressed in a long, blue robe, was waiting by the door.","Lou Yuxue was about to bow when the General smiled and waved her off. \"Let’s talk inside.\"","Lou Yuxue nodded and followed him into the back room of the tailor’s shop.","The messenger stood guard at the entrance.","Once the door was closed.","Lou Yuxue bowed with her fists clasped. \"Sir, was your journey a success?\"","The General sat down at the table, first shaking his head with a smile, then nodding. \"Not entirely, but I’ve made some headway.\"","\"I’ve called you here this time because I’d like your advice.\"","\"Please speak freely, Sir.\"","\"On my trip to the Ancient Tea-Horse Road, I didn’t get to see King Landu, but I did get a firm answer from him.\"","\"If I want to trade for that ’evidence’ he holds, he needs me to do something for him.\"","Lou Yuxue asked hesitantly, \"Is this about Lv Jiunan?\"","From the reports she had been receiving, it wasn’t hard for her to deduce King Landu’s intentions on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.","’He wants to avenge his brother, Lv Jiunan!’","The General sighed. \"His reaction was understandable, yet still surprising.\"","\"I only learned when I arrived that Lv Jiunan wasn’t just his brother. He had also arranged a marriage alliance for him with another horse bandit clan.\"","\"With Lv Jiunan dead, the Peacock King Banner has lost a key ally. No wonder King Landu is so furious.\"","Lou Yuxue’s expression eased slightly. \"So, does this mean he’s determined to have Liu Wu killed?\"","The General nodded and looked at her. \"I won’t hide it from you.\"","\"King Landu’s condition is that we reveal Liu Wu’s whereabouts to his men.\"","\"His men?\"","A thought struck Lou Yuxue. \"Sir, are you talking about... Du Cang?\"","The General let out a sound of surprise. \"How could you know about that?\"","\"Has Du Cang already appeared in Shu State?\"","Lou Yuxue grumbled inwardly. She gave a wry smile and shook her head. \"There’s something you don’t know, Sir.\"","\"I just saw Liu Wu an hour ago. He... he already knows that Du Cang is in Shu State. He even asked me to help track him down.\"","\"Well, that’s... quite the coincidence.\"","’How strange.’","The General found the whole thing odd.","He knew for a fact that Du Cang had come alone. Never mind the general populace of Shu State; very few people even within the Peacock King Banner were aware of his mission.","’So how did Liu Wu find out?’","With this in mind, the General mused aloud, \"Then tell me what you think. Would it be feasible to reveal his whereabouts to King Landu?\"","Lou Yuxue’s immediate impulse was to shake her head, but she caught herself, suppressed the urge, and said with a neutral expression:","\"I believe... that would be unwise.\"","\"Oh? Continue.\"","\"Sir, please take a look at this.\"","Lou Yuxue took a letter from her sleeve and handed it to him. \"Liu Wu gave this to me. It’s a letter written by Lin Huai’an of the Ji State Trading Company to King Landu regarding a trade for ironware.\"","\"Ironware?\"","The General opened the letter. One page was written in the Poshisu script, the other in the official language of the Central Plains.","He focused, however, on the page with the Poshisu script.","After a moment, a faint smile graced his lips, and he muttered \"Good, good...\" a few times.","\"It seems I no longer need to consider making a deal with King Landu.\""]},{"number":456,"title":"Chapter 456 - 279: Upper Fifth Grade","paragraphs":["\"With this, why would I have to worry...\"","The General paused and looked at Lou Yuxue. \"Did Liu Wu give you this? Where did he get it?\"","\"According to him, he was nearby the night Lin Huai’an died. He got this letter from Lin Huai’an as well.\"","\"Did he kill Lin Huai’an?\"","\"That’s what I asked him, but he didn’t admit to it. He claimed someone else was responsible.\"","Having said her piece, Lou Yuxue knew she had dissuaded the General from revealing \"Liu Wu’s\" whereabouts to King Landu. She chose her words carefully and said:","\"Sir, I actually have another plan.\"","The General put the letter away, still pondering the origin of the iron object connected to it. \"Let’s hear it.\"","\"Since ’Liu Wu’ is also looking for Du Cang, why don’t we reveal his location to ’Liu Wu’?\"","\"Oh? You mean... we pretend we’re going to reveal ’Liu Wu’s’ location, but in reality, we lure Du Cang into a trap?\"","\"That is precisely my thinking.\"","\"This way, you can also use the opportunity to obtain more ’evidence’ from King Landu, can’t you, Sir?\"","The General laughed after hearing her out, repeatedly voicing his approval. \"As expected of someone about to be promoted to Golden Banner Officer. You certainly have a quick mind.\"","Lou Yuxue smiled faintly. \"You flatter me, Sir.\"","The General gave her a look that was not quite a smile and asked, \"Aren’t you afraid Liu Wu will die at Du Cang’s hands?\"","Lou Yuxue stiffened for a moment, then bowed. \"Either way, it benefits our White Tiger Guard.\"","’It’d be best if that bastard suffers a huge loss.’","’Hmph.’","’But still...’","’That was just a thought.’","However, Lou Yuxue remembered \"Liu Wu’s\" reaction when he learned of Du Cang’s Cultivation—he was as calm as still water.","It was as if he didn’t take a Black Magic Master with Upper Three Grades Cultivation seriously at all.","’She refused to believe that bastard would dare to be so arrogant.’","\"Then we’ll do as you say. I’ll send a message to the other side shortly. But as for Liu Wu...\"","\"I will explain it to him.\"","\"Good...\"","...","「Xiao Mansion, Spring Lotus Garden.」","Chen Yi, of course, had no idea he had just narrowly avoided a disaster. He was sitting cross-legged on his bed, practicing his Four Symbols Skill.","After the past few days of Cultivation, he had already absorbed some of the Profound Mysteries from the Perfection Realm of [Martial Arts·Body], using them to break through his [Big Spear Pile Skill], [Black Tortoise Concealment Technique], and [Four Symbols Skill] to the Perfect Level.","However, because it had only been a short time, the three Cultivation Techniques still had room for improvement.","Even so, the boost to his abilities was still considerable.","His Power, which had not improved for a long time, had grown to the Power of Five Symbols thanks to the breakthrough in his [Big Spear Pile Skill].","The force of a single punch was a full ten thousand jin, comparable to that of an ordinary Sixth Grade Realm Martial Artist.","The Black Tortoise Concealment Technique had also made significant progress.","Beyond its breath concealment effect, the abilities for Nourishing the Body and increasing essence granted by the [Four Symbols Skill]’s Spiritual Essence had reached an even higher level.","Even without deliberate Cultivation, he could increase his Spiritual Essence just by using the [Black Tortoise Concealment Technique], enhancing the power of all his Techniques.","As for the [Four Symbols Skill] itself, it had naturally improved as well.","It could likely shorten the time needed to break through a minor realm within the Fifth Grade from ten days to eight.","Furthermore, as he gradually absorbed the Profound Mysteries of [Martial Arts·Body] and raised the level of his [Four Symbols Skill], his Cultivation speed would only increase.","Besides these three major Cultivation Techniques, the biggest improvement was to his [Mountain Shattering Fist], which had been elevated to the Celestial Tier thanks to Immortal Bai’s rank-up.","Unlike the [Dragon-slaying Spear]’s advancement to the Celestial Tier, the Celestial Tier [Mountain Shattering Fist] didn’t just add new moves.","Instead, it gained the \"Mountain Shattering Force,\" which possessed the power to shatter mountains and crack the earth.","If he mastered it to Perfection, Chen Yi could stack the \"Mountain Shattering Force\" onto any move he executed.","In other words, when executing the Dragon-Falling Spear Technique, he could use the Mountain Shattering Force to enhance the power of his Spear Technique.","However, this was limited to the instant the Long Spear made contact with an enemy, different from how one could freely project and stack True Essence or the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","Despite this, it still greatly enhanced Chen Yi’s close-quarters combat prowess.","As midnight approached, Chen Yi slowly ended his cultivation session, rising from the bed and clenching his fists.","’Upper Fifth Grade... Tsk, my Cultivation speed has really increased quite a bit.’","’I was right to raise [Martial Arts·Body] to Perfection back then.’","’If I had chosen something like Martial Arts Step or Blade, my current Cultivation and other Techniques would never have progressed this much.’","’Even improving a Fist Technique would have been the same. At most, it would have enhanced my close-quarters combat, not provided such a comprehensive boost like this.’","Chen Yi walked to the window, gazing at the night-time scenery in the courtyard as he mused to himself.","’The Ji State Trading Company are just small fries. The most important one is still... Liu Hong...’","A cold, late-autumn wind blew past, and leaves drifted slowly down.","The tips of his hair danced across his forehead, and a faint smile appeared on his otherwise calm face.","’I should get moving, too.’","’Come to think of it, it’s been a while since Liu Hong’s second son has shown his face.’","Just then, a golden light flashed—","[Daily Intel · Profound-rank Lower Grade: At 9:45 AM, Duke Dingyuan, Xiao Yuan, has requested a meeting with Chen Yi, the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall. A minuscule Opportunity can be obtained.]","After reading it, Chen Yi couldn’t help but chuckle.","’Chen Yi, the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall?’","’This Opportunity is a sure thing...’"]},{"number":457,"title":"Chapter 457 - 280: It’s Really You?","paragraphs":["The night passed uneventfully.","The sky had just begun to brighten.","Gloomy, dark clouds already pressed down on Shu State Prefecture City.","A misty layer of clouds obscured the rising sun in the east, like an extension of the night, reluctant to let the morning come.","But the Night Watchman still made his rounds on time, crying out the hour.","Drums also sounded from the tower above the city gate.","Whenever this happened, bells from the temple in the northwest corner, the academy to the north, and outside Yanhua Lane in the south would answer in chorus.","With the harmonious tolling of bells and beating of drums, a new day arrived.","Chen Yi, of course, didn’t wait until then to get up.","To be precise, he had been rising early these past few days, washing up and dressing before heading to the study.","Of course, he wasn’t going there to practice his calligraphy or to create a few paintings.","He was going there to read.","That’s right.","Chen Yi had been preparing for the Annual Examination at the end of the month for several days now.","Besides the history and geography books he had read during his confinement, this time he was focusing more on the classics and historical records.","Although the Great Wei Dynasty didn’t have the Four Books and Five Classics, it had similar canonical texts.","These included works like Magic Calculation, the River Book, Qian’s Transmission, and the Sayings of the Four Sages, among others.","Covering astronomy, geography, divination, the Medical Dao, and Confucianism, they were required reading for every scholar.","Chen Yi originally had some memories related to these texts, but they were very vague.","But as he read through them, the relevant content would surface in his mind.","Most of it was the original owner of his body’s understanding.","However, most of that understanding was flawed.","At least, in the eyes of Chen Yi, who had stepped into the Dao Realm through Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting, these so-called classics were merely the past sages’ insights into heaven and earth, the Great Dao, life, and the world.","He had his own understanding.","Therefore, after reading through the classics once, Chen Yi simplified the complex, assimilating all the memories for his own use.","Coupled with his absorption of the Profound Mysteries from various Daos, which allowed him to draw parallels and comprehend more broadly, he believed he could hold his own in a debate with the likes of Mr. Zhuo Ying and Mr. Lingchuan.","It was more than enough to handle an ordinary Annual Examination.","Unfortunately, this year’s Annual Examination was anything but ordinary.","Chen Yi had no choice but to make extra preparations.","Just then, Xiaodie entered with two Armored Warriors, each carrying stacks of books. While gesturing where they should place them, she said:","\"Young Master, here are the past exam questions from the Annual and Prefecture Examinations for Shu State and other state capitals.\"","\"However, few people have collected the top-scoring essays, so there are only some scattered pieces.\"","Chen Yi looked up and nodded. \"This will be enough to keep me busy until the Annual Examination.\"","His method was none other than the study habit ingrained in his very being—cramming with practice questions.","As long as he practiced enough, it was hard to say if he’d get an outstanding score, but he could at least pass.","And if he had a flash of inspiration during the exam, or if it touched upon his own areas of knowledge, it wasn’t impossible for him to produce a brilliant, renowned essay.","Seeing him say this, the tension on Xiaodie’s small face eased.","\"Young Master, you should read then. I’ll go prepare breakfast for you.\"","Chen Yi raised a hand to stop her. \"Just prepare some for yourself. I’m going to the academy this morning. I’ll eat something there.\"","Xiaodie said, \"Oh. Young Master, when will you be back? The Eldest Young Miss said there’s a banquet in the mansion at noon.\"","\"I probably won’t make it back before noon.\"","Chen Yi knew exactly who Xiao Wan’er was hosting. It would be a miracle if he showed up.","Yesterday afternoon, after receiving a message from Elder Master Xiao via Wang Ji, he knew that Xiao Wan’er was planning to host him—the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall—today.","That’s why he had planned from early this morning not to stay in the mansion.","To avoid having Xiao Wan’er ask him to keep the guest company.","Xiaodie, unsuspecting, bowed and left the study with the two Armored Warriors.","Chen Yi watched her depart, then put down his book, stood up, and went to the side room to take out his masks and other items.","Once everything was in order, he leisurely left Spring Lotus Garden.","\"Greetings, Young Master.\"","\"Greetings, Young Master.\"","\"...\"","Along the way, the Maids and Household Servants of the Marquis’s Mansion all bowed and greeted him.","Chen Yi returned their greetings one by one. As he passed through the central courtyard, he glanced in the direction of the Qingjing Residence.","Seeing it was just as it had been the past few days, he knew that nothing major had happened in Shu State City.","It wasn’t that the Marquis’s Mansion was particularly well-informed.","Rather, for the past few days, Liu Hong had been visiting daily to report on the situation in the city.","He always came first thing in the morning, as if afraid the Old Marquis would write a petitionary memorial and send it to the Capital Prefecture.","Chen Yi was aware of all this, so he also understood that as long as Asutai didn’t appear and King Landu made no move, there would be no major disturbances in the Prefecture City.","At most, there would only be daily fluctuations in the prices of goods like grain, vegetables, and meat.","He arrived at the front courtyard.","He greeted Wang Lixing, Liu Si’er, and the others, exchanged a few words, and asked about the recent situation.","Although Wang Lixing wasn’t talkative, he didn’t hide anything from him.","\"Scouts flying the Peacock King Banner have been spotted on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road. All caravans have recently suspended their plans to travel west.\"","\"However, many people in the Prefecture City aren’t worried about King Landu coming. Most of them assume he wouldn’t dare.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"Horse bandits excel at moving like the wind, but they’re likely lacking when it comes to storming cities and capturing strongholds.\"","Liu Si’er chimed in, \"The Young Master is right.\"","\"Although King Landu is a Grandmaster, he can only fight ten thousand men at once. Faced with high city walls and passes, he alone would be stretched thin.\"","\"Besides, the western passes are heavily guarded, and there are two experts of the Upper Three Grades Realm within the passes. If the Peacock King Banner wants to break through, they will surely suffer heavy losses.\"","\"Brother Si has a point.\"","\"Still, I kind of hope he does bring his men. That way, the Master and the Second Young Miss can finally lead the Dingyuan Army west.\"","The Armored Warriors were a restless bunch. They all started talking at once, their voices overlapping, but they shared a single desire: war.","For Personal Guards like them, military merit was also necessary for promotion.","Only if Elder Master Xiao or Xiao Jinghong led the troops into battle would they have a chance to see action.","Otherwise, they would be stuck as Personal Guards for their entire lives, unable to become independent commanders like Li Changqing and Pang Xuan."]},{"number":458,"title":"Chapter 458 - 280: It’s Really You?","paragraphs":["Wang Lixing naturally hoped for the same, but he was more rational.","\"My fear is that the Barbarian Race will use the matter of that Crown Prince as a pretext to attack with their army.\"","\"Aren’t you overthinking this, Brother Xing? There’s been no word from outside Mengshui Pass to the south. Things probably won’t get to the worst-case scenario.\"","\"Let’s hope so...\"","After those few brief words, Chen Yi bid them farewell and left the Marquis’s Mansion, heading toward North City.","Although the city was currently in some turmoil, it wasn’t chaotic overall.","The Noble Families and scholars, in particular, were worldly and knowledgeable. They wouldn’t be stirred to action by a few mere rumors.","If they remained calm, the vast majority of the city’s populace wouldn’t panic.","And if the people weren’t in turmoil, the few major grain merchants wouldn’t be too anxious.","Chen Yi had anticipated this long ago.","That was why he had prepared for so long.","’When things reach an extreme, they reverse. To take, one must first give... It’s fine to let them be happy for now...’","Mulling this over, Chen Yi wound his way to a residence next to the East Market.","Wang Ji was already waiting there.","Chen Yi greeted him and, while applying a disguise, asked, \"Have you heard from Zhang Dabao?\"","Holding up a brocade robe that had been prepared earlier, Wang Ji said respectfully, \"They have already rendezvoused with Dabao.\"","\"As you instructed, they’ve split into two groups, one in the west and one in the south.\"","\"They’re just waiting for your order to act.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment. \"Good, as long as the items were delivered.\"","\"Rest assured, my lord. How could this lowly one dare to delay the tasks you’ve assigned?\"","Wang Ji bowed and continued, \"It’s just that the disciples of the Celestial Sect have only just arrived. This lowly one is worried they might leak information.\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"I’ve met Xue Duanyun and the others before. With them there, it shouldn’t be a big problem.\"","It wasn’t that he subscribed to the principle of ’trusting those you employ,’ but rather that he believed Xue Duanyun and the others wouldn’t dare.","Even though the task he’d given Zhang Dabao was of great importance, based on what Xue Duanyun and the others had learned about him these past few days, they would at least try to carry it out first.","If they sensed something was wrong, they’d have an escape route.","Besides, the disciples of the Celestial Sect were all Jianghu People; they rarely concerned themselves with matters of the Imperial Court.","As long as it wasn’t treason or wantonly taking lives, they would do it, even with apprehension in their hearts.","Chen Yi had already considered this point and had made preparations long ago.","That’s why he had Wang Ji deliver the Immortal Drunk and Qingfeng Drunk—to ensure they wouldn’t have to harm anyone.","A short while later, Chen Yi had finished his preparations and looked at his reflection in the Copper Mirror.","His features were handsome, his demeanor calm and extraordinary. He said, \"Remember, from now on, if anyone asks, you are to say that I visited the Old Marquis today only to discuss the expansion of Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","Wang Ji acknowledged, \"Understood,\" and asked, \"Then, what about the young miss?\"","\"Tell her the same thing.\"","Chen Yi had his own plans. He knew there were some things he could discuss with the Elder Master but couldn’t reveal to Xiao Wan’er.","\"This lowly one will remember.\"","\"Good. Let’s go.\"","Soon, Wang Ji drove the horse-drawn carriage out of the residence.","Chen Yi sat upright, leaning back in the carriage and looking outside.","The late autumn wind occasionally blew the curtain aside.","At some point, a light rain began to fall.","The pedestrians on the road quickened their pace.","But there were also many bold members of the Jianghu who, relying on their Cultivation, ambled along unhurriedly, stopping and starting as they pleased.","Most of them carried bamboo hats on their backs, their clothes disheveled, looking travel-worn.","Those traveling in groups would talk about Jianghu matters.","The most discussed topic, naturally, was \"Immortal Bai\"—his purpose for coming to Shu State, when he might arrive, and so on.","But it was clear they were bound to be disappointed.","\"Immortal Bai\" had not only come, but had already left.","Seeing there was no new information, Chen Yi focused his mind, his handsome face settling into a calm expression.","A moment later, the carriage stopped outside the Xiao Mansion.","Wang Ji went forward and exchanged a few words with the Third Steward, Lu Guan, who was guarding the entrance. The main gates then swung open.","Without waiting for Wang Ji to return, Chen Yi stepped down from the carriage.","Lu Guan sized him up and greeted him with a smile, \"Boss Chen, it’s been a while. You’re looking as sharp as ever.\"","Chen Yi bowed slightly without speaking.","Seeing as he had brought the Xiao Mansion a considerable amount of silver, Lu Guan didn’t find his silence arrogant.","He led the way.","Chen Yi and Wang Ji followed behind him.","The three of them had just crossed the front courtyard when they saw two people approaching from a short distance away.","It was none other than Liu Hong and Zhao Liuan.","Lu Guan stopped, whispered their identities, and then bowed respectfully to Liu Hong.","\"Lord Liu.\"","Chen Yi followed suit and bowed as well.","Liu Hong nodded with a smile, but his gaze was sizing up Chen Yi.","Liu Hong didn’t recognize Chen Yi, but he did recognize Wang Ji and knew he was the Shopkeeper of Hundred Herbs Hall.","It wasn’t difficult, then, to guess Chen Yi’s current identity.","Clearly, however, a mere merchant wasn’t worth more than a few words, so he hurriedly left the Marquis’s Mansion with Zhao Liuan.","\"My lord, that man must be the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall, Chen Yu.\"","\"Mm.\"","\"His visit to the Marquis’s Mansion today... could it be that the Old Marquis...\"","\"It’s of no concern. The Xiao Family’s finances now rely heavily on the profits from Hundred Herbs Hall. The Old Marquis summoned him, most likely for the sake of silver.\"","Liu Hong glanced back at the grand, high-gated mansion, a meaningful smile appearing on his face.","For a mere merchant to be received with the main gates of the Xiao Mansion wide open was a clear sign of the Xiao Family’s decline.","Zhao Liuan noticed his expression and made an inference.","\"My lord, are you returning to your residence or going to the Government Office?\"","The smile vanished from Liu Hong’s face. He looked toward South City and said, \"No rush. Let’s make a trip to Spring Rain Building first.\"","Zhao Liuan froze, a look of alarm on his face.","\"My lord, for you to go personally would be a breach of decorum. It would be better to let your subordinate go instead.\"","Liu Hong shook his head. \"For some matters, the result is not important. The attitude is.\"","Lately, he had tried every possible way to find Asutai, but he still couldn’t locate him.","With the deadline Du Cang had given him fast approaching, he had no choice but to seek some outside help.","Of course, this was more about showing something to Du Cang.","That he, Liu Hong, was not afraid of a little slander.","’History has always been written by the victors. As long as I win, who will gossip?’","’And who would dare?’","Chen Yi, of course, was unaware of the pressure Liu Hong had been under recently. He was sitting quietly in the main hall of the Qingjing Residence, waiting for the Elder Master.","He was as calm and composed as he had been when he first met Xiao Wan’er as \"Chen Yu.\"","Although he had never thought of himself as an equal to the Elder Master, he had indeed come today with the intention of showing a bit of what he was capable of.","However, while his face was calm, his ears were burning slightly.","The Elder Master, in the inner hall, was not being discreet about his guest at all, \"whispering\" with the Commander of the Secret Guard, Xiao Jing.","\"Is it him?\"","\"Your subordinate... um... your subordinate cannot be certain.\"","\"However, your subordinate can feel the aura about him. His Cultivation is a great deal stronger than mine.\"","After hearing Xiao Jing’s words, the Elder Master nodded lightly and stood up to walk outside.","As he walked, he gestured. \"You come as well.\"","Xiao Jing hesitated slightly before acknowledging the order and following behind him.","Normally, as the Commander of the Xiao Family’s Hidden Guard, he wouldn’t meet with outsiders, or even members of the Xiao Family outside the main branch.","An order from the Elder Master was the only exception.","Before long, the two of them entered the main hall. Chen Yi calmly rose and bowed. \"Chen Yu of Hundred Herbs Hall greets the Marquis, and... Commander Xiao.\"","Elder Master Xiao’s initially calm smile vanished, and his eyes widened slightly as he sized him up.","In contrast to his master’s composure, shock was written all over Xiao Jing’s face.","\"You... you... it really is you?!\"","Chen Yi naturally knew who he was talking about. He cupped his fist. \"I hope Commander Xiao can forgive me. The situation was urgent, so I had to act according to the circumstances and hide my identity.\"","Before burning the summer grain of the Three Towns, he had rescued Xiao Jing from the Imprisonment Department.","Although Xiao Jing didn’t know his identity at the time, after witnessing him in action several times, he could deduce his general identity.","Especially since he had also revealed some information back then.","Xiao Jing stared at him, still in shock. \"Then, why did you...\"","Before he could finish, the Elder Master raised a hand to interrupt him, a smile returning to his face as he looked at Chen Yi.","\"Heroes have always emerged from the younger generation.\"","\"I didn’t believe it at first, but seeing you today, I know you are worthy of the title ’young hero’.\"","In his eyes, whether it was \"Chen Yu\" or \"Liu Wu,\" both were personas belonging to someone from the Jianghu.","And for doing so much for their Xiao Family, the young man before him was certainly worthy of being called a \"young hero.\"","\"I have only done a few small things. I am unworthy of the Marquis’s praise.\"","\"Heh heh, someone who dares to hire Bright Moon Building to burn the summer grain of the Three Towns doesn’t just do ’small things’.\"","The Elder Master spoke meaningfully, then leaned on his cane and sat in the seat of honor.","Chen Yi watched his back, knowing that last sentence carried a warning, so he didn’t rush to speak.","Seeing this, the Elder Master nodded to himself in approval and gestured for him to sit.","\"Since you’ve already decided to be open and honest with me, you must have come today to discuss a matter of great importance.\"","\"Speak...\""]},{"number":459,"title":"Chapter 459 - 281: Fortunately, This Person Is a Friend, Not an Enemy","paragraphs":["\"Go on.\"","Seeing Elder Master Xiao looking like he was all ears, a slight smile appeared on Chen Yi’s calm face.","It was faint, but sincere.","He had come to see Elder Master Xiao this time with the full intention of being open and honest.","There were two reasons for this.","First, Elder Master Xiao was an important and necessary part of his plans.","If the Elder Master could cooperate with him and react in a logical manner, it would fool the vast majority of people.","Second, there were certain matters Chen Yi had to inform the Elder Master about.","Furthermore, he also wanted to use this opportunity to probe Elder Master Xiao’s intentions, which would aid his subsequent plans.","This included matters concerning Liu Hong, the Jing State Liu Family, and others.","If Elder Master Xiao was unwilling to be ruthless, who in all of Shu State could openly execute them?","Conversely, if he were to use petty tricks like assassination, it would do far more harm than good in resolving the Xiao Family’s predicament.","Imagine if Liu Hong were assassinated by him—what would the numerous Government Offices in Shu State think? What would the Imperial Court think?","They would inevitably suspect the Xiao Family was behind it.","Chen Yi understood this, which was why he had decided to pay the Xiao Family a visit.","\"To avoid leaving anything out, I believe I need to start from the very beginning...\"","The beginning Chen Yi spoke of was the founding of Hundred Herbs Hall.","It was a rather cliché story.","After completing his studies and leaving his secluded life, he came to Shu State, seeking a place to settle down.","Wang Ji had made a grave mistake and was driven out of the Xiao Family by Xiao Wan’er, which led to their acquaintance.","The two hit it off and founded Hundred Herbs Hall.","After that, the details of selling the herbal tea and running the Medicine Hall went without saying.","Chen Yi focused on the night he killed Liu Erhu in front of Xiao Jing and the origins of the incident where the summer grain of the Three Towns was burned.","\"Ultimately, Liu Jing was killed by me.\"","Elder Master Xiao and Xiao Jing exchanged a look, their faces showing that this was just as they had expected.","Seeing this, Chen Yi smiled and said, \"I imagine the Marquis already knows the reason.\"","\"The matter of Liu Jing spending a great sum to commission assassins from Bright Moon Building to go to Hundred Herbs Hall and steal the herbal tea formula.\"","\"If the Xiao Family’s young mistress hadn’t arranged for the two Female Knights, Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang, to arrive at Hundred Herbs Hall beforehand, Wang Ji and the others would have died that night.\"","This was the most suitable reason Chen Yi could think of.","It was also a reason that wouldn’t arouse suspicion in Elder Master Xiao or Xiao Jing.","Unless they had been at the scene that night, Chen Yi’s motive for murder was perfectly sound and logical.","\"So, you killed Liu Jing?\"","\"Aren’t you afraid of retaliation from the Jing State Liu Family?\"","The moment the words left his mouth, Elder Master Xiao understood and shook his head with a smile.","\"I was being foolish.\"","\"You killed Liu Jing, and all of Shu State, as well as the Jing State Liu Family, pointed their fingers at my Xiao Family. No one suspected Hundred Herbs Hall at all.\"","\"And certainly, no one suspected you.\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"As long as Liu Jing was alive, he was a persistent threat.\"","\"It just so happened that at that time, the Xiao Family Medicine Hall had completely crushed Linglan Pavilion, and Liu Jing had also been ordered by the Jing State Liu Family to leave Shu State.\"","\"I was forced to resort to this last measure, implicating the Marquis and causing you trouble with the Liu Family. I hope you can forgive me.\"","Elder Master Xiao looked at him noncommittally.","To be honest, he was indeed somewhat displeased.","’To think that I, the dignified Duke Dingyuan of the Great Wei Dynasty, who has fought in countless campaigns for decades, would be manipulated by a junior in my old age.’","Anyone in his position would have felt some resentment.","Moreover, the matter of \"Liu Jing’s death\" had forced him to activate his secret connection with the Wan Family prematurely.","There were some losses, after all.","Xiao Jing glanced up at the Elder Master, knowing in his heart that given his grandfather’s temperament, he was surely holding back some anger.","After a moment of thought, he spoke up, asking, \"So, you were the one who proactively sought out Liu Jing’s men?\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"Their appearance outside the West Market that night was because I had sent a message to Liu Jing to discuss the herbal tea formula.\"","\"So, what Liu Erhu saw wasn’t entirely a fabrication.\"","Chen Yi paused slightly, then looked at Xiao Jing and said with feigned sincerity, \"I had intended to take care of him myself, but I didn’t expect Commander Xiao to act first.\"","Xiao Jing forced a smile. \"It was just a coincidence.\"","\"That night, I just didn’t want him to open his mouth and accuse the Xiao family.\"","\"If not for...\"","Before he could finish, Elder Master Xiao raised a hand to interrupt him and gestured for Chen Yi to continue.","\"Keep talking.\"","\"As for the burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain, what was your reason for that?\"","Chen Yi nodded and said with a smile, \"Even if the Marquis hadn’t asked, I was going to bring it up.\"","\"But in truth, I was not the one who initiated that incident. It was someone else...\"","He then proceeded, just as before, to tell a story that was ninety percent true and ten percent false.","He concealed the source of his intelligence.","He concealed his true reasons for eliminating Xiao Dongchen and Liu Wen.","He also concealed his connection to the White Tiger Guard and his collaboration with Lou Yuxue.","\"...And so, Liu Wen was killed by me outside Iron Wall Town, and Black Tooth died at the hands of General Jinghong while leading an attack on Cang Lang Military Town.\"","\"As for what happened after that, I’m sure the Marquis is already aware, so I won’t elaborate further.\"","At this point, Chen Yi stood and clasped his fist in his palm. \"Although everything I did was a result of a series of coincidences, it did indeed implicate the Xiao Family. I hope the Marquis can forgive me.\"","He apologized once more, his attitude as sincere as ever.","Elder Master Xiao leaned back in his chair, his expression calm, but his eyes were not.","With his experience, he naturally understood how difficult it was to achieve such an outcome.","This wasn’t something that could be accomplished with brute force alone.","In the Elder Master’s estimation, if he had wanted to pull this off, he would have needed to plant his own people around Liu Wen and Xiao Dongchen.","He would have even needed his men inside Bright Moon Building and among the so-called \"Financiers\" behind the scenes.","Otherwise, with unclear intelligence from all sides, it would only lead to failure.","If any single party had detected something unusual, the course of events would not have unfolded as they did—"]},{"number":460,"title":"Chapter 460 - 281: Fortunately, an Ally, Not an Enemy","paragraphs":["The Xiao Family had benefited, receiving three hundred thousand taels of silver.","The Three Towns suffered few losses; only Iron Wall Town lost some grain due to Li Changqing’s negligence.","Liu Wen and Black Tooth were dead.","Xiao Dongchen had taken his own life.","The second branch of the Xiao Family had fled to Guangyue Prefecture...","Not only had the Xiao Family been largely unaffected, but they had also profited greatly.","But this outcome astonished Elder Master Xiao even more. ’He did all of this by himself!’","Even counting \"Sword Madman\" Liu Lang, it was at most the work of one and a half people.","’How is that possible?’","Even if one man’s schemes were inhumanly clever, how could he have predicted everyone’s reactions? How could he have played all sides? How could he have set so many traps for others?","And it wasn’t as if Liu Wen, Xiao Dongchen, or Black Tooth were fools.","How could they have been so utterly defeated?","It was like two Go players of equal skill facing off. Winning by half a point at the end would be the absolute limit.","But a result of winning by three, four... or even more than ten points could only mean one thing.","The victor’s skill was simply on a completely different level.","Only then would the loser be so thoroughly crushed.","As Elder Master Xiao considered all this, he waved his hand. \"Chen... Young friend Yu, please, have a seat.\"","He had finally switched from calling him \"Young Hero\" to \"Young Friend.\"","Chen Yi relaxed slightly, realizing he had passed the first test of the day. He sat down as instructed.","Silence fell for a moment.","The Elder Master chuckled. \"Young friend, you have done so much for my Xiao Family. Logically, I should trust you.\"","\"But I have two questions, and I hope you will answer them truthfully.\"","The moment he finished speaking, the Elder Master’s posture straightened, and a hint of seriousness crossed his old, wrinkled face.","\"What is your reason for helping my Xiao Family?\"","\"And why are you targeting the Jing State Liu Family?\"","’Here it comes.’","Chen Yi had known all along that Elder Master Xiao wouldn’t be so easily fooled.","His backstory seemed plausible, but it couldn’t withstand real scrutiny. A wandering \"master\" was hardly a sufficient explanation.","The same went for his motives.","Especially killing Liu Wen and luring Xiao Dongchen into his trap.","Chen Yi’s mind raced. He smiled calmly and said, \"Actually, you and I share a certain connection.\"","\"Oh? And what connection might that be?\"","\"Years ago, I was saved by my master on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road, just before the Marquis crushed the Poshisu Country.\"","\"I had originally planned to seek revenge against the Poshisu Country after completing my training, but I later learned they had already fallen to the Marquis’s blade.\"","\"That is why, upon returning to Great Wei, I made Shu State my first stop. I simply wanted to express my gratitude.\"","Chen Yi had prepared this story long in advance.","It had many holes, but it was the most persuasive story he could come up with.","This was especially true given his identity as \"Liu Wu.\"","A young man with a deep-seated blood feud returns after completing his training, only to find his enemies already dead. Naturally, he would feel a sense of goodwill toward the person who had, in effect, avenged him.","And as it happened, he possessed considerable skills of his own.","But Chen Yi knew this alone wasn’t enough. He continued, \"Secondly, three years ago, I traveled with my master to the lands of the Barbarian Race.\"","\"While there, I was shown a kindness by someone.\"","Elder Master Xiao, with an expression that said, ’Let’s see how you’ll spin this,’ asked with a smile, \"And who was this person who showed you kindness, young friend? Surely not a member of the Barbarian Race?\"","\"Those barbarians would love nothing more than to eliminate me. They certainly wouldn’t let you return to Great Wei to help my Xiao Family.\"","Chen Yi smiled at his words and calmly uttered a name: \"She said her name was Fu Wanqing.\"","The moment he spoke, Elder Master Xiao, who had been smiling, shot to his feet, staring at Chen Yi with a mixture of anger, shock, and disbelief.","\"You bastard, do you know what you are saying?!\"","Even Xiao Jing, standing to the side, was stunned and stared blankly at Chen Yi.","\"Sir, you can’t make such wild claims! General Fu, the ’Dragon Spear,’ was surrounded and killed by the Barbarian Grandmaster Wen Kela five years ago. How... how could she be in their lands?\"","Seeing their reactions, Chen Yi knew he had achieved his objective.","He said unhurriedly, \"General Fu Wanqing is indeed still alive. Right now, she is with the Black Bear Tribe of the Barbarian Race.\"","\"Moreover, she is being treated as a guest of honor by Left King Mu Hage, responsible for teaching several of the princes about Great Wei.\"","\"Impossible!\"","\"Even if Wanqing weren’t dead, she would never take orders from the Barbarian Race!\"","\"She... she would never... she would never... COUGH, COUGH...\"","Elder Master Xiao was so furious he couldn’t finish his rebuke. His face flushed red as he hunched over, racked by coughs.","Xiao Jing ignored everything else and rushed forward to pat his back. \"Marquis, please calm yourself! Your health is what’s important.\"","\"COUGH, COUGH... I... I don’t believe you...\"","\"Marquis, I’ll summon a Physician for you at once.\"","\"No, no...\"","Seeing the situation, Chen Yi rose and took two steps forward. \"Commander Xiao, allow me to take a look.\"","Xiao Jing blocked his path, instantly on guard. \"What do you think you’re doing?\"","Chen Yi chuckled, nonplussed. As he activated his Qi Observation Skill to examine the Elder Master’s condition, he retrieved the case of silver needles from his robes.","Xiao Jing froze. \"You...\"","He had forgotten that Chen Yu, the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall, was also a Medical Saint Hand.","Just then, the Elder Master waved a hand, gesturing for him to move aside. He looked at Chen Yi and said through his coughs:","\"If he wanted to harm me, he wouldn’t need to resort to such means.\"","After a brief silence, Xiao Jing stepped aside and bowed. \"Thank you. It was I who was rude.\"","\"No matter.\"","After speaking, Chen Yi observed the Qi Mechanism within the Elder Master’s body, his brow furrowing slightly.","The Elder Master’s physical condition was much worse now than it had been just a few days prior.","His body, already frail from an accumulation of old injuries, now had new blockages and ruptures.","It was one disaster piled on top of another.","\"Elder Master, you haven’t been resting well these past few days, have you?\"","Xiao Jing looked ashamed. \"Lately, with the grain issue at Iron Wall Town, and the matters concerning Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race, the Marquis hasn’t had a single peaceful night’s sleep.\"","The Old Marquis gave a weak wave of his hand, leaned back in his chair, and looked at Chen Yi with a smile."]},{"number":461,"title":"Chapter 461 - 281: Fortunately, He Is a Friend, Not a Foe","paragraphs":["\"I know my own body. Young friend, just do what you must.\"","Chen Yi hummed in acknowledgment, but he couldn’t help but feel a pang of guilt.","His recent actions, besides affecting the people of Shu State, had ultimately implicated the Elder Master.","Fortunately, it wasn’t too late.","At this thought, he took a deep breath. Using his Qi Observation Skill, he clearly saw the locations of the Elder Master’s meridians and Sea of Qi.","Then, he picked up a Silver Needle and inserted it into the Elder Master’s body.","Then came the second, the third...","...until the twelfth Silver Needle was in place.","A Silver Needle now rested on a core acupoint of each of the Elder Master’s twelve meridians.","Only then did Chen Yi move both hands, circulating the True Essence within his body and using his full power to draw upon the surrounding Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","With an extremely exquisite and subtle technique, he guided the Spiritual Mechanism through the Silver Needles and into the Elder Master’s body.","Some of the Silver Needles vibrated unceasingly, some spiraled up and down, and others shifted their angles.","Under the Qi Observation Skill, he could see the Spiritual Mechanism flowing into the Elder Master’s body, mending his frame like silken threads.","Where there were old wounds, he infused life force, causing the old flesh to peel away as new flesh grew rapidly in its place.","Severed meridians were reconnected with the Spiritual Mechanism.","Damaged organs were also repaired.","The shattered Sea of Qi...","Although he couldn’t repair it completely, Chen Yi could at least reduce the extent of the damage.","The Elder Master’s complexion improved visibly, his face regaining much of its color.","Xiao Jing, watching from the side, seemed oblivious to the change. His eyes were fixed solely on Chen Yi, his expression even more shocked than when he had heard that Fu Wanqing was alive.","\"The Meridian Flowing Technique...\"","\"A Medical Skill rumored to be mastered only by those above the level of a Medical Saint Hand... it actually... it actually appeared in Chen Yu?\"","\"Has he... has his Medical Dao reached Great Success?!\"","\"This...\"","Xiao Jing didn’t know how to express what he was feeling.","A Physician who had reached Great Success in the Medical Dao was rare, but there were still several dozen in the entire Great Wei Dynasty.","A Spearman who had reached Perfection in the Spear Dao was also uncommon, but there were still quite a few.","But to find both in a single person was truly a rarity.","Even rarer than Xiao Jinghong, who was a master of both spear and sword.","After all, the Spear Dao and the Sword Dao both belonged to the path of Martial Arts and could offer mutual validation.","The Medical Dao was different.","It was a Great Dao whose threshold many could not cross in their entire lifetime, a path on par with the Dao of Martial Arts.","Yet no matter how shocked or disbelieving he was, the facts were right before his eyes. He had no choice but to believe.","About an hour passed.","Chen Yi waved his hand, pulling out the twelve Silver Needles. He let out a long breath and wiped the sweat from his forehead.","\"Marquis, your chronic ailments are difficult to fully remove. I hope you will take good care of yourself from now on.\"","That was what he said.","But the Elder Master seemed not to have heard him. He stood right up, raising his arms, stretching his legs, and patting his chest.","The expression on his face was complex, a mixture of joy and tears.","\"I... I... am I healed?\"","\"Not—\"","Before Chen Yi could finish, Elder Master Xiao burst out laughing. \"It’s been a long time since I’ve felt this unburdened.\"","\"Young friend, to think you possess such incredible Medical Skill... I, I...\"","Suddenly, he remembered their earlier conversation, and his smile vanished. \"I ask you, is Wanqing truly not dead?\"","Chen Yi was taken aback. He shook his head with a wry smile. \"She was indeed alive three years ago. As for now, I do not know.\"","’What Asutai said should have some credibility.’","’But I can’t be one hundred percent certain.’","\"Good. I’ll believe you for now!\"","Perhaps because his physical condition had improved, the Elder Master now stood remarkably straight and tall.","Although his frame was still gaunt, his imposing aura already showcased the presence of the Great Wei’s Marquis Wu.","He looked directly at Chen Yi and asked in a deep voice, \"You’ve said so much. You must have an important matter to discuss with me, right?\"","Chen Yi wasn’t particularly surprised by his directness and nodded.","\"I have indeed come with a request.\"","\"Let’s hear it.\"","\"In the near future, if a certain upheaval occurs within Shu State City, I hope the Marquis can step in to resolve it.\"","\"What kind of upheaval?\"","\"Marquis, please forgive me. It’s not that I’m unwilling to speak plainly, but the time is not yet right. I’m afraid if the Marquis learns of it in advance...\"","The Elder Master frowned slightly, standing with his hands clasped behind his back, his eyes fixed on him.","Chen Yi remained perfectly composed, meeting his gaze with a calm expression.","Seeing this, Xiao Jing, who stood to the side, subconsciously clenched his fists, feeling his palms grow sweaty.","He was clearly nervous.","After a long moment, the serious expression on Elder Master Xiao’s face gradually softened. A slight smile touched his lips.","\"So be it.\"","\"Since you were able to perfectly resolve the crisis in the Three Towns and have also healed me, I won’t ask too many questions about a small favor.\"","Before Chen Yi could bow in thanks, he continued, \"However, I also have a word of advice for you, young friend.\"","\"Please speak freely, Marquis.\"","\"Do not underestimate anyone, especially Liu Hong!\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. Seeing the Elder Master’s sharp expression, so different from before, he thought to himself, ’The older the ginger, the spicier it gets.’ He simply nodded.","\"I will take it to heart.\"","Hearing this, Elder Master Xiao smiled and nodded. \"Very good.\"","They exchanged a few more pleasantries.","「Near noon.」","Elder Master Xiao walked Chen Yi out of the main hall. \"I very much enjoyed our conversation today, young friend. If you wouldn’t mind, please feel free to visit the residence more often in the future.\"","\"Since the Marquis has invited me, I would be delighted to.\"","Chen Yi spoke insincerely; he had already decided it would be best not to show his face here again.","’This time, I was forced to reveal my identity just to secure a commitment from the Elder Master.’","’Asking him for a small favor, hmm...’","’After that matter is resolved, it will be even more impossible for me to come to the Xiao Family as \"Chen Yu.\"’","’I reckon that by then, the Elder Master will probably want to flay me alive.’","\"Heh, just come and visit when you have time.\"","\"I won’t keep you any longer today. For lunch, I’ll have Wan’er host a banquet for you at Jiaxing Garden. You...\"","The Elder Master paused, sizing up Chen Yi’s face before continuing with a smile, \"I wonder, how old are you, young friend?\"","Chen Yi froze, confused by the question. \"I am... twenty-five.\"","It was a few years older than his actual age.","\"Twenty-five... Excellent, excellent. My eldest granddaughter, Xiao Wan’er, is a bit younger than you. You young people should have a lot to talk about.\"","\"Later, I’ll have someone send some wine over to you...\"","Listening to the Elder Master ramble on, Chen Yi’s expression grew more and more peculiar.","’Is this old man trying to play matchmaker?’","’Me and Xiao Wan’er?’","Without another thought, Chen Yi quickly bowed and took his leave. He walked briskly out of Qingjing Residence, leading Wang Ji toward Jiaxing Garden in the rear courtyard.","Elder Master Xiao watched him walk away, the smile on his face gradually fading.","\"Fortunately, this man is a friend, not a foe...\"","Xiao Jing, standing at his side, nodded at his words, but his thoughts were on the matter of Fu Wanqing.","\"Marquis, what should we do about General Fu’s matter?\"","The Elder Master fell silent for a moment. He looked up at the overcast sky, a touch of melancholy in his expression.","\"First, send someone to confirm whether she is with the Black Bear Tribe...\"","\"And one more thing. Under no circumstances can Jinghong find out about this...\"","\"Yes, sir!\""]},{"number":462,"title":"Chapter 462 - 282: A Fortunate Man’s Blessing","paragraphs":["He walked out of Qingjing Residence.","Chen Yi glanced back, shook his head to himself, and then followed Third Steward Lu Guan, who was leading him and Wang Ji to Jiaxing Garden.","This trip to the Marquis’s Mansion had accomplished his objective.","The process had gone more or less as he’d expected, without many complications.","But the old master was, after all, a Marquis Wu who had fought on the battlefield for decades.","Most of his attempts to probe for information had gone unanswered.","At most, he could tell that the old master was displeased with Liu Hong and the Jing State Liu Family.","But the old master showed no reaction whatsoever to the \"Financier\" who had sent the Evil Demonic Dao from Bright Moon Building to the Three Towns.","Chen Yi suspected one of two things: either the old master simply looked down on those merchants, or he was willing but powerless to act.","Of the two, the latter seemed more likely.","As for Fu Wanqing...","Chen Yi had finally managed to offload this \"hot potato\" onto the Xiao Family.","It wasn’t that he didn’t want to get involved in the matter.","He just didn’t want to bear the burden of this secret alone. Ultimately, the Xiao family needed to know.","Only then could he move forward unburdened.","Besides, Fu Wanqing was currently deep in the heart of Barbarian territory. Rescuing her and bringing her back to the Great Wei Dynasty would come at a tremendous cost.","Fu Wanqing might wait her entire life among the Barbarian Race, and a rescue party might never come.","’Under the circumstances, why should I take on this extra trouble?’","’It’s best to wait and see what the old master does next. I’ll act when the time is right.’","’Sigh... once I’ve dealt with this current mess, I’m definitely going back to the Chishui River.’","’I refuse to believe I can’t catch those damn fish with ’A Little Cold Plum’.’","Though Chen Yi’s mind was racing, his expression remained perfectly calm.","He followed Lu Guan toward Jiaxing Garden.","Just then,","[At the third quarter of the Si hour, Duke Dingyuan Xiao Yuan met with Chen Yi, owner of Hundred Herbs Hall. Chen Yi used Great Success Medical Dao to treat the Duke. Xiao Yuan learned that his daughter-in-law, Fu Wanqing, was not dead...]","[Reward: Military Strategy: *Seven Essentials of Martial Arts*. Opportunity +35.]","[Evaluation: Presence confirmed, reputation heard, decorum observed. Excellent performance.]","Before long, the three of them arrived at Jiaxing Garden.","Xiao Wan’er was already waiting at the entrance with Xie Tingyun, Shen Huatang, and a few others.","Strangely, Cui Qingwu and her maid, Huan’er, were also standing by her side.","The sight made Chen Yi frown inwardly.","Xiao Wan’er, however, didn’t give it much thought. Seeing \"Chen Yu\" arrive, she offered only a faint, polite smile.","She was wearing a plain white cloak, its collar of pure white fur encircling her pale neck, leaving only her rounded chin visible.","Thanks to the nourishing medicinal soups she had been taking, her complexion had a healthy color, a stark contrast to her previous pallor.","It was no longer pale but held a hint of pink, like a plum blossom.","She truly embodied the line from the poem: \"Like Jade Steps and Jade Trees, a beauty such as yourself is a rare sight in this world.\"","\"Young Master Chen, I trust you’ve been well.\"","Chen Yi stopped and gave a calm, slight bow. \"Miss Xiao, I returned to Shu State several days ago. Please forgive me for not paying you a visit sooner.\"","As he straightened, his gaze did not rise above Xiao Wan’er’s waist, a perfect display of decorum.","However, out of the corner of his eye, he noticed Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang—","The cultivation of these two top disciples of the Celestial Sect wasn’t profound, but their perception was keen.","’They’ve likely sensed my current level of cultivation,’ he thought.","Cui Qingwu and Huan’er, in contrast, merely sized him up without showing any particular reaction.","But Chen Yi knew that Cui Qingwu was undoubtedly comparing him to \"Liu Wu.\"","’She’s probably still holding a grudge over the ’poisoning’ incident,’ he mused.","Oblivious to the undercurrents, Xiao Wan’er led him and Wang Ji into Jiaxing Garden and began the introductions.","\"This is Miss Cui Qingwu.\"","\"She happens to be visiting the mansion today.\"","Chen Yi offered a brief, indifferent cupped-fist salute. \"Miss Cui. I’ve heard much about you.\"","Cui Qingwu glanced at him, tilting her head and raising her chin slightly. \"Young Master Chen has heard of me?\"","\"I’ve certainly heard of the proprietor of Yunqing Building.\"","\"Oh, of course. I’d forgotten that Young Master Chen is the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall. Our establishments are both in the West Market.\"","After a pause, Cui Qingwu let out a soft laugh. \"It’s just that Young Master Chen is famously reclusive, so I’ve never had the good fortune to meet you.\"","\"We should interact more in the future. After all, Yunqing Building still relies on the tea from your Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","Chen Yi simply gave a slight nod in response.","’This woman has completely shed her usual arrogance and is actively trying to make conversation,’ he thought. ’She’s clearly up to no good.’","’I’m not falling for it.’","Moreover, Hundred Herbs Hall had been limiting its tea sales recently, and Yunqing Building’s business had suffered as a result.","He didn’t have any extra tea to sell to Yunqing Building regardless.","Xiao Wan’er, unaware of these details, just thought it would be good for the two neighbors to get along, so she said with a smile,","\"You’ve both achieved some success in Shu State City. You should certainly get to know each other better.\"","This was something she would never have said in the past.","But ever since she set her sights on her goal of \"establishing a Medical Dao Academy,\" she found herself able to attempt things she never would have said or done before.","It was just like when she had accepted Cui Qingwu’s proposal to build the academy together.","A moment later.","They all took their seats, and the banquet began.","The feast was a lavish spread of delicacies from land and sea, none of which were new to Chen Yi.","Now, however, he feigned inexperience, keeping his head down and eating his meal in silence.","He ate as if he hadn’t seen food in two days.","Xiao Wan’er noticed his behavior, and though she didn’t understand the reason, she didn’t dwell on it.","Cui Qingwu, however, was not one to sit idle.","Besides, she still suspected that \"Chen Yu\" was actually \"Liu Wu.\"","Thus, she spent the meal probing him with questions, asking where he was from, his age, and other such things.","Chen Yi remained silent for the most part, only offering brief, perfunctory answers when he couldn’t avoid it.","Seeing this,","a look of displeasure inevitably crossed Cui Qingwu’s face. She spoke again, \"Young Master Chen, you must be a practitioner of the Martial Arts. Might I ask what your cultivation level is?\""]},{"number":463,"title":"Chapter 463 - 282: The Blessing of the Man of Qi","paragraphs":["Chen Yi looked up at her and said flatly, \"I only practice Martial Arts for the sake of my Medical Dao. It’s not worth mentioning.\"","\"Then I wonder, what is your Medical Dao Realm?\"","\"Minor Success.\"","Cui Qingwu hummed in acknowledgment as some of the things Lou Yuxue had once said came to mind.","Back when \"Liu Wu\" first appeared at the Spring Rain Building, he had used his Medical Dao to gain Black Tooth’s trust.","’Could he really be \"Liu Wu\"?’","Cui Qingwu wasn’t sure.","Even with her keen eye, she hadn’t found any similarities between \"Chen Yu\" and \"Liu Wu.\"","Their builds were slightly different; Chen Yu was a bit more handsome, a bit more upright in his posture.","Their auras were vastly different.","Chen Yu’s aura was faint. He had the cultivation aura of the Fifth Grade Realm, but it lacked the sharp True Spear Intent that Liu Wu possessed.","The most important thing was his eyes—from the very beginning, Chen Yu’s eyes had been as placid as still water...","’No, it was more like \"ice.\"’","Whether he was facing her or Xiao Wan’er, the man’s gaze had never changed.","Neither had his tone.","It was flat, even cold.","In contrast, that fellow \"Liu Wu\" always had an extremely aggressive look in his eyes, and his tone carried a strange sort of arrogance.","Even when facing her and Lou Yuxue, two White Tiger Guard Silver Banner Officers, Liu Wu’s attitude had been the same.","As Cui Qingwu mulled this over, she continued, \"With such skill in the Medical Dao, Young Master Chen, it’s no wonder Hundred Herbs Hall’s business is so prosperous.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment and lowered his head to eat.","\"May I ask who Young Master Chen’s master is?\"","\"My master is a recluse who shuns the mortal world.\"","\"...And that’s it?\"","Chen Yi gave her a strange look before lowering his head to eat again.","Seeing his attitude, Cui Qingwu didn’t get angry. Her eyes darted, and she changed the subject.","\"I hear you’ve been short on medicinal herbs recently?\"","\"Miss Cui, you ask despite knowing the answer. If Hundred Herbs Hall had enough herbs, we obviously wouldn’t have reduced the supply of our tea drinks.\"","\"Well... would you like me to help you think of a solution?\"","\"If there is a need, I will have Shopkeeper Wang go and ask for help.\"","Hearing this, Cui Qingwu secretly gritted her teeth. ’This man is truly impervious to persuasion.’","\"You...\"","Before she could speak again, Chen Yi put down his bowl and chopsticks and looked at Xiao Wan’er.","\"Miss Xiao, I have matters to attend to later and cannot stay for too long. I hope you’ll forgive me.\"","Xiao Wan’er glanced at the displeased Cui Qingwu, and though she was puzzled, she didn’t intervene.","She only said, \"It’s fine if you must leave first, Young Master Chen.\"","After a pause, she continued with a smile, \"Qingzhou was supposed to be here today as well, but unfortunately, he had business at Guiyun Academy.\"","\"Thank you for taking care of him on previous occasions, Young Master Chen.\"","Chen Yi nodded slightly and said, \"I and Mr. Qingzhou hit it off right away. There’s no need to be so polite, Miss Xiao.\"","\"That’s good to hear...\"","Seeing that Chen Yi was about to leave, Cui Qingwu looked annoyed, but she couldn’t act out in front of Xiao Wan’er.","\"Take care, Young Master Chen. If there’s a chance next time, Qingwu will certainly visit you at Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","\"Of course.\"","Chen Yi stood, bowed, and motioned for Wang Ji to head outside.","But just as they reached the outside of the wooden building, they saw Xiao Shen of the Xiao Family’s third branch arriving at Jiaxing Garden with his men.","Seeing them, Xiao Shen’s gaze fell upon Chen Yi. \"Young Master Chen, are you leaving?\"","Chen Yi nodded with a slight hesitation. \"I have imposed for too long today. It is indeed time for me to return.\"","Xiao Wan’er noticed his expression and took the initiative to say, \"Young Master Chen, this is my third grand-uncle.\"","\"Chen Yu greets Third Master Xiao.\"","Xiao Shen chuckled and waved his hand. \"No need for such courtesy, Young Master Chen.\"","\"I had only heard your name before, Young Master Chen. Seeing you today, you are truly as heroic and extraordinary as the rumors say.\"","Chen Yi didn’t understand what was going on, but his tone remained calm. \"Third Master Xiao, you flatter me.\"","Xiao Wan’er was also a bit curious and said hesitantly, \"Third Grand-uncle, Young Master Chen came today to visit Grandfather.\"","Xiao Shen smiled and said he was aware, then reached a hand out behind him. \"I am here on the Old Master’s orders, to deliver a jar of wine to you all.\"","\"Wine?\"","\"The finest Daughter Red Wine.\"","\"Daughter...\"","Xiao Wan’er stared at the wine jar with its aged paper seal, her eyes suddenly widening.","\"This, this is...\"","Seeing that she recognized it, Xiao Shen nodded slightly, his tone carrying a hint of suggestion.","\"It is the very jar of wine your father personally buried in the ground.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s expression changed. Forgetting everything else, she asked anxiously, \"This, is this Grandfather’s intention?\"","\"If the Old Master hadn’t given the word, I wouldn’t dare make this decision for you.\"","\"But, but...\"","Xiao Wan’er was clearly flustered. Her eyes darted toward Chen Yi, a blush already creeping onto her face. It wasn’t from shyness, but from anxiety.","Seeing this, Chen Yi naturally understood the Old Marquis’s intention and cursed inwardly, ’Does he absolutely have to play matchmaker?’","After a moment’s thought, he had no choice but to step forward and say, \"Thank you for your kind intentions, Third Master. I have already imposed on the residence for too long today. As for this wine... perhaps you and the Marquis should keep it.\"","Xiao Shen was taken aback. He looked Chen Yi up and down and said, \"Young Master Chen is not from Shu State, so you may not know, but this wine...\"","Before he could finish, Xiao Wan’er seemed to let out a breath of relief and quickly said, \"Third Grand-uncle, Young Master Chen has important matters to attend to and cannot stay long.\"","\"I, I’ll see him out first, and then I’ll go with you to Qingjing Residence to pay my respects.\"","Xiao Shen glanced at her, fell silent for a moment, and then nodded.","Seeing him agree, Xiao Wan’er led the way without hesitation, escorting Chen Yi and Wang Ji out of Jiaxing Garden.","\"My apologies for today’s events, Young Master. I... I... my apologies.\"","A hint of a smile flashed in Chen Yi’s eyes, and he feigned ignorance, saying:","\"Miss Xiao, you don’t need to say more. I visited the Marquis today solely for the matter of expanding Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er turned her head to look at him. As her gaze met his, she subconsciously looked away again.","\"Take care, Young Master Chen.\"","For some reason, when she looked into those eyes, she felt a sense of familiarity again.","Just like the first time the two of them had met.","Chen Yi, of course, was unaware of her thoughts. He bowed to the surrounding people and then took his leave with Wang Ji.","Xiao Wan’er and the others stood still, seeing them off in silence.","Only Xie Tingyun called out, \"Young Master Chen, thank you for taking care of my Celestial Sect disciples!\"","She had been holding that sentence in for a long time, and at this moment, she couldn’t be bothered with whether it was appropriate or not.","Chen Yi’s steps faltered slightly. He turned to the side and nodded, then walked out of the rear residence without a backward glance.","Cui Qingwu looked between Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Shen, and the thought of leaving with them faded.","It was clear that she was now more curious about why Old Marquis Xiao favored that \"Chen Yu.\"","He had even brought out the \"Daughter Red Wine,\" which was only to be taken out for Xiao Wan’er’s engagement, to entertain \"Chen Yu.\"","Seeing the situation, Xiao Shen sighed and said, \"Wan’er, I’ll go report back to the Old Master first.\"","\"Take care, Third Grand-uncle.\"","After Xiao Shen left with his men, Xiao Wan’er finally let out a breath of relief. She looked at Cui Qingwu apologetically.","\"Please forgive me, Qingwu. I’m afraid I can’t discuss the matter of the Medical Dao Academy with you today.\"","Cui Qingwu smiled and nodded, then changed the subject. \"Sister Wan’er, that jar of wine just now from the Marquis... was it for you and...\"","She gestured in the direction Chen Yi had left.","Xiao Wan’er nodded with a wry smile. \"I, perhaps...\"","She never would have imagined that the Old Marquis would have such an idea.","She was even more puzzled as to what about \"Chen Yu’s\" visit today had prompted the Old Marquis to do such a thing.","Hearing this, Cui Qingwu asked teasingly, \"So what do you think?\"","Xiao Wan’er shook her head in a slight panic. \"I, I haven’t thought about it.\"","Seeing her reaction, Cui Qingwu didn’t press the matter, but a few speculations formed in her mind.","At the poetry gathering at Guiyun Academy, she had noticed a certain ambiguous air between Xiao Wan’er and that Mr. Qingzhou.","Perhaps Xiao Wan’er’s reluctance to accept \"Chen Yu\" had something to do with Mr. Qingzhou.","’They both have the surname Chen, maybe... ’","With this thought, Cui Qingwu also took her leave.","\"Since it’s inconvenient for Sister Wan’er today, I will come again tomorrow.\"","\"Alright...\"","...","「Elsewhere.」","Wang Ji, driving the carriage in front, couldn’t help but ask in a suggestive tone, \"My lord, is the Marquis planning to have you...\"","Chen Yi, sitting quietly in the carriage, cut him off in a flat tone, \"To Hundred Herbs Hall first.\"","\"Ahem... Yes, my lord!\"","Wang Ji complied, quickly turning the carriage around and heading south along South Street.","Although he hadn’t gotten the answer he wanted, as someone who knew Chen Yi’s true identity, he was inwardly roaring with laughter.","After all, Chen Yi was the husband of General Xiao Jinghong.","If the Old Marquis really wanted \"Chen Yu\" to marry the Xiao Family’s eldest young lady, that would be truly...","’Truly the blessing of having two wives!’","Chen Yi was of course aware of Wang Ji’s sordid thoughts. A wry smile appeared on his face as he shook his head to himself.","’This Old Marquis is truly... muddled.’","’The \"blessing\" of having two wives isn’t something you enjoy like this.’","’At the very least...’","Chen Yi collected his thoughts, deciding that he would not go out under the identity of \"Chen Yu\" for a short while.","He had no desire to give the old man another chance to get ideas about him.","「Not long after.」","The carriage passed by the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office.","Chen Yi lifted the curtain, glanced out, and raised an eyebrow slightly.","’Is there news on Du Cang already?’"]},{"number":464,"title":"Chapter 464 - 283: The String is Broken, and No One Can Fathom the Pain","paragraphs":["[Missing Person Notice: Where at world’s end can I find a kindred spirit!]","On the notice board of the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office, a single line of poetry was written on a large sheet of coarse paper.","It had no beginning and no end.","And yet, it had drawn a sizable crowd.","Among them were many scholars in long robes, pointing and commenting on the notice.","\"’Where at world’s end can I find a kindred spirit...’ The imagery is so vast and lonely. The person who posted this must be a scholar skilled in poetry.\"","\"A pity it’s only half a line. You can’t even call it a fragment—it’s more like a fragment of a fragment.\"","\"Brother Gu, you’re a student of Guiyun Academy with a reputation for talent. Why not complete the line? If word gets out, it would make for a wonderful story.\"","A young man wearing the long robes of a Scholar and a square cap demurred for a moment.","But amid the crowd’s cheerful urging, he began to consider it seriously.","A moment later, a smile broke out on his face. \"I’ve got it.\"","\"Let’s hear it, Brother Gu.\"","\"Where at world’s end can I find a kindred spirit? The zither’s strings are broken, with none to know my grieving heart.\"","\"Excellent! A fine line!\"","\"Kindred spirits are hard to find. Even with the noblest of melodies, there is no one left to grasp its true meaning. All one’s painstaking efforts become but a fading echo in an empty valley!\"","\"Brother Gu...\"","Chen Yi glanced at the lively scene before closing the carriage curtain and shutting his eyes in thought.","According to the parting agreement he’d made with Lou Yuxue and Cui Qingwu yesterday, the phrase \"Where at world’s end can I find a kindred spirit\" was the signal that Du Cang had been found.","But this didn’t align with his own judgment.","It wasn’t that he was overconfident in his deductions. Rather, he had spent days searching for Du Cang to no avail.","And now, after only half a day, the White Tiger Guard had managed to find him?","Either the White Tiger Guard had an incredibly dense network in Shu State City, with Iron and Silver Banner Officers stationed everywhere, allowing them to pinpoint Du Cang’s location by consolidating information.","Or it was a stroke of luck, and Du Cang had turned up right under the nose of a White Tiger Guard member.","Or...","Chen Yi’s thoughts raced. On the chessboard in his mind, several white pieces representing the White Tiger Guard rose and fell.","One of them, a white piece with a more brilliant sheen, vaguely formed an encircling pattern with the other pieces as it moved.","It was the piece representing the \"General.\"","’That’s it.’","’The General previously went to the Ancient Tea-Horse Road to find King Landu. By my calculations, several days have already passed.’","’Whatever his objective was, he would surely be affected by Lv Jiunan’s death.’","’Assuming the General went to make some kind of deal with King Landu, then King Landu would certainly use the matter of Lv Jiunan as a bargaining chip.’","’So the General...’","Chen Yi opened his eyes. He looked at the narrow carriage compartment, his brow furrowing slightly.","’Is he trying to use Lou Yuxue to lure me out?’","But after careful consideration, he dismissed this idea.","The General wouldn’t dare.","Or at least, he wouldn’t dare make such a decision so quickly.","The reason was simple.","It was all because of the White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master’s \"personal appointment.\"","Even though Chen Yi hadn’t accepted it, the General still shouldn’t dare to act on his own authority.","He could surmise as much from the attitude he’d observed in the White Tiger Guard’s Golden and Silver Banner Officers toward their Pavilion Master.","Therefore, the most likely explanation for the notice at the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office was that Lou Yuxue wanted to meet him to discuss something important.","’The matter of Du Cang?’","Chen Yi’s brow relaxed, and a faint smile touched his lips.","It seemed the White Tiger Guard truly didn’t dare to defy their mysterious Lord Pavilion Master.","Thinking of this, Chen Yi tapped on the front of the carriage. \"I won’t be going to Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","Wang Ji was startled for a moment. When he understood, he pulled on the reins and said, \"My lord, I’ll stop the carriage now.\"","\"No need.\"","\"You can head back on your own.\"","Chen Yi paused, then lowered his voice. \"As for that other matter, go take care of it this afternoon.\"","\"This afternoon?\"","\"Haven’t you found the right people?\"","\"No, that’s not it. I’ve already positioned those men near the grain merchants. It’s just...\"","Wang Ji hesitated. \"It’s just that my word alone is no proof. If they don’t believe me, I’m afraid it will affect your plan.\"","\"Don’t worry, they’ll believe it.\"","\"Just go and do it.\"","\"Yes!\"","After speaking, Chen Yi shed his clothes, changed into a set of coarse linen garments he had prepared in a bundle, and leaped nimbly from the carriage.","In an instant, he used the surging crowd for cover and vanished into a side alley.","Wang Ji, completely oblivious, drove the carriage on for another half-mile before asking again, \"My lord, perhaps you’d like to stop at Hundred Herbs Hall first?\"","For a long moment, there was no reply.","He turned and gently lifted the curtain to peek inside. Seeing it completely empty, he couldn’t help but let out a long sigh of relief.","He didn’t know why.","But every time Wang Ji saw Chen Yi in his guise as \"Chen Yu,\" he felt his heart pound with trepidation.","He was clearly very familiar with Chen Yi by now.","And Mr. Qingzhou was usually so gentle with him.","And yet, when facing \"Chen Yu,\" Wang Ji was always on edge, not daring to have a single stray thought or hide anything from him.","’My lord is becoming more and more...’","’Frightening?’","’No, imposing. That’s it.’","With these thoughts, Wang Ji hurried back to Hundred Herbs Hall to carry out Chen Yi’s orders.","...","Chen Yi slipped away just outside the West Market. Peeling off the \"Chen Yu\" mask from his face, he concealed his movements, taking a winding path through quiet alleys until he arrived outside the residence on Chuansi Street.","He hadn’t even gotten close when he heard the voices of Pei Guanli and Pei Qian from inside.","\"Guanli, you spent all that time at the Marquis’s Mansion. What do you think of that Chen Yi?\"","\"Brother-in-law... he’s a very nice person.\"","\"Nice? What do you mean, nice... Huh? Guanli, why is your face so red?\"","\"I-It’s not!\"","Flustered, Pei Guanli’s voice suddenly grew louder. \"Brother, don’t try to turn this on me!\"","\"I’d say you’re the one who still hasn’t given up on Sister Jinghong, right?\"","\"I’m telling you, you should just give up.\"","\"Brother-in-law is a hundred times better than you. No, a thousand times.\"","Pei Qian was clearly choked speechless by her retort, unable to say a word for a long moment.","\"Then tell me, what’s so good about him?\"","\"When it comes to looks, your big brother here is just as handsome.\""]},{"number":465,"title":"Chapter 465 - 283: A Broken String, a Sorrow Unresolved","paragraphs":["\"In Martial Arts, I could knock his teeth out with just one finger.\"","\"And background? Since when are we of the Mountain Race inferior to those Noble Families from the Central Plains?\"","\"Besides, I hear that Chen Yi is just an out-of-favor illegitimate son of the Chen Family.\"","\"And as for knowledge... well... your brother has read a few books, as you know.\"","Pei Guanli let out a pfft, then burst into laughter.","\"Brother, you can’t compare to brother-in-law in a single one of the things you just listed.\"","\"No way! You think he can beat me?\"","\"Of course... he can’t beat you.\"","\"Hmph. I knew you were just trying to get a rise out of me.\"","\"Because it’s true...\"","Seeing how lively the conversation inside was, Chen Yi took the black iron mask from the satchel at his side and put it on.","After confirming no one was around, he slipped into the residence.","Just as Pei Guanli was about to keep arguing with Pei Qian, she saw him arrive, and a look of delight spread across her face.","\"Brother-in— I mean, isn’t it Lord ’Liu Wu’?\"","\"Why do you have time to come over today?\"","Pei Qian also noticed Chen Yi’s arrival. Forgetting all about his argument with Pei Guanli over who was better, him or Chen Yi, he bowed and said,","\"This junior, Pei Qian, greets you, Senior.\"","Chen Yi gave an impassive nod. \"No need for such formalities,\" he said with a smile, then walked straight into the main hall.","Overjoyed, Pei Guanli followed him.","As her fair feet skipped along, the Bell on her necklace jingled incessantly.","Pei Qian glanced at her, wondering privately.","’Could my sister have really fallen for Senior \"Liu Wu\"?’","Then again, he thought they were a good match.","After all, Senior \"Liu Wu\" had earned the title \"Dragon Spear\" and had even displayed his mastery of the Spear Dao outside the city a few days ago.","His Cultivation and Technique were truly formidable.","As Pei Qian’s mind raced, he followed them and said with a smile, \"I didn’t have much to do in the city today, so I came to chat with my sister. I hope I’m not disturbing you?\"","After taking a seat, Chen Yi said, \"Not at all.\"","\"It’s just... now that Liu Zhaoxue is back in Shu State, are you... investigating them?\"","Pei Qian nodded with a smile. \"To be honest with you, Senior, yes, we are.\"","\"The day Liu Zhaoxue returned to Shu State, we sought her out at once, but we only found her with a few juniors from the Five Poison Sect.\"","\"Therefore, after discussing it with the clan elders, this junior decided we should hold off on making a move for now and see if Elder Demon Yan shows up in Shu State.\"","\"Are you confident?\"","\"You jest, Senior.\"","\"If we knew about them ahead of time and still fell into their trap, we’d bring utter disgrace to the Mountain Race.\"","Chen Yi chuckled. \"Good to hear.\"","\"I’ve been quite busy lately and truly haven’t had time to deal with the Five Poison Sect.\"","\"If you need anything later, Brother Pei, just have Guanli notify me in advance.\"","These days, he truly hadn’t had the time to concern himself with Liu Zhaoxue.","He hadn’t paid much mind to the people from the Five Poison Sect, either.","He would wait for Pei Qian and the Mountain Race to get a solid lead, then he would act as he saw fit. After all, he couldn’t simply let go of his grudge with Yan Fusha.","Upon hearing this, Pei Qian stood and clasped his fist. \"You are most righteous, Senior. This junior would not dare refuse your help.\"","He could tell Chen Yi had private matters to discuss with Pei Guanli, so he didn’t linger. He continued,","\"This junior will return now to confer with my third grand-uncle and the others. We’ll see if that band of heretics from the Five Poison Sect’s Evil Demonic Dao has made a move.\"","Chen Yi nodded and didn’t press him to stay.","After a few more pleasantries, Pei Qian left the residence.","After waiting a moment, just as Pei Guanli was about to speak, Chen Yi gestured to her. She instantly understood that her brother hadn’t gone far yet.","She couldn’t help but pout, muttering under her breath about her \"stinky brother\" daring to eavesdrop.","Chen Yi couldn’t help but chuckle. Once he was sure Pei Qian was gone, he signaled that she could speak.","Pei Guanli came forward excitedly, leaning over the tea table to gaze at him without blinking.","\"Brother-in-law, did you come today with a new assignment for me?\"","\"I—I’m not trying to rush you.\"","\"It’s just so mind-numbingly boring here. All I do all day is either Cultivation or space out.\"","\"And also! That Dabao person you arranged to come... he hasn’t been here in days! I almost starved to death...\"","Pei Guanli chattered on endlessly.","Though her words were full of complaints, her tone was brimming with delight.","Chen Yi listened patiently before taking off his mask. He shook his head and said, \"You’ll have to put up with it for a few more days.\"","Pei Guanli pouted, but a moment later, her smile returned.","\"Okay, brother-in-law. I’ll do as you say.\"","Chen Yi, of course, saw her expression. He chuckled and patted her on the forehead.","\"Don’t worry. In five days at most, I’ll have you go stay at the Xiao Family’s estate.\"","’He wasn’t comfortable letting Pei Guanli stay here alone any longer.’","’Pei Qian came today; he could come again tomorrow.’","’There was no telling when Pei Guanli might let something slip and reveal his true identity to Pei Qian.’","\"Okay, I’ll listen to you, brother-in-law.\"","After a bit more small talk, Chen Yi put his black iron mask back on and went to the underground meditation chamber in the inner room.","Inside, Lv Jiunan and Asutai were still deep in a slumber.","However, their conditions were worlds apart.","Due to his prior injuries and not having eaten for days, Lv Jiunan was little more than skin and bones.","Asutai, in contrast, was physically unchanged, as if completely unaffected.","Chen Yi clicked his tongue in amazement, then used two Silver Needles to wake Asutai.","The moment he regained consciousness, Asutai immediately sat up.","When he saw Chen Yi wearing the black iron mask, a wary look flashed across his face as he slowly recalled the previous events.","\"You... Wei man... is it time for the transaction?\"","Chen Yi gave a slight nod, a hint of a smile in his voice. \"I’m ready on my end.\"","\"Now it just depends on whether the Young Master will agree to this transaction.\"","Asutai gritted his teeth, a flicker of hatred showing on his square, slave-branded face.","\"No matter wha— I agree!\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi cut to the chase. \"My offer is this: I will help you return to the Barbarian Race.\"","Asutai was visibly stunned and stared at him in astonishment.","\"I... return to my tribe? But... but they... my revenge... I...\"","\"Your revenge,\" Chen Yi said, raising a hand to cut him off, \"will be yours.\"","\"But you need to understand something. Your enemy isn’t some commoner. He’s Liu Hong, the Left Governor of the Shu State Governor’s Office.\"","\"Do you think you can get your revenge all by yourself?\"","\"Governor... Liu Hong? He... he’s that Wei Dog’s master?\"","Chen Yi knew he meant Zeng Zhifeng. \"That’s right,\" he confirmed with a nod.","\"The reason I didn’t rush to help you with your revenge was that certain necessary conditions weren’t yet in place.\"","\"Now, everything is ready. If you agree, the day you return to your tribe will be the day he dies.\"","Asutai listened, clearly not understanding the connection between the two events. He asked stiffly,","\"Then... doesn’t that mean I can’t be the one to kill him?\"","Chen Yi chuckled. \"My apologies, Young Master. My abilities can only guarantee his death, not that you’ll be the one to kill him with your own hands.\"","\"Besides, if you were to do it, you wouldn’t leave Shu State alive, even with my help.\"","Asutai stubbornly shook his head. \"I just want him dead.\"","He didn’t even care about his own life.","Chen Yi understood his implication and couldn’t help but feel a bit more admiration for him.","’If Asutai weren’t one of the Barbarians, he wouldn’t have minded letting the kid suffer less.’","\"Do you remember what you promised me before?\"","\"My condition for letting you kill Zeng Zhifeng was that you had to promise to do a few things for me.\"","\"Having you return to the Barbarian Race is the first.\"","\"Having Liu Hong die in Shu State—but not by your hand—is the second.\"","Asutai froze again. He opened his mouth to speak, his dark face instantly flushing red.","He wanted to argue or refuse, but he couldn’t get a single word out.","「After a long while.」","He seemed to deflate. \"My teacher taught me that a gentleman’s word is his bond.\"","\"Barbarians must also be true to their word.\"","\"I... I gave you my promise. I won’t go back on it.\"","After a pause, Asutai looked Chen Yi straight in the eyes and said, enunciating each word, \"You just have to promise me... that Liu Hong will die.\"","Chen Yi gave a noncommittal nod. \"I promise you.\"","He added with a smile, \"Even if you weren’t involved, I wouldn’t let him live anyway.\"","At this, Asutai nodded emphatically.","\"What... do you want me to do?\"","\"Don’t be in such a hurry. I still have a third and a fourth thing for you to do...\""]},{"number":466,"title":"Chapter 466 - 284: When You Become the Left King...","paragraphs":["\"The third, the fourth? You...\"","A hint of hesitation appeared on Asutai’s rugged, un-youthful face.","No matter how dull-witted he was, he suddenly recalled something Mr. Fu had once taught him.","Many of the Wei People are masters of intrigue, capable of scheming you to death and getting away with it.","’If this masked Wei person in front of me keeps making demands, won’t I be at his mercy for the rest of my life?’","So, Asutai hesitated for a moment before asking, his tone inevitably cautious, \"Do you... have... a fifth thing?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly, understanding his concern. He asked with a smile, \"And here I thought you Barbarians were all straight arrows.\"","\"What? If I keep giving you conditions, are you planning to back out of our previous deal?\"","Asutai’s face instantly turned a dark, flushed red, and he stammered, unable to get a word out.","He wanted to say that the Panda Celestial God his Barbarian Race worshipped was a figure of immense integrity, and so were his people.","Even without Mr. Fu teaching him the saying, \"a gentleman’s word is his bond,\" he would still honor his promise and never go back on it.","Chen Yi shook his head. \"Don’t worry, there are only these four things. As for anything more...\"","He sized up Asutai and shook his head again. \"With you as you are now, you are far from qualified.\"","In terms of strength, Asutai’s physical power was only equivalent to that of an Eighth Grade Realm Martial Artist.","In terms of status, he was merely the unfavored Crown Prince of the Black Bear Tribe.","In terms of intellect... it was debatable whether he even had any.","If he didn’t have some value to be exploited right now, Chen Yi wouldn’t have bothered making a deal with him at all.","Even though the terms of their deal seemed fair.","Asutai’s expression relaxed a little upon hearing this, but he soon became conflicted again.","\"Then... then when I’m... in the future... will you...?\"","Chen Yi was tempted to say no, but after a moment’s thought, he chose not to be so absolute.","\"If, one day, you can inherit your father’s position and become Asutai, the Barbarian Left King, then perhaps you will be qualified to cooperate with me.\"","\"The... The Left King? Me?\"","Asutai pointed at himself, his face flushing an even deeper red than before. He clearly didn’t believe he could become the Left King.","\"Then... what’s your identity?\"","\"A Prince of the Wei Dynasty? A Duke? Or a Marquis Wu?\"","\"None of those. As for me...\"","The eyes under Chen Yi’s black iron mask met his gaze, and he said with a light chuckle:","\"One day, when you are among the Barbarian Race, you’ll hear tales of a certain Wei person. His Martial Arts Cultivation will be unrivaled, his Medical Dao capable of saving the masses, his Chess Dao supreme in all the world, and his Calligraphy Dao able to reach the Immortal Realm. You’ll hear of his Zither, his Painting...\"","\"That person... will be me.\"","Asutai stared at him blankly, then after a while, started counting on his fingers, muttering things like one, two, three, four, five.","\"You... you’re not one person? Eight? No, ten... ten people?\"","Chen Yi was exasperated. \"Is ten the highest number you know? Or is it just that you only have ten fingers?\"","Then, without waiting for Asutai to answer, he waved his hand dismissively. \"Forget it. Just pretend I never said anything.\"","\"In any case, the things I need you to do are not difficult.\"","\"Of course, with your current intellect, anything too complicated would indeed be a bit much for you.\"","Asutai looked a little indignant.","But when he thought about Chen Yi’s methods, he could only nod and accept it.","\"Tell... tell me. The third and fourth.\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"Very simple.\"","\"Shortly, I will arrange for you to be ’rescued’ by Liu Hong. I need you to return to the Barbarian Race through him.\"","\"Him?\"","Asutai was stunned at first, then he fiercely clenched his fists. \"I... I refuse!\"","Chen Yi laughed nonchalantly. \"If I told you this is the only way for Liu Hong to die, would you still refuse?\"","Asutai stiffened his neck, wanting to remain defiant.","But looking into Chen Yi’s eyes, he gritted his teeth in frustration.","\"I... agree.\"","\"Very good.\"","\"Now I’m starting to believe you’re the little Barbarian who studied under Mr. Fu.\"","\"I’m... not little.\"","\"Haha, little or not... let’s talk about the last thing.\"","With that, Chen Yi’s expression turned serious. \"After you return to the Barbarian Race, I hope you will protect Mr. Fu.\"","Upon hearing this, Asutai’s face showed a hint of confusion. He seemed both perplexed and conflicted.","Just when Chen Yi thought he was going to refuse, he turned his head away and said in a stiff tone:","\"You... pick another one.\"","\"Even if you don’t say it, I will... protect... Mr. Fu.\"","Chen Yi was struck speechless for a moment, then laughed. \"No, this is the one.\"","\"Of course, it would be even better if, while keeping her safe, you could also deliver a few words to her for me.\"","\"You... speak.\"","\"Tell her: ’Everything at home is fine. Don’t worry.’\"","Asutai repeated it under his breath. \"Just... these words?\"","\"That’s right.\"","Chen Yi nodded. A small medicine bottle appeared in his hand as he raised it. He toyed with it as he said with a smile:","\"Remember what you’ve promised me.\"","\"When you wake up again, I guarantee you will already be on your way back to the Barbarian Race.\"","Asutai nodded heavily. \"You... promise... me.\"","\"Don’t worry. He will definitely die!\"","After speaking, Chen Yi tossed the medicine bottle, once again using Immortal Drunk to send Asutai into a deep sleep.","Once the quiet room fell silent.","Chen Yi looked at the Barbarian youth, whose face showed a stubborn expression even in his slumber, and a hint of a smile flashed in his eyes.","’The fourth thing... is predicated on you making it back to the Barbarian Race alive.’","’That old fox Liu Hong is not easy to fool.’","’He will certainly see through this overt scheme. The only question is... whether he can be ruthless enough...’","’Will he choose to kill Asutai to solve the problem once and for all, or will he choose to send Asutai away, risking exposure?’","Chen Yi didn’t know the answer, but he was eagerly anticipating what choice Liu Hong would make.","This time, he was determined to make that old fox reveal his true colors.","Thinking of this, Chen Yi’s gaze fell upon Lv Jiunan.","After a moment’s thought, he decided there was no need to waste his breath on Lv Jiunan and turned to walk out of the quiet room."]},{"number":467,"title":"Chapter 467 - 284: When You Become Left King...","paragraphs":["The moment he opened the door,","Chen Yi saw Pei Guanli on the floor, her head cocked to the side as she listened intently.","’What is Brother-in-law saying to that little barbarian?’","’I can’t hear a thing. Why can’t they speak up...’","\"You mean, loud like this?\"","\"Gah!\"","Pei Guanli jumped in fright at Chen Yi’s sudden shout.","When she saw it was him, Pei Guanli’s face flushed red, and she giggled sheepishly. \"Brother-in-law, I—I wasn’t eavesdropping. I didn’t hear a thing.\"","Chen Yi flicked her on the forehead and chided with a smile, \"I don’t know what goes on in that head of yours all day.\"","\"I’m leaving.\"","\"Brother-in-law, you—you’re going back already?\"","\"Yes. I have some business at Guiyun Academy.\"","Pei Guanli hummed a dejected \"oh,\" then followed closely behind him.","Chen Yi glanced at her sideways and said with a smile, \"Just hang in there for a few more days. This will all be over soon.\"","Pei Guanli pouted and nodded. \"I know.\"","Seeing this, Chen Yi lowered his voice. \"Don’t sleep too soundly tonight. I’ll take you to see a show.\"","\"Really?\"","When Chen Yi nodded, Pei Guanli’s face lit up. \"It’s not that I want to go out, you know.\"","\"But since Brother-in-law is being so considerate, I’ll reluctantly agree. I wouldn’t even mind staying here a few more days.\"","Chen Yi tapped her on the head. \"When did you learn to be such a tease? You’re being improper.\"","Pei Guanli covered her head. \"What tease? I’m not!\"","\"That counts, too.\"","\"Oh...\"","After a bit more banter, Chen Yi glanced at the sky, then zipped away from the residence.","Pei Guanli watched him disappear with a delighted smile, then turned and went back to the main hall to practice her Meteor Butterfly Step.","’A tease... what does he mean by that?’","’Is Brother-in-law telling me to speak the Mountain Race language?’","...","Chen Yi went to Guiyun Academy for one reason: to ask about the Annual Examination.","Previously, Mr. Yue Ming had asked Yang Ye to go and mediate with Ma Shuhan.","Although he only received a very perfunctory reply, it wasn’t a total loss.","At least, thanks to Yang Ye’s intervention, Ma Shuhan had been much more restrained lately.","But while he was restrained on the surface, he was constantly making moves in the shadows.","He was inspecting academies throughout Shu State, recruiting Vice Examiners, and hiring staff officers, one by one.","Even Liu Hong had issued a statement from the Governor’s Office, essentially saying that he expected good performances in this year’s Shu State Annual Examination.","\"Qingzhou, no matter what tricks that Ma Shuhan tries to pull,\"","\"I believe in one thing—in the Dao of literature, what is true cannot be made false, and what is false cannot be made true.\"","Mr. Yue Ming’s expression was righteous. He snorted, \"If that man Ma dares to defy the world and make things difficult for any student during the Annual Examination, I will certainly not let him off the hook!\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"You are right, Headmaster.\"","\"I don’t think he’d dare.\"","However, Ma Shuhan might not dare, but that didn’t mean Liu Hong wouldn’t.","Mr. Zhuo Ying, standing to the side, had the same thought. With his hands tucked into his sleeves like an old farmer, he said pointedly,","\"Headmaster, I wonder if you’ve heard about the recent situation in Shu State City?\"","Mr. Yue Ming was taken aback. \"What situation?\"","\"I’ve heard that because of the changes to the Annual Examination this year, many people from the Noble Families have been visiting the Liu Mansion.\"","\"Liu... Liu Gongmo?\"","\"Who else could it be?\"","\"I’ve also heard that while our Lord Liu didn’t accept the things these people brought, they looked as if they had successfully delivered their gifts when they left.\"","\"Why is that?\"","Seeing that he still hadn’t caught on, Mr. Zhuo Ying glanced at Chen Yi and said, \"What else could it be?\"","\"I suppose our Lord Liu put their minds at ease.\"","Mr. Yue Ming frowned. \"Are you saying Liu Gongmo leaked the questions?\"","Hearing this, Mr. Zhuo Ying didn’t know whether to laugh or cry.","Even Chen Yi felt the same.","\"Headmaster, cheating is such a disreputable business. Even if Liu Gongmo could do it, he wouldn’t.\"","\"Think about it. The purpose of this Annual Examination is to urge students to study hard. As long as they don’t get the lowest grade, there’s leeway with all the other scores.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying gave a wry smile. \"Do you think there’s any real difference between a C-plus and a C-minus?\"","Chen Yi chimed in with a smile, \"It seems our Lord Governor has made some clever calculations.\"","Mr. Yue Ming began to understand, and he sighed with a complicated expression.","\"Liu Gongmo...\"","\"No wonder he agreed to Ma Shuhan’s request earlier.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying shook his head. \"No, you’re wrong. The way I see it, it was probably Ma Shuhan who was following our Lord Liu’s orders.\"","\"In any case, Qingzhou, you must be careful when you take the Annual Examination.\"","\"It’s better not to write anything too fancy and just stick closely to the topic, to avoid giving those with malicious intentions an opening to cause trouble.\"","Chen Yi nodded, then shook his head.","\"I’d actually like to see if they have the guts...\"","...","As evening drew near, long lines still snaked outside several grain stores in the East Market.","Countless commoners clutched burlap sacks or wicker baskets, staring eagerly toward the front of the lines.","Some were looking at the price boards hanging outside the grain stores, pointing and murmuring at the price: thirteen taels of silver per hundredweight.","Others were eyeing the sacks of rice and flour, afraid there wouldn’t be enough grain left by the time they reached the front.","And still others were whispering amongst themselves.","\"I wonder when these rising grain prices will ever stop.\"","\"If this keeps up, who will be able to afford to eat?\"","\"I bet people will start starving to death in Shu State City sooner or later.\"","\"Who knows how much those damn officials are getting from the grain stores. Not only do they do nothing, but they won’t even open the granaries to release grain and stabilize the prices.\"","\"Heh, those high-and-mighty people... no matter how high the price of grain gets, they’ll always have food on their tables.\"","\"Why would they worry about us common folk?\"","The crowd was abuzz with discussion, some cursing the corrupt officials, some damning the black-hearted grain stores, while others offered a bit of hopeful gossip.","\"The way I see it, these prices can’t keep rising for much longer.\"","\"Oh? Do tell, brother.\"","The speaker was a disheveled man in tattered linen clothes, and he chattered on with a thick Mountain Race accent.","\"I just heard it from someone else.\"","\"Turns out, that brother of King Landu from the Poshisu Country didn’t actually die that night.\"","\"He didn’t... he didn’t die?\"","Someone immediately refuted him. \"That night, lots of people outside the West Market saw ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu kill Lv Jiunan.\"","\"So how could he not be dead?\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"It’s not me saying it! A buddy of mine, a lone-wolf merchant, saw it with his own two eyes.\"","The man in linen clothes described it vividly. \"He said that one night, he happened to run into ’Dragon Spear’ and Lv Jiunan.\"","\"He said that ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu was incredibly heroic, dragging Lv Jiunan along like a dead dog while cursing him out.\"","\"’You Poshisu dog! How dare you cause trouble in the territory of Great Wei! You’re courting death!’\"","Hearing this, the others in line looked at him, half-believing and half-doubting.","Although they were reluctant to believe the words of a beggar, they desperately hoped it was true.","\"But then again, if that Lv fellow isn’t dead, then King Landu’s horse bandits really have no reason to raid the border.\"","\"So the grain prices... hmm... I hope what this young brother says is true.\"","\"I hope so too...\"","Similar scenes were playing out in front of nearly every grain store.","Some believed the rumors, some dismissed them entirely, and others used them as an opportunity to stir up trouble.","In a short while, the chief stewards of the several grain stores all received the news.","After exchanging bewildered glances, they didn’t dare delay and passed the message on to their respective masters.","In the Lin Mansion, not far from the East Market,","Lin Zhenghong, the newly appointed Patriarch, sat upright in the main hall, his hands gently stroking the back of his chair, a sentimental look on his face.","\"Oh, Father.\"","\"You really don’t know the cost of living until you’re the one in charge. Back when I was just a rich young master at home, how did I never realize that making money was so... so easy?\"","During this period, thanks to the rising grain prices, the Lin’s Grain Store had made a fortune.","You could say they were raking in gold every day.","This left Lin Zhenghong, who had just taken control of the Lin Family, overjoyed. It even diluted some of the grief from his own father, Lin Huai’an’s, death.","Just as he was lifting his teacup with a broad smile, about to take a sip, he heard footsteps from outside the door.","\"Master, Master, something terrible has happened!\"","Lin Zhenghong frowned slightly, setting down his teacup. He asked imperiously, \"Hm? What’s all the panic about?\"","\"Master, some—someone is saying that Lv Jiunan isn’t dead!\"","\"Who isn’t dead? If Lv Jiunan isn’t dead, then he isn’t—\"","\"Who did you say?!\""]},{"number":468,"title":"Chapter 468 - 285: How Did He Calculate This?","paragraphs":["Lin Zhenghong was startled at first, then his brows knitted together.","\"Tell me everything.\"","\"Well, it’s like this...\"","When the Grain Store Chief Steward, dressed in a blue robe, finished speaking, Lin Zhenghong’s brow relaxed slightly, and he said in a dissatisfied tone:","\"The word of a few beggars? Is that credible?\"","\"Hmph. I think someone saw how much the grain prices have risen and is just trying to stir up trouble.\"","The Grain Store Chief Steward hesitated for a moment. \"Master, if this is true...\"","Lin Zhenghong raised his hand to interrupt him. \"So what if it’s true?\"","\"But...\"","\"Enough with the ’buts.’ Let me ask you, what was the cost of the grain we brought in from Ji State?\"","The Grain Store Chief Steward understood and said with a bitter smile, \"For one stone of fine grain, it was less than a tael.\"","Hearing this, Lin Zhenghong snorted. \"Then what are you panicking for?\"","\"Even if Lv Jiunan isn’t really dead, it would only eliminate the threat of an attack from those horse bandits from Poshisu Country.\"","\"And don’t forget, that Barbarian Prince who ended up in Shu State still hasn’t been found.\"","At this, he picked up his teacup and took a sip. His expression relaxed, and he said nonchalantly:","\"Even if the worst should happen, the Lin’s Grain Store will still turn a profit. It’s just a question of whether we make a lot or a little.\"","The Grain Store Chief Steward watched him, his own brow furrowing imperceptibly.","After a moment of silence, he said softly, \"If your father knew what you’ve become, he’d be angry enough to jump out of his coffin.\"","Lin Zhenghong was stunned, looking at him in astonishment.","It was as if he were seeing him for the first time.","\"You... how dare you!\"","Lin Zhenghong slammed his teacup down, splashing tea and leaves across the table. He glared, furious.","\"Li Sanyuan, you dare to insult my late father!\"","\"Are you taking advantage of the fact that I’ve just taken charge of the Lin Family? Is this a rebellion?!\"","The Grain Store Chief Steward, Li Sanyuan, was no longer meek and subservient. He slowly straightened his posture.","\"They say a tiger father cannot beget a dog of a son. I’m beginning to doubt that.\"","He looked at Lin Zhenghong mockingly. \"Do you really think the Lin’s Grain Store belongs to the Lin Family?\"","\"Didn’t Lin Huai’an tell you, before he died, about the responsibilities he shouldered when he came to Shu State?\"","Lin Zhenghong stood up, about to berate him further, when a sudden thought made his expression change.","\"You... you’re from... Ji State? No, I mean, from the Trading Company?\"","Seeing that he’d caught on, Li Sanyuan snorted. \"So you’re not a complete idiot.\"","Saying this, Li Sanyuan walked forward, forced Lin Zhenghong to one side, and casually sat down in his seat.","He then gently smoothed the hem of his robe over his knees, rested a hand on the arm of the Grandmaster’s Chair, and looked directly at Lin Zhenghong, his expression once again calm.","\"Since you know of the Trading Company, you must have heard the name Pingzheng Hall as well.\"","As he spoke, he produced a Black Iron Token from his sleeve. Inscribed upon it was the single word: \"Pingzheng.\"","\"I am Li Sanyuan, Wind Patrol Envoy of Pingzheng Hall of the Ji State Trading Company. Forgive my impertinence, Patriarch Lin.\"","Though his words were apologetic, his gaze was far more arrogant than before as he stared fixedly at Lin Zhenghong.","In contrast, Lin Zhenghong’s face was now pale, sweat beading on his forehead.","\"I... I... no, it’s... I did hear my father mention Pingzheng Hall. Please... please, forgive me.\"","He couldn’t help but recall Lin Huai’an’s warning before his death—","The full name of the Ji State Trading Company was the \"Ji State Five Prefectures He Yuan Trading Company,\" and it was indeed initially founded by several families within Ji State.","But as time passed, its members had long since gone into hiding.","Even the whereabouts of the five founding families of the Ji State Five Prefectures He Yuan Trading Company were now unknown.","Perhaps they had all assumed new identities.","But the internal organizational structure of the Trading Company was still preserved.","It was a complete hierarchy, from the upper echelons of the Five Mansions Old Hall, the Chief Shopkeeper, and the Hall Masters; down to the six divisions of Accounts, Escorts, Auditing, Works, Transport, and Clients; and further down to the Shopkeepers and Cashiers in every state.","Beyond these, the Ji State Trading Company had also established a unique division known as Pingzheng Hall.","Its name meant \"to pacify turmoil and restore order from chaos.\"","According to Lin Huai’an, the Hall Master of Pingzheng Hall was utterly uncompromising. It was common for him to punish minor offenses severely, and major ones even more so.","Within the Ji State Trading Company, he was known as the \"Living Yama.\"","Consequently, Pingzheng Hall was also called \"Yama Hall\" by those within the Trading Company. Anyone they targeted would be lucky to escape with their life; even then, they would be flayed.","And Li Sanyuan was one of Pingzheng Hall’s three special envoys—the Clear Wind Envoy, the Wind Patrol Envoy, and the Wind Listener—serving as the Wind Patrol Envoy.","His specific duty was to oversee the Trading Company’s branches at the state and county level.","Furthermore, at critical moments, the \"Three Envoys\" of Pingzheng Hall could also intervene in the business affairs of those branches.","When that happened, it almost always meant that the branch’s Shopkeeper and Cashier were about to be punished.","This was what Lin Zhenghong feared.","Li Sanyuan stared at him for a long time, watching until sweat was pouring down his face, before finally giving a slight nod.","\"A man’s greatest fear should be a loss of reverence—reverence for the heavens and the earth, for the Imperial Court, and for his parents.\"","\"The fact that you still hold some reverence for the Trading Company is, at least, a good thing.\"","He paused, his tone shifting. \"However, were it not for Lin Huai’an’s unexpected death... The Company’s plans in Shu State are of great importance. As you are now, you are far from qualified to be promoted to ’Shopkeeper.’\"","Hearing this, Lin Zhenghong bowed in acquiescence. Wiping the sweat from his forehead, he said in a low voice:","\"Your... your criticisms are just.\"","\"I still have many shortcomings. I hope... I hope Lord Wind Patrol Envoy will be lenient with me.\"","Li Sanyuan glanced at him and gestured with a wave. \"Sit down. We can talk.\"","\"Yes.\"","Once Lin Zhenghong was perched on the very edge of his chair, his mind finally began to clear. He forced a smile and asked:","\"My lord, you... you wanted to discuss the matter of Lv Jiunan?\"","Recalling what had just happened, he instantly understood why Li Sanyuan had taken out the Token to reveal his identity.","It had to be because of his dismissive attitude toward the news that \"Lv Jiunan wasn’t dead.\" He had clearly displeased Li Sanyuan, the Wind Patrol Envoy."]},{"number":469,"title":"Chapter 469 - 285: How Did He Calculate This?","paragraphs":["Li Sanyuan glanced at the teacup on the table and said in a calm tone:","\"Your father died too quickly. He didn’t have time to teach you the Trading Company’s rules, nor did he pass on any business experience. I shouldn’t be punishing you.\"","\"But the rule of ’major punishment for minor mistakes’ was set by the Hall Master himself. We dare not defy it.\"","\"So...\"","Li Sanyuan said softly, \"After this, I will report the matter to the Trading Company and let the Hall Master decide your fate.\"","Of course, with his status, he could have punished Lin Zhenghong himself, but Lin Zhenghong was Lin Huai’an’s son, after all.","Perhaps the Trading Company would go easy on Lin Zhenghong out of respect for Lin Huai’an.","\"Sir, this... this...\"","Lin Zhenghong looked at him in terror, feeling his limbs go weak and limp.","After a long moment, he came to his senses and said resignedly, \"I am willing to accept your punishment, Sir. But... but...\"","\"But Sir, could you please tell me exactly what I did wrong?\"","Li Sanyuan shot him a glance. \"I’ll let you die knowing why.\"","\"The grain belongs to the Trading Company, not your Lin Family. That is your first mistake.\"","\"You sought small profits for the Lin Family and forgot the greater profits of the Trading Company. That is your second mistake.\"","\"You learned that ’Lv Jiunan is not dead’ but made no preparations to ’mitigate the risk’...\"","Li Sanyuan said, enunciating each word, \"That is your third mistake!\"","Hearing this, Lin Zhenghong shook his head with a bitter smile. He had only heard that the Trading Company had many rules, but he never expected them to be so meticulous.","Of course he knew the grain belonged to the Ji State Trading Company, but what was wrong with calling it \"his Lin Family’s\" behind closed doors?","The accusation of seeking small profits was also baseless; it wasn’t as if the silver he earned wouldn’t be turned over to the Trading Company.","As for the \"matter of Lv Jiunan,\" well...","At this thought, Lin Zhenghong gritted his teeth and said, \"I had no intention of seeking personal gain, much less of violating the Trading Company’s rules.\"","Li Sanyuan could see his subordinate’s defiance and continued in a lecturing tone:","\"With that kind of talk, the grain price we worked so hard to raise could come crashing down.\"","\"That would be a loss for the Trading Company, an unforgivable blunder.\"","Lin Zhenghong still wasn’t ready to give up. \"May I ask, Sir, in such a situation, how should I...’mitigate’?\"","Li Sanyuan snorted. \"Then let me teach you how to be a proper ’Shopkeeper’ for our Ji State Trading Company.\"","\"First, ’Spread.’ This matter should be shared among several grain merchants.\"","\"You should have sold a portion of the grain in your current warehouses to the other grain merchants at a fair price to ensure the silver you received wouldn’t be too much of a loss.\"","\"Second, ’Transfer.’\"","\"If you determine that the grain price will not rise further, you must transfer all the grain as quickly as possible, preferably to someone outside our circle of grain merchants.\"","\"Third... just like with the previous ’Asutai’ incident, you fabricate more rumors.\"","He looked at the conflicted Lin Zhenghong and asked, \"I’ve laid out the paths for you.\"","\"Which one will you choose?\"","After listening, sweat began to trickle down Lin Zhenghong’s face again. \"I... I don’t know. What would you choose, Sir?\"","Li Sanyuan looked at his pathetic state, shook his head, and stopped his lecture.","\"In my judgment, thirteen silver per shi is the absolute limit.\"","\"Even without the ’Lv Jiunan’ incident, the Government Office would be unable to withstand the pressure from the common people.\"","\"Unless King Landu or the Barbarian Race really make a move, it’s no longer wise for the grain price to keep rising.\"","\"Therefore, I believe we should use the ’Transfer’ method. Find a suitable person to take over.\"","Lin Zhenghong didn’t hesitate for a second. He nodded immediately. \"Alright, I’ll do as you say.\"","\"But a ’suitable’ person... The other grain merchants?\"","\"Unsuitable.\"","Li Sanyuan shook his head, then gestured outside. \"Isn’t there still a certain Miss Cui from the Cui Family who insists on sticking her nose in?\"","\"Her?\"","\"Oh, she is indeed suitable... But... but how could she possibly agree?\"","\"Lure her with profit.\"","Lin Zhenghong understood instantly. \"You mean, a lower price?\"","\"Since she’s so eager to establish a foothold in Shu State, it’s only right she should take some risks, isn’t it?\"","\"You... You’re right...\"","...","「Nightfall.」","A gloomy rain fell, intermittent and unceasing.","The cool wind blew through Tingyu Pavilion, making the wind chimes DING DONG.","The crisp sounds mingled together, a counterpoint to the laughter coming from the rear residence.","\"Miss Cui, you come from the Qinghe Cui Family. Unlike the few of us, you were born to do great things.\"","\"Right now, the grain prices in the Prefecture City are rising sharply. We... we’re truly afraid of getting burned.\"","\"So all of you want to sell your entire stock of grain to me?\"","\"If the price falls, wouldn’t I be the one left holding the bag?\"","\"You’re mistaken, Miss Cui.\"","Lin Zhenghong said with a smile, \"The grain price will fall sooner or later, but not too soon.\"","\"Before that happens, if our shops focus all their efforts on selling, we definitely won’t let you take a loss.\"","\"We’re just afraid of ’having the money but not the life to spend it.’ We hope Miss Cui can lend us a hand.\"","He shot a look at the others and said euphemistically, \"You must remember what you said a few days ago when you came looking for us.\"","\"If you don’t earn this silver, we can’t earn it either.\"","\"That being the case, is it acceptable for us to earn a little less, and for you to earn a little more?\"","The others chimed in with agreement, saying things like \"That’s how it should be.\"","Cui Qingwu leaned back in her chair, watching them calmly, but her mind was racing.","’So these people really did come to me.’","’And they’re trying to sell all their grain to me even before Liu Wu has done those two things.’","’This...’","’Liu Wu... how... how did he do it?’","Compared to this question, Cui Qingwu wasn’t too concerned about Lin Zhenghong and the others showing up.","As long as Liu Wu did those two things—having the Poshisu Country horse bandits and the Barbarian Race scouts attack—the grain price in Shu State definitely wouldn’t fall.","She was certain she wouldn’t lose silver.","’Then what?’","’Would those grain merchants be content to just watch her earn silver?’","’Not likely.’","’Or does Liu Wu just want to make this one pot of silver?’","’But that clearly wouldn’t be enough to achieve his goal of harming the Ji State Trading Company.’","’Unless...’","Cui Qingwu faintly sensed Liu Wu’s true intentions. As understanding dawned on her, she couldn’t help but feel a flicker of admiration.","’This man really has some skill.’","’No wonder Lou Yuxue is so interested in him.’","Thinking this, Cui Qingwu rested her slender hand on the back of the chair. She already knew what choice to make.","\"Since all you bosses are being so sincere, I won’t be tactless.\"","\"But business is business. So, tell me, what price are you offering to get me to agree?\"","Lin Zhenghong bowed. \"Thank you, Miss Cui.\"","Then he continued, \"Before coming, we naturally considered this and decided on a price of eleven silver per shi...\"","Before he could finish, Cui Qingwu raised a hand to cut him off. \"Are you stupid, or do you take me for a fool?\"","\"With that much grain in your hands, at that price, are you trying to bankrupt my Qinghe Cui Family?\"","\"This...\"","Lin Zhenghong and the others exchanged a look, then asked hesitantly, \"Then, Miss Cui, what do you have in mind?\"","\"Eight silver.\"","\"Eight... No, no! That price is far too low! We... we’d be taking a huge loss...\"","Cui Qingwu paid no mind to their protests, signaling to Huan’er. \"Show our guests out.\"","Huan’er understood and stepped forward, glaring at them coldly. \"It’s late. If you please.\"","Obviously, Lin Zhenghong and the others were not going to leave so readily.","Nor were they willing to accept Cui Qingwu’s price.","After a round of haggling.","Cui Qingwu stood up and made her final offer. \"Ten silver per shi, then.\"","Then, before the grain Shopkeepers could speak, she continued, \"However, I don’t have that much silver on hand right now.\"","\"How about we distribute the profits after the grain is sold?\"","Lin Zhenghong and the others looked at each other, knowing this was the best outcome they could hope for, and broke into smiles.","\"Once the contract is signed, we naturally won’t worry about Miss Cui’s integrity.\"","\"The contracts... we brought them with us.\"","Seeing this, Cui Qingwu suddenly laughed. \"It seems you gentlemen truly came prepared.\"","\"In that case, let’s sign and make our marks.\"","\"Yes...\"","Once everything was settled, Lin Zhenghong and the others left Tingyu Pavilion with the contracts.","Before they even got on their carriages,","they were already beaming.","Ten silver per shi! Compared to the initial grain price, they had earned more than ten times their investment.","They had made a fortune.","Even if the grain price rose a bit more, the silver Cui Qingwu earned would still be a drop in the ocean compared to their profits.","\"Brother Lin, your plan... Brilliant!\"","\"Like father, like son, indeed.\"","\"Haha... You’re all too kind...\"","Cui Qingwu heard their voices from afar and couldn’t help but smile as well.","\"Fools. They don’t even know they’ve been had.\"","At her side, Huan’er, who was unaware of the plotting that took place in the Spring Rain Building, heard this and asked:","\"Miss, what if the grain price falls...\"","Cui Qingwu cut her off. \"There is no ’what if’.\"","After a pause, she beckoned. \"Prepare the horses. We’re going out.\"","\"Yes...\"","Cui Qingwu looked toward the central courtyard, faintly hearing the soft sounds of Chen Yunfan practicing his sword forms, and her smile widened.","’To think there’s someone in this world who can compare to Brother Yunfan. He must be quite a character.’","As she thought this, she recalled that other question and couldn’t help but purse her lips.","\"That Liu Wu is always so secretive...\""]},{"number":470,"title":"Chapter 470 - 286: Affection Fills Half the Autumn City","paragraphs":["Huan’er readied the carriage and horses.","Cui Qingwu boarded the carriage and left the rear residence.","As they passed the central courtyard, she couldn’t help but say, \"Stop the carriage.\"","Huan’er pulled on the reins. \"Miss?\"","\"Get an umbrella for me.\"","\"Oh.\"","Cui Qingwu stepped down from the carriage, told Huan’er to wait for her, and then entered the central courtyard holding an Oil Paper Umbrella.","Just as before.","Inside the Martial Arts Arena, a structure with gray tiles and white walls situated by the rockery and pond in the central courtyard, Chun Ying, Ning Yu, and Niu Mountain were holding umbrellas and watching the center of the arena.","Chen Yunfan, wearing only long pants, was bare-chested, practicing his sword in the rain.","Cui Qingwu peeked over for a glance. A faint, almost imperceptible blush colored her cheeks, and she lowered her Oil Paper Umbrella slightly to shield her view.","When Chun Ying and the other two saw her, they quickly bowed. \"Miss Cui.\"","Cui Qingwu acknowledged them with a soft sound and walked to their side, her gaze falling upon Chen Yunfan.","Unlike before, Chen Yunfan was no longer practicing specific swordsmanship techniques. Instead, he had returned to the basics, focusing only on fundamental sword moves.","Thrusts, slashes, parries, and so on.","They seemed simple, yet every strike felt perfectly natural and complete.","It was as if that figure and that Long Sword had merged into the rain, creating a perfectly harmonious scene.","As Cui Qingwu watched, a hint of surprise appeared on her face. \"Brother Yunfan’s Sword Dao... is he about to have a breakthrough?\"","She herself also practiced the Sword Dao, and although she was only at the Minor Success Realm, she could still sense the power of the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","—A power that faintly surpassed that of the Great Success Sword Dao.","Chun Ying, Ning Yu, and Niu Mountain exchanged glances upon hearing her words. Chun Ying was the one to speak.","\"The Young Master has had some insights recently. Perhaps he will break through soon.\"","She used the word ’perhaps’ cautiously.","But to Cui Qingwu’s ears, it meant that Chen Yunfan’s breakthrough to the Perfection Realm of Sword Dao was only a matter of time.","In the Martial Arts, intent and comprehension were paramount.","Some people could achieve a sudden enlightenment and step into the Supreme Realm in a single day.","Others could strive their entire lives and never break through.","That was simply the way of things.","And for someone like Chen Yunfan, it was as if he already had one foot through the door of the Perfect Sword Dao.","All he lacked was the right opportunity.","’Brother Yunfan is working so hard...’","Cui Qingwu took one last deep look at Chen Yunfan, who was still immersed in his Cultivation, and turned to walk away.","\"I have other matters to attend to. I’ll come back when Brother Yunfan is free.\"","She made up her mind. After she was done with her business in the coming days, she too would enter secluded Cultivation.","She didn’t expect to reach Perfection in a single leap, but she had to at least achieve Great Success in her Sword Dao.","Chun Ying watched her walk away, then waited a moment longer until she saw Ning Yu give a signal. Only then did she let out a sigh of relief.","The unwritten secrets of the White-robed Minister could be passed on to Chen Yunfan, but no outsiders could ever learn of them.","Especially not Cui Qingwu.","Not even if she was Chen Yunfan’s fiancée.","’After all, the Qinghe Cui Family... they’re not to be underestimated...’","...","「Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion, Spring Lotus Garden.」","Compared to Chen Yunfan’s diligent and arduous training, Chen Yi seemed much more at ease.","At this moment, he was leaning back in a rocking chair in his study, staring unblinkingly at the book in his hands, titled *Sangyue’s Story*.","The pitter-patter of the ceaseless rain could be heard.","Four oil lamps were lit in the spacious study.","It was brightly illuminated.","The patterned window was pushed open a crack, letting in a cool breeze that made the candlelight flicker and sway.","The chair rocked back and forth, casting shifting light and shadows across Chen Yi’s tranquil face.","\"Sang Yue, the conflict between the Sang Country and the Yue Kingdom, the struggle between the north and south of the Central Plains... they certainly produced many heroes.\"","*Sangyue’s Story* was a historical text similar to the *Spring and Autumn Annals* or the *Records of the Grand Historian*.","It recorded the struggles between two great dynasties, the Sang Country and the Yue Kingdom, that took place on the lands of the Great Wei a thousand years ago.","It also detailed their respective deeds in fighting off invasions from the northern nomads and the southern Barbarian Race.","Many heroes were listed within its pages, including several Saints, Princes, and Grand Generals, and even the most powerful Martial Arts practitioners of that era were chronicled.","\"A few strokes of a brush, and a person’s entire life is written.\"","\"Right and wrong, success and failure—all empty in a blink... is it not the same in our time?\"","Chen Yi let out a soft laugh, set down *Sangyue’s Story*, and looked out the window.","Seeing that it was getting late.","He got up, preparing to return to his private room.","Just then, Xiaodie walked in, light on her feet, carrying a bowl of ginseng soup that she carefully placed on the table.","\"Master, the Eldest Miss had Sister Huatang send over this ginseng soup. She said you should drink it while it’s hot.\"","Chen Yi glanced at it and said with a smile, \"I barely leave the house all day. What do I need replenishing for?\"","Xiaodie shook her head, her twin hair buns bobbing and casting dancing shadows.","\"No, no, the Eldest Miss said you’ve been studying hard lately and need to replenish your strength.\"","Chen Yi chuckled, at a loss for words. He didn’t refuse again, simply picking up the small bowl and downing it in one gulp.","Warmth flowed down his throat.","But soon, the nourishing components of the ginseng soup were completely digested by his body.","With his current level of Cultivation, ordinary soups and liquids could not replenish his body at all.","Only the endless Spiritual Qi and Spiritual Mechanism between Heaven and Earth could possibly supplement his body’s consumption.","Xiaodie knew nothing of this; she was just happy that he had finished the ginseng soup.","\"Master, did you ask about the Annual Examination when you went to Guiyun Academy today?\"","\"I got the general idea.\"","Compared to the County Examination and the Prefecture Examination, the Annual Examination was intended to test one’s knowledge.","Although there would be rankings, it was more of an opportunity to display what one had learned.","It wouldn’t take as long as the others.","The examination would be completed in a single day. Afterward, Ma Shuhan and the others would grade the papers, and the candidates’ results would be posted on the third day.","If there were no major issues, Ma Shuhan would only stay in the Prefecture City for five days before heading to the other counties in Shu State to conduct the next Annual Examination.","Xiaodie pumped her fists encouragingly. \"You’ll have no problem, Master.\"","\"Maybe... no, you’ll definitely be first in the Annual Examination.\"","Chen Yi looked at her and gently tapped her on the forehead.","As he walked out of the study, he said with a laugh, \"I’m not one for fame. Go wash up and get some sleep.\""]},{"number":471,"title":"Chapter 471 - 286: Love Fills Half the Autumn City","paragraphs":["Xiaodie rubbed her forehead as she watched him disappear out the door, a smile blooming on her fair, youthful face.","\"Our second son-in-law, who dislikes fame, is now renowned throughout the world, hehe.\"","Aside from keeping up with the major and minor affairs inside and outside the mansion, she spent most of her days listening to all sorts of rumors about Chen Yi.","For example, she’d hear about the reactions of talented scholars and great Confucian masters when his famous poem, \"Song of the Water Melody,\" spread to another state capital.","Or how Chen Yi had joined the ranks of the Great Wei Dynasty’s contemporary Calligraphy masters with his Perfect Realm Calligraphy Dao.","And other rumors, some plausible and some not.","Whether they were words of praise or criticism, she listened with great interest.","Xiaodie even took the most brilliant compliments and recorded them in a special little booklet, along with all the things, big and small, that Chen Yi did.","She would flip through it from time to time.","Xiaodie had even given the booklet a title: *Biography of the Marquis’s Mansion’s Second Son-in-Law*.","But in her heart, she preferred its full title: *Biography of the Marquis’s Mansion’s Second Son-in-Law and His Little Maid*.","However, just thinking such a thing made her face burn.","In the end, she compromised on the title.","’When I get married someday, I’ll give it to the second son-in-law... hmm... If only I didn’t have to marry and could just stay by his side forever...’","\"Ah!\"","Xiaodie’s face flushed red. She quickly looked away from the door, tidied up the study, and left with the small bowl in hand, her steps light and quick.","’How shameless, how shameless... My heart is overflowing.’","...","Late that night, once the wooden building had fallen silent, Chen Yi listened intently for a moment before changing into a set of black clothes. By the faint light, he altered his appearance to look like Liu Wu.","He had much to do tonight, so he had to leave Spring Lotus Garden early.","’Wang Ji should have spread the news that Lv Jiunan was not yet dead to those grain stores this afternoon.’","’Even if they prepared in advance, they would likely just pay more attention to the movements within the city. It’s unlikely they’d think to go looking for Cui Qingwu.’","’Ultimately, I’ll have to make Lv Jiunan show himself.’","Chen Yi had been plotting for days and knew the plan by heart; he was quite confident.","The goal of this step-by-step scheme was singular: to make those grain stores cough up their grain as quickly as possible.","Otherwise, how could he dig a pit and bury the people from the Ji State Trading Company?","That was the plan, anyway.","But when Chen Yi, after taking a roundabout route, finally arrived at the Spring Rain Building, the news he received from Cui Qingwu was startling.","\"Are you saying that Lin... that Lin’s Grain Store and the others have already sold all their grain to you?\"","Seeing his surprised expression, Cui Qingwu couldn’t help but frown.","\"Isn’t this the result of your scheme? I was about to ask you how you did it.\"","Chen Yi didn’t answer right away. He lowered his head in thought for a moment, then suddenly shook his head and started to laugh.","\"It seems I underestimated those people’s intelligence.\"","\"To think there were such characters who thought themselves so clever.\"","Cui Qingwu and Lou Yuxue exchanged a glance, and Cui Qingwu couldn’t help but ask, \"What? Did something unexpected happen?\"","\"You were the one who instructed me to agree to their request without fail if they came looking for me.\"","\"If you back out now, you’ll have to compensate me for the silver I lost.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi waved his hand. \"I’m not backing out. I just didn’t expect it to happen so quickly.\"","Cui Qingwu’s brow furrowed slightly. \"They didn’t come because of you?\"","\"Yes and no.\"","Chen Yi said, holding back a laugh, \"I only spread the news that Lv Jiunan wasn’t dead. My original intention was to make them slow the pace of their grain price hikes. Forcing them to seek you out was supposed to be the next step.\"","\"But I never imagined they would sell the grain to you without even waiting to verify if the news was true.\"","\"This is good, too. It makes my plan even more certain.\"","\"It’s just that...\"","\"Wait!\"","Before Chen Yi could finish, Lou Yuxue seized on the key point of his words, staring at him and demanding:","\"Who did you say isn’t dead?\"","Chen Yi stopped and repeated with a smile, \"Lv Jiunan isn’t dead.\"","Cui Qingwu reacted as well. \"Lv Jiunan? Isn’t he dead?\"","Lou Yuxue nodded. \"You were the one who killed him with a single spear thrust that day.\"","The smile on Chen Yi’s face grew wider. \"It’s not wrong for you to think so.\"","\"He was indeed on the brink of death that day, but I saved him afterward.\"","\"Saved... You...\"","Cui Qingwu’s mouth fell open. She thought of his Medical Dao and understood that such a thing was indeed possible.","But what surprised her even more was that Liu Wu had already been planning all of this back then.","Otherwise, why would he have saved Lv Jiunan?","Lou Yuxue was equally shocked. \"You, you, you...\"","\"Lv Jiunan not being dead is huge news! Why didn’t you say so earlier?!\"","\"Do you know how close we were? I... King Nalandu was about to hire other masters to deal with you!\"","Chen Yi glanced at her and asked with a smile, \"The General came to see you last night, right?\"","The agitated look on Lou Yuxue’s face froze. \"How did you know?\"","\"Did you follow me last night?\"","Chen Yi let out a laugh, shaking his head. \"I don’t have that much free time.\"","\"Then how did you find out?\"","\"It’s simple. You used the signal we agreed upon last night, appearing at the entrance of the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office at noon today. It clearly wasn’t because you had found Du Cang.\"","\"Thinking it over, the only possibility was that you had something to discuss with me.\"","Lou Yuxue understood, but her words were still stubborn. \"Then tell me, what business did Lord General have with me?\"","Chen Yi shot her a look, a half-smile on his face. \"Do you really want me to say it?\"","Lou Yuxue turned her head away. \"You could never guess.\"","Seeing her still acting stubborn, Chen Yi had no choice but to say, \"I’m guessing he came to you to discuss joining forces with King Landu’s band of horse bandits to ambush and kill me.\"","\"You...\"","Before Lou Yuxue could speak, Chen Yi continued, \"But I don’t think someone with your intelligence would have agreed.\"","\"But as his subordinate, you couldn’t refuse him outright, so...\"","\"So you gave him that letter?\"","Lou Yuxue’s eyes went wide as she stared at Chen Yi, her pointing finger trembling as if she were looking at a monster.","\"You... you... you guessed all of that?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. \"From your reaction, it seems that letter is quite important to you all.\"","\"Important enough to make the General give up his deal with King Landu?\"","Hearing this, Lou Yuxue’s face turned pale, then red. After a long moment, she said dejectedly:","\"I don’t know.\"","She truly didn’t know the General’s intentions; she could only guess.","Chen Yi smiled at her but didn’t press the matter.","’A single letter in exchange for all that grain from Cui Qingwu... that’s comparable to three hundred thousand silver coins. It’s a good deal either way.’","He was, however, curious how the White Tiger Guard would handle that letter.","’Use it to investigate Zhu Hao, the Deputy Commander of the Shu State Capital Commandery?’","’Or keep it as a trump card?’","Chen Yi couldn’t know for sure, but he guessed that after the White Tiger Guard gave up their deal with King Landu, they would certainly come up with another plan.","\"So, tell me, what does your ’Lord General’ have planned?\"","Lou Yuxue subconsciously glanced at Cui Qingwu, who was listening with pricked ears, then gritted her teeth and said stiffly:","\"The Lord wants to join forces with you to ambush and kill Du Cang.\"","Chen Yi wasn’t surprised. He clapped his hands with a smile. \"Now that’s something the White Tiger Guard ought to be doing.\"","\"Tell me, what’s the plan?\"","\"The Lord has already sent a message to King Landu, pretending to agree to his request. He will leak your whereabouts to Du Cang to lure him out.\"","Chen Yi understood. \"So you want me to be the bait?\"","Lou Yuxue grunted in affirmation. \"If you want to find Du Cang, this is the fastest way.\"","Chen Yi didn’t deny this point.","It was just that he was always the one scheming against others. To suddenly be \"schemed against\" himself felt a bit strange.","He thought for a moment.","He nodded. \"Alright, we’ll do it your way.\"","\"Then what should we tell them?\"","\"Just say... that in five days, I will have another sparring match with Liu Lang at the Chishui River.\"","\"Another one?\"","Lou Yuxue thought of the traces left by the Chishui River outside the city. \"So it really was you and Liu Lang.\"","After listening to their conversation, Cui Qingwu spoke up with a smile, \"Besides him, who else could create such a massive disturbance?\"","In Shu State Prefecture City... no, in the entire Jianghu of Shu State, besides \"Dragon Spear\" Liu Wu, who else could shatter a hundred zhang with a single spear thrust?","There was a moment of silence.","Lou Yuxue finally calmed down. Remembering something, she said, \"There’s one more thing from today.\"","Chen Yi raised a hand, gesturing for her to just say it.","\"At noon, someone came to Bright Moon Building and paid a hefty deposit.\"","\"For what?\"","\"The person wants to find the Barbarian Prince, Asutai!\"","\"Oh?\"","Chen Yi looked at her with some surprise, thought for a moment, and asked, \"What do you think his identity is?\"","Lou Yuxue thought back for a moment and shook her head. \"The person didn’t reveal anything at all.\"","\"But... he shouldn’t be very old.\"","\"Anything else?\"","\"Anything else...\"","\"There was an old servant with him... his eyes were very familiar. I feel like I’ve seen him somewhere before...\""]},{"number":472,"title":"Chapter 472 - 287: Are These Two of Sufficient Weight?","paragraphs":["’Familiar eyes?’","’What kind of identifying feature is that?’","Given Lou Yuxue’s position, she saw a staggering number of people every day in the Spring Rain Building alone.","Trying to find someone based only on their \"eyes\" was no less difficult than when he’d found Lv Jiunan based only on his voice.","It was no exaggeration to call it looking for a needle in a haystack.","Chen Yi thought for a moment. \"Be more specific.\"","Lou Yuxue felt a wave of exasperation, but she also wanted to know who would commission the Bright Moon Building to find Asutai.","\"The young man was slender, with a somewhat scholarly air about him. His Martial Arts Cultivation was average.\"","\"His eyes.\"","\"...They were very intense. What’s with that look? He... he didn’t even show his eyebrows, and I only saw him for a split second.\"","Chen Yi discreetly pursed his lips. \"And the old servant? Was he the same?\"","Lou Yuxue crossed her arms, her voice laced with displeasure and a hint of indignation. \"They were dressed similarly.\"","\"Which way did they go when they left?\"","\"West.\"","Chen Yi let out an \"oh.\" \"East, then.\"","\"No, it was—\"","Just as Lou Yuxue was about to correct him, she caught on. \"Are you saying they were trying to throw us off?\"","As he mulled over their identities, Chen Yi said snidely, \"When you do clandestine things, you also try to lead people astray.\"","’Damn, I’m an idiot,’ Lou Yuxue cursed inwardly, ’letting this bastard mock me for nothing.’","However, her initial assumption hadn’t been entirely flawed—she had thought the two were members of the Evil Demonic Dao from West Market’s Heiyu Lane.","’On second thought, that bastard \"Liu Wu\" is right.’","Members of the Evil Demonic Dao were indeed skilled at concealing their identities, but their Martial Arts Cultivation was never weak.","Yet the old man and the youth who had come during the day possessed only average martial arts.","And a lucrative job like finding the \"Barbarian Prince,\" worth a fortune, would normally attract some heavy hitters.","Like the previous \"Financier\" who had proposed the major job of \"burning the Three Towns’ summer grain\"—the Ji State Trading Company.","\"Even if you rule out the area east of the Spring Rain Building, you can still figure out who they are?\"","Upon hearing this, Cui Qingwu also looked at Chen Yi, a smile playing on her lips. \"’Dragon Spear,’ she may not believe in you, but I do.\"","She had previously doubted that \"Liu Wu\" had the power to move heaven and earth.","But after personally witnessing Lin Zhenghong and his men arrive, she was certain that this man not only possessed immense Martial Arts Cultivation, but his intellect was also far beyond that of an ordinary person.","Lou Yuxue opened her mouth to retort, but just shot Cui Qingwu a glare and stubbornly held her tongue.","Chen Yi glanced between the two, paying no mind to their squabbling, and said thoughtfully,","\"There is one person who fits the description.\"","\"But if it really is him... then it seems he’s been backed into a corner.\"","\"Who?\"","\"’Dragon Spear,’ do tell us.\"","\"Liu Hong.\"","Lou Yuxue and Cui Qingwu froze. \"Liu Hong?\"","\"But he...\"","Just as Lou Yuxue was about to object, the memory of those familiar eyes suddenly surfaced in her mind. A look of astonishment spread across her face.","\"It was him! It was really him!\"","Seeing her confirmation, a faint smile touched Chen Yi’s lips.","He had a pretty good idea why Liu Hong had come—it must have been the result of his meeting with Du Cang.","It was a threat.","Du Cang had likely forced Liu Hong to find Asutai by a certain deadline.","As for the reason...","Either the Barbarian Race had gone to the Ancient Tea-Horse Road and given those horse bandits an ultimatum.","Or King Landu wanted to exchange Asutai for the Barbarian Race’s aid, allowing him to lead his army across the border and avenge Lv Jiunan.","In any case, all the pressure was now on Liu Hong.","After all, he was the one who’d lost Asutai.","As these thoughts flashed through his mind, Chen Yi couldn’t help but grow curious.","’Just what has Liu Hong, the Governor of Shu State, done for the Barbarian Race and Poshisu Country to make him so afraid that he’d risk coming to the Bright Moon Building?’","Seeing him fall silent, Lou Yuxue couldn’t resist asking, \"You know something, don’t you?\"","\"Why would Liu Hong come here?\"","\"And why does he want to find Asutai?\"","Based on the intelligence she had previously received from the General, it wasn’t hard to guess that Liu Hong was a man with deep secrets.","He not only maintained a private army but might also have ties to Poshisu Country.","But Asutai was the son of Left King Mu Hage of the Barbarian Race; he had nothing to do with Poshisu Country.","\"Could it be... he wants to help King Landu find Asutai?\"","Chen Yi considered this. \"That’s a possibility.\"","\"Remember what I said about Du Cang meeting with Liu Hong? I suspect that on that day, Du Cang threatened him, forcing him to find Asutai.\"","\"Du Cang...\"","Lou Yuxue relaxed slightly. \"If that’s the case, then it’s understandable why he came to the Bright Moon Building.\"","After all, the Barbarian Race wasn’t on the same level as King Landu. They were the Great Wei Dynasty’s greatest threat, a matter that allowed for no carelessness.","Seeing her relax, Chen Yi decided not to mention Liu Hong’s connections to the Barbarian Race and changed the subject.","\"Whatever his objective is, it doesn’t affect our cooperation.\"","\"Right now, the most important thing is to deal with the people from the Ji State Trading Company.\"","Cui Qingwu had been waiting for these words. \"So, tell us. How do you plan to make those grain Trading Companies take the bait?\"","After learning why Lin Zhenghong and his men had come, and having prior knowledge of the \"major event\" Chen Yi was planning, she had already guessed his intentions.","—Before they faked an invasion from Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race, the grain had to be back in the hands of those grain Trading Companies.","Only then would the Ji State Trading Company suffer a massive loss.","Otherwise, in the current situation, the grain Trading Companies controlled by the Ji State Trading Company would, at most, just make a little less silver.","Their foundation would remain unscathed.","Chen Yi smiled. \"We’ll just let someone go and tip them off.\"","He then turned to Cui Qingwu. \"When the time comes, I’ll have to ask Miss Cui’s subordinates... not to hold back.\"","A rare smile graced Cui Qingwu’s face. \"You’re already forcing their heads onto the chopping block. How could I possibly hesitate?\"","Seeing the two of them joking around, Lou Yuxue, who was standing to the side, remained preoccupied with Liu Hong.","\"Enough chitchat. I’m going to find Lord General now.\"","But before she could even rise to leave the private room, a soft knock sounded at the door."]},{"number":473,"title":"Chapter 473 - 287: Is Their Weight Sufficient?","paragraphs":["\"A report, my lord. Lord General requests your presence.\"","Lou Yuxue raised a single eyebrow and replied, \"One moment. I’ll be right there.\"","But the person outside hesitated. \"Forgive me, my lord, but Lord General wishes to invite Lord Simurgh Phoenix to discuss an urgent matter.\"","\"...\"","Lou Yuxue’s expression flickered for an instant before she sat back down.","Although Cui Qingwu found the situation amusing, the thought of the General didn’t exactly please her either.","Still, after a moment’s thought, she rose and headed for the door.","\"’It seems I’m the one who’ll have to report these matters to Lord General, then.’\"","Lou Yuxue couldn’t resist reminding her, \"Especially the business with Liu Hong.\"","Cui Qingwu glanced back at her. \"Is there anything else?\"","The words had barely left her mouth when she turned to Chen Yi, a suggestive look on her face.","\"Oh... and then there’s the matter of ’Lord Dragon Spear’?\"","\"I never thought Lord Simurgh Phoenix would be so ruthless. ’Lord Dragon Spear’ just did you a great service, yet you’re already thinking of selling him out?\"","Lou Yuxue remained unfazed. She snorted, \"This was agreed upon between me and Lord General.\"","\"So... you’re more concerned about ’Lord Dragon Spear’?\"","\"You!?\"","\"Haha...\"","Seeing her flustered, Cui Qingwu laughed, turned, and walked out of the meditation room, leaving with the person who had summoned her.","Once the meditation room fell completely silent, Chen Yi glanced at Lou Yuxue, whose chest was rising and falling unevenly, and said with a smile, \"Well then, I’ll be on my way.\"","\"Wait.\"","\"Hm?\"","Meeting Chen Yi’s gaze, Lou Yuxue stammered, \"That Du Cang... his cultivation is high. You... you be careful.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"Thank you for your concern, Lord Lady Tiger.\"","\"But shouldn’t this be a joint operation between the White Tiger Guard and me?\"","\"Or are you saying you have no intention of getting involved at all?\"","Lou Yuxue’s face flushed red, and she turned her head away. \"My cultivation is too low. If anyone from our side makes a move, it will be Lord General.\"","\"Him? That works.\"","Despite what he said, Chen Yi never actually expected the White Tiger Guard to truly join forces with him against Du Cang.","’If you’re going to put on a show, you have to see it through.’","’Either way, he’d have to face off against Du Cang eventually.’","After a few more words of idle chat, Chen Yi rose and took his leave.","The meditation room fell completely silent once more.","Lou Yuxue stared wordlessly at the oil lamp on the table, seemingly oblivious to Chen Yi’s departure.","Her thoughts were a jumble.","’She had been the one to propose the ambush on Du Cang, but now that the time was near, she was starting to worry.’","’I hope his Martial Arts are strong enough.’","’Du Cang... he’s no easy target...’","Chen Yi didn’t need Lou Yuxue’s reminder; he knew full well that Du Cang was a powerful adversary.","A ruthless man capable of becoming King Landu’s right hand and training the Jackal Army wouldn’t just sit back and wait to be killed.","’He’d probably have to go and sweep the burial site he’d chosen for Du Cang ahead of time.’","At this thought, Chen Yi gave a wry smile. ’Five days... I hope he can last that long.’","’Originally, he was confident that Du Cang would choose to remain in Shu State after learning of his presence.’","’But because those clever-for-nothing idiots from the Ji State Trading Company had given the grain to Cui Qingwu ahead of schedule, he had to alter his plans.’","’Forget it. I’ll spare Lv Jiunan for now. He might be useful later.’","Chen Yi glanced at the dark clouds gathering in the night sky, then darted off toward the residence on Chuansi Street.","’Alright, first, I’ll deal with Asutai!’","...","「About a quarter of an hour later.」","Cui Qingwu arrived at the West Market by carriage. As was her custom, she instructed Huan’er to wait for her outside the Yunqing Building.","She then proceeded alone to the tailor shop.","Just as he had when meeting Lou Yuxue, the General was standing at the entrance to welcome her.","After exchanging greetings, the two entered a meditation room deep within the tailor shop.","Cui Qingwu sat calmly on a stool and, in a level voice, recounted the events that had taken place at the Spring Rain Building.","\"’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu has agreed to the White Tiger Guard’s request. We hope to lure Du Cang to the Chishui Riverbank in five days.\"","The General was unsurprised by this news. He nodded with a smile. \"It seems your relationship with Lady Tiger has thawed a bit lately.\"","Cui Qingwu’s expression remained neutral. \"You jest, my lord. Lady Tiger and I are both White Tiger Guard Silver Banner Officers. How could we possibly be at odds?\"","The General gave a choked laugh and didn’t press the matter.","’How could he deny such \"camaraderie between colleagues\"?’","Cui Qingwu continued, \"Second, Liu Hong came to the Bright Moon Building in disguise today.\"","The General looked at her, slightly surprised. \"Liu Hong? He went to the Bright Moon Building himself? Why?\"","\"He wanted to hire the Bright Moon Building to find the ’Barbarian Prince,’ Asutai.\"","\"Him... Because of King Landu?\"","Cui Qingwu affirmed with a hum. \"Lady Tiger guessed as much. She said you previously mentioned that Liu Hong harbors treacherous intentions and is in contact with King Landu.\"","The General nodded slightly. \"And?\"","\"Also... I was wondering why you summoned me tonight, my lord?\"","Hearing this, the General paused. Realizing she had nothing more to report, he lowered his head in thought.","After a moment, he asked out of the blue, \"Do you want the Governor or the Commander-in-Chief?\"","Cui Qingwu froze, clearly not expecting such an ambiguous question.","’The Governor... that must mean Liu Hong, right?’","’But the Commander-in-Chief... who is he referring to?’","’Li Fu or Zhu Hao?’","’But why is the General asking about them? And why is he making her choose?’","Cui Qingwu pushed down her confusion and asked, \"I don’t understand what you mean, my lord.\"","The General fixed his eyes on her, a smile spreading across his face. \"Do you remember the question I asked you last time?\"","\"I do. You asked me my purpose for coming to Shu State.\"","\"If you intend to rehash old topics, my lord, then I must take my leave.\"","\"No rush, no rush.\"","The General waved his hand dismissively. \"Your reason for being here isn’t that hard to guess, actually.\"","Cui Qingwu’s brow furrowed instinctively, a hint of anger showing on her face.","\"What do you mean by that, my lord?\"","\"Are you warning me?\"","The General shook his head with a smile, no longer beating around the bush. He said bluntly, \"What if I told you that my goal is the same as yours?\"","Hearing this, Cui Qingwu almost let her surprise show, but she maintained her composure and said impassively:","\"I don’t know what you’re talking about, my lord.\"","Seeing her unwillingness to talk, the General didn’t press her further, instead returning to his earlier question.","\"Right now in Shu State, the Old Marquis is holed up in the Xiao Family estate, Xiao Jinghong is lying low at the Wu Mountain Mutual Market, and Lord Tang of the Inspectorate Office is also keeping his head down.\"","\"Besides them, among the handful of courtiers for whom our White Tiger Guard holds incriminating evidence, are Liu Hong and Commander-in-Chief Zhu Hao.\"","\"Is the weight of these two men sufficient?\"","When Cui Qingwu heard this, a flicker of suspicion crossed her eyes.","’She hadn’t expected the General to actually know her purpose for coming to Shu State.’","’Although she never intended to hide it, she had never mentioned it to anyone, either.’","’Even her deal with Gray Wolf Xiao Dongchen had been conducted in secret.’","’The General... how did he find out?’","’And another thing, why did he say their goals were the ’same’?’","’Could it be that he...’","’No, could it be that the White Tiger Guard also wants Brother Yunfan to be promoted and rise in rank?’","Cui Qingwu’s mind was filled with doubt, but seeing the General’s all-knowing expression, she gave her answer first:","\"Commander-in-Chief Zhu Hao.\"","’If she were to find out the White Tiger Guard was plotting against Chen Yunfan, she wouldn’t just pretend she knew nothing.’","The General, who had naturally guessed some of what was on Cui Qingwu’s mind, nodded with a smile.","\"Just as I thought.\"","\"He’s currently stationed in the Governor’s Office. If he were to gain the Holy Emperor’s favor by collecting evidence of his superior’s crimes, I’m afraid it would be detrimental to his future career.\"","Seeing him so openly speak Chen Yunfan’s name, Cui Qingwu’s expression turned cold as she asked:","\"I wonder if you could clarify, my lord, why the White Tiger Guard wants to help... him?\"","The General knew she would ask, but he simply shook his head and murmured an apology.","\"You know the rules of the White Tiger Guard. Even I cannot disclose certain top-secret matters.\"","\"What I can tell you is this: he is also held in high regard by the Pavilion Master.\"","\"The Lord... Pavilion Master?\"","Cui Qingwu’s expression was a whirlwind of emotions—doubt, surprise, and a faint trace of panic.","Ever since joining the White Tiger Guard, she had heard countless tales of the Lord Pavilion Master’s ruthless and decisive methods.","Whatever he set out to do, he accomplished.","Whoever he wanted to kill, none could escape.","No one who dared to defy him or stand in his way ever met a good end.","\"He, why...\"","The General raised a hand, cutting her off. \"I would advise you not to probe any further.\"","\"The Lord Pavilion Master is not me. He will not abandon a long-standing plan simply because of your relationship with that young gentleman.\"","He paused, a slight smile touching his lips. \"But you needn’t worry. The Lord Pavilion Master will not harm the young gentleman.\"","Cui Qingwu glanced at him, then lowered her head slightly.","After a long moment, she held out her hand. \"Let me have it.\"","\"What?\"","\"Zhu Hao.\"","’Regardless of how the General knew, or what his true objective was, she planned to get her hands on the evidence against Zhu Hao first.’","’At least until she could ascertain the Lord Pavilion Master’s true intentions, she needed to help Chen Yunfan’s career skyrocket.’","’Only then would she and Chen Yunfan have any chance of dealing with the troubles that lay ahead!’"]},{"number":474,"title":"Chapter 474 - 288: A Good Show","paragraphs":["The night rain fell without end.","Huan’er drove the carriage into Tingyu Pavilion.","As they neared the central courtyard, Cui Qingwu was roused from her deep thoughts by faint voices reaching her ears.","\"...I’ve been saying it all along! As long as I’m a little more diligent, my Sword Dao is bound to improve.\"","\"Before, I was just... lying low.\"","\"That’s right, that’s the word! I... Chun Ying, what’s with that look? You dare to laugh at me?\"","\"I wouldn’t dare, I wouldn’t dare.\"","\"I’d think not... Hmm? Niu Shan, what are you laughing at?\"","\"Young Master, I wasn’t...\"","\"Not laughing? I clearly saw you grinning from ear to ear...\"","Listening to Chen Yunfan’s boisterous voice from inside, Cui Qingwu could easily picture him.","’He’d be wearing a thin robe, his long hair tied back messily, his handsome face lit up with a triumphant expression. He’d be laughing and cursing as he tapped the tall and burly Niu Shan with the hilt of his sword.’","As she pictured the scene, Cui Qingwu couldn’t help but smile.","The unease and agitation she had felt after meeting the General dissipated significantly.","She tapped on the carriage wall, instructing Huan’er to stop, and stepped out.","Seeing the smile on her mistress’s face, Huan’er felt a wave of relief and drove the carriage toward the stables.","Just as before, Cui Qingwu held her Oil Paper Umbrella and walked alone through the covered walkway.","Chen Yunfan, having heard her approach, shot a look at Chun Ying and the others, straightened his clothes, and went to greet her.","\"Qingwu, you went to a restaurant in such heavy rain?\"","He had a strong suspicion that Cui Qingwu was busy with White Tiger Guard affairs, but since it wasn’t his place to interfere, he pretended not to know.","But to his surprise, Cui Qingwu shook her head. \"I... I went to the White Tiger Guard.\"","Chen Yunfan let out a slightly surprised \"oh.\" \"The White Tiger Guard?\"","’He hadn’t expected Cui Qingwu to openly admit her identity with the White Tiger Guard right now.’","’Even when he had revealed his Martial Arts Cultivation, she hadn’t said a word.’","’Why now?’","Cui Qingwu lifted her chin slightly, her tone a little smug. \"I didn’t tell you, Brother Yunfan, but I’m now a White Tiger Guard Silver Banner Officer.\"","\"My title is—Simurgh Phoenix.\"","\"A Silver Banner Officer? Simurgh Phoenix? A fine name.\"","As Chen Yunfan spoke, he studied Cui Qingwu carefully, and a few doubts surfaced in his mind.","’She seems a little different from her usual self.’","\"But you’re the great young lady of the Cui Family. Why would you join the White Tiger Guard?\"","\"It’s a long story...\"","Of course, Cui Qingwu didn’t reveal the real reason. She just said it was an arrangement by her family’s elders for her to gain experience in the White Tiger Guard.","\"...I was originally assigned to the Capital Prefecture, but since Brother Yunfan happened to be coming to Shu State, I followed.\"","Chen Yunfan hummed in acknowledgment, but he only believed about half of her story.","\"So, the White Tiger Guard summoned you tonight... Did they give you an assignment?\"","Cui Qingwu nodded, then shook her head. \"There’s an assignment, but I don’t want to follow their orders.\"","Chen Yunfan let out a short laugh. \"That sounds just like you.\"","\"Like me? Does Brother Yunfan think I’m willful?\"","\"Mm, a little bit.\"","If Chen Yi were here, he would probably cover his face and pretend he didn’t know the man.","Any man with the slightest understanding of women would never be so direct.","But this was Chen Yunfan, and he had never been one to mince words.","Seeing him admit it so directly, Cui Qingwu’s face took on a look of mock indignation. \"So that’s how awful I am in Brother Yunfan’s heart.\"","\"Well, not quite...\"","After exchanging a few more jokes, Chen Yunfan didn’t press her further about the White Tiger Guard’s assignment.","It was just as he had told Chen Yi—he didn’t dislike Cui Qingwu herself, he only resented the marriage alliance between the Chen and Cui families.","For some reason, he didn’t feel that such an alliance would benefit either family.","Cui Qingwu said no more, but a great weight had been lifted from her heart now that she no longer had to hide her White Tiger Guard identity from Chen Yunfan.","Her expression relaxed considerably.","After their conversation ended, she smiled and returned to the rear residence.","The curtain of rain pattered against her Oil Paper Umbrella with a steady DRIP-DROP.","Illuminated by a few lanterns, the droplets scattered like flower petals along the small path leading to the rear residence.","Chen Yunfan watched her silhouette disappear beyond the covered walkway, the smile on his face gradually fading.","After a moment’s thought, he called for Chun Ying.","\"Has anything been happening in the Prefecture City lately?\"","Chun Ying’s heart seized, thinking he had found out about her sneaking out a few days prior.","\"Happening? It’s the same as always.\"","\"There’s constant news about King Landu of the Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race launching a major invasion at the border... However, this afternoon in the East Market, someone was saying that Lv Jiunan isn’t dead.\"","\"Lv Jiunan isn’t dead?\"","An image of Chen Yi surfaced in Chen Yunfan’s mind. ’Could the White Tiger Guard’s assignment for Cui Qingwu be related to Chen Yi...’ he wondered. ’To \"Liu Wu\"?’","After a moment of silence, as Chun Ying waited with some trepidation, Chen Yunfan gave his order: \"Investigate all the shady characters in the city. See if anything is out of the ordinary.\"","\"Also, Ning Yu... have him continue to follow her.\"","Chun Ying saw him gesture toward the rear residence and understood he meant Cui Qingwu. She let out a breath of relief and nodded.","\"I’ll go make the arrangements right away.\"","\"Wait.\"","Chen Yunfan stopped her, adding thoughtfully, \"I want to send another letter to my father.\"","Chun Ying hesitated, but seeing his serious expression, she nodded again.","\"I’ll go and ask about it shortly.\"","\"Good...\"","...","「Meanwhile.」","Chen Yi had just left the residence on Chuansi Street with Pei Guanli.","To be precise, it was the three of them walking through the dim, unlit rain, with him carrying the Barbarian youth Asutai.","He wore a black cloak and a bamboo hat, his face concealed by a black iron mask.","Asutai remained unconscious. Slung over Chen Yi’s shoulder, his hands and feet nearly scraped the ground.","It was easy to imagine just how tall he was.","Beside him, Pei Guanli was also dressed in Night Clothes. She stuck close to Chen Yi’s side, her eyes darting about everywhere.","Her expression was one of excitement.","\"Sis— My lord, where are we going now?\""]},{"number":475,"title":"Chapter 475 - 288: A Good Show","paragraphs":["\"You... You said you were taking me to see a show. What kind of show?\"","\"Are we sending this barbarian boy away? Why didn’t you kill him?\"","\"And, and, is there a good show to watch with the person left in the room, too?\"","Pei Guanli chattered on endlessly.","Fortunately, she knew to be discreet and deliberately kept her voice down.","Otherwise, on a rainy night like this, she might have alerted even more people.","With Chen Yi’s sharp hearing, he could already tell that some of the nearby Wandering Martial Artists had heard something.","He lifted his hand, grabbed Pei Guanli by the scruff of her neck, and said in a low voice, \"One more word out of you and I’m leaving you here.\"","Pei Guanli stuck her tongue out, knowing he was just trying to scare her.","\"I promise, I promise I’ll shut my mouth.\"","Chen Yi shook his head helplessly, and with her still by the scruff, he soared into the air.","\"I don’t believe you.\"","Pei Guanli immediately stopped caring whether he believed her or not.","She felt the ground drop away from her feet and instinctively hugged Chen Yi. Though she was a little scared, she was mostly excited.","Every now and then, she would glance down below.","\"We’re flying so high this time!\"","\"Broth... Sir, can you take me out like this again next time?\"","\"Shut up.\"","With a burst of True Essence from his feet, Chen Yi flew straight down, landing on South Street with Pei Guanli.","At his current level of Cultivation, he could only travel through the air for short distances. He couldn’t fly all the way from Iron Wall Town to the Prefecture City like Xiao Jinghong.","Even so, within this small Prefecture City, he could still reach the Liu Mansion in the span of three breaths.","\"This place is...\"","After getting a clear look at her surroundings, Pei Guanli was about to speak but remembered Chen Yi’s warning and quickly covered her mouth.","Chen Yi glanced at her, then without pausing, led her and Asutai straight into the Liu Family’s estate.","Speed is paramount in war.","So he directly executed the Meteor Butterfly Step at the Great Success Realm, his body becoming a streak of light as he cleared out the guards, one circle after another.","As he reached each person, he would strike out with a palm, knocking them unconscious.","He continued all the way to the rear courtyard where Liu Hong was.","Chen Yi scanned his surroundings. His gaze fell upon a side room from which he could faintly hear some movement.","Evidently, Liu Hong and the others had already noticed something was amiss outside.","From inside the room, Zhao Liuan’s low shout could be heard, \"Who dares trespass in the residence of Lord Liu of the Governor’s Office?!\"","\"Do you have a death wish?!\"","A hint of a smile flashed in Chen Yi’s eyes. He didn’t respond, simply placing Asutai on the ground.","He then flicked a Silver Needle into Asutai’s Forehead Acupoint.","Pei Guanli watched him, covering her mouth while glancing at the side room with a disdainful look in her eyes.","She even brandished her small fists a few times, like a fox borrowing the tiger’s might.","’If my brother-in-law hadn’t told me not to speak, I’d have cussed you out until you dropped dead.’","A moment later, Asutai came to. He stood up, took in his surroundings, and understood the situation. In a stiff tone, he said:","\"Has... it started?\"","Chen Yi gave a slight nod and pointed toward where Liu Hong and the others were. \"Be careful. Don’t die.\"","\"Die?\"","Before Asutai could react, Chen Yi pulled Pei Guanli along and leaped into mid-air.","In another flash, he landed on a rooftop not far from the Liu Mansion’s rear courtyard.","Pei Guanli watched him, knowing the show was about to begin. She covered her mouth and stared at Asutai without blinking.","She still didn’t understand what \"good show\" her brother-in-law was talking about.","But she knew that since her brother-in-law had said it, it was bound to be a good one.","Soon, the door to Liu Hong’s study opened. Zhao Liuan emerged cautiously, holding a Long Sword, and his eyes immediately fell on Asutai outside.","After sizing him up, his expression suddenly changed.","\"Asutai?!\"","Asutai, in contrast, was much calmer. Although a hint of hatred flickered across his squarish, dark face, he firmly remembered Chen Yi’s instructions.","So he just stood there in the rain without a word.","Hearing Zhao Liuan’s voice, Liu Hong and Liu Taoyao also came out of the study.","He frowned, studying Asutai with a thoughtful expression, then looked at Zhao Liuan.","\"Are you sure it’s him?\"","Zhao Liuan stared at Asutai and nodded. \"I previously saw him once with Zeng Zhifeng. It is indeed him.\"","Beside them, Liu Taoyao couldn’t help but ask doubtfully, \"Then why would he be here?\"","\"Even when Father went to the Bright Moon Building this afternoon...\"","He didn’t dare say more.","It was obvious Asutai hadn’t been sent by the Evil Demonic Dao from the Bright Moon Building, nor could he have found his own way here.","Liu Hong was also aware of this. After scanning the area, his eyes returned to Asutai.","\"Speak. Why are you here?\"","Asutai looked at Liu Hong. Even though he didn’t recognize him, he knew his identity in his heart—the one ’that person’ had called the Governor of Shu State.","He suppressed the hatred in his heart and said stiffly, \"I don’t know. I was here when I woke up.\"","\"Woke up? So you were unconscious before?\"","\"Yes.\"","Liu Hong thought for a moment, then asked, \"Do you remember what happened that day?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","\"Who abducted you?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","Seeing that he was getting nowhere, a flash of annoyance crossed Liu Hong’s face. He asked in a deep voice, \"Then do you know who I am?\"","Asutai shook his head again, but then nodded. \"That person... told me... you can... send me back to the Barbarian Race.\"","Hearing this, Liu Hong’s brow furrowed tightly, his gaze on Asutai flickering with uncertainty.","At his side, Liu Taoyao couldn’t remain calm. His face was a mixture of joy and worry.","After a moment of thought, he gritted his teeth and said, \"Father, there are only a few days left before the deadline that Jackal gave us.\"","\"Since he wants this Barbarian Prince, why don’t we just tell him to come and pick the man up?\"","Zhao Liuan immediately shook his head. \"We can’t.\"","\"Asutai’s appearance here is too strange. I’m afraid... I’m afraid...\"","He didn’t dare say what he was afraid of.","But for Liu Hong to have reached the position of Governor of Shu State, he was naturally no fool."]},{"number":476,"title":"Chapter 476 - 288: A Good Show","paragraphs":["He naturally thought of everything Zhao Liuan had.","Moreover, he deduced the mastermind’s intent: to wait and see how he would handle the hot potato that was Asutai.","’Kill him, or not?’","Killing Asutai would certainly thwart the mastermind’s scheme and temporarily clear him of any suspicion of colluding with the Barbarian Race.","But if he did, that jackal Du Cang would undoubtedly publicize the matter to protect the Peacock King Banner and the security of the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.","At that point, even if he wasn’t executed, his death would not be far off.","But if he didn’t kill Asutai...","Liu Hong was deeply unwilling to let the mastermind’s plot succeed!","After wrestling with the decision, a look of grim resolve settled on Liu Hong’s face. He directly ordered Liu Taoyao to take Asutai away and place him under guard.","\"To think the Barbarian Prince was actually abducted by those horse bandits and brought to Shu State. I shall immediately report this to the Imperial Court and ask the Holy Emperor for his judgment.\"","Liu Taoyao froze. \"Father...\"","\"Enough nonsense. Guard him well. If he escapes, not even I can save you!\"","Time was tight. The best solution Liu Hong could devise was to preserve himself while passing this hot potato to Du Cang.","Liu Taoyao understood. He stepped forward and said to Asutai in a low voice, \"Follow me.\"","Asutai didn’t object, following him out.","Just before he left, he turned to look at Liu Hong, as if to burn the man’s face into his memory.","’I, Borergu Asutai, will wait for the day of your execution!’","Though Liu Hong could not know his thoughts, he understood the look in the prince’s eyes, and his own expression grew grim.","Zhao Liuan, standing to the side, thought for a moment. \"My lord, who do you think it was?\"","Previously, both he and Liu Hong had suspected Zeng Zhifeng.","But given the current situation, the person who brought Asutai to the Liu Family could not possibly have been Zeng Zhifeng.","After all, the Liu Family estate was currently guarded inside and out by Death Warriors.","Even if the Death Warriors’ cultivation wasn’t particularly high, a Martial Artist of the Middle Three Grades Realm like Zeng Zhifeng could never have slipped past them unnoticed.","Hearing this, Liu Hong lowered his head slightly, letting the rain beat down on him.","It was as if only this could calm him.","\"For Asutai to have been brought here, the mastermind must have pried open Zeng Zhifeng’s mouth after abducting the prince.\"","\"Zeng Zhifeng?\"","\"He... If he learned your identity, my lord, why would he send Asutai here?\"","\"There can only be two reasons.\"","\"Either they want leverage over my dealings with the south, or they want to get on my good side.\"","Liu Hong raised his head and scanned his surroundings, as if searching for the mastermind.","\"Which one do you think it is?\"","Zhao Liuan already had the answer. He gritted his teeth and said, \"Their methods... are truly ruthless!\"","Liu Hong couldn’t agree more. Finding nothing, he turned and headed back to his study.","\"But no matter what their objective is... how could I let them have their way?\"","Seeing this, a hint of a smile flashed in Chen Yi’s eyes before he vanished with Pei Guanli.","Today’s \"good show\" was merely an appetizer, but it had given him a clear look at Liu Hong’s character.","He wasn’t a decisive strongman, nor was he a petty man. He was a cunning hegemon.","A decisive strongman would have killed Asutai immediately to solve the problem once and for all.","A petty man would have committed to the act, handing Asutai over to the Government Office for imprisonment to at least earn the Imperial Court’s trust.","Cunning hegemon was the highest praise Chen Yi could offer.","If Liu Hong hadn’t dared to raise a private army and collude with the Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race, he would be a mere treacherous court official at best.","Calling him a \"hegemon\" at all was a compliment.","Pei Guanli, oblivious to all this, had lost her earlier excitement. She pouted and grumbled,","\"A good show? That wasn’t fun at all.\"","Chen Yi chuckled, but just as he was about to speak, a golden light flashed before his eyes—","[Daily Intelligence - Yellow-level Middle Grade: At 9:45 AM, outside the East Market, Yuan Liu’er will sell herself to pay for her father’s burial. A minuscule amount of Opportunity can be obtained.]"]},{"number":477,"title":"Chapter 477 - 289: Liu Wu!","paragraphs":["Yellow-level Middle Grade?","Information that was better than nothing, I suppose.","Chen Yi gave it a quick glance before closing the light screen.","He had a lot on his plate right now and didn’t really have the spare time to chase after every spectacle.","Therefore, unless it was directly related to his plans, he would usually decide whether or not to pursue an Opportunity based on his schedule for the day.","It wasn’t that he was lacking in Opportunities.","Rather, as his Martial Arts Cultivation and Techniques improved, he had already gained a certain ability to protect himself.","Especially after his Martial Arts Body broke through to the Perfection Realm, his Pile Skill and Inner Strength progressed by leaps and bounds.","The few Opportunities he might gain from a trip outside were less significant than the progress he made by cultivating the Four Symbols Skill.","After a short while, Chen Yi made two loops to confirm that no one was following him, then took Pei Guanli to the residence on Chuansi Street.","Pei Guanli was still muttering, saying things like how tonight’s \"good show\" wasn’t very fun.","She even begged Chen Yi to take her to see something more fun next time.","Chen Yi smiled and nodded, not bothering to explain the behind-the-scenes details of Liu Hong’s performance tonight.","Besides, even if he did, he figured the Tiger Girl wouldn’t be interested in the drama of \"Liu Hong’s inner struggle and torment.\"","After some small talk, Chen Yi removed his disguise, packed away his clothes neatly, and said with a smile:","\"You stay here and be good. In a few days, I’ll send that person downstairs on his way.\"","Pei Guanli nodded. \"Brother-in-law, who are you planning to send him to?\"","\"King Yama.\"","Chen Yi lightly tapped her forehead and then darted away.","Pei Guanli rubbed her smooth forehead and pouted at his retreating back before breaking into a smile.","She looked down and tapped her bare feet on the ground a few times.","\"Sending you to see King Yama.\"","\"Hee hee.\"","Hearing her voice, Chen Yi broke into a small smile and made up his mind to take the Tiger Girl to see a truly good show next time.","’I just don’t know when \"next time\" will be.’","「Not long after.」","Chen Yi quietly returned to Spring Lotus Garden, shed his black clothes, changed into a fresh, dry robe, and his expression returned to one of peace.","By this time, the rain had grown heavier.","Inside Spring Lotus Garden, raindrops pattered down. A cool wind blew, causing the flowers, grass, and trees to rustle. Floating leaves could be faintly seen drifting through the courtyard.","Most of the residences in the rear courtyard were silent.","The nearby Jiaxing Garden, the empty Four Directions Hall, and several other residences farther away were all the same.","In contrast, some sounds could be heard coming from the central courtyard.","The clanking of the Personal Guards’ Armor as they moved about, their conversations during the changing of the guard, and the Old Marquis’s deep laughter from within Qingjing Residence.","\"I haven’t fought in a long time. What do you think of my spear technique?\"","\"Congratulations, Marquis! Your Spear Technique should be at fifty percent of its peak power.\"","\"Fifty percent?\"","\"You rascal, you’re not being honest. I haven’t recovered my Martial Arts Cultivation yet. I’m still far, far from my peak...\"","Hearing the Old Marquis’s words, Chen Yi couldn’t help but chuckle.","He hadn’t thought healing the Old Marquis earlier in the day was anything worth mentioning.","After all, the Old Marquis’s chronic injuries, accumulated over many years, couldn’t be eradicated with a single application of Meridian Flow.","It would still require a regimen of medicinal soups and long-term Acupuncture to restore the Old Marquis to a state appropriate for his age.","But he had forgotten something.","The Old Marquis had been tormented by illness and pain for five years. To have it suddenly relieved brought a joy that was beyond words.","Just look at him now, able to brandish a greatspear in the courtyard.","Chen Yi smiled and shook his head. \"I hope the Old Marquis can still laugh this happily in a few days.\"","He then turned, sat cross-legged on the bed, and began cultivating the Four Symbols Skill.","’Over the past few days, I’ve absorbed a considerable amount of the Profound Mysteries of [Martial Arts·Body], and both my Pile Skill and Inner Strength have progressed significantly.’","’If my deductions are correct, once my Cultivation Techniques reach the Perfect Level, my cultivation speed will be several times more efficient than it is now.’","’In other words, it took me eight days to break through from the Middle Fifth Grade to the Upper Stage. With a Perfect Level Four Symbols Skill, it might only take two or three days.’","’Such a rate of improvement is simply terrifying.’","\"If all goes smoothly, perhaps by the time my lady returns from her inspection of the Three Towns, my Cultivation will have broken through to the Third Grade Realm.\"","\"At that time...\"","...","Chen Yi and the Xiao Family were safe and sound, but many people were destined to have a sleepless night.","Inside Tingyu Pavilion, the matter concerning Cui Qingwu had dampened Chen Yunfan’s joy over his progress in the Sword Dao, and he was, for once, meticulously reviewing official business.","He would occasionally stop to think about the recent situation in Shu State, trying to figure out what the White Tiger Guard was planning.","Cui Qingwu, on the other hand, was worried because of what the General had said. She clutched the letter written by Lin Huai’an, her mind racing.","In the end, she couldn’t figure anything out.","However, she did think of a viable solution.","’My own mind might not be up to the task, but I know someone whose is.’","’I might have to find that person and make a deal to avoid the worst-case scenario.’","Meanwhile, in the Liu Family Mansion on South Street, all the Guards who had been knocked unconscious were kneeling in the rear residence.","Zhao Liuan stood before them with a frigid expression, his gaze sweeping over each one as he asked in a cold voice:","\"Did anyone see the intruder’s face?\"","The Guards shifted slightly, glancing left and right, but no one spoke.","The Guard Commander at the head of the group cupped his fists, his face full of shame, and said:","\"We didn’t see the intruder clearly. We only saw a black shadow approach in the blink of an eye. With a wave of his hand, he knocked us all unconscious.\"","\"A black shadow?\"","Zhao Liuan didn’t reprimand them. His voice was indifferent as he said, \"That means he was wearing black.\"","\"What else?\"","\"Well...\"","\"Let me remind you, this matter is of the utmost importance. Not a single, tiny detail can be overlooked!\"","Hearing this, the Guard Commander sighed in relief, knowing that their lives were safe for the moment. He then began to recall the events in earnest.","And he did, in fact, remember something—or rather, he recalled a few details he had missed."]},{"number":478,"title":"Chapter 478 - 289: Liu Wu!","paragraphs":["\"It was only for a moment, but I sensed his cultivation hasn’t reached the Upper Three Grades Realm. He should still be in the Middle Three Grades.\"","Zhao Liuan frowned slightly. \"Fourth Grade?\"","\"No, I can’t be certain.\"","\"His True Essence is profound, to be sure, but he didn’t exhibit the aura of a nascent True Gang, which is characteristic of the Fourth Grade Realm. I don’t believe he has reached it.\"","The Guard Commander said evasively, \"Or... or perhaps he just didn’t reveal it.\"","Zhao Liuan was clearly not satisfied. \"Is that all?\"","The Guard Commander bowed his head. \"I am ashamed. I await your punishment, my lord.\"","Most of the other guards reacted similarly.","After a moment of silence, Zhao Liuan waved his hand impatiently, dismissing them.","He even had to waste a few words to placate them.","But after most of the guards had left, a guard with delicate features remained kneeling on the ground.","Zhao Liuan glared at him coldly. \"Why aren’t you gone?\"","Who would have thought that as soon as he finished speaking, the guard began to twist his body and limbs bizarrely.","Like a shadow puppet being dangled by an artisan.","As he swayed back and forth, two scarlet glows suddenly erupted from his eyes.","Startled, Zhao Liuan quickly retreated a few steps. \"Guards! Guards! Someone, quick!\"","But no matter how he shouted, his surroundings seemed to be sealed off by something, and no sound could escape.","Just then, the guard seemed to finally notice him. His scarlet eyes fixed on Zhao Liuan as he let out a sinister laugh.","\"It’s only been a few days. Don’t you recognize me?\"","Zhao Liuan fought back the fear in his heart and stared at him. \"You... you... you’re... Du Cang?!\"","\"Heh heh, besides me, who else would dare to brazenly barge into the Lord Governor’s residence?\"","But just as Du Cang finished speaking, his eyes swept around the area, and he let out a sound of surprise.","\"A master was here earlier?\"","\"There’s no mistaking this aura. It’s the scent of a Great Success Body Technique.\"","\"Tsk tsk, the Great Wei Dynasty is truly teeming with talent. To think someone could achieve Great Success in the Dao of a Technique that is so easy to learn yet so difficult to master.\"","Zhao Liuan was stunned. ’Great Success Body Technique?’","He suddenly thought of the person who had delivered Asutai earlier and quickly said, \"You... you’re right.\"","\"Someone was here before. And... and they delivered Asutai to my lord.\"","\"Oh?\"","Du Cang’s tone held a hint of surprise. \"Asutai... has been found?\"","Zhao Liuan nodded, but just as he was about to reply, his expression changed.","He suddenly remembered—according to Liu Hong’s plan, they couldn’t hand Asutai over to Du Cang yet.","At least, Asutai could not leave the Liu Family estate until they received a reply from the Imperial Court.","Thinking of this, he gritted his teeth and said, \"As for the specific details, it would be better for my lord to explain them to you.\"","Du Cang stared at him, thought for a moment, and said there was no hurry.","Then he ignored Zhao Liuan and began circling the courtyard on his own.","From time to time, wisps of aura glittering with black light drifted down around the area.","Within the spreading black mist, faint silhouettes could be vaguely seen.","Zhao Liuan didn’t understand what was happening, but the pressure on his body hadn’t lifted, making even a single step difficult. So he stood obediently in place.","However, he did understand Du Cang’s intention: he was investigating the mysterious person who had been there earlier.","\"Besides the Body Technique, there’s another very familiar scent on him.\"","\"Very familiar, very familiar... The scent my pet finds so familiar is...\"","Du Cang chanted for a moment, the red glow in his eyes intensifying, and then he burst into laughter.","\"I was wondering who it was. So it was him!\"","Zhao Liuan quickly asked, \"Who?\"","\"Liu Wu!\"","\"Liu Wu? ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu?!\"","\"How could it be...\"","Du Cang’s laughter stopped short. He turned his head to look at him and asked coldly, \"Are you doubting the keenness of my pet’s sense of smell?\"","\"No, no...\"","\"Hmph!\"","\"My pet’s sense of smell is indeed a bit dull, but that couldn’t hide the fact that Liu Wu was here for a considerable time.\"","\"Just like the scent he left behind when he sparred with Liu Lang on the Chishui Riverbank. Some of it is bound to linger.\"","In fact, Du Cang had not been idle these past few days.","While hiding in the shadows, he was also searching for \"Dragon Spear\" Liu Wu.","He had not only gone to the ravine on the Chishui Riverbank ravaged by Spear Dao and Saber Dao, but also to places like West Market’s Heiyu Lane.","All in order to find some trace of Liu Wu.","Unfortunately, too much time had passed, and relying on his Black Magic God, he had only managed to catch an extremely faint scent.","A scent mixed with the fragrance of flowers and sandalwood.","This suggested that \"Liu Wu\" resided in an elegant and well-appointed house.","As Du Cang spoke, he looked around, shook his head, and said, \"Let’s go. Take me to see Liu Hong.\"","Hearing this, Zhao Liuan didn’t hesitate. Once he felt the pressure on his body vanish, he quickly led him to the wing where Liu Hong was.","As they walked, he asked, \"Since your... your pet can smell Liu Wu, it must be able to track him, right?\"","Du Cang shot him a sidelong glance. \"Do I need you to remind me?\"","\"If I could find him, I would have hunted him down and killed him already. But alas...\"","’Alas, it’s raining tonight. Unless \"Dragon Spear\" Liu Wu stopped somewhere on his way here or back, there’s no way for me to track him.’","Of course, Du Cang wouldn’t say any of this out loud.","Before long, Du Cang arrived at a quiet room.","Liu Hong looked at his Liu Family guard uniform, a bit puzzled.","Zhao Liuan stepped forward and whispered a few words in his ear. Liu Hong frowned slightly, then his expression relaxed. He stood up and beckoned.","\"Since you’re here, General Du, please sit and talk.\"","As he spoke, he gestured for Zhao Liuan to go out and close the door.","After Zhao Liuan left, Du Cang surveyed his surroundings. Seeing the Buddha statues and Immortal Paintings enshrined in the quiet room, he couldn’t help but sneer.","\"Does Lord Liu also worship the Buddha and follow the Dao?\"","Liu Hong said impassively, \"I’m merely seeking peace of mind.\"","\"Unlike your King Landu, who roams freely along the Ancient Tea-Horse Road, I, the Governor of Shu State, must always tread on thin ice.\"","Du Cang grinned, walked over, and sat down opposite him. \"If Lord Liu were willing, His Majesty would surely welcome you with open arms.\"","\"Heh, is that so?\"","Liu Hong gave a noncommittal laugh, sat down, and said seriously, \"You’ve come at a good time. Asutai has been found.\"","\"I already know about that. Tell me, why did ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu bring him to you?\"","\"As far as I know, Liu Wu is supposed to be a Wandering Martial Artist. Even if he killed my man, Lv Jiunan, it should have been impossible for him to know Asutai’s whereabouts.\"","Du Cang’s confusion was understandable.","All the intelligence he had received stated that Liu Wu was a Spearman of supreme talent and that killing Lv Jiunan was likely an accident.","He couldn’t imagine what reason the man would have to abduct Asutai, only to then return him to Liu Hong.","It defied all logic.","Unless \"Liu Wu\" wasn’t a man of the Jianghu, but rather someone from one of Shu State’s great Noble Families or a high-ranking official in the Government Office.","Otherwise, it would be impossible for him to get involved in Imperial Court matters, much less concern himself with the conflicts between the Wei Dynasty, Poshisu Country, and the Barbarian Race.","That was the hallmark of an ordinary man of the Jianghu.","Hearing this, Liu Hong first nodded, then shook his head. \"There is something you don’t know, General Du.\"","\"That Liu Wu...\"","He then laid out everything he knew about Liu Wu, and after explaining it all in detail, he concluded:","\"If my guess is correct, then ’Liu Wu’ should be one of the Xiao Family’s men.\"","Du Cang’s scarlet eyes flickered. \"The Xiao Family?\"","He thought for a moment, then it dawned on him. \"That is indeed a possibility.\"","\"From what you’ve said about the burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain, your Liu Family suffered heavy losses, while the Xiao Family, in contrast, reaped considerable benefits.\"","\"If that old man, the Emperor, hadn’t intervened, the Xiao Family would be living much more comfortably right now. At the very least, the five hundred thousand silver taels your Liu Family gave them wouldn’t have been needed to cover the grain tax deficit for the Three Towns.\"","Liu Hong nodded slightly, then continued, \"But there is one thing I don’t understand.\"","\"It seems the Xiao Family was also kept in the dark about ’Liu Wu’s’ help. I’ve tested Xiao Yuan several times, but he hasn’t let anything slip.\"","\"I haven’t even found the slightest clue within the Xiao Family itself.\"","Du Cang let out a sinister laugh. \"Xiao Yuan... That old relic, Duke Dingyuan, how could he be so easy to deal with?\"","\"In his day, he trampled through Poshisu Country and repelled the Barbarian Race’s grand army several times. Even now that he’s old and toothless, he is still a tiger.\"","\"Be that as it may, after ’Liu Wu’ meddled in our affairs, I am now at risk of being exposed. Likewise...\"","Liu Hong pointed at him. \"...you will also have a hard time carrying out King Landu’s order—to avenge General Lv Jiunan.\"","Du Cang’s laughter died. He stared at him for a moment, then snorted coldly. \"Trying to provoke me is useless!\"","Liu Hong smiled and shook his head. \"That was not my intention.\"","\"Hmph! Regardless of your intentions, Liu Wu’s life is mine for the taking!\"","\"As for the Xiao Family... never mind.\"","\"Before I leave, I will also give them a grand gift!\"","Hearing this, Liu Hong beamed. \"In that case, my thanks, General Du.\"","\"Don’t mention it, don’t mention it. After all, you found Asutai...\""]},{"number":479,"title":"Chapter 479 - 290: September 14th, Auspicious for Travel","paragraphs":["Liu Hong had no desire to let the mastermind behind this—\"Dragon Spear\" Liu Wu—get his way.","With Asutai in his hands, he had options, whether to press forward or fall back.","But with Du Cang’s arrival, he had to rein in any personal motives.","\"Liuan, bring Asutai over.\"","\"Yes.\"","Du Cang let out a laugh, directing the handsome-looking guard he was controlling to sit imposingly across from them.","During the wait,","Liu Hong slowly closed the unfinished memorial on his desk. He lowered his head slightly, a sinister look lingering in his eyes.","\"I won’t question what General Du intends to do, but I do have one suggestion.\"","Du Cang sneered. \"Is Lord Liu worried I might take Xiao Yuan’s life?\"","Liu Hong nodded, his eyes instantly turning clear and sharp as he looked up.","\"As long as Old Marquis Xiao is around, he can keep the hot-blooded members of the Dingyuan Army in check. What’s more, his presence forces Xiao Jinghong to be more cautious.\"","\"But if he were to die unexpectedly, do you think Xiao Jinghong would hesitate to lead her army to the Ancient Tea-Horse Road?\"","\"Furthermore, the Dingyuan Army suffered heavy losses in the last invasion by the Barbarian Race. Now that they’ve regained some of their strength, they are spoiling for a fight.\"","\"Your King’s Peacock Banner is conveniently located, and their forces are weaker than the main armies of Poshisu Country or the Barbarian Race. They would make a perfect target.\"","He left it at that.","The smile on Du Cang’s face faded slightly. He nodded. \"Lord Liu has a point.\"","\"True, that old bastard Xiao Yuan is a great enemy of Poshisu Country. Taking his head back to the King would surely bring me favor, but it would indeed lead to disaster.\"","He paused, then looked at Liu Hong. \"I wonder, what is Lord Liu’s suggestion?\"","\"I’ve come all the way to Shu State. I can’t leave without some kind of trophy.\"","\"Chen Yi.\"","\"Chen Yi?\"","\"I’ve heard that name. Xiao Jinghong’s husband, the man famous throughout Great Wei as Mr. Qingzhou, am I right?\"","\"The very same.\"","Du Cang’s scarlet pupils narrowed slightly. He asked with a smile, \"Why him?\"","Liu Hong’s expression was serene. \"The reason is simple. Chen Qingzhou is the most suitable target.\"","\"He may be famous throughout Great Wei for his Perfect Calligraphy Dao and poetry, but to the Xiao Family, he’s just a live-in son-in-law. They don’t value him.\"","\"And yet, his status is unique. He is not only Xiao Jinghong’s husband, but he also hails from the Chen Family of Jiangnan Prefecture.\"","\"Killing him would not only bring shame upon the Xiao Family, but it would also send a shockwave through the Central Plains. What do you think, General Du?\"","Du Cang raised an eyebrow. After a moment’s thought, he nodded. \"Acceptable.\"","As far as he was concerned, anyone besides \"Liu Wu\" was just a target of opportunity.","Besides, the Xiao Family was a shadow of its former self, held up by a single woman, Xiao Jinghong.","’Aren’t they his for the taking?’","Seeing him agree, Liu Hong fell silent. He sat quietly in his chair, waiting for Zhao Liuan to return with Asutai.","To be honest,","He would have much preferred for Xiao Yuan to die at Du Cang’s hands.","But he knew all too well that the drawbacks of Xiao Yuan’s death far outweighed the benefits.","Not only would it unchain Xiao Jinghong, but it would also shake the imperial court, attracting the attention of the Holy Emperor and the Nine Ministers.","At that point, the slightest disturbance in all of Shu State would be put under a microscope.","That would be detrimental to Liu Hong’s own plans.","But if the target were Chen Yi, then he wouldn’t have any of those concerns.","In fact, an attack on Chen Yi would allow him to probe for reactions from the Capital Prefecture.","Especially from the Chen Family of Jiangnan Prefecture.","With Chen Xuanji away from Great Wei, Chen Xuandu’s response would reveal the Chen Family’s stance on Shu State.","Killing two birds with one stone.","As Liu Hong considered this, he sneered inwardly.","’If you manage to survive even this, then I... will have all the more reason not to let you live!’","「Not long after.」","Zhao Liuan led Asutai to the door and said softly, \"My lord, I’ve brought him.\"","Liu Hong grunted in acknowledgment, then rose and looked at Du Cang. \"General, if you please. Forgive me for not seeing you out.\"","Du Cang gave him a meaningful look. \"Rest assured, Lord Liu. When I see the King, I will be sure to pass on your regards.\"","\"Heh, General Du is too kind.\"","After forcing a smile, Liu Hong watched him leave the study, his expression darkening.","’King Landu... Du Cang!’","Outside, Du Cang couldn’t care less what Liu Hong was thinking. He had leverage over the man, so he wasn’t worried in the slightest.","He was now sizing up Asutai. Forcing a smile, he cupped his hands in a salute.","\"Du Cang of the Peacock King Banner greets the Young Master.\"","Asutai looked down at him, a muscle twitching in his square-jawed face. A hint of hatred flickered in his eyes.","Having come from the Barbarian Race to Shu State, he had of course heard the name \"Peacock King Banner\" many times.","According to the horse bandits of Poshisu Country, the Peacock King Banner was the most powerful group of their kind on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.","But in his eyes, the Peacock King Banner was the very culprit responsible for capturing and plundering him and his kinsmen.","It didn’t matter that a different group of horse bandits had been the ones to infiltrate the Barbarian Race this time.","When Asutai remained silent, a flicker of mockery crossed Du Cang’s eyes. Without another word, he waved his hand, releasing a cloud of black mist.","Asutai stared at him, then collapsed stiffly to the ground.","Du Cang sneered. \"Why don’t you take a nap, Young Master. When you awaken, you’ll be able to return to the Barbarian Race.\"","With that, he ignored Zhao Liuan, hoisted Asutai onto his back, and vanished in a flash.","「After he was gone.」","Zhao Liuan swallowed hard, then turned and entered the study.","\"My lord...\"","Liu Hong raised a hand to cut him off. A ferocious look contorted his face as he violently swept everything off the desk and onto the floor.","CRASH, CLATTER.","Zhao Liuan hastily dropped to his knees, cold sweat beading on his forehead.","He had been with Liu Hong for three years, but this was the first time he had ever seen his master lose his composure like this.","After a long while,","Liu Hong’s breathing evened out. He sat back down in his chair, his expression once again calm.","\"Have our men find the whereabouts of ’Liu Wu.’ If they locate him, notify Du Cang immediately.\"","\"Also, I’ll be staying at the Government Office for a while. If anyone comes to call, tell them I’m busy with official matters.\""]},{"number":480,"title":"Chapter 480 - 290: September 14th, Auspicious for Travel","paragraphs":["\"Go tell Yao’er not to show his face either.\"","\"Yes...\"","...","「The next day.」","The day was overcast and rainy, the light dim.","At four in the morning.","Xiao Wuge was already up, washing and dressing with Xiaodie’s assistance.","He wore a short brocade tunic, its sash tied tightly at his waist.","His hair was pulled into a simple topknot, giving his refined features a sharp, capable air.","After so many days of Martial Arts training, Xiao Wuge had gradually grown accustomed to this lifestyle.","He would wake early to practice his Martial Arts, read in the afternoon, and spend his evenings fishing, playing chess, or in the study with his brother-in-law, Chen Yi.","Disciplined and fulfilling.","Though he sometimes envied the other children his age in the mansion as they played and laughed, he knew he couldn’t join them.","The time spent with his brother-in-law had taught him the importance of maintaining one’s integrity even when alone, and the truth in the saying that Heaven tests those it deems for great responsibility.","He had already long endured the \"suffering of the heart and mind\" that the proverb spoke of.","For instance, the deaths of Xiao Fengchun and Fu Wanqing in battle, and the humiliation the Xiao Family suffered at the hands of the Jing State Liu Family.","He saw it with his own eyes and etched it into his heart.","It wasn’t a matter of hatred or resentment.","Instead, he saw these events as trials to temper him, hoping that one day he could become a man like his grandfather, Xiao Yuan, or his father, Xiao Fengchun.","To guard the borderlands and protect the common folk.","And so, Xiao Wuge willingly accepted his present life.","No matter how exhausting or difficult it became, he would grit his teeth and endure.","At a quarter past four, Xiaodie watched Xiao Wuge leave Spring Lotus Garden with Wang Lixing, who had come to fetch him. Then, she began her chores.","She swept and scrubbed, tidying Spring Lotus Garden until it was spotless, inside and out.","Once she was done,","she went to the study and lit a stick of Rich Plum incense.","A cool, serene plum blossom fragrance—blended from agarwood, sandalwood, and cloves—gradually filled the room.","Then, she flipped a page on the Astronomical Bureau’s imperial almanac hanging to the side:","The Fourteenth of the Ninth Month.","Auspicious for travel, marriage, and seeking medical treatment.","Inauspicious for trade, hanging plaques, and moving into a new home.","Three lines of vermilion script.","Xiaodie committed the words to memory, tore off the previous day’s page, and a smile blossomed on her little face.","’Auspicious for travel. Perfect.’","Besides her love for gossiping about matters big and small within the Marquis’s Mansion, the little maid also had a penchant for storybooks about gods, ghosts, and monsters.","Over time, she had started to pay special attention to the auspicious and inauspicious listings on the imperial almanac.","She would only leave the Marquis’s Mansion on days the almanac deemed \"auspicious for travel.\"","This mostly applied to her own personal errands.","When it came to errands from Chen Yi, however, she would conveniently forget to check the almanac’s recommendations.","For example, that time long ago when Chen Yi sent her to the mounting shop to pick up some art, she’d run into Mr. Yue Ming. That day had been marked \"inauspicious for travel.\"","And sure enough, Mr. Yue Ming had \"made\" her cry that day.","With everything in order,","Xiaodie glanced at the sky outside, then listened carefully for any sound from upstairs. There was nothing.","She wiped the sweat from her brow and trotted off toward the rear kitchen.","Just as she exited Spring Lotus Garden, she came face to face with Shen Huatang, who was approaching with Cui’er and Sister Juan’er. They carried a tray laden with plates of various sizes.","Pastries, congee, soup, and buns, all steaming hot.","Xiaodie grinned and gave a small curtsy. \"Sister Huatang, Sister Cui’er, Sister Juan’er, good morning.\"","Shen Huatang grunted in acknowledgment. Knowing Xiaodie was headed to the rear kitchen, she reminded her,","\"The Eldest Miss had the kitchen prepare chicken soup for Master Chen Yi. Remember to bring it along.\"","Xiaodie blinked a few times, smiled, and said she would remember. Then she scurried off toward the rear kitchen.","’Nourishing chicken soup is best served hot; she didn’t dare to dawdle.’","Once she was a good distance away,","Shen Huatang—holding an umbrella in one hand and the tray in the other—glanced at the flowers and greenery on the walls of Spring Lotus Garden before heading back to Jiaxing Garden.","Xie Tingyun was waiting at the entrance.","Taking advantage of Shen Huatang’s distraction, she snatched two buns from the tray and promptly stuffed one into her mouth.","\"Junior Sister Huatang, I’m going to see Junior Brother Xue and Junior Sister Liu. I’m off now.\"","She was about to use her Body Technique to dash off, but Shen Huatang sidestepped to block her path.","Xie Tingyun halted, giving an awkward smile. \"Something wrong, Junior Sister?\"","Shen Huatang gave her a cool look. \"Did you speak with the Eldest Miss?\"","\"Of course. I’m always one to follow the rules.\"","\"When will you be back?\"","\"By noon... No, I’ll be back before three this afternoon.\"","Xie Tingyun rarely had a chance to leave the Marquis’s Mansion, so she wanted to spend a little more time with her junior brothers and sisters.","Shen Huatang, of course, understood the thoughts of her Eldest Senior Sister and continued, \"Are Junior Brother Xue and the others doing well?\"","\"They’re fine. Everything’s normal.\"","\"Then please relay a message for me, Senior Sister. Tell them I’ll be coming over tomorrow morning to test their Martial Arts.\"","Xie Tingyun froze for a moment. When she recovered, she managed a strained smile. \"Alright, I’ll tell them.\"","’We’re doomed. We’re so doomed.’","’My dear junior brothers and sisters, it’s not that I don’t want to help you, but I’m terrified of your Senior Sister Shen, too.’","’You’ll have to fend for yourselves.’","After Xie Tingyun had gone,","Shen Huatang watched her go for a moment longer, then carried the breakfast into the main hall and arranged it neatly on the table.","Xiao Wan’er entered, walking with her usual grace.","She was dressed a little differently today. Though still wrapped in a heavy cloak, this one was clearly newer and brighter.","Beneath it, she wore a pale blue dress, and at her waist hung the Jade Pendant that signified her status in the Xiao Family.","The main difference was that she had clearly taken extra care with her appearance. Her hair was intricately styled, and a glittering ruby rested upon her brow.","It added an air of nobility to her already exquisite face.","Xiao Wan’er sat down at the table. As she gestured for Shen Huatang and the others to join her, she asked with a smile,","\"Did you speak to Xiaodie?\"","\"I happened to run into her on my way back just now. I told her about the chicken soup.\"","Shen Huatang added reluctantly, \"And I made sure to tell her that you were the one who ordered it.\"","Xiao Wan’er paused. A faint blush rose to her cheeks, making her look even more beautiful beneath the glimmer of the ruby on her brow.","\"He’s been studying so hard these past few days. He ought to have something nourishing.\"","’Whatever you say, my lady.’","Shen Huatang lowered her head and ate in silence, keeping her thoughts to herself.","Perhaps realizing her explanation was unnecessary, Xiao Wan’er changed the subject.","\"I’m going to Tingyu Pavilion later. Little Sister Qingwu invited me to discuss matters regarding the Medical Dao Academy. We’ll leave as soon as we finish eating.\"","\"We’ll likely be back late, so bring the gifts we prepared earlier.\"","Shen Huatang acknowledged the order.","\"On the way back, Huatang, don’t forget to remind me to purchase some fabric.\"","\"The weather is turning cold. It’s time to have some thicker clothes made for Grandfather... for them.\"","\"And also...\"","Seeing her so unusually talkative, Shen Huatang knew that her earlier comment had flustered her. She could only say,","\"Miss, why not ask Master Chen Yi if he’d like to go to Tingyu Pavilion?\"","\"I recall that Advisor Chen said he wanted to treat him to a meal.\"","At her words, Xiao Wan’er glanced toward Spring Lotus Garden. She hesitated a moment before shaking her head. \"Not this time.\"","\"With the Annual Examination less than half a month away, it’s better to let him stay in the mansion and study.\"","Having said that, her earlier fluster seemed to subside, and she said no more.","After the meal, she departed with her attendants.","Meanwhile, in Spring Lotus Garden, just a wall away,","Chen Yi had just sat down at his own dining table. He could, of course, hear the sound of carriage wheels in the distance.","He knew Xiao Wan’er was going to see Cui Qingwu today, so he didn’t give it much thought and simply started on his breakfast.","Standing nearby, Xiaodie glanced at him, her eyes fixed on the bowl of chicken soup.","\"Young Master, the Eldest Miss had chicken soup prepared for you today.\"","\"Oh? That’s nice.\"","\"Drink it while it’s hot, Young Master.\"","Chen Yi glanced at her, a smile touching his lips when he saw her covetous expression. He poured some of the soup from his bowl into another and placed it in front of her.","\"You have some too. For nourishment.\"","Xiaodie fidgeted. \"Young Master, this is for you from the Eldest Miss. I... I can’t drink it.\"","\"Can’t? Or don’t want to?\"","\"Both... B-both...\"","\"Fine, forget it. There’s barely enough for me as it is.\"","\"No, no, no...!\"","Watching Xiaodie hastily grab the bowl and gulp down the soup, Chen Yi chided her with a laugh:","\"Next time, if you want to eat or drink something, just say so. It’s not like I’d stop you.\"","After she finished, Xiaodie wiped her mouth and grinned. \"You’re too good to me, Young Master. But I can’t forget my place.\"","\"If people from the other courtyards found out, they’d gossip.\"","\"You little rascal... always so quick-witted...\"","After they finished breakfast amidst their banter, Xiaodie asked while clearing the table, \"Are you going out today, Young Master?\"","\"I don’t think so.\"","\"In that case, could I go out for a bit?\"","\"The first day of winter is coming soon, and I wanted to get some clothes ready.\"","\"My needlework isn’t very good, though. I’ll need to learn from the other sisters in the mansion. I can practice on my own clothes...\"","After listening to her ramble, Chen Yi nodded with a smile. \"Go on. Just remember to have some of the mansion’s Armored Warriors go with you.\"","\"Yes, yes! Don’t you worry, Young Master...\"","Not long after, Chen Yi was the only one left in Spring Lotus Garden.","Even the neighboring Jiaxing Garden was deserted.","Chen Yi tried to read for a while, but he couldn’t seem to focus. The words on the page felt bland and uninteresting.","He looked up at the sky.","On a whim, he stood, opened an Oil Paper Umbrella, and left Spring Lotus Garden.","’A walk might be nice,’ he thought. ’I might as well go see that business about someone selling herself to pay for her father’s burial...’"]},{"number":481,"title":"Chapter 481 - 291: Chess Dao Perfection","paragraphs":["Chen Yi actually quite liked overcast, rainy weather.","Especially in autumn.","A cool breeze carried a chilly rain that gently brushed against his cheeks, leaving a refreshing sensation far more comfortable than the sweltering heat of a sunny day.","But sometimes, he didn’t like the rain.","The hem of his long silk robe was low, and if he wasn’t careful, it would get splashed with muddy water.","Specks of mud would cover his shoes and legs.","Unlike neat embroidery, they were scattered chaotically, as jumbled as Xiao Wuge’s Golden Carp.","Some large, some small.","Because of this, Chen Yi would walk very carefully.","Even on the relatively flat grounds of the Marquis’s Mansion, he walked at an unhurried pace, taking each step with steady deliberation.","Fortunately, while the Xiao Family’s courtyard was large, it was nowhere near the extravagant opulence of \"a new tower every five steps, a new pavilion every ten, with winding corridors and eaves pecking at the sky.\"","A short while later,","Chen Yi passed through the central courtyard and arrived behind the spirit screen in the front courtyard.","Wang Lixing and Liu Si’er weren’t around. Only two vaguely familiar Armored Warriors stood guard.","Outside the gatehouse not far away, a hunched-over old man was sweeping fallen leaves from the ground, his head lowered.","\"Mr. Qingzhou.\"","The Armored Warriors greeted him. Chen Yi smiled and nodded. When he caught sight of the Iron Banner Officer of the White Tiger Guard—the stooped old man—out of the corner of his eye, he called out a greeting as well.","\"Uncle Gui.\"","As usual, Uncle Gui just gave him a cold glance before lowering his head and continuing his work.","Chen Yi didn’t mind. He opened his umbrella, walked out of the Marquis’s Mansion, and headed for the East Market.","The two Armored Warriors watched him go, their voices filled with emotion.","\"When the second young master-in-law first arrived at the mansion, who could have imagined he’d achieve what he has today?\"","\"Yeah, back then, forget the Second Miss—which of us brothers didn’t want to beat him to death?\"","\"The one who wanted to beat him up the most was that kid, Yan Hong. Haha, but he won’t get the chance anymore.\"","\"The second young master-in-law is now the world-renowned Mr. Qingzhou. A single page of his calligraphy is worth more than Yan Hong’s life three times over.\"","\"I hear that many visitors to Guiyun Academy now are there just to buy the young master-in-law’s calligraphy. They say a single character is worth a hundred gold.\"","\"Especially the original manuscript of *Song of the Water Melody: Mid-Autumn*. It’s priceless! Too bad the young master-in-law lost it...\"","Uncle Gui overheard their conversation. He put away his broom and other tools, then slowly followed them out of the Marquis’s Mansion.","The drizzle was endless and the pedestrians hurried along, their forms quickly swallowing his figure.","In contrast, Chen Yi, walking down South Street, stood out like a crane among chickens.","His figure was already tall and slender.","After taking up the practice of Martial Arts, his body had become even more robust.","It was just that he usually wore loose, flowing robes, and the concealing effect of the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique made him appear somewhat frail and scholarly.","Walking among the passersby, he always seemed the most transcendent of them all.","He attracted the sideways glances of many women.","\"That young master looks very unfamiliar. I wonder which family he belongs to?\"","\"Sister Chun’er, is he unfamiliar? I feel like I’ve seen him somewhere before.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"It seems... it seems...\"","Before the woman in the goose-yellow cotton dress could remember, a few scholars nearby spoke up.","\"That’s Mr. Qingzhou. He isn’t just some family’s young master.\"","\"Mr. Qingzhou? Ah, so he’s Mr. Qingzhou!\"","\"The Mr. Qingzhou of ’May we live long and share the moon’s beauty, though a thousand miles may part us’?\"","\"If that’s him, then isn’t he... isn’t he... General Jinghong’s husband?\"","The unmarried young women revealed looks of disappointment, but they didn’t say anything catty.","Aside from Chen Yi’s rather unseemly status as a live-in son-in-law, they also simply didn’t dare compare themselves to Xiao Jinghong.","Setting aside whether they could compete in terms of family background or appearance, the mere fact that Xiao Jinghong commanded the Dingyuan Army through her mastery of Martial Arts was enough to crush them completely.","Chen Yi heard these discussions but remained calm, ignoring the pointing and whispering around him.","As his fame spread, it wasn’t just at the Xiao Family estate or Guiyun Academy; many people in Shu State City now recognized him.","Occasionally, when he walked down the street, people would even come forward to greet him formally.","Fortunately, most of them were scholars who only expressed their admiration. Otherwise, Chen Yi feared he wouldn’t dare to go out so easily.","Walking at a leisurely pace, it took him about half an hour to reach the East Market.","He remembered that the last time he’d come here was because of Immortal Bai.","When he met that legendary figure, he hadn’t felt excited. Instead, a thought had come to him: ’Keep a respectful distance.’","Besides his apprehension about Immortal Bai’s prophecy, there were also those eyes of his, which seemed to see through everything.","Even with the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, which at the time could fool Xiao Jinghong and the others, Chen Yi feared he had nowhere to hide from Immortal Bai’s gaze.","Musing on this, Chen Yi glanced at the bustling Xinglin Hall, then walked straight to Jishi Medicine Hall.","Compared to the clamor last time, there were clearly fewer people outside the Medicine Hall now.","There were only two patients who had come to fill prescriptions.","Even the usual Jianghu artisans who came here to chat were nowhere to be seen.","Liu Quan was clacking away on an abacus. When he saw Chen Yi enter, he quickly stood up to greet him.","\"Shopkeeper, you’re here.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment, surveyed the inside of the Medicine Hall, and casually asked, \"Has business been affected?\"","Liu Quan’s face soured as he poured out his grievances. \"Shopkeeper, you can see for yourself.\"","\"Now that Xinglin Hall has a Medical Saint Hand in residence, their diagnoses are nearly flawless. Add to that their low prices for medicinal herbs, and who would still come to our place?\"","\"If it weren’t for the herbal teas we sell, I’m afraid our expenses would have exceeded our income this month.\"","Chen Yi hummed in response, offering a few words of comfort with a smile, then called Ma Liangcai to join him as they headed inside.","Ma Liangcai bowed deeply. \"Shopkeeper.\"","Chen Yi sized him up with a glance. \"Sit and talk.\"","\"Yes.\"","Ma Liangcai had changed quite a bit during this time.","Before, his grasp of the Medical Dao was poor, and he mostly relied on a few remedies he’d picked up from who-knows-where to put on a show."]},{"number":482,"title":"Chapter 482 - 291: Chess Dao Perfection","paragraphs":["By now, he had officially crossed the threshold of the Medical Dao. He knew the principles of Yin Yang Five Elements, the Four Diagnostic Methods, and the Eight Principles by heart.","Reaching the Minor Success Realm and earning the title of \"Medical Saint Hand\" would depend on his own insight.","Of course, Chen Yi hadn’t summoned him to give him pointers on the Medical Dao.","\"You must have heard that the Young Miss plans to build a Medical Dao Academy.\"","Ma Liangcai’s heart stirred. \"Sir, are you... are you thinking of having me...\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"You should understand the benefits once the Medical Dao Academy is built, not just for the Xiao Family, but also for Physicians like yourself.\"","Excitement washed over Ma Liangcai’s face, and he stammered, \"I... I naturally understand. I’m just afraid my Medical Skill isn’t refined enough and I’ll lead the students astray...\"","Chen Yi waved his hand dismissively. \"A lack of skill is only relative. Your grasp of medical theory is solid. The only thing you lack compared to other Physicians is experience.\"","\"Once you master and integrate all you’ve learned, advancing your Medical Dao will just be a matter of time.\"","\"Of course, the position of the academy’s dean is not for you, at least not for now.\"","Hearing this, Ma Liangcai immediately dropped to his knees. \"You jest, Sir.\"","\"Just being able to enter the Medical Dao Academy is a tremendous Opportunity for me. How could I dare to covet the dean’s position?\"","Chen Yi gestured for him to rise and speak. Once Ma Liangcai’s expression had calmed, he continued:","\"I’m sending you to the Medical Dao Academy because you are the most suitable candidate, but also because I have some other tasks for you.\"","\"Please give me your orders, Sir.\"","\"Right now, the Medical Dao Academy is no longer under the Young Miss’s sole control. A young lady from the Qinghe Cui Family is also involved.\"","\"I need you to be my eyes and ears. If you notice anything unusual at the academy, remember to send word to me.\"","Ma Liangcai understood. \"Rest assured, Sir. I will handle this matter for you without fail.\"","Chen Yi nodded and then changed the subject to idle chatter.","Although he had been the one to orchestrate Xiao Wan’er’s agreement to let Cui Qingwu join the Medical Dao Academy, he knew ’it was wise to be on guard against others.’","There was no guarantee that after witnessing the academy’s influence, Cui Qingwu or the Cui Family wouldn’t get any crooked ideas.","It was just like with Xinglin Hall not far away—even members of the same Liu Family could fall into dispute.","How much more so for the Xiao Family and the Cui Family?","Furthermore, Chen Yi’s plan to place Ma Liangcai in the Medical Dao Academy also included having him handle certain matters on his behalf.","Such as compiling medical texts and the like.","It wasn’t convenient for him to show his face, so having Ma Liangcai act in his stead was a fitting arrangement.","He had to find a way to ensure Xiao Wan’er’s Medical Dao Academy succeeded, one way or another.","Seeing that it was the Hour of the Serpent, Chen Yi stood up, walked to the entrance of the Medicine Hall, and gazed toward the entrance of the East Market not far away.","Before long, he saw a tattered figure pushing a flatbed cart to the area just outside the entrance.","It appeared to be a young girl, about twelve or thirteen years old, and extremely gaunt.","Not only was there barely any flesh on her bones, but her face was also so thin it was almost unrecognizable.","After struggling to steady the cart, she took out a wooden sign from on top of it, held it to her chest, and knelt silently on the ground.","The sign was brief, with just three lines.","\"Selling myself to bury my father. Seeking a kind person. Willing to be a slave for life.\"","Passersby who saw the scene mostly gathered around, though some colder-hearted individuals simply walked away without a second glance.","Amidst the pointing and whispering, the gist of the situation became clear.","\"That child is from Lotus Lane in the east of the city. A pitiful one, she is.\"","\"When her father was healthy, he could carry three hundred sacks a day at the Wharf. With that hard labor, he could just about support her and the family.\"","\"But during the heavy rains last month, a ship’s mooring rope snapped at the Wharf, and her father was severely injured.\"","\"That shouldn’t have been the end of it; he should have recovered with some rest. But as they say, when it rains, it pours.\"","\"With the soaring prices of grain and medicine these past few days, she couldn’t even afford to buy medicine, let alone food.\"","\"She emptied out everything they had, but in the end, she still couldn’t save her father...\"","Chen Yi stood outside the crowd, silently listening to the murmurs, his eyes reflecting the image of the little girl named Yuan Liu’er.","Although the rise in Shu State’s grain prices was a plot by the Ji State Trading Company, and prices would have skyrocketed even without his interference, he had, in fact, played a dishonorable role in it all.","’What is this?’","’I did not kill Boren, yet Boren died because of me?’","Watching Yuan Liu’er’s kneeling figure, Chen Yi gave a bitter, silent laugh.","The unexpected consequence caught him off guard, leaving a sour taste in his mouth.","He watched quietly for a moment.","Chen Yi let out a breath. After a moment’s thought, he summoned Liu Quan and Ma Liangcai.","\"Shopkeeper?\"","Chen Yi pointed at Yuan Liu’er and instructed, \"Go to the accounts, withdraw some silver, and find someone to give him a proper burial.\"","Liu Quan froze. \"This...\"","\"Shopkeeper, you... you want to buy that little girl?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"Not me. And no, not buying.\"","He didn’t explain further, instead turning to Ma Liangcai, his tone leaving no room for argument:","\"That girl has a decent talent for the Medical Dao. Take her on as an apprentice and teach her well.\"","Ma Liangcai didn’t hesitate. He bowed in acknowledgement and then walked over.","Seeing this, Liu Quan didn’t linger either. He hurried back into the Medicine Hall to get some silver and followed.","The rest of the matter proceeded as a matter of course.","Amidst Yuan Liu’er’s profound gratitude, Liu Quan dispersed the crowd and used the money to hire people from a funeral service to bury her father.","She had intended to sell herself into servitude, but Ma Liangcai refused, taking her in as an apprentice instead and allowing her to stay at Jishi Medicine Hall.","\"Thank you, benefactor, thank you...\"","Although Ma Liangcai was puzzled about her supposed talent for the Medical Dao, he didn’t dare, nor would he ever, question an order from Chen Yi.","\"The one who saved you wasn’t me, but...\"","Ma Liangcai paused and glanced back at Chen Yi. Seeing him shake his head slightly, he understood and said:","\"But yourself.\"","Tears streamed down Yuan Liu’er’s grimy face as she asked, \"Myself?\"","\"You have a good talent for the Medical Dao. From now on, you’ll follow me as an apprentice.\"","\"If you work hard enough, you’ll be able to learn a skill to survive here at Jishi Medicine Hall.\"","A look of confusion flickered across Yuan Liu’er’s face. \"The... the Medicine Hall? An apprentice?\"","She clearly had no idea what talent she possessed for the Medical Dao, but she knew for certain that she had met a kind person.","Kneeling on the ground, she was overcome with tears.","The onlookers who hadn’t yet dispersed saw this unfold. Some marveled at the girl’s good fortune, others admired Ma Liangcai for his eye for talent, and still others remarked that this was just what you’d expect from someone of the Xiao Family Medicine Hall.","But few mentioned Chen Yi.","Even though he was standing right there in front of the Medicine Hall, he remained like an outsider, watching calmly.","His thoughts were inscrutable.","’The world knows that Heaven and Earth are not benevolent and treat all things as straw dogs, but few speak of how the Saint is not benevolent and treats the people as straw dogs.’","’Alas, I am no Saint, yet I too will harm the innocent to achieve a goal.’","Chen Yi knew this, but he couldn’t change it.","All he could do was his best to make amends and bring these matters to an end as quickly as possible.","Thus, as he stood there quietly observing the scene before him, the chessboard in his mind began to move again.","The entire situation within Shu State City formed a massive chessboard.","All the white and black pieces leaped across it, transforming into different board positions—","’Elder Master Xiao’s health has improved; he should take on more responsibility.’","’Liu Hong has already fallen into the trap. Whether he sends Asutai away or not, his defeat is only a matter of time.’","’Liu Zhaoxue of the Jing State Liu Family and the Five Poison Sect are being watched by people from the Mountain Race. As long as we are careful, they can’t stir up any trouble.’","’The White Tiger Guard’s schemes are gradually becoming clearer. I can faintly see their purpose in stirring up trouble in Shu State...’","’And the people from the Ji State Trading Company are laughing now. It’s time to make them cry!’","Chen Yi was like a giant, looking down upon the entire chessboard, laying out each and every matter with black and white pieces.","Deducing outcomes, making adjustments, and... deciding the life and death of certain people!","It seemed like a single instant, and yet also like countless years had passed.","—The board froze.","[Chess Skill has advanced. Thousand Hands Chess Manual has broken through to the Perfect Level. You have glimpsed the meaning of Chess Dao Perfection.]","[Chess Dao: Great Success, Progress +1000, Perfection Realm reached.]","A thunderous roar exploded in Chen Yi’s mind.","Countless Profound Mysteries of the Chess Dao emerged, and innumerable chess manuals converged within him.","As a result, the chessboard in his mind that covered Shu State Prefecture City expanded even further.","Not only was it clearer than before, involving more intricate details, but it also expanded to encompass the entirety of Shu State and even some regions of other state capitals.","And Chen Yi was the sole Chess Master on this board.","—Like a true Saint, looking down upon the world!"]},{"number":483,"title":"Chapter 483 - 292: A Familiar Smell","paragraphs":["What is the Chess Dao?","Everyone has a different understanding.","For some, it is a minor art for entertainment and self-improvement. For others, it is like a clash on the battlefield. For still others, it is a way to comprehend the ultimate principles of life, or even the universe.","But in Chen Yi’s eyes at this moment, the world was the \"chessboard,\" and all of creation, the \"pieces.\"","As the player, he could change a person’s fate with every piece he placed.","Especially here in Shu State.","It was like a small world of its own.","Countless people became his pieces. Mountains and rivers formed the grid, and the very flow of destiny bent to his will.","In this sense, the Chess Dao shared a common origin with Yi Shu Divination.","But divination followed the way of Heaven; every sip and every peck was fated.","The Chess Dao, however, depended entirely on the whims of the player.","’So this is... \"Heaven and Earth are not benevolent; they treat the myriad things as straw dogs.\"’","Chen Yi slowly opened his eyes, his mind a swirl of Profound Mysteries and chaos, and a deep sense of awe washed over him.","He hadn’t expected his Dao Realm epiphany to come at a time like this.","He had thought it was just an ordinary, trivial matter, but it had unexpectedly pushed his Chess Dao to a breakthrough into the Perfection Realm.","He looked toward where Ma Liangcai and the others were, his gaze falling on the still dazed and helpless Yuan Liu’er.","[At the third mark of the Serpent Hour, you witnessed Yuan Liu’er selling herself to bury her father, thereby accepting the resulting karma and helping Yuan Liu’er.]","[Reward: \"Eight Methods of Weaving,\" Opportunity +20.]","[Evaluation: Arrived on site. Heard the sounds. Witnessed the scene. Performance: Excellent.]","Chen Yi glanced at the prompt. ’Thank you,’ he thought.","Not long after, the crowd dispersed, and Liu Quan led Yuan Liu’er away to bury Father Yuan.","Ma Liangcai returned alone and cupped his hands. \"Shopkeeper, it’s done.\"","\"Once Liu’er finishes with her father’s funeral, she will come to the Medicine Hall.\"","Chen Yi hummed in acknowledgment. He watched the flatbed cart trundle unhurriedly into the distance before he spoke.","\"Teach her well.\"","With that, he patted Ma Liangcai’s shoulder and turned to leave.","Beneath the overcast sky, the rain grew heavier.","On the somewhat dim Chuandong Street, the crowd surged, yet the figures in their raincoats and bamboo hats seemed frozen in an Ink-Wash Painting.","Only an amber-colored Oil Paper Umbrella moved through them, growing ever more distant.","Ma Liangcai stared for a long time, then shook his head and returned to the Medicine Hall.","He vaguely sensed that Chen Yi was in a strange mood, so in the end, he didn’t dare to ask any questions about Yuan Liu’er’s talent for the Medical Dao.","’It must be fate bringing them together as master and disciple.’","Once the commotion outside the East Market died down, a cacophony of other sounds followed.","Shouts, arguments, haggling, and laughter all mingled together.","Huddled in the long line outside Xinglin Hall, Uncle Gui watched Chen Yi walk away, a hint of confusion on his wrinkled face.","’This \"fledgling’s\" behavior today seems to contradict his usual \"indifference\" toward everything. To think he’d be so kind as to help a mere slip of a girl.’","A mocking expression flashed across Uncle Gui’s face. ’The charity of the great Noble Families?’","After waiting a moment, Uncle Gui lowered his profile slightly and slowly headed toward the Marquis’s Mansion.","But when he turned onto South Street, there was no sign of Chen Yi.","He looked toward the West Market and Yanhua Lane, but still saw no trace of him and couldn’t help but frown.","’Lost him?’","’For an old veteran of the Dingyuan Army, an Iron Banner Officer of the White Tiger Guard like himself, losing certain people was perfectly normal. It could happen with Martial Arts masters, or if he was unfamiliar with the terrain. But for a scholar who only knew a bit of Fist and Foot to escape his pursuit... that was truly bizarre.’","Uncle Gui scanned the area again. Still seeing no sign of Chen Yi, he turned back toward the Xiao Mansion, a sinister look in his eyes.","He ran into a few acquaintances along the way, the greetings of \"Uncle Gui!\" coming one after another.","He turned a deaf ear, his body hunched as he walked at an unhurried pace.","But as he turned into the alley where the mansion gate was, a sinister laugh sounded in his ear.","\"Uncle Gui?\"","Uncle Gui was sure the voice did not belong to anyone from the mansion, and he turned to look.","Just as he was about to get a clear look at the person, he suddenly met those eyes—a pair of eyes as scarlet as blood.","\"You...\"","Before Uncle Gui could finish speaking, his body froze. His once murky and sinister eyes flickered through several colors.","From black to red, then from red back to black.","\"It is your good fortune that this old man has taken a fancy to your body.\"","\"Uncle Gui\" muttered to himself and walked into the Marquis’s Mansion with a strange gait.","As he went deeper, not a single person noticed anything odd about him. Many Armored Warriors even greeted him with a smile.","This caused \"Uncle Gui’s\" mouth to stretch into an even wider grin as he lowered his head.","But just as he reached the rear courtyard and was about to look for Chen Yi, a flash of scarlet shot through his eyes, and he stared straight at the Spring Lotus Garden.","\"There... a familiar scent...\"","\"Uncle Gui\" sized it up for a long moment, the smile on his face vanishing bit by bit.","Surprise, astonishment... followed by immense joy.","\"Hahaha... hahaha... Is it you? Is this your hiding place?\"","He found it hard to believe, yet he would never doubt his ’treasure’s’ sense of smell.","A scent that strong could not be mistaken—it was the scent of \"Dragon Spear\" Liu Wu!","\"Uncle Gui\" listened for a moment. Confirming that there was no one inside the residence, he no longer hesitated and walked straight over.","In the tranquil courtyard, stray leaves and petals danced in the air.","Lush trees surrounded two wooden buildings, and a pavilion stood by the edge of a pond.","A faint scent of lotus flowers lingered on the bluestone path.","It mingled with the sweet fragrance of grass and trees.","And from one of the wooden buildings drifted wisps of a strong plum blossom scent.","The smile on \"Uncle Gui’s\" face grew wider. \"So, you’re here.\"","He walked toward the wooden building, muttering in a low voice, \"Liu Hong was right. That ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu is indeed a member of the Xiao family.\"","\"He lives right here with the Xiao Family.\"","\"No wonder the Xiao Family suffered no losses after the summer grain of the Three Towns was burned. It must have been the work of that old bastard, Xiao Yuan.\"","\"But who is the master of this courtyard?\"","\"Let this old man see... let’s see...\"","\"Uncle Gui\" pushed open the door of the wooden building. He glanced at the elegantly furnished living room, then walked toward the study, where the intense scent of plum blossoms was strongest."]},{"number":484,"title":"Chapter 484 - 292: A Familiar Scent","paragraphs":["The moment he entered, he saw a piece of calligraphy hanging behind the desk.","\"Song of the Water Melody: Mid-Autumn: When will the bright moon appear, with a cup of wine... Though a thousand miles apart, we share the same moon’s light—Chen Yi, Chen Qingzhou.\"","A Cloud Immortal Realm drifted above the study, and within it, a figure stood proudly.","Perhaps sensing an intruder, he raised his head and looked down at the newcomer from under his half-lowered eyelids.","\"Uncle Gui\" stared blankly at the calligraphy, stared blankly at the figure within the Immortal Realm, his mouth hanging slightly open.","\"Chen Yi, Chen Qingzhou... Liu Wu...\"","...","「West Market, Hundred Herbs Hall.」","After leaving Jishi Medicine Hall, Chen Yi came straight here.","To avoid being recognized, he had deliberately changed into his \"Chen Yu\" disguise and summoned Wang Ji.","\"Have your men get ready. As soon as we get the signal from Dabao, they are to head to the Lin Family Grain Store immediately.\"","’Since that clever Lin Zhenghong took it upon himself to approach Cui Qingwu ahead of time, it’s only fitting he handles this part too.’","Wang Ji bowed his head in agreement.","But after some thought, he asked in a low voice, \"Sir, this is all very sudden. I’m afraid Dabao’s side might not be adequately prepared.\"","\"It’s fine.\"","\"All I need is a spark. As for how brightly the fire burns...\"","Chen Yi stood by the window of the quiet room, his hands behind his back. He gazed out at the gloomy rain through a crack in the woven rattan blinds and said softly, \"That’s not up to me.\"","\"The greedier they are, the more this fire will burn until there’s nothing left of them but ashes.\"","Originally, he had indeed planned to wait a few more days, to let the people from the Ji State Trading Company grow complacent and count their silver while enjoying a few sweet dreams.","But after what happened with Yuan Liu’er, he couldn’t afford to wait any longer.","Or rather, the people of Shu State City couldn’t afford to wait.","If he waited any longer, today it was Yuan Liu’er, but tomorrow there would be a Zhao Liu’er, and a Sun Liu’er.","He could accept letting the poor go hungry for a few meals in order to root out the cancer that was the Ji State Trading Company.","But he could not just stand by and watch them die.","He was unwilling, and unable.","’Conscience is the kind of thing that, once you lower its standards even an inch, that inch is lost forever. Trying to raise them again later isn’t just as hard as climbing to heaven; it’s laughable, especially to those who suffered undeserved calamities. Even on the road to the underworld, they would be able to laugh loud enough to shake the heavens.’","Chen Yi had no desire to be filled with regret one day.","「After waiting for about two hours.」","Chen Yi saw a flash of fire in the western sky, followed by another in the southern sky, and turned to leave the quiet room.","Wang Ji, not daring to hesitate, hurried downstairs and whispered something to a Guard from the Celestial Sect.","The young-looking Guard nodded and ran out of Hundred Herbs Hall, his face alight with excitement.","Chen Yi glanced over, gave a nod to Wang Ji, and left as well.","He had only taken a few steps, however, when he sensed a familiar aura beside him, followed by a cheerful voice:","\"Boss Chen, we meet again.\"","Chen Yi turned to see Xie Tingyun greeting him while simultaneously shouting to the Celestial Sect disciple who was running off into the distance:","\"Junior Brother Jin Peng, what are you running so fast for?\"","The Celestial Sect disciple named Jin Peng waved without looking back. \"Eldest Sister, I’ll tell you when I get back!\"","Xie Tingyun didn’t think much of it. She walked up to Chen Yi’s side and, with the casual familiarity of an old friend, went to slap his shoulder.","\"Boss Chen, thank you for taking in our Celestial Sect disciples.\"","Chen Yi dodged without a trace of effort and said coolly, \"I should be the one thanking you.\"","Xie Tingyun’s hand froze in midair. She looked at him, then at her own hand, and praised with a smile, \"Boss Chen, your Martial Arts are quite impressive.\"","\"I only know some crude Fist and Foot techniques. Nothing worth mentioning.\"","\"You...\"","Before she could finish, Chen Yi gave a slight bow. \"I have other business to attend to. Please excuse me.\"","Xie Tingyun let out a cry of protest, but before she could say anything, he was already far away.","She froze for a moment, looked down at her clothes, and scratched her head in confusion.","’Am I really that scary?’","Chen Yi paid her no mind. After confirming no one was following him, he returned once again to the East Market.","To be precise, he entered a small tavern across from the Lin Mansion.","「It was just past noon.」","The tavern wasn’t very crowded.","Chen Yi took a seat by the window and ordered a pot of yellow wine, half a catty of beef, and a bowl of clear noodle soup.","As he ate, he listened for any activity from inside and outside the Lin Mansion.","「About fifteen minutes later.」","The sound of urgent hoofbeats arrived, followed by frantic knocking on a door.","\"You, why are you back? Weren’t you with the caravan heading to the black market beyond the Ancient Tea-Horse Road?\"","\"Quick, take me to see the Master! Something terrible has happened!\"","The voices carried over intermittently, filled with ceaseless sounds of shock and fear.","\"Is it true?\"","\"Did those horse bandits from Poshisu Country really attack?\"","\"It’s absolutely true!\"","\"I saw it with my own eyes! Those horse bandits were killing passing merchants just beyond the Ancient Tea-Horse Road! It wasn’t far from the border pass!\"","\"They... they were riding tall horses with their hooves wrapped in cloth, and every one of them looked like a vicious demon...\"","\"Uncle Hao, Third Master... they’re all dead...\"","\"No, impossible!\"","\"How could King Nalandu dare to do such a thing?!\"","\"Master, it’s true, it’s true, WAHHH...\"","The clamor stopped abruptly, as if someone else had arrived, silencing everyone, including Lin Zhenghong.","\"What happened?\"","\"Lord Wind Patrol Envoy, you’re... you’re finally here! That... King Nalandu has actually led a great army to attack the border.\"","\"What?!\"","\"Did... did you go find that person from the Cui Family?\"","\"Your orders... of course I wouldn’t dare... wouldn’t dare *not* to. I already made a contract with Miss Cui last night...\"","\"Sir, now isn’t the time to talk about this! Shouldn’t... shouldn’t we be making plans?\"","\"Idiot!\"","\"King Landu’s attack is the perfect opportunity for us to make a fortune, and you... you’re thinking of running away?\"","\"Quick, before Miss Cui hears the news, go to her immediately and get that contract back!\"","\"But... but... Miss Cui’s people already took possession of the grain this morning...\"","\"You!?\"","\"I don’t care what method you use, I want to see that grain back in your Lin Family’s storehouses before nightfall!\"","\"Ah, I...\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi glanced toward the Lin Mansion. ’How fortunate. So the \"clever\" one wasn’t Lin Zhenghong, but the person standing behind him. I had wondered how a temporary replacement for Lin Huai’an could be so vigilant, transferring the grain to Cui Qingwu the moment he heard Lv Jiunan was still alive. It seems the Ji State Trading Company has other people in Shu State. They say \"those who are good at swimming are the ones who drown.\" This saves me a lot of trouble.’","Chen Yi chuckled to himself, finished the wine in his pot in one gulp, and rose to leave the tavern.","’The rest depends on how big Cui Qingwu’s appetite is...’","...","After a few twists and turns,","Chen Yi removed his disguise and, holding an Oil Paper Umbrella, leisurely returned to the Xiao Family estate.","Everything was as usual along the way.","Armored Warriors, Household Servants, and Maids greeted him warmly and called out to him without pause.","Chen Yi smiled and nodded to each of them in return, his mood much improved from when he had witnessed Yuan Liu’er’s plight.","’According to my calculations, now that the Ji State Trading Company has the news, they’ll immediately go looking for Cui Qingwu. In a day or two at most, I can have Liu Lang’s side make their move. Combined with the information from Asutai, Lv Jiunan, and the others... if the Ji State Trading Company doesn’t lose at least a million taels of silver, it’ll be an insult to all my hard work and planning.’","However, Chen Yi’s good mood only lasted until the moment he stepped into Spring Lotus Garden—","It was as if heaven and earth had transformed.","The gloomy, rainy weather outside was chilly, but its chill was nothing compared to the bone-piercing cold inside Spring Lotus Garden.","Wisps of crimson mist filled the garden, and black, feather-shaped snowflakes drifted in midair.","The ground was no longer damp bluestone slabs, but a field of thorns.","Vines as thick as the mouth of a bowl twisted and crawled across the entire courtyard, their barbs oozing a dark green fluid.","Towering, giant trees stood in dense ranks, and deep within them, two wooden buildings and a small pavilion could be vaguely seen.","The smile on Chen Yi’s face gradually faded. He surveyed the scene before him, then glanced back over his shoulder.","It was the same dense thicket of thorns.","It was as if his step hadn’t taken him through the gate of Spring Lotus Garden, but thousands of miles away into a bizarre forest.","\"Perfection Realm... an Illusion Skill?\"","The words had barely left his lips when he heard a sinister laugh from beside him:","\"Illusion Skill?\"","\"This is the secret art of Poshisu Country—Black Magic!\"","A thin old man dressed in the uniform of a Marquis’s Mansion Household Servant stood on a nearby giant tree, looking down with crimson eyes.","\"Your Excellency, ’Dragon Spear,’ or should I say, Mr. Qingzhou, you’ve certainly kept this old man waiting!\""]},{"number":485,"title":"Chapter 485 - 293: You Are Not Chen Yi","paragraphs":["Uncle Gui?","Du Cang!","Chen Yi tilted his head back slightly, his gaze fixed on the figure atop the giant tree.","It was indeed the spitting image of Uncle Gui, the gatekeeper of the Marquis’s Mansion and an Iron Banner Officer of the White Tiger Guard.","But the cold, sinister aura emanating from him declared his true identity without a doubt—Du Cang, the \"Jackal\" of the Poshisu Country’s Peacock King Banner!","Confirming his identity, Chen Yi activated his Qi Observation Skill.","Du Cang. Cultivation: Upper Three Grades. Possesses a Black Magic Secret Skill at the Perfection Realm.","He had an ability similar to Lv Jiunan’s, allowing him to control others’ bodies.","His cultivation seemed to be suppressed due to the limitations of the puppet body. His true cultivation level was likely Upper Third Grade.","Furthermore, he could create a small domain resembling an Illusion Realm...","Chen Yi’s thoughts raced. ’His cultivation and Technique Realm are secondary. The most troublesome thing right now is that he knows my identity.’","’On top of that, I’m still inside the Spring Lotus Garden. One wrong move, and all the plans I’ve hidden for so long will go up in smoke.’","’The consequences aren’t just that the Xiao Family will grow suspicious of me; it will also alert Liu Hong, the Ji State Trading Company, and the others.’","Now was not the time!","As these thoughts crossed Chen Yi’s mind, the newly formed chessboard world in his mind’s eye exploded.","Countless pieces rose and fell, the state of the game shifting constantly—","’Du Cang discovering my identity must have been an accident.’","’There are two reasons: he hasn’t been in Shu State for long, so even if he had some way of tracking me, the clues would be too messy and fragmented for him to get a clear direction.’","’Plus, we’ve never met. It should have been impossible for him to find me here.’","’Then there’s only one possibility—the person he came to the Marquis’s Mansion to find was me, Chen Yi.’","’And then, by combining that with some earlier discovery, he finally confirmed my true identity.’","’As for his reason for coming to kill me... Liu Hong?’","’It could only be him.’","Chen Yi was so certain of this because Lv Jiunan, under Liu Hong’s orders, had once controlled his original body to make him flee his own wedding.","Perhaps Liu Hong was unwilling to hand over Asutai and decided to pull the same trick again, making a deal with Du Cang.","Or perhaps Du Cang already intended to cause trouble for the Xiao Family before leaving Shu State, and Liu Hong’s persuasion simply led him to set his sights on Chen Yi.","Of course, it was also possible that Du Cang had come to the Xiao Family by pure coincidence and happened to sense his presence.","But that was highly unlikely.","The old master lived in Qingjing Residence year-round. If Du Cang wanted to do something big, he had no reason to come to the back courtyard, to this Spring Lotus Garden.","A thousand thoughts swirled in Chen Yi’s mind.","The pieces shifted, connecting and forming patterns on the chessboard that was this small world, conjured by Du Cang’s Black Magic.","He deduced several possible outcomes.","As expected.","It was impossible for Chen Yi to kill Du Cang silently while keeping his identity concealed.","It was just like that night during the Mid-Autumn Festival when Yan Fusha had threatened him—killing her inside the city would have only resulted in his identity being exposed.","If he wanted to remain hidden, unless...","It all happened in an instant.","A playful smile appeared on Chen Yi’s calm face. \"You must be... Du Cang?\"","Du Cang was a little surprised. \"You actually know who I am?\"","He had planned on revealing his identity after succeeding, just so he could savor the despair and pain on Chen Yi’s face before death.","But he never imagined Chen Yi would state his name directly.","He had only shown his face to Liu Hong these past few days.","At all other times, he remained hidden in the shadows, leaving not a single trace.","Even within the Peacock King Banner, no more than three people knew he had come to Shu State.","How could Chen Yi possibly know?","Hearing this, Chen Yi just smiled and stopped using the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique to hide his cultivation and Technique Realm.","The moment his Upper Fifth Grade cultivation was released, the True Essence from the three Seas of Qi in his body instantly flooded his entire being.","His Spear Dao Divine Intent, at the Perfection Realm, shot toward the heavens but was still trapped within this small world.","It merely shattered the surrounding thorns, the black, feather-like snow, and several of the giant trees.","\"I’ve heard that General Du’s talent for Black Magic is exceptional, that you made a name for yourself in the Peacock King Banner in just a few short years.\"","\"Seeing you today, General Du, you are indeed as extraordinary as the rumors say.\"","As Chen Yi spoke, he rolled up the long sleeve on his left arm, pulled out the Five-section Spear from within, and began assembling it nonchalantly.","\"However, by coming here with only a puppet body, are you not looking down on this Liu?\"","\"This Liu?\"","Du Cang didn’t even bother asking how he knew his identity anymore. He sneered, \"Death is at your door, and you, the live-in son-in-law, still intend to deceive me?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"Deceive you?\"","\"No, no, no... My surname has always been Liu. I am the fifth child in my family. How could this be deception?\"","\"As for this live-in son-in-law, Chen Yi... hehe... Surely General Du knows where he is now, don’t you?\"","He paused, then looked up at Du Cang and said meaningfully, \"After all, it was your Peacock King Banner’s very own Lv Jiunan who took action back then.\"","Du Cang froze for a moment, his crimson pupils locking onto him.","He scrutinized him.","\"You’re not Chen Yi!\"","Reaching this conclusion, a look of sudden realization dawned on Du Cang’s face. \"I see.\"","\"His Majesty and I were wondering back then. General Lü clearly reported that Chen Yi was already dead, so how could he possibly still be alive?\"","\"What’s more, that Chen Yi was just a weak scholar. It would be impossible for him to achieve your level of Martial Arts Cultivation in just a few short months.\"","Du Cang, believing he had seen through everything, gave an even colder smile. \"So that’s how it is!\"","\"It must be the Xiao Family’s arrangement—they had you replace Chen Yi as Xiao Jinghong’s husband, all to make Xiao Jinghong stay in the Xiao Family.\"","\"Haha... To think that the insignificant scholar Liu Hong spoke of was actually a deep-cover agent of the Xiao Family!\"","\"Good. Very good!\"","Yes, very good indeed.","Anyone who knew of Chen Yi’s situation when he first arrived in Shu State would be suspicious of his Martial Arts Cultivation and Technique Realm.","There was no other reason.","The time frame was simply too short.","Chen Yi’s smile never faltered as he watched Du Cang standing on the giant tree. He gave the Long Spear in his hand a twirl."]},{"number":486,"title":"Chapter 486 - 293: You Are Not Chen Yi","paragraphs":["\"That’s right. I’ve been hiding in the Xiao Family for so long. Did you really think I’d die so easily here, at your hands?\"","\"What do you think?\"","Hearing this, Du Cang’s laughter died. A sinister look darkened his withered face. \"All the more reason you can’t be allowed to live!\"","The words had barely faded.","The red light in his eyes flared, and a crimson brilliance spread throughout the entire pocket realm.","The tips of the black, feather-like snowflakes were dyed red.","The thorny vines oozed a dark red liquid.","The towering trees were cloaked in red. Branch after branch twisted and extended, hanging in midair like whips, their tips shaped like blades.","In the next moment, the realm’s killing intent erupted:","The black snow fluttered down, seemingly slow but deceptively fast.","The undulating thorny vines tore the ground into ravines.","Those branches stabbed out in unison.","—Their target: Chen Yi!","Chen Yi, in contrast, stared intently at Du Cang’s position.","Instead of retreating, he advanced.","He swept his Long Spear in a circle, clearing the thorny vines at his feet, and shot straight up.","The Long Spear cleared the way.","A golden radiance from his spear formed a pair of wings, shattering the black snow and sword-like branches. As if tearing the very fabric of this realm, he thrust toward Du Cang.","—Dragon-Falling Spear: Soaring Dragon Style!","In an instant, the Golden Radiance Spear Intent enveloped Chen Yi’s body, transforming him into a Five-Clawed Golden Dragon that shattered and dissipated the giant trees and black snow in its path.","The golden dragon opened its maw, as if to swallow Du Cang whole.","ROAR!","The dragon’s roars came one after another.","But Du Cang didn’t move an inch, allowing the Five-Clawed Golden Dragon to whistle through his body.","His smile was cold and sinister.","Chen Yi’s figure froze. He hovered on another giant tree, his face grave.","’This is... Black Magic?’","’I have to admit, this realm is quite formidable.’","’Even though I haven’t used my full strength, Du Cang’s ability to turn illusion into reality is not to be underestimated.’","Du Cang looked back at him and sneered, \"I already told you. This is the Black Magic Secret Skill of Poshisu Country, a supreme skill of the National Preceptor himself.\"","\"It’s not something your common Black Magic can compare to.\"","His gaze fell on the Long Spear in Chen Yi’s hand. \"But you... Liu... Wu. Your Spear Dao should have just entered the Perfection Realm, correct?\"","\"If you were given a few more years to mature, you would surely become a great enemy to the King.\"","\"Fortunately, I discovered you in time. You will surely die!\"","As he spoke, he raised his hands, fingers spread, as if pulling the strings of a marionette.","The snow, branches, and thorns that Chen Yi had previously shattered re-formed and tangled together.","In the blink of an eye, they formed a Wooden Man with a body woven from branches, clothed in thorns, and with the black, feather-like snow for hair.","It also held a Long Spear in its hand.","The moment it formed, it thrust its spear at Chen Yi.","Chen Yi, intending to test it, also thrust his spear forward.","A flash of golden Spear Intent appeared and vanished, pressing against the branch-woven, thorn-covered spear.","CLANG!","Chen Yi was forced back a step, his body moving uncontrollably.","Amidst Du Cang’s sneer, the Wooden Man then stepped forward and thrust its spear again.","Chen Yi frowned slightly. He no longer blocked it head-on, twisting his body to dodge.","He swept his Long Spear, stabbing into the Wooden Man’s torso from an odd angle.","Spear Intent flared.","Golden light burst from the cracks in the Wooden Man. Rays of spear radiance shattered the snowflakes, branches, and thorns.","Leaving this pocket realm in shambles.","But the Wooden Man remained completely unharmed. Its first strike having missed, it thrust its spear again.","Like an immortal, unkillable monster, its focus was locked on Chen Yi.","What was even stranger was that while its body was as large as a mountain, its movements were not slow.","Each thrust was faster than the last.","Frowning, Chen Yi dodged each attack, occasionally thrusting his own spear to find a way to destroy it.","’So this is the Black Magic Secret Skill?’","’General Du, what a skill!’","Du Cang stood on a giant tree, watching him at leisure, and said with a sneer:","\"Liu Wu, I know you haven’t used your full strength yet.\"","\"But it doesn’t matter. With this treasure of mine, your defeat is only a matter of time. Let’s see how long you can last!\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, his heart stirring. ’Treasure?’","His eyes scanned the area but found nothing. He stopped worrying and continued to fight the Wooden Man.","In a lull in the fighting, he used his Qi Observation Skill again,","to probe this pocket realm.","The giant trees, the feather-like black snowflakes, the thorny vines...","But in the end, he still couldn’t find the \"treasure\" Du Cang had mentioned.","Chen Yi sighed inwardly, having made a decision.","He then shot toward the Wooden Man’s waist, looking as small as one of the branches on its body.","But from the Long Spear in his hand, a golden spear radiance shot straight up, barely managing to connect with a wisp of Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism despite the realm’s restrictions.","A bolt of golden lightning descended from the dim, lightless sky, striking the Long Spear in Chen Yi’s hand.","The next moment.","Chen Yi’s entire body merged with his spear as a golden radiance erupted.","Like a golden sun, it radiated a brilliant light that dispelled the surrounding darkness.","The black snowflakes melted away.","The giant trees turned to sawdust.","The thorny vines froze their advance and withered into ash.","Even the pocket realm itself began to dissolve.","Seeing this, Du Cang’s face darkened, and he subconsciously crossed his hands over his chest.","Wisps of scarlet fluorescence shone from his chest as he tried to maintain the pocket realm’s existence.","But Chen Yi obviously wouldn’t give him the chance. The moment the realm above began to dissolve, he connected with the heavens and the earth, his Spear Intent blanketing the area of Spring Lotus Garden.","without letting a single trace escape.","The sky was thick with dark clouds, and the heavy rain still poured, pounding against the stone slabs in Spring Lotus Garden.","DRIP. DROP. DRIP.","Without the cover of the pocket realm, Du Cang was standing in a pavilion, watching Chen Yi while still holding his chest.","Chen Yi, in contrast, was using his Long Spear to support himself. He struggled to stand tall, his once-ruddy face now ghastly pale, and blood trickled from the corner of his mouth.","He looked at the sinister-faced Du Cang, wiped the blood from his mouth, and coughed.","\"General Du, are you still going to kill me?\"","\"My Cultivation may be a bit weaker than yours right now, but your true body isn’t here. I still have ways to fight you to the death.\"","Before Du Cang could speak, he continued, \"Cough, cough... how about I make a deal with you?\"","Du Cang stared at him for a long time, then let his hands fall to his sides. In a hoarse voice, he said:","\"Even if you used your Supreme Spear Dao to break my Black Magic Secret Skill, you’re a spent force. What gives you the right to bargain with me?\"","Chen Yi forced a smile and uttered five words: \"Lv Jiunan... is still alive.\"","Du Cang’s scarlet pupils flickered. His brow furrowed instantly, and he glared at him fiercely.","\"Are you toying with me?\"","\"Everyone saw you kill Lv Jiunan that day. If not for that, His Majesty would not have been enraged and sent me here.\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"How could any outsider know better than I whether Lv Jiunan is alive or not?\"","He paused, then explained, \"Actually, I had intended to kill Lv Jiunan that day.\"","\"But after learning he was King Landu’s brother, and later that he had manipulated Chen Yi into fleeing his own wedding, I changed my mind.\"","\"If he hadn’t told me, how do you think I would know the truth about General Jinghong’s wedding day, General Du?\"","Chen Yi took a deep breath and stood up straight. \"Furthermore, he told me that King Landu wants him to marry into another clan of horse bandits. He cannot die.\"","He looked at Du Cang seriously. \"If you don’t believe me, General, you are welcome to come to the Xiao Family again.\"","Du Cang’s expression flickered with uncertainty.","His preconceptions swayed him; he was already ninety-nine percent convinced.","After a long moment, he spoke in a sinister tone, \"I’ll believe you for now and agree to this deal.\"","\"But, since it’s a deal, it ought to be fair.\"","\"Hm?\"","Before Chen Yi could ask, he sensed another sinister aura from outside the Marquis’s Mansion.","It was identical to the aura of the \"Uncle Gui\" before him.","The next moment, a panicked voice cried out from outside the mansion:","\"Young Mistress! Who dares to kidnap the daughter of the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion?!\"","’The daughter...’","’Xiao Wan’er...’","A flash of intense killing intent appeared deep in Chen Yi’s eyes as he stared at Du Cang. \"What... are you doing?\"","A sinister smile spread across Du Cang’s face.","\"Liu Wu, I will only wait for you for half a day. If you don’t come, she will surely die, hahaha...\"","\"Remember, bring General Lü!\""]},{"number":487,"title":"Chapter 487 - 294: No Greater Sorrow than Parting in Life","paragraphs":["\"Three hundred li outside the city, at Puyin Temple on the Chishui Riverbank. I’ll be waiting for you there!\"","\"Haha... Liu Wu, don’t keep an old man waiting too long!\"","Du Cang’s laughter was like a blade.","Pine needles snapped in two, drifting down like withered petals.","They partially obscured the body that had once belonged to Uncle Gui.","In an instant, he vanished from the Spring Lotus Garden.","As if he had never been there at all.","Chen Yi stared at the spot where he had been, but his eyes followed the wisp of cold aura.","It joined with the other cold aura—the one that had abducted Xiao Wan’er from the Marquis’s Mansion—and sped toward the North City.","’North City... then head west... Puyin Temple...’","Chen Yi retracted his gaze and straightened his chest. The pallor vanished from his face as the internal organs he had deliberately injured began to heal rapidly.","He then erased all traces of his presence in the Spring Lotus Garden, suppressed his aura once more, and hurried to the study.","He couldn’t wait half a day.","Even an hour was too long.","Du Cang was not like Yan Fusha. He was decisive, ruthless, insidious, and cunning. There was no guarantee he wouldn’t realize he’d been deceived.","If Xiao Wan’er was harmed because of this...","Chen Yi feared he would regret it for the rest of his life.","His self-recrimination grew even stronger after he deduced that her coincidental return was likely connected to him.","’If I hadn’t been in such a hurry to deal with the Ji State Trading Company and made Zhang Dabao act ahead of schedule, Lin Zhenghong and the others wouldn’t have gone to Tingyu Pavilion.’","’If they hadn’t gone, Xiao Wan’er wouldn’t have returned to the mansion early to avoid suspicion.’","’And she wouldn’t have run right into Du Cang...’","As Chen Yi connected the dots, the killing intent in his heart intensified.","He wished he could tear Du Cang limb from limb.","But he also knew he couldn’t be rash. When facing a vicious man like Du Cang, anything out of the ordinary could arouse his suspicion.","So, although he was burning with anxiety, Chen Yi still needed to make some preparations before setting out.","Meanwhile, the Xiao Family had been thrown into chaos.","When Xiao Wan’er was abducted at the gate of the Marquis’s Mansion, the Third Steward Lu Guan and several Personal Guard Armored Warriors were right there.","With the anxious return of Shen Huatang, who had lost Du Cang’s trail, everyone in the Xiao Family had naturally gotten the news.","Shen Huatang didn’t have time for formalities. She barged directly into the Qingjing Residence, shouting anxiously,","\"Elder Master, the person who abducted the Eldest Miss practices the Black Magic of Poshisu Country! His Cultivation should be in the Upper Three Grades Realm!\"","\"Please, Elder Master, you must find a way to save her!\"","\"Those dogs from Poshisu Country! How dare they be so audacious and reckless?!\"","Elder Master Xiao, who had just recovered from a serious illness, was enraged. He threw down his cane, intending to track Du Cang himself.","But Xiao Shen, who had rushed over after hearing the news, stopped him.","\"Big Brother, the villain has taken Wan’er, and her whereabouts are unknown. If you leave now, the entire Xiao Family will be without a leader.\"","\"If, by some chance, something were to happen to you, I’m afraid the whole Xiao Family would...\"","He didn’t finish the sentence.","But Elder Master Xiao understood.","His tall, gaunt frame trembled several times, his expression flickering.","\"Wan’er...\"","\"I have already failed Fengchun and Wanqing. I absolutely cannot let their child come to harm!\"","「A moment later.」","Elder Master Xiao made his decision. Standing tall outside the Qingjing Residence, he suppressed his rage and gave his orders.","\"Third Brother, inform all Government Offices to investigate every person from Poshisu Country within the city. If any resist, kill them on sight!\"","\"Lixing, take my command medallion, mobilize the garrison outside the city, and lock down the Western Passage and the Chishui River.\"","\"Huatang...\"","Elder Master Xiao looked at her with slight hesitation. \"You... I must ask you and Miss Tingyun to find a way to pursue the villain.\"","\"If you find anything, inform me immediately.\"","Shen Huatang nodded firmly, immediately using her Body Technique to leave the Marquis’s Mansion and find Xie Tingyun.","A Black Magic Master of the Upper Three Grades was far beyond her ability to handle. For now, she could only hope her Senior Sister would be strong enough.","Without hesitation, Wang Lixing took Duke Dingyuan’s command medallion and headed north out of the city.","Xiao Shen hesitated, leaving with the words, \"I hope you can remain calm, Big Brother,\" before quickly departing as well.","Seeing them go, Elder Master Xiao’s expression remained tense. He looked at Xiao Xuanshuo, who was standing nearby, and said,","\"Take Wuge and hide in the secret chamber. Do not leave for any reason until you hear from me!\"","Xiao Xuanshuo understood the gravity of the situation, accepted the order, and left.","After they had all departed, Elder Master Xiao stared at the rain outside the Qingjing Residence. After a moment of thought, he gestured to the shadows nearby.","\"Go to Hundred Herbs Hall. Ask that person to make a move!\"","Xiao Jing acknowledged the order in a low voice. As he was about to leave, he turned and saw a calm figure standing inside the Qingjing Residence.","\"You...\"","Xiao Jing froze for a second. When he saw the person’s face, he was overjoyed. \"Elder Master, he... he’s here!\"","Elder Master Xiao looked back, a flash of confusion in his eyes, but he had no time to dwell on it. He said urgently,","\"Your Excellency, ’Dragon Spear,’ you’ve come at the perfect time! Wan’er... Wan’er has been abducted by a villain. I must ask for your help!\"","The newcomer was none other than Chen Yi.","Or rather, Chen Yi disguised as Chen Yu.","He was dressed in black brocade, and beneath his calm expression was a hint of deadly seriousness.","He wasted no time on pleasantries, getting straight to the point.","\"Marquis, the one who abducted Wan’er... the Eldest Miss... is Du Cang, a Grand General under King Landu of Poshisu Country.\"","Xiao Jing was shocked. \"Du Cang?!\"","\"How... how could he be in Shu State? Is it because of Lv Jiunan?!\"","Elder Master Xiao’s expression also grew heavy.","For years, he had indeed not stepped out of the Marquis’s Mansion, but that didn’t mean he was oblivious to the world. He had naturally heard the name Du Cang before.","He knew Du Cang was a ruthless bandit who had been ravaging the Ancient Tea-Horse Road in recent years, earning the moniker \"Jackal.\"","He had always been vicious, cruel, insidious, and cunning.","Many Wandering Martial Artists escorting caravans to the Western Regions had died at his hands."]},{"number":488,"title":"Chapter 488 - 294: No Greater Sorrow Than Parting in Life","paragraphs":["At this, Elder Master Xiao’s voice grew grave. \"Since you know it was him, you must also be clear on why he came to our Xiao Family.\"","Chen Yi nodded slightly, his eyes on the darkening sky as he spoke softly.","\"He came to Shu State for me, but I am only one of his targets.\"","\"Besides me, he also needs to bring the Barbarian Prince, Asutai, back to the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.\"","\"I suspect someone from the Barbarian Race went to the Ancient Tea-Horse Road to pressure King Landu, which is why he dispatched Du Cang.\"","\"I just didn’t expect him to make a move against the Xiao Family.\"","Elder Master Xiao and Xiao Jing exchanged a confused look.","\"How do you know all this?\"","\"And is the Barbarian Prince truly in Shu State? I had previously assumed that was just a rumor deliberately spread by the city’s grain merchants.\"","\"It’s a long story. I will explain it to you later, Marquis.\"","Chen Yi paused. His gaze fell upon Elder Master Xiao, and he continued in a tone that brooked no argument.","\"Right now, there are two more important matters that I need you, Marquis, to handle.\"","Before Elder Master Xiao could speak, he continued, \"First, there is the matter I brought up during my previous visit.\"","\"Today, I had men disguise themselves as horse bandits from Poshisu Country and as Barbarian Race scouts. They are positioned outside the Ancient Tea-Horse Road to ambush and kill passing merchants.\"","\"By tomorrow at the latest, news will have reached everyone in the city. I hope you, Marquis, will make preparations to prevent anyone from taking advantage of the chaos to stir up trouble.\"","Upon hearing this, Elder Master Xiao’s worried expression turned to sheer astonishment. \"You—what did you say?!\"","\"You sent men to impersonate horse bandits from Poshisu Country, and—and even impersonate the Barbarian Race’s Scout Army?!\"","\"You... you are unbelievably audacious! How could you... How dare you...\"","At this moment, even though Elder Master Xiao needed Chen Yi’s help, he desperately wished he could have him court-martialed.","An invasion by the Barbarian Race had never been a small matter, not at any point in history.","Forget him—even his ancestors, the successive Dukes Dingyuan for the past two hundred years, had never encountered such a thing.","If anything went wrong, alerting the Imperial Court and the Holy Emperor, then no matter how exceptionally talented Liu Wu was, he would undoubtedly become a wanted man.","At that point, there would be no place left for him in the entire world.","More importantly, Liu Wu had told him everything, essentially dragging him and the entire Xiao Family into this mess.","Xiao Jing, standing to one side, felt much the same. He also couldn’t understand why Chen Yi would do such a thing.","Chen Yi, in contrast, remained perfectly calm. \"My apologies, Marquis. I will explain everything after I bring the Young Lady back.\"","Elder Master Xiao’s expression was stormy. He tremblingly clenched his old fist.","In the end, for Xiao Wan’er’s sake, he chose to trust Chen Yi. He asked through gritted teeth, \"And the second matter?\"","\"Liu Hong!\"","Chen Yi uttered the name, his face turning icy. \"I hold evidence of his collusion with King Landu and the Barbarian Race.\"","\"Er...\"","Elder Master Xiao was stunned. Even the shock and anger on his face froze as he stared blankly at him.","If he hadn’t just learned of the earth-shattering thing Chen Yi had done, hearing now that Liu Hong was colluding with the enemy would have made him even more furious.","\"Are... are you talking about Liu Hong, Liu Gongmo, the Left Governor of the Shu State Governor’s Office?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"It was because of the matter concerning the Barbarian Prince, Asutai, that I discovered Liu Hong’s involvement with Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race.\"","\"In fact, Lv Jiunan appeared in Shu State at Liu Hong’s request. His objective was to rescue Asutai, who had been taken as a barbarian slave.\"","\"However, I interfered. Lv Jiunan was killed, forcing Liu Hong to temporarily halt his plan to send Asutai back to the Barbarian Race.\"","\"Du Cang came this time to resolve this very issue.\"","After briefly explaining the situation with Asutai, Chen Yi took several sheets of paper from his robes and placed them in Elder Master Xiao’s hands.","\"Marquis, indecisiveness breeds disaster.\"","\"You... have lain dormant for far too long. It’s time to draw your blade.\"","With that, Chen Yi took a few steps back, offered a cupped-fist salute, and turned to leave.","Elder Master Xiao snapped back to his senses. Ignoring the papers in his hand, he shouted at Chen Yi’s retreating back.","\"You must save Wan’er! I... I will reward you handsomely!\"","\"I... will!\"","Chen Yi’s figure vanished over the horizon, leaving only his words behind.","His voice was soft, but the resolute certainty within it was unmistakable.","Elder Master Xiao’s expression relaxed slightly, but after he finished reading the papers, his face turned ashen.","\"Liu Hong! Liu Gongmo, you treacherous dog!\"","\"You... death is too good for you!\"","It took a long moment for Xiao Jing, who was standing beside him, to recover. He asked gravely,","\"Marquis, this matter is of the utmost importance. That... that Liu Wu is right.\"","Elder Master Xiao took a deep breath, his gaze turning in the direction of South Street. His expression was glacial as he said,","\"This time, I will see him, and the entire Liu Family, reduced to ashes!\"","His Dingyuan line had fought bloody wars against the Barbarian Race for two hundred years. The two sides had long ago become mortal enemies.","When it came to hating the Barbarian Race, if the Xiao Family claimed to be second, who in the entire Great Wei Dynasty would dare claim first?","Therefore, the ones he hated most were those who colluded with the Barbarian Race.","Any such traitors the Xiao Family discovered—every last one of them—had to die!","\"However, this matter cannot be rushed. Allow me to consider it carefully.\"","He paused, then said, \"Send a message to Jinghong at once. Tell her to return as soon as possible.\"","\"After I’ve discussed this with her, we will decide how to deal with Liu Hong.\"","\"Yes, sir,\" Xiao Jing replied, then vanished in a flash.","「Once Qingjing Residence grew quiet.」","Elder Master Xiao steadied himself, carefully put away the papers, and his thoughts returned to Xiao Wan’er.","’Liu Wu... Chen Yu...’","’No matter who you are or what your plans may be, as long as you can save Wan’er, I... I will promise you anything... Anything!’","The figures of Xiao Fengchun and Fu Wanqing surfaced in his mind, and a look of sorrow inevitably crossed his face.","’If anything happens to Wan’er... how could I ever face my son again!’"]},{"number":489,"title":"Chapter 489 - 294: No Greater Sorrow Than Parting in Life","paragraphs":["At this thought, the Old Master called out for the mansion’s steward and gave him a few instructions.","Soon, everyone in the Marquis’s Mansion had returned to their respective courtyards, anxiously awaiting news from outside.","「In Spring Lotus Garden.」","Xiaodie had just returned. When she learned the news, her face instantly turned deathly pale, and tears streamed down her cheeks.","Not daring to linger outside, she hurried back to Spring Lotus Garden to tell Chen Yi what had happened.","After searching for some time, she finally heard a noise from within the study.","\"Young Master, Young Master, it’s terrible! The Young Miss... The Young Miss... *sob*... she’s been taken by bad men!\"","She anxiously pushed open the door, only to see \"Chen Yi\" sitting at the desk. He forced a smile.","\"I already know. For now... for now, let’s just wait for news from the Old Master and the others.\"","\"But... but...\"","\"Listen to me.\"","\"Sister Wan’er is a good person; heaven will watch over her. She’ll be all right.\"","With tears in her eyes, Xiaodie could only look at him. \"I know, but... but I...\"","Before she could finish, \"Chen Yi\" waved a hand. \"Go back and rest.\"","\"Until we have news of Sister Wan’er, let me... be alone for a while.\"","Xiaodie studied his expression, then bit her lip and nodded. She backed out of the study and closed the door.","Her tears flowed uncontrollably.","Faintly, she heard a voice from behind the door.","It was Chen Yi’s voice.","\"No sorrow greater than being parted while alive, no joy greater than a new acquaintance...\"","...","Chen Yi, of course, paid no mind to the situation within the Xiao Mansion.","He had deliberately waited until the Old Master finished making his arrangements before revealing himself.","This was partly out of concern that revealing everything too soon would influence the Old Master’s decisions, but it was also a matter of caution.","Du Cang possessed the Black Magic Secret Skill of Poshisu Country; there was no guarantee he hadn’t left a contingency plan behind in the Xiao Family estate.","If he had pursued Du Cang directly without first visiting Qingjing Residence, he might have alerted him.","He couldn’t afford to make that kind of mistake again.","「Not long after.」","Chen Yi rushed nonstop to the house on Chuansi Street. He was met by a surprised Pei Guanli, whom he immediately instructed:","\"Pack your things and go to your brother’s place right now.\"","\"Don’t return to the Xiao Family estate until you hear from me.\"","Pei Guanli was taken aback. \"Brother-in-law, what’s happened?\"","Chen Yi explained briefly as he strode quickly toward the underground meditation room:","\"Something happened back at the Xiao Family estate. It’s not safe there for now.\"","\"Do as I say. Go stay with your brother for a few days. I’ll come find you once I’ve taken care of things.\"","Hearing this, Pei Guanli hesitated but suppressed her doubts. She ran off to erase any trace of their presence in the house and pack her bags.","When Chen Yi emerged carrying an unconscious Lv Jiunan, she couldn’t help but say:","\"Brother-in-law, no matter what you’re going to do, you... you have to be careful! I... I’ll wait for you!\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment, patting her on the head. He forced a slight smile.","\"There are plenty of people in this world who could kill me, but the one I’m about to deal with isn’t on that list.\"","Pei Guanli’s face immediately brightened. \"I knew it... huh?\"","Before she could say anything else, Chen Yi had vanished from her sight.","After a stunned moment, Pei Guanli muttered a few words to herself and hurried off toward Kangning Street.","Although she could be mischievous at times, she knew how to act when something serious was clearly happening.","It was only when she got outside and saw government officials and the City Guard Army pouring into the streets that she realized just how serious the situation was.","’Sister Wan’er... Sister Wan’er was kidnapped?’","’Heavens, no wonder Brother-in-law was acting like that. He... he must be absolutely furious.’","She wasn’t wrong.","Chen Yi was seething with rage. After hastily donning the \"Liu Wu\" mask, he didn’t even bother to hide his movements as he charged out of the North City Gate, dragging Lv Jiunan with him.","The Wandering Martial Artists along the road sensed his powerful aura. Smelling that something big was about to happen, they all began to follow him.","\"That person... is that ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu?\"","\"It’s him.\"","\"I saw him kill Lv Jiunan in Heiyu Lane from a distance earlier... wait... huh?!\"","\"Am... am I seeing a ghost?\"","\"What is it?\"","\"That... that person ’Dragon Spear’ is carrying... why does he look so much like Lv Jiunan?\"","\"He’s still alive?!\""]},{"number":490,"title":"Chapter 490 - 295: What Gives You the Confidence to Kill Me?","paragraphs":["Chen Yi had no desire to deal with the wandering martial artists in the city.","But nor would he lead them to Puyin Temple.","Thus, the moment he left the North City Gate, he immediately channeled the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism through his Martial Arts: Step Realm to empower his Meteor Butterfly Step.","In an instant, he vanished over the horizon.","The many wandering martial artists who had hoped to follow him and watch the spectacle exchanged glances, swallowing involuntarily.","\"A Body Technique like that... My eyes aren’t deceiving me, are they?\"","\"No mistake.\"","\"What ’Dragon Spear’ used was indeed a Body Technique at the Dao Realm—a path in Martial Arts that is easy to learn but difficult to master. Even if his cultivation is only in the Middle Three Grades, a Body Technique at the Great Success Realm is comparable to the very best of the Upper Three Grades.\"","\"But... but...\"","\"Don’t say it. You’ll just make us all envious.\"","Despite their awe, many were unwilling to miss the show. They left the North City Gate and gave chase in the direction Chen Yi had gone.","\"I just heard that the young lady of the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion was kidnapped. ’Dragon Spear’ leaving the city right now must have something to do with it.\"","Amid the commotion, Shen Huatang arrived on Kangning Street with Xie Tingyun. Upon hearing the news, they followed the other wandering martial artists without a moment’s hesitation.","\"Tingyun, if anything happens to the Young Lady, I... I... I’ll never forgive you!\"","\"I... I didn’t think this would happen either, Huatang...\"","\"Hmph!\"","Though Shen Huatang said this, in her heart, she mostly blamed herself.","As Xiao Wan’er’s personal maid, she had failed in her duty to protect her.","Wasn’t blaming Xie Tingyun just a way to ease her own conscience?","Xie Tingyun blamed herself as well.","If she hadn’t used \"visiting a friend\" as an excuse to sneak out and have fun today, none of this would have happened.","’No matter what, and no matter who’s behind this, I’ll risk my life to bring the Young Lady back.’","Everyone makes mistakes. Some can be fixed, others cannot.","Risking one’s life was just a way to suffer a little less when it came time to atone.","Such was the case for Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang in this moment.","So too was it for the White Tiger Guard General, Lady Tiger Lou Yuxue, Simurgh Phoenix Cui Qingwu, and others who received the news.","...and for Chen Yunfan, after he heard the news.","\"Young Master, the Governor’s Office has issued a warning. You must remain in the Government Office and await orders.\"","Chun Ying looked at Chen Yunfan’s cold expression and forced herself to continue her admonishment. \"The Xiao Family’s incident has already thrown the Prefecture City into chaos. You... you...\"","\"It’s truly not the right time for you to get involved. You... you cannot go.\"","Chen Yunfan was unmoved. As he fastened a long sword to his waist, he gestured to Ning Yu.","\"Ready the horses! Forget everyone else—we follow ’Dragon Spear’!\"","Ning Yu glanced at Chun Ying but dared not hesitate. He went to the stables and brought back three fine horses.","Chen Yunfan vaulted onto his horse, and with a sharp tug on the reins, galloped toward the North City.","His stern voice drifted back. \"Chun Ying, this is the last time I’m warning you—don’t try to restrain me with the White-robed Minister’s doctrines!\"","\"In this world, where can I not go?!\"","Ning Yu and Niu Mountain followed close behind him.","Chun Ying stared blankly at their retreating figures, a bitter look on her face.","She had been with Chen Yunfan for some time and knew his temperament well.","But in some matters, her hands were tied.","Chun Ying sighed. Just as she was about to return to the study to help Chen Yunfan with his unfinished work, she heard a soft voice nearby.","\"Young Master... is he going to help the Xiao Family?\"","Chun Ying looked at the speaker and nodded lightly. \"The Young Master has changed a lot recently.\"","Despite the gloomy, rainy weather, the man wore only a bamboo hat, a light tunic, and a pair of straw sandals on his skinny calves.","In the dim light, he looked up slightly, revealing the face of a middle-aged man with thick hair and a dense beard. His two coarse eyebrows were particularly striking.","He looked at Chun Ying and asked with a smile, \"When did the Young Master start to change?\"","\"It must have been... right after he arrived in Shu State.\"","\"Oh?\"","Chun Ying recalled, \"Ever since the Young Master met Young Master Yi, he... seems much happier than before.\"","\"But because of that, he’s also become more invested in the Xiao Family’s affairs.\"","\"Young Master Yi?\"","The man stroked his full beard, thought for a moment, and shook his head with a smile. \"They are brothers, after all. It’s only natural that the Young Master wants to help Young Master Yi.\"","He paused, then began to walk away.","\"Just focus on the tasks the master assigned you. I’ll go have a look.\"","\"Be careful...\"","At that moment, Shu State City was in an uproar.","The Governor’s Office, Inspectorate Office, Prefectural Magistrate’s Office, Imprisonment Department, and City Guard Army had all mobilized to search the city for suspicious individuals.","The garrison outside the city, on Duke Dingyuan’s orders, sealed off all major roads, stopping and inspecting everyone who passed.","All this left many citizens deeply unsettled.","\"The Xiao Family is still the Xiao Family. Once the Old Marquis gives an order, it doesn’t matter what anyone else thinks. They all have to fall in line.\"","\"That’s the truth... The Old Marquis, sigh...\"","\"Let’s just hope the heavens are watching over the Xiao family’s young lady...\"","...","Three hundred li northwest of Shu State Prefecture City, a dilapidated temple lay hidden among the barren mountains and untamed wilderness.","Its walls were crumbling, and the grounds were choked with weeds.","Thunder boomed, and lightning tore through the rainy night.","Barely visible through the thick cobwebs next to a pillar near the entrance was a battered plaque: Puyin Temple.","Yet deep within, in a Buddhist Hall, a fire flickered.","It cast several silhouettes onto two toppled Buddha statues. At a glance, the stone statues, with their mouths and noses broken off, looked particularly sinister.","Du Cang stood with his hands clasped behind his back, watching the violent storm outside the window. The gloomy look on his face was gone, replaced by a hint of a smile.","Behind him, Uncle Gui and a young swordsman dressed in the attire of one of Liu Hong’s guards stood watch over a woman, their faces devoid of expression.","It was none other than Xiao Wan’er, tied to a roof beam.","She stared around in bewilderment, still unable to understand why these people had brought her here.","Especially since among them was Uncle Gui from the Marquis’s Mansion, as well as two burly men with the distinct features of barbarians."]},{"number":491,"title":"Chapter 491 - 295: Where Do You Get the Confidence to Kill Me?","paragraphs":["\"Could it be... Could it be the Barbarian Race kidnapped me to force Grandfather into submission?\"","Xiao Wan’er bit her lip. \"If that’s the case, I... I will never let them have their way!\"","But even in her defiance, a figure quietly emerged in her mind’s eye.","A handsome young man in brocade robes, holding a calligraphy brush and a book, gazing at her with a gentle smile.","She could almost hear his voice in her ear, comforting her:","\"Sister, don’t be anxious. Perhaps things will take a turn for the better soon.\"","’A turn for the better...’","Xiao Wan’er lowered her head, the look on her beautiful face gradually firming with resolve.","’If my brother-in-law were here, he wouldn’t just do nothing, like I am.’","At this thought, Xiao Wan’er took a deep breath, composed herself, and spoke:","\"Who... who are you? Why did you bring me here?\"","Hearing her voice, Du Cang glanced back, a sneer appearing on his face, which was as gaunt and withered as tree bark.","\"Patience, Eldest Miss Xiao. You’ll find out soon enough.\"","With that, he ignored Xiao Wan’er and turned to the two Barbarians at the door—Asutai and Yuan Jingxuan.","\"Legend has it that Puyin Temple was built before the chaos of the Qianyang Dynasty, back when your Barbarian Race still ruled the lands of Shu State.\"","\"Now, ’returning to your old home,’ what are your thoughts?\"","Yuan Jingxuan was a head taller than Asutai, his rugged face marred by a hideous scar that cut across one cheek.","He wore a heavy, oversized fur coat, its collar gaping open at the chest to reveal half of a bear’s head tattoo.","At these words, he looked down at Du Cang and spoke in a rough, gravelly voice, his Great Wei official speech broken and halting.","\"Our people... will... return. Sooner or later.\"","\"Of course, of course. With the Left King’s ambition, he is certain to conquer Mengshui Pass one day.\"","After offering his smiling flattery, Du Cang turned to Asutai, bowed with cupped hands, and said, \"I have caused some offense previously. I hope you will not hold it against me, Young Master.\"","Asutai shot him a look but ignored him, turning his head to continue staring at Xiao Wan’er with a strange expression.","Having been here for a while, he had naturally learned of Xiao Wan’er’s identity and noticed her resemblance to a certain Mr. Fu from his tribe.","He wanted to strike up a conversation, but with Yuan Jingxuan at his side, he didn’t dare say a word.","Du Cang, having been snubbed, was secretly annoyed, but there was nothing he could do about Asutai.","Yuan Jingxuan’s arrival on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road represented, to a certain extent, the official stance of the Barbarian Race.","If he failed to take the hint, he feared the Peacock King Banner and the other horse bandit factions would face total annihilation.","The Barbarian Race wouldn’t even need to send a great army; a few Grandmasters from Wen Kela’s line alone would be enough to obliterate everyone on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.","Xiao Wan’er looked between the men, her gaze finally settling on Asutai. She gritted her teeth and spoke again.","\"Are you using me to threaten the Xiao Family?\"","\"I’d advise you to give up on that idea!\"","Asutai glanced at the silent Yuan Jingxuan, then said stiffly,","\"We of the Barbarian Race would never stoop to using ’threats,’ not even against Duke Dingyuan!\"","A flicker of approval crossed Yuan Jingxuan’s cold, menacing face. \"Well said.\"","Du Cang looked at the two Barbarians and cursed them in his heart. ’Fools. She tricked them into talking, and they’re pleased with themselves.’","He then approached Xiao Wan’er and said with a sinister smile, \"Since Miss Wan’er is in such a hurry, I won’t beat around the bush.\"","\"The two envoys from the Barbarian Race are correct. I abduc— *invited* you here not to threaten Xiao Yuan, but to deal with someone else from your Xiao Family.\"","Xiao Wan’er froze. \"Someone else?\"","\"’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu. Or, to put it another way, your brother-in-law—Chen Yi!\"","The familiar name, spoken by Du Cang, struck Xiao Wan’er like a thunderclap, leaving her in a daze.","She stared blankly at Du Cang. \"Who... who did you say? Chen Yi?\"","She grew frantic. \"My brother-in-law... how could he possibly be this ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu?\"","\"He... he’s just a scholar! He only has a rudimentary knowledge of Fist and Foot. You... you must be mistaken.\"","\"Mistaken?\"","Du Cang snorted. \"If that weren’t the case, why would I have bothered with a sickly thing like you?\"","He paused, then added mockingly, \"But I can understand why you wouldn’t know the truth.\"","\"With Xiao Yuan still around, why would he let you in on his arrangements?\"","\"Don’t worry. When he gets here, you’ll understand everything. Heh heh heh...\"","Xiao Wan’er still refused to believe it, but hearing his certainty, she couldn’t help but recall her time with Chen Yi over the past few months.","Every little moment.","Moments of happiness, sadness, gratitude, and affection.","’Were all those moments a lie? All part of Grandfather’s plan?’","’No, impossible!’","Before Xiao Wan’er could speak again, Yuan Jingxuan glanced at the sky and said,","\"The boat is here.\"","\"We go.\"","Asutai glanced at the downcast Xiao Wan’er, nodded, and said something in the Barbarian tongue.","Du Cang stopped paying attention to Xiao Wan’er and followed them with a smile. \"Take care, you two. When you return, please send regards to Lord Left King on behalf of my King.\"","Without breaking stride, Yuan Jingxuan grabbed Asutai with one hand and pointed southeast with the other.","\"You. Deal with them.\"","\"I don’t want... to be followed.\"","Du Cang looked where he was pointing. Beneath the gloomy, overcast sky, two figures were rapidly approaching. He snorted coldly.","\"Rest assured, my lord. I’ve made preparations.\"","Yuan Jingxuan gave a slight nod, took a few quick steps to hoist Asutai onto his back, and then leaped powerfully into the air.","An instant later, he had landed at the foot of the mountain and was sprinting toward the distant Chishui River.","His speed wasn’t as fast as a true Martial Arts Body Technique, but it possessed a brutish, unstoppable momentum.","Asutai clung obediently to his back, turning his head to look at the figures hurtling toward them from a distance. He recognized one of them—Lv Jiunan."]},{"number":492,"title":"Chapter 492 - 295: What Gives You the Confidence to Kill Me?","paragraphs":["Asutai came to his senses, his eyes flying open as he stared at the figure carrying Lv Jiunan, as if trying to burn the man’s appearance into his memory.","As if sensing his reaction, Yuan Jingxuan asked in the barbarian tongue without turning his head, \"Do you know him?\"","\"It has to be him.\"","\"Him?\"","\"He’s the one who delivered me to Liu Hong.\"","Yuan Jingxuan stopped in his tracks. \"He’s also the one who abducted you?\"","Asutai hesitated before nodding. He then said, \"Grandfather, he’s one of the Xiao Family. I want to deal with him myself in the future. May I?\"","It wasn’t that he was afraid Yuan Jingxuan would kill the man, but the impression the man had left on him during their previous encounters was too profound.","Especially his eyes—wise and sharp, as if they could pierce right through to his soul.","For some reason, he was inexplicably certain that the man would not die at the hands of Du Cang.","Yuan Jingxuan, unaware of these thoughts, just laughed at his words. \"The little cub of the Black Bear Tribe has grown up.\"","\"Excellent.\"","\"Grandfather gives you his word. Once your training is complete, you will be the one to kill him.\"","After speaking, Yuan Jingxuan glanced back, a savage grin spreading across his rugged face. \"I’m just afraid he won’t live that long!\"","Asutai grunted in agreement, not bothering to explain the strange feeling in his heart. He just silently watched the figure land before Puyin Temple.","’If he dies, then I’ll just have to kill Liu Hong myself!’","Chen Yi seemed to sense something. He glanced to the side at the two tall figures running off into the distance, and understanding dawned on him.","’Asutai has been taken away by his people from the Barbarian Race.’","But knowing that was one thing. Right now, he had more important things to do.","Chen Yi then dragged Lv Jiunan into the Buddhist Hall. His eyes swept over the scene, finally landing on Xiao Wan’er.","Seeing that she was unharmed, a great weight was lifted from Chen Yi’s heart.","But Xiao Wan’er’s expression was complicated as she looked at him. She sized him up carefully, a bitter feeling rising in her heart.","His figure, his appearance, his eyes—they were all so different from her brother-in-law’s.","’Is a person like this really my brother-in-law?’","Chen Yi, of course, was unaware of this. Following his earlier plan, he bowed to Xiao Wan’er.","\"Eldest Miss, please wait a moment. This subordinate will take you back to the manor shortly.\"","Without waiting for Xiao Wan’er to respond, he turned to Du Cang, a grave expression on his handsome face.","\"I’ve brought you the man you wanted. Let’s make the exchange.\"","Du Cang glanced at him. \"So this is your real face, is it? You look deceptively human.\"","After the jab, he turned to look at Lv Jiunan. He sized him up for a moment, and his expression instantly darkened.","\"You crippled his Martial Arts Cultivation?\"","Before the words had even left his mouth, Uncle Gui and the young Swordsman behind him flickered into motion, landing behind Chen Yi.","They formed a triangle, trapping Chen Yi in the center.","Chen Yi remained unfazed. His gaze remained fixed on Xiao Wan’er out of the corner of his eye. Seeing her looking heartbroken and confused, he had a vague inkling of what was wrong.","’It seems I was too late...’","’In that case, there’s no need to play along with Du Cang any longer!’","\"It was a necessary precaution. If General Du and King Landu are so inclined, they can always find a Medical Master to heal him.\"","Du Cang stared at him with a sinister expression, then, after a long moment, he suddenly broke into a laugh.","\"In that case, I suppose I’ll leave a little ’parting gift’ on this sickly little thing myself...\"","But before he could even finish his sentence, Chen Yi was already in motion!","Even with Du Cang blocking his path, he shot forward like a phantom, his speed so great he was little more than a black blur.","Du Cang flew into a rage, roaring, \"You dare attack in my very presence?\"","He had managed to grievously wound Chen Yi with a Puppet before, so naturally, he didn’t consider him a threat.","Now, seeing Chen Yi charge at him, he didn’t hold back either.","A flash of crimson light flared from his chest. The surrounding Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism instantly roiled, forming two pillars of crimson light that connected him to Uncle Gui and the Swordsman.","A majestic pressure smashed down like a mountain—","A small world, just like the one in Spring Lotus Garden earlier that day, unfurled before Chen Yi.","Only this time, the sinister, icy aura was even heavier and more real.","The air filled with black, feather-shaped snowflakes that spiraled and danced, their whistling creating sharp, cutting winds.","Countless colossal trees shot up from the ground, surrounding Chen Yi from all sides.","The ground roiled and trembled as thorny vines erupted from the cracked earth.","Chen Yi took in the scene before him, but his eyes were fixed on the figure in its very depths—Xiao Wan’er, who was now tied to the top of a giant tree.","\"There’s actually one thing I don’t understand...\"","He spoke softly, his forward momentum unbroken.","While using the Wandering Dragon and Phoenix Body Technique to evade the deadly attacks of the Black Magic Secret Skill, the aura around him underwent a subtle change.","A majestic aura, utterly different from the sharp, killing intent of Martial Arts, abruptly descended upon the small world.","In the blink of an eye, it transformed into a vast, boundless chessboard that descended as if to crush the entire small world beneath it.","Then, under Du Cang’s stunned and disbelieving gaze, the giant trees, snowflakes, and thorns of the small world all became pieces on the chessboard.","Or rather, black stones.","And the only white stone was held in Chen Yi’s hand.","He paid Du Cang no mind, instead smiling at Xiao Wan’er, who was shouting something in the distance.","He raised his hand and pressed down.","CLACK.","The white stone landed squarely in the center of the board.","With a single stone, he established a dominant position, forming a five-clawed white dragon—so lifelike that its individual scales shimmered with astonishing might.","It raised its head and let out a resounding dragon’s roar.","It then charged forward, devouring the black stones.","Wherever it passed, the black stones were swallowed into its maw.","And Chen Yi stood atop the long white dragon, riding it through the layers of obstructing black stones into the depths of this small world.","He arrived at Xiao Wan’er’s side.","Only then did Chen Yi say mockingly:","\"I don’t understand. Where did you get the confidence to think you could kill me?\""]},{"number":493,"title":"Chapter 493 - 296: Why Bother?","paragraphs":["\"Where do you get the confidence to kill me?\"","\"...Where does this confidence come from?\"","Chen Yi’s voice echoed through the vast, empty space.","He stood atop the head of a colossal, pale dragon that shimmered with light. Ignoring the stunned and disbelieving Du Cang, he turned to Xiao Wan’er and offered a faint smile.","He smiled warmly. \"Wan’er, I’ve come to take you home.\"","Xiao Wan’er stared at him, stunned. \"You...\"","Before she could finish, Chen Yi cut the ropes binding her and pulled her to his side.","\"Don’t say anything. Don’t ask any questions. I’ll tell you everything after this is over.\"","Xiao Wan’er felt the warmth of his hand on hers. Meeting his faintly smiling eyes, she murmured softly in agreement.","\"I’ll be waiting.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded, then waved his hand, as if bidding farewell to the vast chessboard behind him.","The white dragon roared again.","Rays of silver-white light then burst from the dragon’s body, shooting out in all directions.","With a series of sharp CRACKS, the pocket dimension crumbled and fell apart.","When they could see again, the group found themselves back in the abandoned Buddhist Hall.","Only now, Chen Yi had taken Du Cang’s place, standing beside Xiao Wan’er.","Du Cang, in contrast, had his back to them. His crimson eyes stared blankly ahead, still in utter disbelief.","At some point, the doll in his hand, pieced together from blood and bone, had cracked in two and fallen to the ground with a CLATTER.","In front of him, Uncle Gui and the Swordman stood in a pincer formation, still in their previous positions, staring at Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er with lifeless eyes.","Outside the Buddhist Hall, the night rain pattered down as the mountain wind howled.","A few claps of thunder boomed, and lightning tore across the sky.","It illuminated Du Cang’s withered, wrinkled face, making him look even more ferocious and terrifying.","After a moment of silence, Du Cang slowly turned around. His crimson eyes, as if dripping blood, were fixed on Chen Yi.","\"Chess Dao at the Perfection Realm, a world born from your Mental Realm... No wonder you could shatter my precious Phantom Bone.\"","His voice was shrill and strange. \"Chess Dao, Calligraphy Dao, and Spear Dao... all three at the Perfection Realm!\"","\"To think I’d stumble upon someone like you...\"","\"Good. Very good indeed!\"","Du Cang paused, then bared two rows of black teeth in a grin. \"It’s been a long time since I’ve wanted to kill someone this badly!\"","A torrent of killing intent gushed forth, flooding the entire Buddhist Hall.","Cracks spiderwebbed across the long-neglected walls, tiles shattered, and beams splintered.","Raindrops began to drip down from the holes in the roof.","Seeing this, Chen Yi turned to shield Xiao Wan’er and said softly, \"Crouch down, close your eyes, and cover your ears.\"","\"I’ll take you home soon.\"","Xiao Wan’er did as she was told, even tucking her head inside her cloak as she crouched motionlessly behind him.","Chen Yi glanced back at her, placed the satchel from his waist on the ground beside her, and only then turned to face Du Cang.","His own killing intent was no less potent than Du Cang’s.","It wasn’t just because Du Cang had abducted Xiao Wan’er; it was also because he had discovered too many of Chen Yi’s secrets.","If Du Cang left here alive, he would be a source of endless future trouble.","The figures of Du Cang, Uncle Gui, and the young guard reflected in Chen Yi’s eyes as he held his Long Spear horizontally.","\"Come!\"","He unleashed the full power of his Four Symbols Skill. True Essence instantly flooded his body, causing his brocade robes to billow.","The black shaft of his Long Spear turned golden, inch by inch, as the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism poured into it.","Even its tip glinted with a sharp, golden light.","The aura it emanated was now powerful enough to rival Du Cang’s.","A savage smile twisted Du Cang’s face. His Protective True Gang solidified around him as he shrieked:","\"Your Cultivation is a full two major Realms below mine! I don’t need to use my Black Magic Secret Skill to kill you!\"","WHOOSH!","WHOOSH!","WHOOSH!","Three sharp, piercing sounds like a snake’s hiss tore through the air.","Du Cang led the charge. He reverse-gripped a foot-long short blade in each hand and, ducking low, appeared before Chen Yi.","He spun, his blades carving two arcs of light through the air.","Behind him, Uncle Gui and the young guard bypassed the fight and charged straight for Xiao Wan’er.","Their opening move was a feint.","Ruthless, decisive, and showing no mercy.","Aware of their every move, Chen Yi’s body remained as steady as a mountain. With a flick of his wrist, he thrust his Long Spear.","Golden light flashed.","Three golden lotuses abruptly blossomed into existence, simultaneously blocking Du Cang and his Puppets.","They absorbed the two gleaming arcs from the blades and forced Uncle Gui and the young guard to retreat three Steps.","Protected by his True Gang, Du Cang didn’t retreat. Instead, he advanced, doing his best to dodge the spear’s afterimages while his hands became a blur.","His Saber Dao, at the Great Success Realm, drew upon the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, and hundreds of blade gleams instantly enveloped Chen Yi.","\"In a battle to the death, you think you can protect her?\"","His intentions were venomous. Even though he was certain his Cultivation was far superior to Chen Yi’s, he still chose the most foolproof method.","He was banking on the fact that Chen Yi had to protect Xiao Wan’er, that he wouldn’t dare to dodge, that he *couldn’t* dodge. Thus, every one of his slashes aimed not only for Chen Yi, but also for Xiao Wan’er.","Chen Yi was well aware of this, yet he remained perfectly composed.","Gripping his Long Spear with both hands, he spun it to create a ring of golden light, intercepting every last bit of the Sword Intent.","He then reversed the spear’s momentum and thrust it toward Du Cang.","The Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism erupted—Dragon-Falling Spear: Earth-Splitting!","The floor of the Buddhist Hall rumbled. As the tip of the Long Spear moved forward, a trench of shattered brick and stone tore through the ground, heading straight for Du Cang.","Du Cang’s eyelid twitched. Though reluctant, he had no choice but to evade the overwhelming might of the spear strike.","But the spear’s momentum didn’t falter.","In the blink of an eye, it pierced through the chest of Uncle Gui, who was standing behind Du Cang. The Spear Intent erupted, tearing the puppet’s body to pieces.","Bits of flesh and blood flew everywhere.","The spear’s light traveled a hundred yards before dissipating, leaving behind a trench several yards deep.","Having landed a successful blow, Chen Yi shot a sidelong glance at Du Cang. \"I can protect her. Can you protect those two Puppets?\"","Du Cang glanced back and flew into a rage. \"We’ll see how long you can protect her!\"","This time, he didn’t charge straight ahead. He tossed one of his blades to the young guard, then pulled several palm-sized Wooden Men from his robes and threw them out."]},{"number":494,"title":"Chapter 494 - 296: Was That Really Necessary?","paragraphs":["Just as with Lv Jiunan before, the few Wooden Man statues began to expand crazily the moment they landed.","Their bodies twisted and spun a few times, transforming until they were as tall and sturdy as adult members of the Barbarian Race.","Their eyes glowed crimson, and their hands gripped wooden blades, spears, clubs, and axes. They fanned out, surrounding Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er.","Only then did Du Cang attack again.","The surrounding Wooden Men and the young Guard attacked alongside him.","However, only Du Cang and the young Guard targeted Chen Yi; under his control, the Wooden Men still charged toward Xiao Wan’er.","Chen Yi’s expression turned cold. He no longer stood his ground. Empowering himself with his Great Success Martial Arts·Step, he executed the Wandering Dragon and Phoenix Step Technique.","His speed increased severalfold.","He vanished from Du Cang’s sight, leaving almost no trace behind.","\"You... Great Success in Step Dao?!\"","His only reply, however, was the roar of Wooden Men being shattered one after another, and the dull thud of the young Guard being sent flying backward into a wall, his head pierced through.","In the blink of an eye, the previously crowded Buddhist Hall was left with only Du Cang, Chen Yi, and Xiao Wan’er.","As if he had never moved, Chen Yi stood once again between Du Cang and Xiao Wan’er. His Long Spear dragged at his side as he stared calmly at Du Cang and said:","\"I can protect her for a lifetime!\"","Xiao Wan’er’s body trembled, and she curled up even smaller, until almost nothing but a few strands of her hair were visible outside her cloak.","She had obediently covered her ears and closed her eyes as told.","But as the constant roars echoed around her, she grew too worried for Chen Yi’s safety and couldn’t help but lower her hands and open her eyes.","By the dim light and the intermittent flashes of lightning, she gazed at the back of the figure standing before her.","Naturally, she also heard the two things he said.","\"I can protect her!\"","\"I can protect her for a lifetime!\"","At that moment, Xiao Wan’er had already forgotten everything Du Cang told her. Her chaotic thoughts grew surprisingly calm.","’That’s right. Her brother-in-law is her brother-in-law. Whether he’s Chen Yi or Liu Wu, he’s the one who has been with her all this time.’","’Even if this was her grandfather’s arrangement, what does it matter?’","’At least he didn’t hide his identity to harm the Xiao Family, or to possess her younger sister... and her.’","’That’s enough!’","Chen Yi, of course, knew none of this. His entire focus was on Du Cang.","He was, after all, a Martial Artist of the Upper Three Grades Realm.","Even without the Black Magic Secret Skill that made him famous, Du Cang’s Great Success Saber Dao and his Cultivation alone far surpassed the Yan Fusha of the past.","Besides, he surely had other hidden techniques.","Du Cang, on the other hand, now wore a frighteningly grim expression. Though not as ferocious as before, the icy aura emanating from him was even more intense.","His bone-shaping illusion was broken.","His Puppets were broken.","His Wooden Men were broken.","Even his Saber Dao couldn’t gain the slightest advantage.","It was the first time in his life he had ever encountered such a thing—a Middle Three Grades Martial Artist had thwarted him time and time again.","Du Cang’s expression shifted for a moment. He raised a hand, recalling the short blade from the young Guard’s hand, and stared at Chen Yi with deathly still, crimson eyes.","’Perfection in Chess Dao, Calligraphy Dao, and Spear Dao... and on top of that, he’s even cultivated his Step Technique Realm to Great Success.’","’A peerless prodigy, the likes of which are rarely seen in all of history.’","’But for that very reason, Du Cang could not let this opportunity go. He knew all too well the power such a prodigy would wield once they fully matured.’","Just like Xiao Fengchun and Fu Wanqing back then.","If the Barbarian Race Grandmaster Wen Kela hadn’t personally intervened, those two would now be at least on par with King Landu in strength.","They were only five years short.","’But for this Chen Yi before him? Five years?’","’Du Cang figured that in just two years, he would be able to rampage across the Ancient Tea-Horse Road and sweep through the numerous horse bandits.’","’Add another year, and even King Landu would probably...’","At this thought, Du Cang tightened his grip on his two short blades. \"Your strength is indeed beyond my expectations, but...\"","\"Even if I have to risk my life, I will kill you today to eliminate this future threat!\"","As his voice fell, he threw out several more Wooden Men, which charged at Chen Yi.","As he unleashed his full power, the Gang Qi formed from his True Essence pressed down within the Buddhist Hall. The short blades in his hands stirred it into a swirling vortex.","Like a whirlpool in the deep sea, it pulled everything nearby toward him.","Even Xiao Wan’er, crouching behind Chen Yi, was caught off guard and yanked forward.","Chen Yi frowned slightly. He reached out an arm to encircle Xiao Wan’er, stomped his foot, and retreated abruptly.","But Du Cang seized the opportunity, knowing Chen Yi couldn’t easily wield his Spear Technique, and transformed into an afterimage, his short blades dancing.","Flashes from the blades scattered like flower petals, each one a killing blow aimed at the Xiao Wan’er held in Chen Yi’s arm.","Chen Yi fought as he retreated, wielding his spear with one hand—parrying, thrusting, and blocking. Amidst a cacophony of CLANGS, he intercepted every move.","Instead of being worried, Du Cang was delighted. He sneered and continued his pursuit.","Meanwhile, the Wooden Men behind him seized the chance to block Chen Yi’s path, their blades, spears, swords, and clubs crashing down.","Chen Yi dodged like a phantom, weaving between the Wooden Men and flipping them over one by one with his Long Spear.","For a moment, the two sides were locked in a fierce struggle.","Neither held back a single move, and the aftershocks of their battle left the already dilapidated Puyin Temple in complete ruins.","Only shattered tiles, bricks, and fragments of plants remained, sent flying before being beaten to the ground by the rain.","Feeling the large hand around her waist, Xiao Wan’er felt increasingly at ease.","Although her seemingly boneless body was being flung up and down, causing her heart to pound relentlessly, her mind was calm.","Her eyes were fixed on the side of Chen Yi’s face.","His appearance had indeed changed, and his aura was no longer that of a scholar, but his determined eyes held a hint of familiarity.","Just like that time in the Fengchun Building, when Chen Yi had stood up to Liu Wen for her.","\"Brother-in-law, be careful.\"","Her soft whisper was almost inaudible, but Chen Yi heard it.","In the brief moment after shattering a Wooden Man, he grunted in acknowledgment. His breathing remained steady, as if to say, ’Don’t worry, just watch me slaughter him.’","When the nearby Du Cang heard her, his crimson eyes were no longer like stagnant water.","\"If that’s how it is, then I’ll grant you your wish to be together!\"","The moment he finished speaking, his eyes flared with brilliant red light, and his entire body bizarrely dissipated.","Before Chen Yi could react, the Wooden Man he had just pierced through transformed into Du Cang.","—That \"Jackal\" truly lived up to his name, taking a wound to the chest just to get a death grip on the Long Spear.","Furthermore, Du Cang slashed out several times toward Chen Yi’s hands, forcing him to release the Long Spear and dodge.","Seeing this, Du Cang began to laugh. \"Liu Wu!\"","\"Without this Long Spear, how much of your combat strength is left?!\"","Chen Yi had a strange look on his face. He looked at the spear that had completely run through Du Cang’s chest and opened his mouth:","\"You... was all this really necessary?\"","But Xiao Wan’er, at his side, grew tense, her hands gripping the corner of his clothes tightly.","\"Y-you should probably run, shouldn’t you?\"","Before Chen Yi could speak, Du Cang violently pulled the Long Spear out and stabbed it into the ground beside him. He pressed a few points on his chest to stop the bleeding and grinned viciously.","\"Run?\"","\"I told you, I’ll kill you both today even if it costs me my life!\"","With that, he charged forward ferociously again. He was nothing like the cunning and shrewd man of the rumors, but instead barreled ahead like a Grand General leading a vanguard to slaughter the enemy.","Chen Yi, in contrast, held Xiao Wan’er tighter and patted her reassuringly, the strange smile on his face growing wider.","\"That’s right. Without my Long Spear, I can’t unleash the full power of my Spear Dao.\"","\"But what you don’t know is that when I first began my Martial Arts journey, the very first Technique I cultivated was the Fist Dao.\"","\"So what? Can your fists really... can... can...\"","Du Cang charged right up to him, only to suddenly feel an aura as heavy as a mountain press down on him, making it impossible for him to finish his sentence.","But more than that, his heart trembled, and an irrepressible fear filled his body.","\"You, your fist... Great, Great... your physical body is at... Per-Perfection?\"","The smile on Chen Yi’s face grew even brighter. Facing the figure just inches away, he threw a punch that seemed slow but was deceptively fast.","\"That’s right. My fist is in no way weaker than my spear!\"","Mountain Shattering Fist: Quake!","The Celestial Tier Mountain Shattering Fist, enhanced by Martial Arts·Body, smashed thunderously into Du Cang’s face.","Terrifying power, infused with the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism and further enhanced by Mountain Shattering Force, ground Du Cang’s Protective True Gang to dust, inch by inch.","After breaking through, it slammed violently into his head.","SPLAT!","Specks of white pulp mixed with blood flew in all directions.","A bolt of lightning streaked across the sky.","It illuminated the silhouette of Chen Yi’s thrown punch, as well as the gaunt corpse slowly slumping to the ground.","Amidst the RUMBLE of thunder and the downpour of rain, a faint chuckle could be heard:","\"Of course, my body isn’t weak either...\""]},{"number":495,"title":"Chapter 495 - 297: His Name is Unknown","paragraphs":["Thankfully, Du Cang was as dead as one could be.","His head was shattered.","There was no sign of life.","Otherwise, had he heard Chen Yi’s words, he would have been half-dead with rage, and would have stammered:","\"Perfection in the Chess Dao, Calligraphy Dao, Spear Dao, and Body Dao, and Great Success in the Fist Dao... You... what else do you have?\"","To this question, Chen Yi would most likely have just smiled without a word.","Just as he was doing now.","Hearing the silence, Xiao Wan’er timidly lifted her head. She took in the surrounding wreckage and Du Cang’s corpse before her gaze finally landed on Chen Yi.","\"Is it over?\"","Chen Yi just smiled, first nodding, then shaking his head. He beckoned to retrieve his Long Spear before sweeping her into his arms and speeding toward Puyin Temple.","Xiao Wan’er was still in his embrace. Even though she had just come to a clear resolution—’I won’t worry about whether he is the real Chen Yi’—she still felt a little flustered.","Now that the threat of Du Cang was gone, she was actually quite embarrassed.","Chen Yi, however, paid no mind to her feelings. He carried her to the Buddhist Hall and spoke softly.","\"Weren’t you asking if it was over?\"","\"Actually, there’s one last thing.\"","He looked toward a corner of the Buddhist Hall, now even more dilapidated from the collapse. Lv Jiunan lay weakly in the rubble, his face and body a bloody mess, lacerated by debris.","Xiao Wan’er noticed Lv Jiunan as well and turned her head away, unable to bear the sight.","Although she didn’t know Lv Jiunan, she recognized his Poshisu Country features.","Even if she couldn’t bear to see an injured man lying in the rain, she wouldn’t utter platitudes about the sanctity of life right now.","Besides, her Xiao Family were mortal enemies of both the Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race.","\"What... what are you going to do?\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"I told you before that I would explain everything. I was just considering whether to start from the very beginning—from our wedding day.\"","He then pointed to Lv Jiunan. \"This is the Black Magic Master who caused me to flee our wedding.\"","Xiao Wan’er froze. \"Him? He made you flee the wedding?\"","But she quickly processed it. \"Flee the wedding... You, you...\"","\"But the man who just died, he clearly said you were... that you were arranged by Grandpa to impersonate... to impersonate...\"","Chen Yi met her gaze and shook his head with a smile. \"I was lying to him.\"","\"There were reasons. I had no other choice, but I never expected it would cause you to suffer such a disaster, sister. It almost led me to make a terrible mistake.\"","Though still confused, Xiao Wan’er let out a sigh of relief.","\"Then your face...\"","Chen Yi lifted a hand and peeled back a corner of his mask, revealing half of the familiar face that put Xiao Wan’er’s heart at ease. He then smoothed it back down. \"A Disguise Skill.\"","Xiao Wan’er relaxed completely, the last trace of apprehension and doubt in her heart dissipating like smoke.","At least she could be certain that the man before her was Chen Yi, and not the Liu Wu that Du Cang claimed her grandfather had arranged to take his place.","The idea that it had all been an \"act\" of \"false affection\" had been far more upsetting to her. In comparison, she didn’t care about his reasons for fleeing the wedding, or why he was traveling under the identity of \"Liu Wu.\"","She didn’t even care that Chen Yi had hidden his proficiency in the Martial Arts.","\"Um... shouldn’t we head back to the Marquis’s Mansion first? If we’re late, Grandpa... Grandpa will start to worry.\"","Chen Yi paused. \"You don’t want to know everything that happened?\"","Xiao Wan’er gently shook her head. \"I trust you.\"","After a pause, a blush rose on her cheeks. She half-shrank into the collar of her cloak and continued:","\"I-I mean, we have plenty of time. After... after today, it won’t be too late for you to tell me.\"","\"If we go back... go back late, Grandpa will really worry about me...\"","Her voice was barely a whisper, but it carried a touching sense of thoughtfulness.","Chen Yi chuckled, suddenly understanding her feelings. He decided to go along with it.","\"You’re right. We’ve been out for a long time. If we stay any longer, someone is bound to show up.\"","As he spoke, Chen Yi flicked his spear, piercing Lv Jiunan’s heart and giving him a painless death.","He had originally planned to wake Lv Jiunan and have him confess the truth about how he had manipulated \"Chen Yi\" into fleeing the wedding before killing him.","Now, that was clearly unnecessary.","’He got off easy.’","Chen Yi looked at Xiao Wan’er, who still had her head ducked, and could guess that her neck was probably flushed red as well.","A sense of relief washed over him.","Xiao Wan’er... her understanding was so profound it made his heart ache for her.","With that thought, Chen Yi found his bag and took out the bamboo hat from within. He placed it on Xiao Wan’er’s head as he explained:","\"I will take you back to the Marquis’s Mansion. If the Old Marquis and the others ask questions, just put all of it on me.\"","\"Remember the name: ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu.\"","Xiao Wan’er gently lifted the brim of her bamboo hat. On her pale, faintly flushed cheeks, a few strands of rain-soaked hair clung to her skin.","\"You... you don’t want Grandpa... or Jinghong to know about any of this?\"","Chen Yi grunted in affirmation. He took a clean cloth from his bag, gently wiped the rain from her face, and said:","\"It’s not time to tell them yet. I hope you can keep this secret for me, sister.\"","Xiao Wan’er didn’t hesitate, nodding. \"I promise.\"","’A secret...’","’Just like the secret poem he had written for her...’","For her, this wasn’t difficult.","\"Let’s go.\"","Chen Yi packed his bag, wrapped an arm naturally around Xiao Wan’er’s waist, and was about to leap into the air.","As he looked up, he suddenly froze, his expression turning grave as he stared into the dark clouds of the night sky.","There, suspended in mid-air, a figure was watching them. How long he had been there, Chen Yi didn’t know.","Amidst the rumbling thunder, a flash of lightning tore across the sky, illuminating the figure and allowing Chen Yi to see his face clearly.","—He was dressed in robes as white as snow, his long black hair tied back with a red ribbon, flowing behind his stern, handsome face.","His features were merely ordinary, but his eyes were as deep as the abyssal sea.","More importantly, the man was currently standing on a long, single-edged sword, shaped like a Tang-style blade.","Like a true Sword Immortal."]},{"number":496,"title":"Chapter 496 - 297: I Know Not His Name","paragraphs":["Their eyes met for a moment, and Chen Yi decided against using his Qi Observation Skill to probe the newcomer’s aura.","It wasn’t because he could read the man’s aura, but because he couldn’t see it at all.","This reminded him of his previous attempt to probe Immortal Bai.","’For some reason, I’m certain this swordsman in the sky is as strong as Immortal Bai.’","Xiao Wan’er noticed his expression. She glanced up, but saw nothing. \"What’s wrong?\" she asked.","Chen Yi shook his head. \"It’s nothing. Let’s go.\"","’If someone that powerful were my enemy, I wouldn’t be able to escape even if I wanted to.’","So he simply pulled Xiao Wan’er close and shot off toward the distant Shu State Prefecture City.","But he had only flown about a third of a mile when a clear, somewhat cold voice sounded in his ear:","\"On the fifteenth of the tenth month, I will duel Gongye Bai on the upper Chishui River.\"","\"You... are qualified to watch.\"","Chen Yi heard the words clearly. He fought the urge to look back and flew away even faster.","’I knew I wasn’t mistaken.’","’A swordsman who could go up against Immortal Bai... I couldn’t beat him even if he fought me with one hand tied behind his back.’","’Luckily, the guy isn’t too bright. He just said some nonsense about me being \"qualified.\"’","’What a joke.’","’Whether I’m qualified has nothing to do with whether I’ll actually go and watch.’","’Why would I get involved if there’s nothing in it for me?’","’When immortals fight, it’s the mortals who suffer.’","The swordsman in the sky watched them disappear into the distance. Then, with a light step, his sword became a streak of rainbow light, and in the blink of an eye, he was gone.","Only Yuan Jingxuan, who had just boarded a small boat with Asutai, remained. He stood in the rain, staring dazedly after the elegant, white-robed figure.","Asutai, beside him, paid this no mind. He only watched Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er fly away, a smile playing on his lips.","\"He’s not dead.\"","\"Then... that means Liu Hong is a dead man.\"","The voice snapped Yuan Jingxuan out of his daze. His rugged face was filled with solemnity. He didn’t respond to Asutai, but instead barked:","\"Hoist the sails!\"","Asutai froze, turning his head in surprise. \"Grandfather, you...\"","Before he could finish, Yuan Jingxuan raised a hand to cut him off and whispered in halting Wei Language:","\"Don’t ask. Shut your mouth. We have to get back as quickly as possible!\"","Asutai let out a soft \"oh.\" He glanced one last time in the direction Chen Yi had disappeared, then turned and went back into the cabin.","This left only Yuan Jingxuan standing alone at the stern, his tall, sturdy frame like that of an upright savage bear.","He stared warily at the sky, as if expecting a sword to come flying down from the heavens at any moment.","\"I’m not mistaken!\"","\"The Great Wei Dynasty is truly a land of wonders, to produce such a young... Land Immortal!\"","’Compared to that peerless swordsman, even Chen Yi—who just now dominated and killed Du Cang, a Third Grade expert, with only a Fifth Grade Cultivation—is hardly worth mentioning.’","\"I just wonder what his name is...\"","...","Chen Yi came like the wind, and so he left.","Soaring high in the heavens.","Unhindered by the wind and rain.","Even Xiao Wan’er, shielded by his True Essence, was barely touched by the wind and rain.","In just a quarter of an hour, the two had already flown for dozens of miles.","They spotted some Wandering Martial Artists who had followed them from the Prefecture City, hoping to watch the excitement.","Among them was that shabbily dressed beggar.","He heard a faint sound of rushing air and looked up to see the two figures in the sky. A flicker of surprise crossed his face.","\"It’s over?\"","When Chen Yi paid him no mind, the old beggar wasted no more words and immediately dashed off in the direction from which Chen Yi had come.","’It might be over, but I at least have to go see where this \"Liu Wu\" fought his battle.’","Meanwhile, Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang, who were also in the crowd, wordlessly turned and raced back toward the Prefecture City.","As she ran, Shen Huatang couldn’t contain her joy. \"Senior Sister, it’s the Young Mistress! The Young Mistress is back!\"","Xie Tingyun was overjoyed as well. She pulled her into the sky, exclaiming, \"Damn right, I knew it! The Young Mistress is blessed by the heavens, I knew she’d be okay!\"","Several nearby Wandering Martial Artists also reacted, but they had only heard the sound, not seen Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er.","\"Beggar Cao, did you see ’Dragon Spear’?\"","\"Saw him. He’s heading back.\"","\"Then there’s no show to watch? A pity... We were already kicking ourselves for missing the duel between Liu Wu and Liu Lang, and now we’ve missed this one too.\"","\"Huh? Beggar Cao, you’re going the wrong way! That’s not the way back to the Prefecture City.\"","\"I’m going to see who Liu Wu was fighting.\"","\"Over there? We’ll go too.\"","The old beggar Cao kept his head down and hurried on, paying them no mind as they followed.","The group’s commotion also attracted the attention of others searching in different directions.","After leaving the North City Gate, most people had no idea where Chen Yi had gone, so they were left to wander around and try their luck.","This included the trio of Chen Yunfan, Ning Yu, and Niu Mountain, who had arrived a step too late.","As well as the middle-aged man trailing far behind them.","Even the General, accompanied by Lou Yuxue and Cui Qingwu, had hidden their tracks and was now watching the distant figures in the sky.","\"’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu is alive... which means Du Cang is dead?\"","Given the White Tiger Guard’s network in Shu State, the General was naturally able to deduce the identity of Xiao Wan’er’s kidnapper.","It could only be the absurdly audacious Du Cang.","Lou Yuxue also breathed a sigh of relief and smiled. \"Lord Pavilion Master, your high regard for ’Dragon Spear’ must mean you’ve long known of his extraordinary talent.\"","Cui Qingwu remained silent, her gaze lost in thought as she watched Chen Yunfan and the others pulling on their reins in the distance.","The General nodded. After a moment’s thought, he too followed the crowd.","\"Let’s go. We’ll go take a look as well. We should be able to learn something.\"","For example, they could gauge the true extent of \"Dragon Spear\" Liu Wu’s power, and confirm whether Du Cang was truly dead.","Of course, Lou Yuxue wouldn’t refuse, and she followed after him.","Cui Qingwu was silent for a moment, then followed as well—she had seen that Chen Yunfan’s group also had no intention of returning to the Prefecture City.","And indeed, that was the case.","When Chen Yunfan saw \"Liu Wu\" returning with Xiao Wan’er in his arms, he felt a wave of relief, but he couldn’t help cursing under his breath."]},{"number":497,"title":"Chapter 497 - 297: I Know Not Who He Is","paragraphs":["\"I rushed all the way here in a panic, and for what? I didn’t even get to draw my sword.\"","\"That son of a bitch. If you were this capable, you should’ve damn well said so earlier! You made me rush all the way here for nothing.\"","At his side, Ning Yu didn’t quite understand his master’s reaction.","It wasn’t that his master seemed particularly angry.","It was more like indignant grumbling.","But he had been with Chen Yunfan for so long and had never once heard of him having any contact with \"Dragon Spear\" Liu Wu.","Niu Mountain was even more baffled. \"Brother Yu, is the young master cursing that man with the long spear?\"","\"He is.\"","\"But didn’t he already rescue the Xiao family’s young lady?\"","\"Don’t ask me. Go ask the young master yourself.\"","\"I don’t dare.\"","Ning Yu shot him a sidelong glance. \"Then shut up.\"","\"Brother Yu...\"","\"Shut up!\"","Meanwhile, the middle-aged man in the short coat and bamboo hat behind them overheard this and shot away before anyone else.","He was so fast, he was even a notch quicker than Chen Yi’s Meteor Butterfly Step when it was empowered by the Step Dao.","Moving ahead of everyone, he landed on the mountaintop where Puyin Temple was situated.","The middle-aged man surveyed the tracks and scars left by the great battle. His gaze fell upon Du Cang’s corpse, and his expression grew pensive.","’Jackal’ Du Cang practiced the Black Magic Secret Skill of the Jade Dragon National Preceptor from Poshisu Country, a technique capable of seizing one’s soul and thoughts.’","’’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu is strong, but it’s impossible for him to have killed Du Cang without a single scratch.’","He examined Du Cang’s corpse closely, then carefully sensed the lingering Spiritual Mechanism of Heaven and Earth in the air. His expression shifted slightly.","’The Fist Dao... Liu Wu practices the Fist Dao as well?’","Surprised, he scanned the area, and several images of the battle flashed through his mind.","He saw Du Cang, risking injury, trying to snatch away Liu Wu’s long spear. He also saw Liu Wu smash Du Cang’s head with a single punch.","As he pictured the scene, a question arose in his mind. ’’Dragon Spear’ has a method to counter Du Cang’s Black Magic Secret Skill?’","’Neither the Spear Dao nor the Fist Dao should have the power to counter a Black Magic Secret Skill. Unless... his cultivation technique is special...’","’Something like the White Tiger Guard’s secret Four Symbols Skill, for example. If one had the complete Celestial Tier version of the cultivation technique, it could be empowered by Spiritual Essence to break through a Black Magic Secret Skill.’","After a moment of thought, the middle-aged man still couldn’t be certain. He simply committed his findings to memory and stopped dwelling on it.","But when he saw the bodies inside the Buddhist Hall—Uncle Gui, Lv Jiunan, and the young guard—he let out a soft sound of surprise.","’Lv Jiunan?’","’So he was here too.’","He had followed Chen Yunfan out of the city earlier, so he hadn’t been aware that Chen Yi had brought Lv Jiunan with him.","He was surprised, but upon detecting faint sounds approaching from behind, he made an instant decision.","He hoisted Lv Jiunan’s corpse onto his shoulder and flew off toward the Chishui River.","’No sense letting a perfectly good achievement go to waste...’","「Not long after.」","Chen Yunfan and his group finally arrived.","When they saw the state of the scene, they were all stunned into silence.","Even Chen Yunfan, who had long suspected the extent of Chen Yi’s power, wore a complicated expression.","\"’The wooden men, the puppets... and the peacock tattoo on the emaciated corpse’s arm... There’s no mistaking it. That’s ’Jackal’ Du Cang, one of King Landu’s Grand Generals!’\"","\"’So it was Du Cang who kidnapped the Xiao family’s young lady?’\"","\"’Du Cang must have used the Xiao family’s young lady to force ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu to appear, so he could kill him and avenge Lv Jiunan.’\"","\"’He just never expected...’\"","\"’...that ’Dragon Spear’ would be able to kill him despite only having a Fifth Grade Cultivation!’\"","Listening to the murmurs of praise and speculation from the surrounding Wandering Martial Artists, Chen Yunfan tightened his grip on the long sword at his waist and spurred his horse away.","\"We’re leaving!\"","\"Sir?\"","\"What the hell are you still standing around gawking for?\"","\"That guy is a Fifth Grade who just took down a Third Grade! You two... and me, this idiot... if we don’t get back to our cultivation, we won’t even be worthy of carrying his shoes!\"","This sudden burst of competitiveness left Ning Yu completely bewildered.","But seeing Chen Yunfan ride off without a backward glance, he had no choice but to call Niu Mountain and hurry after him.","Cui Qingwu witnessed this and started back toward the Prefecture City on her own, completely uninterested in the aftermath of the battle on the mountain.","Jiang Xing glanced at her but paid her no further mind. He led Lou Yuxue to a secluded corner of the mountain, concealing their presence.","Once he had a clear view of the situation, even a man of his standing—a Golden Banner Officer of the White Tiger Guard—couldn’t help but click his tongue in wonder.","\"Lady Tiger, you were right.\"","\"That ’Dragon Spear’ is indeed worthy of the Lord Pavilion Master’s attention.\"","Lou Yuxue didn’t respond. Her beautiful eyes were fixed on Du Cang’s corpse, a mixture of joy and melancholy swirling in her heart.","She was certainly glad that Liu Wu had killed Du Cang.","But it also meant she could no longer seek her \"revenge\" against him.","That was a \"grudge\" worth one hundred fifty thousand taels of silver, after all.","Lou Yuxue watched the surrounding Wandering Martial Artists, their chatter growing louder, and took a deep breath before speaking softly.","\"For ’Dragon Spear’ to face Du Cang alone with only a Fifth Grade Cultivation... his potential is far greater than I imagined.\"","\"Sir, do you think we need to ask the Pavilion Master for further instructions?\"","Jiang Xing considered her words for a moment, then nodded. \"You’re right. We should send a message and ask the Lord Pavilion Master for instructions.\"","\"Along with the other two matters...\"","...","「About an hour later.」","Carrying Xiao Wan’er, Chen Yi arrived outside the Xiao Family estate. He gazed at the brightly lit residence in the distance and said softly,","\"We’re here.\"","Xiao Wan’er snapped back to her senses. She lifted her head to look at the bright patch of light in the darkness below and blurted out,","\"Already?\"","\"Soon?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow with a smile. \"Young Lady, you were the one who said we couldn’t let the old... er, the Marquis, worry.\"","Xiao Wan’er heard the teasing in his voice. Her cheeks flushed, and she couldn’t help but pat him lightly.","\"Stop teasing me.\"","Chen Yi chuckled. \"I wouldn’t dare.\"","Their eyes met, and for a moment, neither spoke.","After a moment, Xiao Wan’er’s face grew even redder. She lowered her head slightly and murmured,","\"It’s getting late. You should take me back.\"","\"Alright.\"","\"And you...?\"","\"Don’t worry about me. I’ve already made arrangements.\"","Chen Yi thought of how he had used the one hundred Opportunity points he’d just accumulated to upgrade his Painting Dao before he left, and a smile touched his lips.","Just as he’d guessed, now that his Painting Dao had reached the Great Success stage, his paintings possessed a certain power to create illusions of himself.","Although it couldn’t be used for assassinations like Du Cang’s pocket dimension, it gained a certain level of sentience when infused with the Spiritual Mechanism of Heaven and Earth.","It was more than enough to deceive prying eyes.","As he spoke, Chen Yi descended while still holding Xiao Wan’er, leaning close to her ear to whisper,","\"Remember what I told you. One day, I’ll explain everything.\"","Xiao Wan’er flinched slightly and hummed in agreement. \"I’ll wait for you.\"","Chen Yi smiled, then landed with Xiao Wan’er outside the gates of the Xiao Family estate. He called out in a clear voice, \"Marquis! I have fulfilled my duty. The young lady is safe and sound!\"","The steward and the Armored Warriors who had been standing guard at the gate all rushed over.","\"Thank the heavens, the young lady has returned safely!\"","\"This subordinate deserves death for failing to protect the young lady!\"","\"Please punish us, Young Lady!\"","Amidst the clamor, Xiao Wan’er waited for some strength to return to her limbs, then gently slipped from Chen Yi’s arms and stepped forward. \"Please, rise. I’m alright...\"","Seeing this, Chen Yi smiled faintly and turned to leave.","’Xiao Wan’er was back safely, and he could finally breathe a sigh of relief. It was time to get back to Spring Lotus Garden before his painting-decoy caused any trouble.’","As if sensing his departure, Xiao Wan’er glanced over her shoulder. Seeing him leave, a small smile graced her lips.","It was a smile of sweetness, and perhaps, pride.","A short while later, Elder Master Xiao arrived, having heard the news. Seeing Xiao Wan’er returned safely, he finally let out a long sigh of relief.","Xiao Wan’er hurried forward to greet him. \"Grandfather,\" she said apologetically, \"I’ve made you worry.\"","\"As long as you’re back, that’s all that matters...\"","Elder Master Xiao helped her to her feet, dismissed the surrounding Armored Warriors, and led her into the manor.","\"Ah, Wan’er, this is all thanks to Chen Yu. If he hadn’t stepped in so righteously, I... I fear I would have had to...\"","He had already buried too many of the younger generation; he couldn’t bear to lose another family member.","But when Xiao Wan’er heard the name \"Chen Yu,\" she froze, her eyes filled with confusion.","\"Grandfather, are you saying that Chen... Yu... is ’Liu Wu’?\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"Now, don’t blame your grandfather for meddling, but you’re not getting any younger.\"","\"This young man, Chen Yu... I’ve had a look on your behalf. Not only are his Martial Arts profound, but his skill in the Medical Dao is also excellent. He would be a fine match...\"","\"Grandfather, that’s... that’s not appropriate!\"","\"How is it not appropriate? If he were to become your husband, there might be hope for your illness to be cured.\"","\"It’s really... really not appropriate...\"","Xiao Wan’er stammered, unable to explain why. An impatient urge welled up inside her.","She desperately wanted to go find Chen Yi right now and ask him just how many secrets he was hiding from everyone.","But before she could leave, the Elder Master continued, \"Enough. I will arrange your marriage.\"","\"Coincidentally, Jinghong is about to return. When she does, I’ll have her vet him for you.\"","\"What?!\""]},{"number":498,"title":"Chapter 498 - 298: \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu","paragraphs":["’Let Xiao Jinghong be the judge?’","’Let Xiao Jinghong meet Chen Yi—oh, no, Chen Yu... or is it Liu Wu?’","’If she finds out, the consequences will be... they’ll be...’","Xiao Wan’er pictured that dreadful scenario and was suddenly at a complete loss.","A wave of guilt and anxiety washed over her, and she felt she could hardly face her younger sister, Xiao Jinghong.","She felt like a thief who, having just pilfered gold and jewels from a mansion, suddenly heard the owner’s footsteps approaching the door.","All she wanted was to find a crack in the floor to disappear into.","But Xiao Wan’er had no idea how to refuse Elder Master Xiao’s arrangement.","’I can’t just come out and say that Chen Yu is Chen Yi, can I?’","’No, that won’t do.’","’I just promised Chen Yi I wouldn’t reveal his secret.’","’Besides, if I really told them...’","’...things might get even worse. There’s no telling how Elder Master Xiao would react.’","’Maybe... maybe he would...’","Xiao Wan’er couldn’t say for sure what might happen, but one thing was certain: she was panicking inside.","Even when an excited Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang came looking for her, she could only force a weak smile and offer a few placating words.","Then, with the two of them as her guards, she returned to Jiaxing Garden.","Elder Master Xiao, however, didn’t give it much more thought.","It was only natural for men and women to marry when they came of age.","Especially for a man like \"Chen Yu\"—a supreme talent with transcendent Martial Arts, brilliant strategies, youthful promise, and who had even achieved Great Success in the Medical Dao.","His family background couldn’t compare to the Xiao Family’s, but faced with such a dazzlingly brilliant prodigy, Elder Master Xiao felt it was necessary to set aside concerns about social standing.","After seeing Xiao Wan’er return safely to Jiaxing Garden, he finally let out a long sigh of relief and summoned Xiao Jing.","\"What is the situation outside? Has any news arrived?\"","Xiao Jing’s face lit up with joy. He bowed and said, \"Marquis, Du Cang is dead!\"","Then, his voice rising with excitement, he added:","\"Liu Wu, the ’Dragon Spear,’ decisively killed ’Jackal’ Du Cang inside Puyin Temple outside the city!\"","\"The Wandering Martial Artists who went to watch didn’t see the fight itself, but after investigating Puyin Temple, they discovered that Du Cang was killed by the ’Dragon Spear’s’ Punch.\"","\"The ’Dragon Spear’... his Fist Dao has actually reached Great Success as well!\"","Elder Master Xiao’s bright, sharp eyes widened slightly. \"Are you saying that besides his Spear Dao and Medical Dao, he has also cultivated his Fist Dao to the Great Success Realm?\"","Xiao Jing smiled and nodded. \"That must be how he was able to kill the Upper Third Grade Du Cang with his Upper Fifth Grade Cultivation.\"","\"Marquis, some busybodies are already saying Liu Wu is now on par with the Second Miss.\"","Elder Master Xiao chuckled. \"’Spear and Sword Dual Mastery’ Xiao Jinghong, and ’Spear and Fist Dual Mastery’ Liu Wu?\"","\"No. At first, the name spreading by word of mouth was ’Dragon Spear and Tiger Fist’ Liu Wu. But soon, it was shortened to just two words: ’Dragon Tiger’!\"","\"’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu!\"","\"Dragon Tiger, Dragon Tiger... HAHA! Excellent, excellent, excellent!\"","Elder Master Xiao was immensely gratified, praising him repeatedly. \"Wind follows the dragon, clouds follow the tiger. A Fifth Grade killing a Third Grade... how domineering!\"","\"He is truly worthy of being the husband I chose for Wan’er. Only with such an achievement is he fit to be her match.\"","’Husband?’","Xiao Jing froze for a moment. Realizing what the Marquis meant, he bowed. \"Congratulations, Marquis. The Eldest Miss has finally found a worthy match.\"","He had previously sensed the Elder Master had this in mind, but hearing it confirmed, he couldn’t help but feel happy for Xiao Wan’er.","His thoughts aligned with the Elder Master’s—with \"Dragon Tiger\" around, there was a chance to save Xiao Wan’er’s life.","Even if he couldn’t cure her completely, with his Great Success Medical Dao, \"Dragon Tiger\" could at least prolong her life.","Elder Master Xiao stroked his beard and nodded. \"For Wan’er to have suffered such a calamity, this could be considered a blessing in disguise.\"","\"When Jinghong returns, I’ll have her pay a visit to Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","\"The Second Miss?\"","Realization dawned on Xiao Jing. \"Indeed, the Second Miss should go and meet Liu Wu.\"","Firstly, Liu Wu was a great help to the Xiao Family regarding the Three Towns’ summer grain. It is only right that Xiao Jinghong go and thank him.","Secondly, if Liu Wu truly becomes the Eldest Miss’s husband, he would be a great asset to the Xiao Family.","’The Marquis probably intends to have Liu Wu take up a position in the Dingyuan Army.’","’Third, and most importantly, sending the Second Miss would be an opportunity to probe Liu Wu, or perhaps give him a little warning.’","’After all, the Xiao Family can’t afford to weather any major storms right now. Every step must be taken with extreme caution.’","Elder Master Xiao knew he couldn’t hide some things from Xiao Jing, so he spoke frankly.","\"If Jinghong deems him acceptable after meeting him, it will resolve a long-held wish of mine.\"","As he spoke, Elder Master Xiao couldn’t help but sigh. \"That child, Wan’er... she hasn’t had an easy life.\"","Xiao Jing lowered his head slightly, his smile fading. He said no more.","A moment later.","A smile returned to Elder Master Xiao’s face. He waved his hand and said, \"Let’s put family matters aside for now.\"","\"By now, Liu Gongmo should have received the letter.\"","\"Next, I want you to go and oversee things personally. This time, make sure they have no escape!\"","\"Yes, sir!\"","Without a moment’s hesitation, Xiao Jing accepted the order and departed.","Elder Master Xiao watched him go, his gaze drifting to a mass of dark, oppressive clouds in the distance.","’Dragon Tiger... Heh. Even a youngster couldn’t stand my past behavior...’","’I suppose I have been a bit indecisive...’","...","A similar scene was unfolding elsewhere.","Liu Hong stood quietly in a courtyard pavilion, also watching the rain-swept night.","The torrential downpour bent the plantain leaves beside the pavilion, their tips brushing against the muddy ground with every gust of cold wind.","Thunder boomed as lightning tore across the sky.","The flashes faintly illuminated his slightly aged face and his ink-black eyes.","\"The victor is crowned a prince, the loser is branded a villain.\"","\"I have trod carefully for decades, yet I still cannot escape the shackles of fame and fortune.\"","Though his hands, clasped behind his back, trembled slightly, a cold sneer played on his lips.","\"According to His Lordship’s plan, the first signs of chaos in Shu State are beginning to emerge.\""]},{"number":499,"title":"Chapter 499 - 298: \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu","paragraphs":["\"Grain prices continue to rise. They’ll reach a critical point soon.\"","\"The three counties downstream on the Chishui River are suffering from famine, and they’ll be affected too. Add a plague to that...\"","\"Heh heh, all that’s missing is the final fuse. Just that one fuse.\"","\"When that time comes, Shu State will surely erupt in rebellion. The Imperial Court... the Imperial Court will issue an order, and the Dingyuan Army will have no choice but to suppress it...\"","\"That lord of mine can also use this as an opportunity to meddle in Shu State and lead the Northern Soldiers south.\"","\"Once the rebellion is crushed, even if the Holy Emperor wants to launch a northern expedition, this situation will force him to shift his attention south.\"","\"If the southern campaign is successful... I’ll be able to turn the tables in a single stroke!\"","\"At that point, who will still question what I’ve done in the past? Who would dare?!\"","A vicious glint appeared in Liu Hong’s eyes, his face twisting into a savage snarl. \"But this entire scheme is about to be utterly ruined by a few bastards!\"","\"Dragon Spear\" Liu Wu.","\"Jackal\" Du Cang.","King Landu, Yuan Jingxuan, Asutai, and even Duke Dingyuan, Xiao Yuan—they all deserve to die!","Liu Hong wished he could take a blade and stab them all to death, one by one.","\"They all deserve to die!\"","A murderous aura, imposing and cold, swept out like a dagger’s slash, snapping countless banana leaves.","「A long while later.」","Liu Hong calmed down and asked in a low voice, \"Has any news come from the outside?\"","Hearing his voice, Zhao Liuan, who had been waiting at the courtyard gate, hurried over. His face and clothes were covered in water, though it was unclear if it was sweat or rain.","\"Reporting, Lord Liu. It’s been confirmed that ’Jackal’ was killed by Liu Wu.\"","Liu Hong seemed to have expected this. \"And Asutai?\"","\"I have confirmed with the Cao Gang. The ship has now left the Prefecture City’s vicinity and is heading south.\"","\"The Government Office? The Xiao Family?\"","\"The Xiao Family’s eldest daughter has returned safely. The army garrisoned outside the city sounded the retreat, as did the City Guard Army and others.\"","\"Only the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office and the Imprisonment Department are working through the night to interrogate the captured people from Poshisu Country. As soon as there’s any news, I will report immediately.\"","After speaking, Zhao Liuan glanced at Liu Hong’s expression, then gritted his teeth and continued, \"There’s been no movement from the Xiao Family for now.\"","\"However, I learned that a white-headed eagle was sent from the Xiao residence this evening. Judging by its direction, it should be headed for the Wu Mountain Mutual Market.\"","The corner of Liu Hong’s mouth curved into a cold sneer. \"As it should be.\"","\"Xiao Yuan is old. After an incident like this, the first person he could think of would only be Xiao Jinghong. It could only be Xiao Jinghong.\"","\"That’s good. Heh heh.\"","With Xiao Yuan making no moves, he, the Left Governor, was safe for the time being.","\"What about the Ancient Tea-Horse Road? Was it really King Landu’s scouts clearing out loiterers in preparation for a great battle?\"","Zhao Liuan hesitated for a moment before shaking his head. \"We can’t be certain yet.\"","\"For some reason, none of the spies I sent there earlier have reported back.\"","Hearing this, Liu Hong frowned slightly. He turned his head to look at him and ordered in a tone that brooked no argument, \"You must investigate the situation there thoroughly.\"","\"If necessary, you may use my Seal to dispatch the Hidden Guard. Have them cross the Ancient Tea-Horse Road and attempt to make direct contact with the Peacock King Banner.\"","\"Yes, sir!\"","Just as Zhao Liuan was about to step back and leave, he heard Liu Hong continue, \"Has any letter come back from the north?\"","Zhao Liuan froze, quickly lowering his head even further. \"I... I have not seen a message eagle yet.\"","Liu Hong was silent for a moment, then waved his hand. \"You may go.\"","Zhao Liuan bent low at the waist in a deep bow, took a few steps back, then turned and hurried away.","Once the courtyard fell completely silent, Liu Hong’s expression grew even more ferocious. A strange cackle, like that of an old crow, escaped his lips.","\"No reply. Heh heh, no reply, haha...\"","\"It seems he’s sensed something is wrong and wants to sever ties with me. Good, very good!\"","To think that he, Liu Hong, had served him so loyally for so many years. Which task, which matter, had he not carried out according to that lord’s wishes?","Even when asked to risk his own head to create chaos in Shu State, he hadn’t hesitated.","But now, at the first sign of a setback, that lord was ignoring his letter asking for help.","It was truly disheartening!","It truly made him want to laugh!","’Since it has come to this, then you can’t blame me, a discarded pawn, for being \"ungrateful\"!’","Just then, a chuckling voice came from the side. \"My apologies, Lord Liu. I’ve arrived a step late.\"","Liu Hong immediately schooled his features. As he turned, a slight smile appeared on his face as he looked at the newcomer.","He was dressed in black with his face obscured, wearing a bamboo hat, revealing only a pair of vertical pupils like a venomous snake’s.","\"Elder Yan, your esteemed presence graces us. I have failed to welcome you properly. It is I who should be asking for forgiveness.\"","\"Lord Liu, you are too kind. I am but a humble man from the mountains, unworthy of your praise.\"","\"I have heard of the name Yan Jingchen of the Five Poison Sect since I was young. Seeing you now, your grace is as impressive as ever, Elder.\"","The two exchanged a few pleasantries.","Liu Hong then led him into a quiet room, offered him a cup of tea, and asked with a smile:","\"I truly didn’t expect you to come in person, Elder Yan. Was your journey smooth?\"","Yan Jingchen pulled down the black cloth covering his face, revealing a fair complexion that didn’t seem to belong to an old man. Sipping his tea, he said:","\"Smooth enough. However, the Mountain Race got word of it in advance, which forced me to go to a bit of extra trouble.\"","\"The Mountain Race... Heh heh, I had forgotten that your Five Poison Sect has a deep-seated grudge against them.\"","But as soon as Liu Hong’s voice fell, Yan Jingchen set down his teacup and shook his head.","\"I wouldn’t call it a ’deep-seated grudge.’ It’s just an old affair.\"","\"Oh? Does this mean you no longer wish to seek revenge on the Mountain Race, Elder?\"","\"That was merely a means for me to revive the Five Poison Sect. In the face of true power, grudges and favors are fragile things.\"","Liu Hong understood now. He said with a half-smile, \"After this, perhaps you’ll change your mind, Elder Yan.\"","The Five Poison Sect had been nearly wiped out by the Mountain Race in the past. He didn’t believe that a man named Yan wouldn’t want to avenge that bloody feud.","Yan Jingchen said with a smile, \"I hope so.\"","They made small talk for a few more moments. Then, Liu Hong’s smile faded, and he asked with a serious expression, \"What is the situation over there?\""]},{"number":500,"title":"Chapter 500 - 298: \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu!","paragraphs":["Yan Jingzhen was beaming with smiles. He nodded and said, \"I must say, Lord Liu’s older brother has raised an excellent daughter.","\"Liu Zhaoxue has only been in Shu State for a few days, yet she has already made Xinglin Hall a booming success. I can begin making arrangements tomorrow.\"","\"As long as Elder Yan is satisfied, that’s all that matters. Zhaoxue... well, that girl Zhaoxue is still a bit inexperienced after all,\" Liu Hong said with profound meaning. \"In that case, I will quietly await Elder Yan’s good news.\"","\"It will be my pleasure...\"","In Spring Lotus Garden.","Although it was late at night, the courtyard was still filled with cheerful voices and laughter. With Xiao Wan’er returning safely, Du Cang killed, and the Xiao Family’s high alert lifted, Xiao Wuge was finally able to emerge from the secret chamber. As soon as he returned, he rushed straight to Jiaxing Garden without stopping. Upon seeing Xiao Wan’er, he naturally broke down into loud wails of relief. Xiao Wan’er offered him a few words of comfort and briefly explained what had happened, which finally helped him calm down.","Then, Xiao Wuge wanted to return to Spring Lotus Garden to share the good news with Chen Yi and Xiaodie. Xiao Wan’er, who was currently troubled by the old master’s arrangements, took the opportunity to say she would escort him back. That was how the current lively scene in Spring Lotus Garden came to be.","Although Chen Yi was a little surprised, after dispelling the Mental Realm illusion of his self-portrait in the study, he chatted and laughed with Xiao Wan’er as if nothing had happened.","Xiaodie was naturally overjoyed as well. However, seeing Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er together reminded her of the poem she had overheard in the study earlier. After a moment of hesitation, she decided to pretend she hadn’t heard anything. She silently jotted down the line in her small notebook, being very careful not to note the date or the context. After all, such words—just like the poem Mr. Chen had previously written for Miss Wan’er—would not be good if they were spread around.","After chatting and laughing for a while, Xiao Wan’er stood up to leave with Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang, but not before secretly slipping a note to Chen Yi.","\"Chen Yi, please don’t see us out. I... I’m fine,\" she said.","Chen Yi quietly tucked the note away. Noticing the slight unnaturalness on her face and guessing it had something to do with his secret identity, he offered some ambiguous comfort. \"Wan’er, after surviving this ordeal, you should get some good rest in Jiaxing Garden.","\"Even if the sky falls, there are taller people to hold it up. You don’t need to worry.\"","He then looked at Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang, smiling as he asked, \"Wouldn’t you agree?\"","Feeling a bit guilty, Xie Tingyun turned her head away. \"I-I suppose so.\"","Shen Huatang, however, was more solemn. \"Mr. Chen is too kind.","\"It was my dereliction of duty this time. Fortunately, Miss Wan’er is kind-hearted and did not blame me.","\"But such a thing cannot happen twice. From now on, I will do everything in my power to protect Miss Wan’er’s safety.\"","Hearing this, Xie Tingyun hurriedly nodded and patted her chest in assurance. \"The same goes for me.\"","Xiao Wan’er shot Chen Yi a reproachful look before turning to comfort the two martial sisters from the Celestial Sect. However, she also understood the underlying meaning in Chen Yi’s words, and her heart settled slightly. She only hoped that things were truly as Chen Yi said. Otherwise... she really wouldn’t know how to face Xiao Jinghong.","After they left, Chen Yi instructed Xiaodie to attend to Xiao Wuge’s rest before heading to the study alone. He opened the note, read it, and couldn’t help but chuckle. \"The old master’s habit of arbitrarily playing matchmaker is acting up again.\"","The note read: [Grandfather wants to betroth me to Chen Yu!!]","In the dried ink, a heavily scribbled out word \"you\" could faintly be seen just before the name Chen.","Chen Yi read it one more time before raising his hand and reducing the paper to ashes. \"If I had known, she could have just listened to what I had to say before coming back.\"","Originally, he had intended to tell Xiao Wan’er everything, including what he had done under the aliases of Liu Wu and Chen Yu. Now that Xiao Wan’er had learned of his \"Chen Yu\" identity from the old master, it was inevitable that her imagination would run wild. This only complicated matters.","Sitting in silence for a moment, Chen Yi looked out the window at the dim courtyard, now free of thunder and lightning, and sorted through the entire chessboard of events in his mind once again. Once he was certain there were no mistakes or oversights, he finally let out a long breath and managed to relax slightly.","\"Mrs. Chen’s return should be because of the matter concerning Liu Hong.","\"Even if the old master arranged some private matters for her, she will have to deal with Liu Hong first, which means there are still a few days left.\"","Chen Yi stretched lazily, feeling an all-over exhaustion, and immediately got up to return to his room. \"There is no rush. At worst, I’ll just disappear for a few days...\"","He wouldn’t dare go see Xiao Jinghong right now using the identity of \"Chen Yu\" or \"Liu Wu.\" Much like Xiao Wan’er, he was feeling somewhat guilty.","\"However, after Mrs. Chen receives the news, she must be very anxious, right?\""]}]);
